</node>
<node id="Diabetes Control">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes control is the management of blood glucose levels, improved by proper insulin application and site rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes control is the management of blood glucose levels, improved by proper insulin application and site rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes control is the management of blood glucose levels, improved by proper insulin application and site rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes control is the management of blood glucose levels, improved by proper insulin application and site rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes control involves monitoring HbA1c levels, C-peptide levels, and insulin requirement; worsening control on non-insulin therapies, abrupt HbA1c changes, low C-peptide, or need for insulin within three years suggest beta-cell dysfunction and support type 1 diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Angle">
  <data key="d0">Needle Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle Angle refers to the degree at which the needle enters the skin during insulin injection, a critical factor in ensuring that insulin is delivered accurately into the subcutaneous fat layer rather than intramuscular tissue. Proper needle angle is essential for effective insulin absorption and to minimize complications such as inconsistent glucose control or tissue damage. The recommended angle can vary depending on individual patient characteristics and equipment used.

Typically, a 45° angle is advised for individuals with less subcutaneous fat, such as children or thin adults, to reduce the risk of intramuscular injection. In contrast, a 90° angle is often appropriate for those with more subcutaneous fat, particularly when using shorter needles. The choice of needle angle is influenced by factors including needle length, patient age, and body composition. Shorter needles may allow for perpendicular insertion regardless of body type, while longer needles may require adjustments in angle to ensure proper placement.

Ultimately, the appropriate needle angle should be determined and personalized according to clinical guidance from a healthcare professional, taking into account the patient’s anatomy and the injection technique recommended for their specific insulin delivery method. This ensures optimal therapeutic outcomes and patient safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The needle angle refers to the angle at which the needle is inserted into the skin during insulin injection, determined by factors such as age, needle length, and subcutaneous tissue thickness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnant Women">
  <data key="d0">Pregnant Women</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnant women require special considerations and guidance for insulin administration, particularly during the third trimester of pregnancy, due to significant physiological changes such as abdominal expansion and altered subcutaneous tissue distribution. These anatomical changes increase the risk of intramuscular insulin delivery, especially when injecting in the abdominal area, which can lead to altered insulin absorption and compromised glycemic control. As a result, abdominal insulin injections are generally discouraged in late pregnancy, and healthcare providers often recommend avoiding this site altogether to ensure both maternal and fetal safety.

To enhance the accuracy and safety of insulin delivery, pregnant women are consistently advised to use the subcutaneous fold technique during insulin injection, even when employing short 4 mm needles. This method involves lifting a skin fold to ensure that the insulin is administered into the subcutaneous tissue rather than deeper muscle layers. When abdominal injections are considered necessary, a 45° angle of insertion with a 4 mm needle may be recommended to further minimize the risk of intramuscular injection, although this approach is still approached with caution during advanced stages of pregnancy.

Given the variability in individual anatomical changes throughout gestation, personalized medical consultation is essential for pregnant women managing insulin therapy. Healthcare providers should be actively involved in determining appropriate injection sites and techniques tailored to the stage of pregnancy and the patient’s specific needs. These individualized adjustments support optimal insulin delivery, effective glucose management, and overall maternal-fetal health during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women require specific insulin administration guidelines, especially regarding abdominal injections during different trimesters.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women require special considerations for insulin injection due to uterine expansion and thinning of subcutaneous tissue, especially in the third trimester.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnant women require special considerations for insulin injection, including the use of subcutaneous pinch and specific needle angles, with abdominal injections not recommended in late pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Team">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Healthcare Team plays a critical role in managing complex medical conditions, particularly in the context of diabetes care, by working closely with patients to tailor treatment strategies to individual needs. A key responsibility of the Healthcare Team involves collaborating with patients who require multiple daily insulin injections, ensuring that their insulin regimens are effectively adapted based on ongoing assessment and patient feedback. This collaborative approach emphasizes patient engagement and shared decision-making, allowing for personalized adjustments that improve treatment adherence and clinical outcomes.

In specialized contexts such as pregnancy, the Healthcare Team provides targeted guidance and support to manage gestational or pre-existing diabetes. They assist patients in adjusting both insulin dosages and dietary intake in response to real-time glucose monitoring, aiming to maintain optimal glycemic control for the health of both mother and fetus. This requires close supervision, frequent evaluation of glucose readings, and timely interventions to prevent complications. The repeated emphasis across descriptions on adapting insulin plans and integrating dietary modifications highlights the team’s holistic and dynamic approach to patient care, particularly in high-risk or complex cases.&lt;SEP&gt;The healthcare team provides guidance on insulin administration, disposal, and site selection, especially for special populations.&lt;SEP&gt;The healthcare team is responsible for providing guidance on insulin use, including injection practices and management during physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639924</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Vial">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Vial</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin vial is a sealed container designed to store liquid insulin, a medication used to manage blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes. These vials are typically made of glass or plastic and feature a rubber stopper that must be disinfected with alcohol before each use to prevent contamination. Proper handling of the insulin vial is essential for safe and effective administration.

The insulin vial must be stored according to specific guidelines to maintain its potency. Prior to use, it should be refrigerated; however, once in use, it can be kept at room temperature to minimize injection discomfort. When preparing a dose, air should first be injected into the vial to equalize pressure, facilitating smooth withdrawal of the insulin using a syringe. For insulin formulations that are suspensions, such as NPH insulin, the vial should be gently rolled between the hands to ensure proper mixing without creating foam or bubbles, which could affect dosing accuracy.

Consistent emphasis is placed on correct preparation techniques, including cleaning the rubber stopper and using sterile practices during each injection. These steps are critical to ensure both the safety of the user and the efficacy of the medication. Overall, the insulin vial serves as a vital component in insulin therapy, requiring careful storage, handling, and preparation to support effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a container of insulin that must be prepared correctly, including cleaning the rubber stopper and injecting air before drawing the dose.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a sealed container holding insulin; it must be cleaned with alcohol before use and stored properly after opening.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a container of insulin that must be prepared correctly, including cleaning the rubber stopper and injecting air before drawing the dose.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a glass container used to store insulin, typically used with syringes for dose preparation and susceptible to air bubble formation if shaken.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a glass container holding multiple doses of insulin, used with syringes for administration and requiring proper storage and handling.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin vial is a container holding insulin, used with syringes for manual insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
