<node id="Alcohol 70%">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol 70%</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol 70% is a liquid antiseptic commonly used in both healthcare and public settings to maintain hygiene and reduce the risk of infection during insulin administration. Its primary purpose is to disinfect the skin at the injection site before insulin is administered, effectively minimizing microbial contamination and supporting safe injection practices. To ensure maximum effectiveness, Alcohol 70% must be allowed to dry completely on the skin prior to the injection. This standard procedure is widely adopted in both clinical environments and self-administration routines by individuals managing diabetes.

In addition to skin antisepsis, Alcohol 70% plays a critical role in maintaining the sterility of insulin delivery equipment. It is routinely applied to clean the rubber stopper of insulin vials before needle insertion, preventing microbial contamination of the insulin solution. The disinfectant is also used to sanitize the area where the needle attaches to an insulin pen, further ensuring a sterile connection during preparation. These multiple applications—on the patient’s skin, the vial stopper, and the pen attachment site—highlight the compound’s integral function in comprehensive infection control protocols.

The consistent use of Alcohol 70% across various touchpoints in insulin delivery underscores its importance in safeguarding both the medication and the patient. By disinfecting surfaces that come into contact with the insulin or the injection process, Alcohol 70% helps prevent contamination and infection, contributing to safe and effective diabetes management. Its use is considered a standard and essential practice in professional medical care as well as in personal insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is used to disinfect the insulin vial and application site before injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is used for cleaning the skin before insulin injection to prevent infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is used for skin disinfection before insulin injection and must be allowed to dry to ensure proper hygiene and prevent irritation.&lt;SEP&gt;An antiseptic solution used for skin and equipment asepsis before insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is used for skin cleaning in institutional settings before insulin injection, requiring complete drying before administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
