</node>
<node id="Insulin Types">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Types</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin types refer to different forms of insulin, such as rapid-acting and intermediate-acting, which may be mixed in the same syringe for better glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin types refer to different forms of insulin, such as rapid-acting and intermediate-acting, which may be mixed in the same syringe for better glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin types refer to different forms of insulin, such as rapid-acting and intermediate-acting, which may be mixed in the same syringe for better glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin types refer to different forms of insulin, such as rapid-acting and intermediate-acting, which may be mixed in the same syringe for better glycemic control.</data>
