  <data key="d5">1776688979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variabilidade Glicêmica">
  <data key="d0">Variabilidade Glicêmica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variabilidade Glicêmica refers to the fluctuations in blood glucose levels throughout the day, with lower variation indicating better stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica refers to the fluctuations in blood glucose levels throughout the day, with lower variation indicating better stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels over time, assessed through repeated capillary glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels over time, assessed through repeated capillary glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica measures how much blood glucose levels fluctuate throughout the day, with lower variation indicating better stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels over time, assessed through repeated capillary glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade glicêmica refere-se às flutuações nos níveis de glicose no sangue, medida pelo coeficiente de variação (CV), com meta recomendada inferior a 36%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, typically measured in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL), and is a critical parameter in the management and monitoring of diabetes. It is commonly assessed using devices such as glucometers or continuous glucose sensors, which provide real-time readings to help individuals track their blood sugar levels. Regular measurement of glicemia is essential for people with diabetes to maintain optimal glycemic control and adjust treatment plans, including diet, exercise, and medication.

The term is used interchangeably with blood glucose levels and plays a central role in diabetes care, where both short-term and long-term complications are closely linked to fluctuations in glucose concentration. Effective monitoring allows for timely interventions to prevent hyperglycemia (high blood sugar) and hypoglycemia (low blood sugar). Additionally, specific glycemic targets may be established for different populations, such as pregnant women with diabetes, who require tighter control to ensure maternal and fetal health. Overall, glicemia serves as a fundamental indicator in clinical and self-management contexts for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5acf61a3a7ae9c09040830d5a662f612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/HIPO_HIPER.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low levels of glucose in the blood, typically defined as a blood glucose concentration below 70 mg/dL or below the detection limit of the monitoring device. It is a common and potentially serious complication in the treatment of diabetes, particularly associated with insulin therapy. The condition arises when insulin is administered incorrectly—such as into muscle tissue instead of subcutaneous fat—or when there is an imbalance between insulin dosage, food intake, and physical activity. Hipoglicemia can manifest in various forms, including nocturnal, symptomatic, and severe episodes, and is a well-recognized risk that requires vigilant monitoring and management.

Symptoms of hipoglicemia include shakiness, cold sweats, trembling, excessive sweating, and confusion, often described colloquially by patients as "the sugar dropped" or "I'm shaking." These occur because the brain depends on a steady supply of glucose, and low levels disrupt normal neurological function. If not promptly treated, hipoglicemia can progress to seizures, loss of consciousness, or coma, posing significant health risks. The condition is frequently monitored through capillary glucose testing, and advancements in technology have enhanced detection and prevention. Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems, such as the MiniMed® 640G and MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754, play a critical role by providing real-time glucose readings, issuing alerts, and automatically suspending insulin delivery to prevent dangerous drops.

The use of sensor-augmented insulin pump therapy with integrated continuous glucose monitoring (SICI) has been shown to reduce the frequency of hipoglicemia episodes compared to multiple daily insulin injections (MDI). CGM technology has proven effective in reducing hypoglycemic events in both adults and children with diabetes. Combined with patient education on proper insulin administration, symptom recognition, and timely intervention, these technological tools significantly mitigate the risks associated with hipoglicemia. Overall, effective management involves a combination of medical devices, treatment strategies, and patient awareness to maintain safe blood glucose levels and prevent acute complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia is a condition of low blood glucose levels, one of the risks monitored through capillary glucose testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia é uma condição médica caracterizada por níveis anormalmente baixos de glicose no sangue, podendo ser perigosa e requerer atenção médica imediata.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia occurs when blood glucose drops below 70 mg/dL and is a common risk in patients using insulin or certain medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia is a condition of low blood glucose levels, one of the risks monitored through capillary glucose testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia é uma condição em que os níveis de glicose no sangue caem abaixo de 70 mg/dL, sendo considerada grave quando abaixo de 54 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dff1c37dd504c2e0f6d3e3541019e15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a45688326f1b9dbe3fc7ae4ba51043a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-993ef3cd53aca15e211c42cb48f1b4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc1ebe811024ff43dc507d9ab063076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5acf61a3a7ae9c09040830d5a662f612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1136d6aac4c2e881387a4db1a0f4a3a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
