<node id="Hipoglicemia Grave">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia Grave is a severe form of low blood sugar, defined as glucose levels below 54 mg/dL, requiring immediate attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Grave is a severe form of low blood sugar, defined as glucose levels below 54 mg/dL, requiring immediate attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Grave refers to severe hypoglycemia, a dangerous condition requiring assistance, which was reduced by insulin analogs in clinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Grave is a severe form of low blood sugar, defined as glucose levels below 54 mg/dL, requiring immediate intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Grave is a serious medical condition characterized by dangerously low blood sugar levels, particularly risky in elderly diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a45688326f1b9dbe3fc7ae4ba51043a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
