<node id="Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin is a hormone produced by the beta cells of the pancreas, specifically within the islets of Langerhans, and plays a central role in regulating blood glucose levels and carbohydrate metabolism. It facilitates the uptake of glucose into cells, where it is utilized for energy production, making insulin essential for normal metabolic function. Originally termed "Isletin" due to its origin in the islets of Langerhans, insulin was discovered through pioneering research at the University of Toronto in 1921 by Frederick Banting, Charles Best, James Collip, and John Macleod. This breakthrough transformed diabetes mellitus—a once-fatal condition—into a manageable disease, marking a pivotal advancement in medical history.

As a therapeutic agent, insulin is primarily used to treat diabetes mellitus, including type 1 diabetes, where the body fails to produce sufficient insulin, and type 2 diabetes, characterized by insulin resistance. It is also indicated for monogenic forms of diabetes when sulfonylureas are ineffective or when the condition necessitates insulin therapy. Insulin is administered via subcutaneous injection or continuous delivery through insulin pumps, with dosing measured in international units. Various formulations—such as rapid-acting, short-acting, intermediate-acting (e.g., NPH), and long-acting analogs—are available to meet individual metabolic needs, differing in onset, peak, and duration of action. Due to the risk of severe hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia from improper dosing, insulin is classified as a high-alert medication.

Insulin is the recommended and most widely used treatment for cystic fibrosis–related diabetes (CFRD), where it helps achieve individualized glycemic targets and supports metabolic stability. In this context, insulin therapy is particularly valued not only for glucose control but also for its anabolic effects, which promote weight gain and counteract the catabolic state often seen in cystic fibrosis. Additionally, insulin is used in managing post-transplant diabetes mellitus, further underscoring its therapeutic versatility. Proper administration requires careful site selection, regular rotation of injection sites to prevent complications such as lipodystrophy or impaired absorption, and strict adherence to storage guidelines to maintain potency. Patients must be educated on hygiene, accurate dosing, storage, and safe disposal practices, with ongoing monitoring to adjust dosing in response to changes in health, weight, or lifestyle, thereby minimizing the risk of long-term complications such as neuropathy, retinopathy, and cardiovascular disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone used in diabetes treatment, particularly for adjusting doses based on blood glucose readings to maintain glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone used as a medication to manage blood glucose levels in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11ac81b4dee4dbb3636b8dc2403e0661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69124f1cc2248b019af52b9d2e71c12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036e7cdb0e2bea999e115a813d0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-030fb051231df38c20ff2e1c1e73153d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb6354e9611023f50fce6a399d619a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9864deffdfa4a86915e3d7985867376&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b5ce540c7784f49191a479629af78e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
