<node id="Médico">
  <data key="d0">Médico</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Médico is a healthcare professional responsible for managing and treating patients with diabetes, providing essential medical advice and overseeing treatment plans. This role involves interpreting data related to glycemic control, including blood glucose readings, to evaluate a patient’s condition and make informed decisions about therapy adjustments. The Médico plays a central role in ensuring that diabetes management is tailored to the individual, using recorded glucose information to optimize outcomes.

In addition to monitoring glycemic levels, the Médico guides patients on the appropriate type of insulin to use, the correct timing for insulin administration, and necessary modifications to their treatment regimen. This includes ongoing assessment and personalized recommendations to maintain stable blood sugar levels and prevent complications. Whether described in Portuguese or English, the core responsibilities of the Médico remain consistent across the descriptions: delivering medical care, interpreting clinical data, and adjusting therapeutic strategies for effective diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
