<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Type 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 is a chronic autoimmune condition characterized by the progressive destruction of insulin-producing beta (β) cells in the pancreas, resulting in an absolute deficiency of insulin secretion. This autoimmune etiology is often confirmed by the presence of detectable autoantibodies, which not only support the diagnosis but also inform screening recommendations for first-degree relatives of affected individuals. Early identification through autoantibody testing in at-risk populations can facilitate timely intervention and help prevent acute complications such as diabetic ketoacidosis. Although traditionally diagnosed in childhood or adolescence, Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 is increasingly recognized in adults, underscoring its occurrence across a broad age range.

The hallmark of Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 is the body's inability to produce sufficient or any insulin, leading to chronic hyperglycemia and impaired glucose regulation. This insulin deficiency is typically confirmed by low or undetectable levels of C-peptide, a marker of endogenous insulin production. While some patients may retain residual beta-cell function shortly after diagnosis, all individuals with this condition ultimately require lifelong exogenous insulin therapy for survival. Treatment regimens commonly involve multiple daily insulin injections or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion to achieve and maintain glycemic control. Effective management also includes individualized glycemic targets tailored to patient-specific factors, particularly in non-pregnant individuals, to balance optimal glucose control with the risk of hypoglycemia.

Ongoing management of Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 is essential to prevent both acute and long-term complications. Chronic hyperglycemia, if uncontrolled, can lead to microvascular and macrovascular complications, while treatment-related issues such as lipohipertrophy—localized fat accumulation at insulin injection sites—can further complicate therapy by altering insulin absorption and glycemic stability. Therefore, comprehensive care includes regular monitoring, patient education, and adjustments in insulin delivery techniques. As a lifelong metabolic disorder, Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 demands continuous, multidimensional management to optimize health outcomes and quality of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed9228bfdd30fe45392a8a9fb8d106b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49920639f738eae3de220d132cbc081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1abe83ba7814c7afe7a123e2f79a10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
