<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a medical technology designed to continuously track glucose levels in individuals with diabetes by measuring interstitial fluid glucose concentrations through a small, subcutaneous sensor placed on the skin. The sensor collects glucose data at regular intervals—typically every few minutes, often as frequently as every 5 minutes—providing real-time, dynamic insights into glucose trends, fluctuations, and patterns throughout the day and night. Unlike traditional finger-prick blood glucose testing, which offers only intermittent snapshots, CGM delivers a comprehensive view of glycemic control, enabling early detection of hypoglycemic and hyperglycemic events. This allows individuals, particularly those with type 1 diabetes or type 2 diabetes requiring insulin therapy, to make timely adjustments to insulin dosing, diet, or physical activity, thereby improving glycemic outcomes and reducing the risk of complications.

CGM systems enhance diabetes management by reducing the need for frequent blood sampling, minimizing patient discomfort, and supporting better adherence to monitoring regimens. Many systems include real-time alerts for rapid glucose changes or values outside preset thresholds, facilitating proactive interventions. CGM is frequently integrated with insulin pumps, forming hybrid closed-loop systems that automatically adjust insulin delivery based on current glucose levels, enabling more precise and individualized glycemic regulation. Clinical guidelines increasingly recommend CGM for individuals on insulin therapy due to its demonstrated benefits in reducing hypoglycemia and improving overall glucose control. The technology is also utilized in retrospective analysis and virtual or hospital-based clinical settings, where continuous data supports informed treatment decisions and improved patient outcomes.

Beyond general diabetes care, Continuous Glucose Monitoring has been discussed in international consensus statements and studied for specialized applications. For instance, CGM may be more sensitive than the oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) in detecting early risk for progression to cystic fibrosis–related diabetes, although it is not currently recommended for routine screening in this context. Additionally, CGM data can be compared with A1C measurements to provide a more complete picture of long-term and daily glucose control, bridging the gap between laboratory results and real-time monitoring. As a transformative advancement in diabetes management, CGM supports safer, more informed, and personalized care, representing a significant evolution from traditional blood glucose monitoring methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a method that tracks glucose levels in interstitial fluid, providing real-time data and parameters such as Time in Range (TIR), hypoglycemia time, glucose variability, and estimated average glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring is a technology used to track glucose levels in real time, improving glycemic management and reducing hypoglycemia risk in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring is a method used to obtain glycemic data including Time In Range, hypoglycemia levels, and glycemic variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b712afd345ff5f7503205905d3131f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db64ab86a0fa43346644d41501429015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6dadde3434f68ef74ebdf23be6a24ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862cb6f254fb8ebb4f3e1080dbf4f53c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c7e3d6615d1076ae20653358419ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af4e8af9934463f38c5951016d9664b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f731774e5187eb76527ebeabefeeeb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4</data>
