<node id="Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The sensor is a medical device placed under the skin to measure glucose levels in interstitial fluid and transmit data to a reader or smartphone.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor is a medical device used for continuous glucose monitoring, requiring careful handling to remain in place.&lt;SEP&gt;The sensor is a medical device placed under the skin to measure glucose levels in interstitial fluid and transmit data to a reader or smartphone.&lt;SEP&gt;A sensor is a medical device used to monitor glucose levels continuously, potentially reducing the need for frequent use of a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;A sensor is a medical device used to monitor glucose levels continuously, potentially reducing the need for frequent use of a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;A sensor is a medical device used in CGM systems to measure glucose levels in the interstitial fluid, requiring calibration in some models.</data>
