<node id="Interstitial Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial fluid is the bodily fluid between cells where glucose is measured by the CGM sensor, with values closely correlating to blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial fluid is the bodily fluid between cells where glucose is measured by the CGM sensor, with values closely correlating to blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial fluid is the bodily fluid between cells where the glucose sensor measures glucose levels, which closely correlate with blood glucose but may have a time lag of approximately 10 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial fluid is the bodily fluid between cells where the glucose sensor measures glucose levels, which closely correlate with blood glucose but may have a time lag of approximately 10 minutes.</data>
