</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Pump is a medical device designed for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII), serving as a critical tool in the management of diabetes. It delivers rapid-acting insulin in precise amounts through a cannula inserted under the skin, either via tubing or in a tubeless design, providing both basal insulin to maintain background levels and bolus insulin for mealtime or correction doses. The device is small, computerized, and typically worn on the body, enabling flexible and personalized insulin therapy that supports intensive treatment regimens such as the SICI system. It is frequently compared with multiple daily injections and is studied in both outpatient and hospital settings for its efficacy in improving glycemic control.

Insulin Pump technology is often integrated with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems to enhance treatment safety and effectiveness. These integrations support automated insulin dosing and enable advanced features such as sensor-augmented pumping, low-glucose suspend (LGS), and predictive low-glucose suspend (PLGS) functions, which automatically adjust or halt insulin delivery based on real-time glucose readings. This integration allows for proactive diabetes management, reducing the risk of hypoglycemia and promoting greater glucose stability. The device plays a key role in both commercial and DIY closed-loop systems, where it works in concert with CGM data to optimize insulin delivery.

Given its essential function, the reliability of the Insulin Pump is paramount; any system failure can disrupt insulin flow and potentially lead to acute metabolic complications such as diabetic ketoacidosis, requiring immediate intervention including ketone testing and alternative insulin administration. Users must therefore remain vigilant about device operation and be prepared to respond to malfunctions. Overall, the Insulin Pump represents a significant advancement in diabetes care, offering a more responsive, accurate, and convenient method of insulin delivery that supports improved long-term outcomes for individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8085de73bd4812f966c059205e5d3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49920639f738eae3de220d132cbc081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94e98f4cb6f97fceae5e6d8c30c871b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e1858f15899659bc0116977a6e1e000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862cb6f254fb8ebb4f3e1080dbf4f53c</data>
