</node>
<node id="Lag Time">
  <data key="d0">Lag Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lag time is the approximately 10-minute delay between glucose levels in interstitial fluid (measured by CGM) and blood glucose levels (measured by finger prick).&lt;SEP&gt;Lag time is the approximately 10-minute delay between glucose levels in interstitial fluid (measured by CGM) and blood glucose levels (measured by finger prick).&lt;SEP&gt;Lag time is the approximately 10-minute delay between glucose levels in the interstitial fluid (measured by the sensor) and blood glucose levels (measured by finger prick), requiring users to interpret trend arrows alongside numerical values.&lt;SEP&gt;Lag time is the approximately 10-minute delay between glucose levels in the interstitial fluid (measured by the sensor) and blood glucose levels (measured by finger prick), requiring users to interpret trend arrows alongside numerical values.&lt;SEP&gt;Lag time refers to the delay between blood glucose levels and interstitial glucose measurements as detected by CGM sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Lag Time is the average 10-minute delay between capillary blood glucose and interstitial glucose measurements, affecting real-time interpretation.</data>
