<node id="FreeStyle Libre">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle Libre is a commercially available glucose sensor and standalone continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system designed for individuals with diabetes to track glucose levels. It functions as an intermittently scanned CGM, meaning users must actively scan the sensor with a compatible reader or smartphone to access real-time glucose data, rather than receiving automatic, continuous alerts. The system is widely used in Brazil and other regions due to its ease of use and reliability.

The FreeStyle Libre sensor operates for up to 14 days without requiring calibration through finger-prick blood glucose tests, offering a convenient alternative to traditional monitoring methods. This calibration-free feature enhances user compliance and reduces discomfort associated with frequent blood sampling. However, while the system is designed for continuous glucose monitoring, it is not fully real-time; data are only retrieved when the user scans the sensor.

It is important to note that the accuracy of FreeStyle Libre readings can be affected by certain external factors. High doses of ascorbic acid (vitamin C) and other medications or substances may cause sensor interference, potentially leading to inaccurate glucose measurements. Users are advised to be aware of these limitations, particularly when taking supplements or medications known to impact sensor performance. Overall, FreeStyle Libre provides a practical, minimally invasive solution for glucose monitoring, balancing functionality with user accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is a continuous glucose monitoring system developed by Abbott, used to obtain glycemic values via a sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is a glucose monitoring system by Abbott that does not require calibration during its 14-day sensor lifespan and is recently commercialized in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre é um sensor de glicose que exige escaneamento para visualizar os níveis de açúcar no sangue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8651ec88cb5333f03b8af01fee4d3cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211</data>
