<node id="Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration is the process of aligning CGM sensor readings with blood glucose values obtained from finger-prick tests, required by some sensors but not all.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration is the process of aligning CGM sensor readings with blood glucose values obtained from finger-prick tests, required by some sensors but not all.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration is the process of aligning CGM sensor readings with blood glucose values obtained from finger-prick tests, required by some sensors but not by others like FreeStyle Libre.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration is the process of aligning CGM sensor readings with blood glucose values obtained from finger-prick tests, required by some sensors but not by others like FreeStyle Libre.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration is a process required by some real-time CGM systems, where the user adjusts the device readings based on blood glucose measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
