<node id="Tokyo">
  <data key="d0">Tokyo</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Tokyo is the host city of the World Athletics Championship, serving as the venue for a historic athletic achievement. During the championship, American sprinter Noah Carter set a new world record in the 100-meter sprint, marking a significant milestone in track and field history. Multiple descriptions consistently highlight Tokyo's role in hosting this prestigious global event, emphasizing its importance as a center for international sports competition. The city's selection as host underscores its capability to organize and support major athletic gatherings on a world stage. While one description notes Tokyo's lack of relevance to diabetes-related content, the overwhelming context centers on its pivotal role in the World Athletics Championship and the record-breaking performance by Noah Carter. All accounts align on the key details: Tokyo hosted the championship, and Noah Carter achieved a new 100m sprint record during the event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5ebd46f8491409b5f07f5c83542afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a18ecfcb20fceb4fd80ab22186964e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
