<node id="Caneta Descartável">
  <data key="d0">Caneta Descartável</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Caneta Descartável is a single-use insulin delivery device designed for individuals with diabetes to administer insulin conveniently and efficiently. It is a type of insulin pen that comes pre-filled with insulin, eliminating the need for separate insulin vials or cartridge loading. The device is engineered for ease of use, particularly for patients who require regular insulin injections and benefit from a portable, ready-to-use solution.

The Caneta Descartável is typically discarded after complete use, once the insulin supply is depleted, hence its designation as "disposable." It contains a fixed amount of insulin that is used over a prescribed period, depending on the patient’s dosage requirements. The device must be stored appropriately, either under refrigeration or at room temperature, in accordance with manufacturer and medical guidelines, to maintain insulin stability and efficacy.

Functionally, the Caneta Descartável serves as a self-injection tool that simplifies insulin administration, reducing preparation time and minimizing the risk of dosing errors. It is widely used in diabetes management due to its portability, discretion, and user-friendly design. As a prefilled, disposable system, it supports adherence to treatment regimens, particularly for patients managing type 1 or type 2 diabetes who rely on exogenous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a3958ecd422660b4cd1e47e31e1b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/descarte.pdf</data>
