<node id="Álcool 70%">
  <data key="d0">Álcool 70%</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Álcool 70% is an antiseptic solution commonly used for skin disinfection in medical and clinical settings. It is primarily applied to clean the site of insulin injection, ensuring a sterile environment before the administration of insulin, particularly in healthcare facilities such as health clinics. In addition to insulin application, it is also used to disinfect the area where the needle attaches to the insulin pen, helping prevent contamination and infection at the device interface.

The solution is further utilized in capillary glucose testing, where it serves to disinfect the skin prior to blood sampling. This application is critical in maintaining hygiene and accuracy during glucose monitoring procedures, especially in diabetic care. While some descriptions refer to Álcool 70% as an antiseptic and others as a disinfectant, both terms reflect its primary function of reducing microbial load on the skin and medical equipment surfaces. The consistency across multiple descriptions highlights its standard role in pre-injection and pre-testing protocols, emphasizing its importance in infection control practices within both clinical and self-care contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Álcool 70% is an antiseptic liquid used for skin disinfection before blood sampling in capillary glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40</data>
