<node id="HbA1c">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c, or glycated hemoglobin, is a clinical biomarker that measures the percentage of hemoglobin in red blood cells that has become glycated, reflecting average blood glucose levels over the past two to three months. It is a standardized blood test widely used in the diagnosis, screening, and ongoing management of diabetes mellitus. A threshold of ≥6.5% HbA1c is recognized by the International Expert Committee and various clinical guidelines as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes, while values between 5.7% and 6.4% indicate prediabetes, signifying an increased risk of developing type 2 diabetes. As such, HbA1c serves as a critical tool for early detection, risk assessment, and long-term glycemic monitoring across diverse clinical and research settings.

Beyond diagnosis, HbA1c is a cornerstone in evaluating long-term glucose control in individuals with diabetes. It is frequently used as a primary endpoint in clinical trials assessing treatment efficacy, including insulin therapies such as continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII) and multiple daily injections (MDI), with evidence showing CSII may improve HbA1c outcomes in certain populations. Different insulin formulations, like insulin lispro and regular human insulin, have demonstrated comparable effects on HbA1c in pediatric patients, indicating similar efficacy in glycemic control. The biomarker also correlates with time in range (TIR) derived from continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), and CGM use has been consistently linked to lower HbA1c levels, reinforcing its value in optimizing diabetes management.

HbA1c plays a vital role in guiding treatment decisions, particularly in high-risk groups such as pregnant women with diabetes. Clinical recommendations emphasize tight glycemic control during pregnancy, with target HbA1c levels below 6.5% for women planning conception or in the first trimester, and even stricter goals below 6.0% in later stages to minimize maternal and fetal complications. Structured diabetes education programs have been shown to significantly reduce HbA1c, highlighting the importance of patient education and self-management. Despite its widespread utility, HbA1c has limitations—it does not capture acute glucose fluctuations such as hypoglycemia or postprandial spikes—yet it remains a reliable, objective, and globally adopted measure for assessing long-term glycemic control and treatment effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is a measure of long-term blood glucose levels and is used as a target for glycemic control in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is a measure of long-term blood glucose control, with tighter targets evaluated in multiple diabetes trials.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is a measure of average blood glucose levels over time and is used as a target in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is a measure of long-term blood glucose control and is used as a key indicator in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c é uma medida de glicemia média ao longo de aproximadamente 2 a 3 meses, usada como indicador do controle glicêmico em pessoas com diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a45688326f1b9dbe3fc7ae4ba51043a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
