<node id="Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring (AMGC) is a method where a person pricks their finger to obtain a blood sample for glucose measurement using a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring (AMGC) is a method where a person pricks their finger to obtain a blood sample for glucose measurement using a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring (AMGC) is a method where a person pricks their finger to obtain a blood sample for glucose measurement using a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose monitoring is a technique used in diabetes management to measure blood sugar levels from fingerstick samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose monitoring is a technique used in diabetes management to measure blood sugar levels from fingerstick samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed2aa7fa8ee59d19d7f3898042c3742</data>
