<node id="Blood Glucose Variability">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose variability refers to fluctuations in blood sugar levels, often increased in patients with lipohypertrophy due to inconsistent insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose variability refers to large fluctuations in blood sugar levels throughout the day, often caused by inconsistent insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose variability refers to large fluctuations in blood sugar levels throughout the day, often caused by inconsistent insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose variability refers to large fluctuations in blood sugar levels throughout the day, often caused by inconsistent insulin absorption in lipodystrophy-affected areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
