<node id="Insulin Needle">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin needle is a disposable component used for subcutaneous insulin injection, recommended to be replaced after each use to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous injection is the method of administering insulin under the skin, commonly in the abdomen, with absorption influenced by site, technique, and insulin temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous injection is the method of delivering insulin into the fatty tissue beneath the skin, avoiding muscle to prevent altered absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous injection is the standard method of insulin administration, delivering insulin into the fat layer beneath the skin for gradual absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous injection is the standard method of insulin administration, delivering insulin into the fat layer beneath the skin for gradual absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous injection is a method of administering insulin into the fatty tissue beneath the skin, requiring proper technique to ensure accurate dosage delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous injection is the recommended method of insulin administration, involving injection into the fatty tissue beneath the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdomen">
  <data key="d0">Abdomen</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The abdomen is the preferred site for insulin injection, widely recognized for its fast and consistent absorption rate. This efficiency is attributed to the area's rich vascularization, which facilitates rapid insulin uptake into the bloodstream, making it particularly effective for timely glucose management. As a result, the abdomen is frequently recommended for subcutaneous insulin administration in clinical and self-care settings.

However, proper injection technique is essential to ensure safety and effectiveness. The area within three to four finger widths of the navel should be avoided to prevent complications and ensure optimal absorption. Despite minor variations in phrasing across descriptions, all emphasize the abdomen’s reliability and speed in insulin delivery, reinforcing its status as a primary injection site. Collectively, the information underscores the abdomen’s clinical importance in diabetes management due to its physiological advantages and practical accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The abdomen is a common site for insulin injection, considered safe during the first and second trimesters of pregnancy if proper technique is used.&lt;SEP&gt;The abdomen is the preferred injection site for insulin due to faster and more consistent absorption compared to other body regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdomen is a recommended site for insulin injection, particularly the right and left lateral regions, three to four fingers away from the umbilical scar, with special considerations during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Activity">
  <data key="d0">Physical Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Activity is a critical factor in diabetes management, significantly influencing blood glucose levels and insulin dynamics. It affects insulin absorption, often accelerating it during and after exercise, which can increase the risk of hypoglycemia. As a result, individuals with diabetes—particularly those using insulin therapy—must carefully consider the timing and dosage of insulin administration in relation to physical activity. Adjustments in insulin dosing are frequently necessary to maintain glycemic stability, and real-time glucose monitoring is essential to guide these modifications effectively.

The impact of Physical Activity on insulin needs extends to advanced diabetes technologies, such as hybrid closed-loop insulin delivery systems, where physical activity must be manually announced to enable the system to adapt insulin dosing appropriately. This proactive input helps prevent hypoglycemia by temporarily reducing insulin delivery in anticipation of increased glucose utilization. Additionally, the selection of insulin injection sites plays a crucial role, as exercising muscles can enhance insulin absorption from nearby sites, further elevating hypoglycemia risk; thus, site rotation and strategic placement are recommended safety measures.

Beyond glycemic control, Physical Activity, particularly regular aerobic exercise, offers broader metabolic benefits. It is recommended for improving both glycemic and lipid control, especially in patients with conditions such as lipodystrophy, where metabolic dysregulation is prominent. As a modifiable lifestyle intervention, Physical Activity serves not only as a preventive and therapeutic strategy but also as a dynamic variable that must be integrated into personalized diabetes care plans using data from continuous glucose monitoring and patient self-reporting.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity is a factor in the ADA risk test; lack of it adds one point to the diabetes risk score.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity is a lifestyle intervention that enhances insulin sensitivity and helps prevent or manage type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity is a recommended intervention for weight loss and diabetes prevention in individuals with prediabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Technique Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Technique Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin technique assessment involves observation and palpation to evaluate proper injection practices and detect complications like lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Palpation">
  <data key="d0">Palpation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Palpation is a physical examination technique used to detect lipohypertrophy by feeling for tissue changes at injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observation">
  <data key="d0">Observation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Observation is a visual assessment method used to evaluate injection sites for signs of lipodystrophy or improper technique.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dosing">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dosing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin dosing refers to the amount and frequency of insulin administration, tailored to individual needs based on diet, activity, and metabolic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dosing is a critical medical procedure in hospital settings that relies on accurate glucose measurement, typically using point-of-care blood glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Manufacturer Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Manufacturer Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin manufacturer guidelines specify the duration for which in-use insulin can be stored at room temperature, varying by product.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NPH Insulin">
  <data key="d0">NPH Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH insulin, also known as Protaphane HM, is an intermediate-acting form of human insulin used in the management of diabetes. It is characterized by its cloudy appearance and must be gently mixed or homogenized before administration to ensure proper resuspension, which is critical for consistent pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics following subcutaneous injection. This resuspension step is essential to maintain uniformity and therapeutic efficacy.

NPH insulin is commonly used in combination with faster-acting insulins, such as regular insulin or ultra-rapid insulin, to provide both basal and prandial glucose control. When preparing mixed insulin regimens, NPH insulin should be drawn into the syringe first to prevent contamination of the rapid-acting formulation with the intermediate-acting suspension. It is compatible for mixing with regular or ultra-rapid insulins in the same syringe, offering flexibility in insulin therapy regimens.

Once opened, NPH insulin has a shelf life of approximately 30 days, after which its potency and safety may diminish. As a slow- to intermediate-acting insulin, it provides a prolonged duration of action compared to rapid-acting forms, making it a foundational component in many insulin treatment plans for both type 1 and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;An intermediate-acting insulin type that can be mixed with regular insulin in the same syringe using a defined preparation sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH insulin is an intermediate-acting insulin that is less flexible and associated with higher risks of hypoglycemia and postprandial hyperglycemia compared to rapid-acting analogs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fc83e266bdeb54c4139a50adf2b793a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641722</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Regular Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular Insulin is a short-acting form of insulin used in the management of diabetes, particularly for controlling blood glucose levels. It is characterized by its clear appearance and rapid onset of action, making it suitable for use in both standalone therapy and in combination with intermediate-acting insulins. A key application of Regular Insulin involves its use in mixtures with NPH (Neutral Protamine Hagedorn) insulin, where it contributes to achieving balanced and sustained glucose control in diabetic patients.

When preparing mixed insulin injections, Regular Insulin must be drawn into the syringe before NPH insulin. This sequence is critical to prevent contamination of the Regular Insulin vial with the NPH insulin, which contains protamine and is cloudy in appearance. To maintain purity and efficacy, healthcare guidelines emphasize that Regular Insulin should be aspirated first due to its clear formulation. This procedural step ensures that the short-acting component remains uncontaminated by the intermediate-acting insulin, preserving its pharmacological properties.

Unlike NPH insulin, Regular Insulin does not require mixing or resuspension before use, as it remains in a clear, soluble form. This characteristic simplifies its administration and reduces the risk of dosing inaccuracies. Overall, Regular Insulin plays a vital role in insulin regimens, especially in settings where precise timing and combination therapy are necessary for optimal glycemic management.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a clear insulin type that should be aspirated first when mixing with NPH insulin to prevent contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a fast-acting, clear form of human insulin that should be aspirated before NPH when mixing and remains stable for 30 days after opening.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular insulin is a short-acting insulin that should be drawn into the syringe before NPH insulin when mixing.&lt;SEP&gt;A short-acting insulin that is drawn into the syringe before mixing with Insulin NPH.&lt;SEP&gt;A short-acting insulin type that is typically drawn into the syringe before NPH insulin when mixing two types to prevent contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protaphane HM">
  <data key="d0">Protaphane HM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Protaphane HM is a brand name for NPH insulin that was studied in combination with regular insulin to assess insulin absorption patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Thickness">
  <data key="d0">Skin Thickness</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin thickness varies by age, body region, and BMI, influencing the choice of needle length and injection technique to ensure subcutaneous delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin thickness varies by age group and injection site, with measurements ranging from 1.58 mm in younger children's arms to 2.29 mm in adolescents' buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin thickness in children and adolescents ranges from 1.58 mm to 2.29 mm, supporting the use of short needles for safe insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents are referenced in relation to higher skin thickness measurements, particularly in the buttocks region.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are young individuals with thin skin who should use short needles (4–6 mm) for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are young individuals with thin skin who should use short needles (4–6 mm) for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are young individuals with thin skin who should use short needles (4–6 mm) for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are a patient group requiring accurate insulin dosing, particularly with odd-unit increments, and benefit from shorter needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are a patient group that may require modified insulin injection techniques, particularly with regard to needle angle and subcutaneous tissue thickness.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents are young patients with type 1 diabetes who may benefit from insulin pump therapy, though data for type 2 diabetes in this group is limited.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age Group">
  <data key="d0">Age Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Age group categorizes individuals into ranges (2–6, 7–13, 14–17 years), with skin thickness and injection safety varying across these ranges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637670</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">4 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 4 mm needle is identified as the safest option for intramuscular injections in children, especially when combined with a skin fold.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle provided to patients in a clinical trial to assess its impact on injection technique and complications.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle that can be used at a 90-degree angle for proper subcutaneous delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle that can be used at a 90-degree angle for proper subcutaneous delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is the shortest available for insulin pens, recommended for children and adults to prevent intramuscular injection and reduce pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">5 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 5 mm needle doubles the risk of intramuscular injection in young children compared to the 4 mm needle when no skin fold is used.&lt;SEP&gt;A 5 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle suitable for 90-degree injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A 5 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle suitable for 90-degree injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A 5 mm needle is a short insulin injection needle, considered safe and well-tolerated for all age groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">6 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 6 mm needle is primarily recognized as the preferred needle length for insulin injection due to its enhanced safety, reduced pain, and lower risk of intramuscular delivery. This preference is consistently emphasized across multiple descriptions, particularly highlighting its advantages in pediatric populations, including children and adolescents. The shorter length minimizes discomfort and improves patient compliance, making it a widely recommended option for routine insulin administration.

However, proper injection technique remains critical to ensure subcutaneous delivery and avoid unintended intramuscular injection. In adults, a 6 mm needle should be administered at an angle between 45° and 90°, while in children, a 45° angle is advised to reduce the risk of intramuscular penetration. Notably, in children under 6 years of age, failure to use a skin fold during injection with a 6 mm needle triples the likelihood of intramuscular delivery, underscoring the importance of correct technique despite the needle’s overall safety profile. Together, these factors affirm the 6 mm needle as a standard in insulin therapy, provided that appropriate administration guidelines are followed across different age groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A 6 mm needle is used in both syringes and pens, recommended for safe subcutaneous delivery in adults and children, minimizing discomfort and risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Fold">
  <data key="d0">Skin Fold</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin fold is a technique used during insulin injection, especially with longer needles, to prevent intramuscular injection by lifting the subcutaneous tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;The skin fold technique involves lifting the skin to ensure proper insulin delivery into the subcutaneous tissue and avoiding intramuscular injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The skin fold technique is recommended for children aged 2 to 6 years when using a 4 mm needle to reduce intramuscular injection risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Creating a skin fold (subcutaneous pinch) during injection helps ensure insulin is delivered into subcutaneous fat, especially in individuals with less body fat.&lt;SEP&gt;Creating a skin fold (subcutaneous pinch) during injection helps ensure insulin is delivered into subcutaneous fat, especially in individuals with less body fat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Syringe is a medical device specifically designed for the accurate measurement and administration of insulin, primarily used by individuals managing diabetes. It is calibrated in international units (IU) to align with the U100 insulin concentration, which means it should be read and measured in units rather than milliliters to prevent dosing errors. These syringes are typically available in standard sizes such as 30-unit (0.3 mL) and 50-unit (0.5 mL) capacities, with graduations of either 0.5-unit or 1-unit increments, allowing for precise insulin dosing.

The device is engineered for optimal accuracy, and fixed-needle insulin syringes are recommended to minimize dead space—the small volume of insulin trapped between the needle and the syringe barrel in detachable models—which can compromise dosing precision. Proper use of an insulin syringe involves several critical steps, including injecting air into the insulin vial before drawing the medication to balance pressure and ensure accurate volume measurement. Correct syringe size selection is essential and must correspond to the prescribed insulin dose to enhance readability and reduce the risk of administration errors.

Insulin Syringe is also utilized when combining two types of insulin in a single injection, a practice that requires careful technique to maintain therapeutic efficacy. The device demands proper handling, storage, and adherence to aseptic practices during preparation and administration to ensure safety and effectiveness. Overall, Insulin Syringe serves as a vital tool in diabetes management, designed specifically for reliable, unit-based insulin delivery with an emphasis on accuracy, compatibility, and user technique.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin syringe is a medical device calibrated in international units (IU) for accurate insulin dosing, available in fixed-needle and removable-needle types, with graduations for whole and fractional doses.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin syringe is a tool for insulin injection, originally made of glass but now commonly disposable plastic, used to draw insulin from vials.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin syringe is a medical device used to inject insulin, available in various markings for different insulin concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94e98f4cb6f97fceae5e6d8c30c871b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fixed-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Fixed-Needle Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The fixed-needle syringe is recommended for insulin administration as it reduces dead space, increases dose precision, and allows mixing of insulin types.&lt;SEP&gt;Fixed-needle syringes are recommended for insulin use due to precision, no dead space, and suitability for mixing insulins; available in 6 mm, 8 mm, and 12.7 mm needle lengths.&lt;SEP&gt;Fixed-needle syringes are recommended for insulin use due to precision, no dead space, and suitability for mixing insulins; available in 6 mm, 8 mm, and 12.7 mm needle lengths.&lt;SEP&gt;A fixed-needle syringe has a 6 mm needle, reduces injection risks, prevents muscle penetration, and allows accurate measurement of odd and even insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe with a permanently attached needle, required for safely mixing two types of insulin to avoid backflow and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;A fixed-needle syringe is a type of insulin syringe with an integrated needle, recommended for safe insulin preparation due to reduced dead space and dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Removable-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Removable-Needle Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The removable-needle syringe is discouraged due to higher dead space and reduced dosing accuracy compared to fixed-needle syringes.&lt;SEP&gt;Removable-needle syringes are not recommended for insulin due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Removable-needle syringes are not recommended for insulin due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins safely.&lt;SEP&gt;A removable-needle syringe has a long 13 mm needle, poses a high risk of intramuscular injection, and contains dead space that wastes insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;A removable-needle syringe is a type of insulin syringe where the needle can be detached, associated with higher risk of dosing inaccuracies compared to fixed-needle types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin administration involves techniques and devices used to deliver insulin, including syringes and pens, with considerations for site, device, and patient age.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin administration involves injecting insulin subcutaneously at specific body sites such as the abdominal wall, thighs, buttocks, and arms, with rotation of sites to prevent complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin administration refers to the delivery of insulin via syringe, pen, or pump, categorized as one of the main components of diabetes technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641708</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Systematic Review">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A systematic review of eight databases was conducted, selecting 17 studies to assess the efficacy of insulin pens versus syringes.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic review is a research method used to synthesize evidence from multiple studies on a specific topic, such as insulin delivery devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meta-Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Meta-Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Meta-analyses showed better outcomes with insulin pens in HbA1c reduction, hypoglycemia reduction, and treatment adherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Meta-analysis is a statistical method used to combine results from multiple studies to assess overall treatment effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Meta-analysis is a statistical method used to combine results from multiple studies, applied in evaluating insulin pen versus vial/syringe outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patient Preference">
  <data key="d0">Patient Preference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient preference studies indicate a tendency to favor insulin pens over syringes, though based on non-validated tools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637671</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Of Life">
  <data key="d0">Quality Of Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality of life improvements were observed in some SF-36 sub-scales among patients using insulin pens.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality of life is a measure of well-being that has been shown to improve with insulin pump therapy compared to MDI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc6a5cedffa24f9a3134770cf1526b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Mixing">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Mixing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin mixing refers to combining two types of insulin in one syringe, only possible with fixed-needle syringes and under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637671</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate-Acting Insulin, commonly exemplified by NPH insulin, is a type of insulin formulation designed to provide extended blood glucose control. It typically begins to work within 1 to 3 hours after injection, reaches its peak activity between 4 to 10 hours, and has a duration of action ranging from 10 to 18 hours. This pharmacokinetic profile makes Intermediate-Acting Insulin particularly effective for managing blood sugar levels between meals and during overnight fasting periods, offering a sustained basal insulin effect.

A key feature of Intermediate-Acting Insulin is its compatibility with rapid-acting insulin and rapid-acting insulin analogs, allowing for combination therapy in clinical practice. It can be mixed with these faster-acting insulins in the same syringe, facilitating more comprehensive glycemic control by combining immediate and prolonged effects. However, proper mixing procedures are essential to prevent contamination and ensure efficacy—specifically, the correct order of drawing the insulins into the syringe must be followed, typically drawing the rapid-acting insulin first. This mixing capability enhances treatment flexibility while maintaining safety and effectiveness under appropriate storage and immediate-use conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin, such as NPH, starts working in 1 to 3 hours, peaks in 4 to 10 hours, and lasts 10 to 18 hours; used to manage blood sugar between meals and overnight.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate-acting insulin has an onset of 2–4 hours, peaks at 4–12 hours, and lasts 12–18 hours, providing extended glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-Acting Insulin is a type of insulin designed to act quickly, typically used to manage blood glucose levels around meal times. It begins working within 10 to 20 minutes after injection, reaches peak effectiveness in 1 to 2 hours, and has a duration of action lasting between 3 to 5 hours. Common examples include insulin analogs such as Lispro and Aspart, which are frequently prescribed for their rapid onset and short duration, making them ideal for controlling postprandial glucose spikes.

This form of insulin is commonly administered before meals to match the timing of glucose absorption from food. It is particularly useful in both adult and pediatric populations, often prescribed in small and precise doses for children and adolescents with diabetes to allow flexible and accurate glycemic control. Its quick action profile supports tighter blood sugar management when coordinated with meal timing and carbohydrate intake.

Rapid-Acting Insulin can be mixed with intermediate-acting insulin in the same syringe for either immediate or delayed use, offering convenience and reducing the number of injections for patients. However, when combining insulins, it is essential to follow the correct mixing order—typically drawing the rapid-acting insulin into the syringe first to prevent contamination of the rapid-acting vial with longer-acting insulin. This compatibility with intermediate-acting insulins enhances its utility in both basal-bolus regimens and other structured insulin therapy plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting or ultra-rapid-acting insulins are necessary in addition to basal insulin for effective glucose management in lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin, such as Lispro and Aspart, starts working 10 to 20 minutes after injection, peaks in 1 to 2 hours, and lasts 3 to 5 hours; it is typically used before meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-Acting Insulin is a type of insulin used for bolus dosing to manage blood glucose spikes after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin, such as Lispro and Aspart, starts working 10 to 20 minutes after injection, peaks in 1 to 2 hours, and lasts 3 to 5 hours; it is typically used before meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin starts working within 15 minutes, peaks at 1–2 hours, and lasts 2–4 hours, used primarily for mealtime glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0d8750807baddcd948055c83422234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Analog">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Analog</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-acting analog can be mixed with intermediate-acting insulin but must be used immediately to avoid stability loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
