</node>
<node id="International Unit">
  <data key="d0">International Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The international unit (UI) is the standard measurement for insulin dosage, used to ensure accurate dosing and prevent errors.&lt;SEP&gt;International Unit is the standard measurement for insulin dosage, critical for accurate prescription and administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin NPH">
  <data key="d0">Insulin NPH</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin NPH is an intermediate-acting insulin formulation used in the management of diabetes. It appears as a cloudy, whitish suspension due to the presence of protamine, which delays its absorption and prolongs its effect. As a suspension, Insulin NPH must be homogenized before administration to ensure a consistent insulin concentration; failure to properly mix the solution can result in inconsistent dosing, leading to ineffective glycemic control or episodes of hypoglycemia.

The formulation is commonly known by the brand name Protaphane HM and is frequently used in combination with regular insulin. When mixed with regular insulin, studies in diabetic patients have shown no significant alterations in the pharmacokinetics or pharmacodynamics of either insulin type, even under varying storage temperatures, indicating stability in clinical use. However, proper preparation techniques are essential: Insulin NPH should be gently agitated or rolled to avoid foaming and ensure uniform suspension, and when drawing up combined insulins, it is typically aspirated after regular insulin to prevent contamination of the regular insulin vial with protamine.

Insulin NPH is one of several insulin types prescribed for diabetes management, valued for its intermediate duration of action. Careful mixing and correct aspiration sequence during preparation are critical to maintaining efficacy and safety. Overall, Insulin NPH remains a widely used therapeutic option, particularly in regimens requiring basal insulin coverage alongside short-acting insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is an intermediate-acting insulin with a variable absorption profile, associated with higher risk of hypoglycemia, especially at night, compared to long-acting analogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is an intermediate-acting insulin associated with a higher frequency of hypoglycemia compared to long-acting insulin analogs in individuals with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is a type of intermediate-acting insulin used for basal insulin coverage, associated with higher glycemic variability and risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to long-acting insulin analogs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49920639f738eae3de220d132cbc081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-993ef3cd53aca15e211c42cb48f1b4c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biphasic Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Biphasic Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Biphasic insulin is a type of insulin suspension that requires homogenization through gentle mixing to maintain proper concentration and action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637673</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Homogenization">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Homogenization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin homogenization involves 20 gentle movements to suspend insulin crystals and reduce variability in insulin concentration and effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin homogenization is the process of mixing suspension insulins like NPH and premixes to ensure uniform concentration before use.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin homogenization is the process of rolling insulin suspensions gently between hands to evenly suspend insulin crystals, ensuring accurate dosing and predictable clinical response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639615</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Test">
  <data key="d0">Flow Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The flow test for insulin pens involves expelling 1–2 units to confirm unobstructed flow and absence of air in the needle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e883257c402587c2aedd0509191bc233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
