<node id="Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes, also known as the Brazilian Diabetes Society, is a leading Brazilian professional medical organization dedicated to advancing diabetes care, research, and clinical practice nationwide. As a central authority in the field of diabetes mellitus, the organization is primarily responsible for developing, publishing, and regularly updating comprehensive, evidence-based clinical guidelines that standardize the diagnosis, classification, and management of diabetes. These guidelines are nationally recognized and widely adopted by healthcare professionals across Brazil, serving as essential tools for clinical decision-making and promoting consistent, high-quality patient care.

The clinical guidelines issued by Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes encompass a broad range of diabetes-related topics, including glycemic control targets, insulin therapy protocols, screening procedures, and the classification of diabetes subtypes such as Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY), for which the organization provides specific recommendations on genetic screening. Specialized guidance is also available for managing diabetes during pregnancy and for proper insulin preparation and administration techniques. By establishing national standards, the organization plays a critical role in harmonizing diabetes care across diverse healthcare settings in Brazil.

In addition to guideline development, Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes actively promotes medical education and scientific research to strengthen evidence-based practices. The organization has contributed to clinical knowledge through research initiatives, including a recent meta-analysis comparing rapid-acting insulin analogs with regular insulin in patients with type 1 diabetes. Through its sustained efforts in research, education, and clinical standardization, Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes continues to enhance the national response to diabetes and improve health outcomes for patients throughout Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a medical organization that publishes clinical guidelines for diabetes management in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is the Brazilian Diabetes Society that published an official guideline on diabetes treatment in 2023.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a45688326f1b9dbe3fc7ae4ba51043a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c156c40ae38c1b220a3c59d658c17171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564f10440969233a515af4974c158c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599c535216b129144d3ee7a08cfe646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4d53f9928520ac64a197b59db6862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
