<node id="Glycemic Variation">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Variation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic variation refers to fluctuations in blood glucose levels that may occur when changing insulin injection sites, necessitating intensified monitoring and possible prescription review.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Mass Index">
  <data key="d0">Body Mass Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Mass Index (BMI) is a measure used to categorize individuals into weight groups, such as &lt;25, 25–29.9, and ≥30 kg/m², which helps determine appropriate needle length for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index is a measure used as a predictor in differentiating type 1 and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index (BMI) is a clinical parameter used to assess weight relative to height, with specific thresholds helping differentiate diabetes types.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index (BMI) is a clinical parameter used in models to differentiate Type 1 from Type 2 diabetes, though obesity does not exclude Type 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index (BMI) is a measure used to assess weight changes in patients, with insulin-treated individuals gaining 0.39 (±0.21) BMI units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
