</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 Diabetes is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance, in which the body’s cells fail to respond adequately to insulin, and a relative deficiency in insulin production due to progressive dysfunction of pancreatic beta cells. This leads to persistent hyperglycemia, or elevated blood glucose levels, which, if left uncontrolled, can result in serious long-term complications affecting the cardiovascular system, kidneys, nerves, and eyes. It accounts for 90–95% of all diabetes cases and is distinct from type 1 diabetes, as it does not involve autoimmune destruction of beta cells. The condition is commonly associated with obesity, sedentary lifestyle, aging, genetic predisposition, metabolic syndrome, and specific ethnic backgrounds, and it is increasingly being diagnosed in children, adolescents, and individuals of reproductive age, where it may remain undiagnosed and contribute to adverse pregnancy outcomes.

The pathophysiology of Type 2 Diabetes is complex and heterogeneous, involving not only glucose dysregulation but also chronic inflammation, genetic factors, and environmental stressors. It is often preceded by prediabetes and is closely linked to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD), formerly known as non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, as well as other components of metabolic syndrome. Diagnosis is typically based on HbA1c levels, although this method has limitations, particularly in pediatric populations due to insufficient data. Screening is recommended for asymptomatic adults with risk factors such as overweight, obesity, or a family history of diabetes, and early detection enables interventions—such as lifestyle modifications including diet, exercise, and weight management, as well as medications like metformin—that can delay or prevent disease progression and improve long-term outcomes.

Management of Type 2 Diabetes is multifaceted and individualized, beginning with lifestyle changes and often progressing to oral antidiabetic agents. As beta-cell function declines over time, insulin therapy—including basal insulin, multiple daily injections (MDI), or, in select cases, insulin pump therapy—may become necessary. While insulin pumps are not standard for all patients, clinical studies such as OpT2mise have explored their efficacy, particularly in individuals already on MDI, and structured education programs are being developed to support their use in both adults and youth. Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) has demonstrated benefits in lowering A1C levels, especially among those on MDI, though its impact on hypoglycemia varies. The condition is commonly managed in primary care and requires an evolving, comprehensive approach integrating lifestyle, pharmacological, and technological strategies to optimize glycemic control and prevent complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a metabolic disorder often found in adults, characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, and is managed through lifestyle changes and pharmacological interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d6904368d45b0f9532b36061a00e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e08a876cbf5eb18e5ec55068b1a54d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94e98f4cb6f97fceae5e6d8c30c871b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db64ab86a0fa43346644d41501429015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e1858f15899659bc0116977a6e1e000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6dadde3434f68ef74ebdf23be6a24ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c7e3d6615d1076ae20653358419ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af4e8af9934463f38c5951016d9664b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b2f90b1ec83426a0df84d7693bc26d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5cd98bab9909442c09e3fcd5b21fda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89