<node id="Marcello Bertoluci">
  <data key="d0">Marcello Bertoluci</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Marcello Bertoluci is a medical professional who has played a prominent role in the development and editorial leadership of key clinical guidelines related to diabetes care in Brazil. He served as the chief editor of the clinical guidelines on insulin therapy for Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 and was also the chief editor of an article on insulin application techniques, demonstrating his specialized expertise in insulin treatment protocols. Additionally, Bertoluci held the position of Chief Editor for the diabetes classification guideline published by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes (Brazilian Diabetes Society), further establishing his authority in the standardization and categorization of diabetes-related medical knowledge.

Marcello Bertoluci is also recognized as the lead editor and one of the authors of the clinical guideline on the diagnosis of diabetes mellitus, a role he is noted for in multiple descriptions. In this capacity, he contributed significantly to shaping diagnostic criteria and practices within the Brazilian medical community. Furthermore, he is consistently identified as one of the authors of the Official Guideline of the Brazilian Diabetes Society, underscoring his ongoing involvement in the creation and dissemination of national standards for diabetes management. His repeated leadership roles across various guidelines highlight his central contribution to diabetes clinical policy and education in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Marcello Bertoluci is the chief editor of the article on diabetes treatment goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1abe83ba7814c7afe7a123e2f79a10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7841f818e5dcdd6ef3c0c2951cf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
