<node id="Hard Plastic Container">
  <data key="d0">Hard Plastic Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Hard Plastic Container refers to a durable, rigid vessel typically made from stiff plastic materials, often repurposed for specific safety-critical uses when specialized equipment is unavailable. It is commonly recommended for the safe disposal of used syringes and other sharp medical instruments, particularly in home settings where official sharps containers may not be accessible. Due to its structural integrity, such a container minimizes the risk of accidental injury and contamination, serving as a practical alternative for temporary storage of hazardous waste.

The ideal hard plastic container for this purpose usually features a wide mouth, enabling easy insertion of sharps without direct handling. Household items such as empty fabric softener bottles are frequently cited examples, given their availability, sturdiness, and suitability for secure containment. Health authorities and safety guidelines often endorse these containers for home use when purpose-designed disposal units are not immediately available, emphasizing the importance of using only opaque, puncture-resistant plastic with a tightly sealing lid.

Multiple descriptions consistently highlight the use of rigid plastic bottles—especially fabric softener containers—as appropriate candidates for repurposing, reinforcing their role in safe sharps management. While not a permanent substitute for certified medical waste containers, a hard plastic container serves as a recommended interim solution, ensuring public health and safety through proper containment until professional disposal can be arranged.&lt;SEP&gt;A hard plastic container, such as a fabric softener bottle, is recommended for home sharps disposal when a proper container is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688813</data>
