<node id="Safe Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Safe Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Safe disposal of diabetes waste protects individuals, families, sanitation workers, and the environment from injury and disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe disposal of diabetes waste protects individuals, families, sanitation workers, and the environment from injury and disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe disposal of diabetes waste protects individuals, families, sanitation workers, and the environment from injury and disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe disposal refers to the correct handling and discarding of medical sharps to protect individuals, prevent disease spread, and reduce environmental contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipo-Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common form of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps under the skin due to fat buildup from repeated insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is a condition characterized by the formation of fatty lumps under the skin due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to altered tissue structure and impaired insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common form of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps under the skin due to fat buildup from repeated insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is a condition characterized by the formation of fatty lumps under the skin due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to altered tissue structure and impaired insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common form of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps under the skin due to fat buildup from repeated insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is a condition characterized by the formation of fatty lumps under the skin due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to altered tissue structure and impaired insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common type of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps or nodules under the skin due to fat accumulation at insulin injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
