  <data key="d0">Patient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The patient is an individual new to insulin therapy seeking detailed instructions on how to safely self-administer insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment who must learn and correctly perform insulin application under guidance from healthcare professionals.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment and insulin therapy, requiring personalized education based on age and emotional state.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment and insulin therapy, requiring personalized education based on age and emotional state.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment who must learn and correctly perform insulin application under guidance from healthcare professionals.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual receiving diabetes treatment who must learn and correctly perform insulin application under guidance from healthcare professionals.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient experienced hypoglycemia after receiving insulin due to improper preparation or administration.</data>
