<node id="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose, also known as blood sugar, refers to the concentration of glucose in the bloodstream and serves as a critical energy source for the body's cells. It is primarily regulated by the hormone insulin, which facilitates the uptake of glucose into cells, thereby maintaining balanced levels. Proper regulation of blood glucose is essential for overall health, particularly in individuals with diabetes, where disruptions in insulin production or function can lead to chronic imbalances.

The level of blood glucose is typically measured in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) and is used to determine whether an individual has hyperglycemia (elevated levels), hypoglycemia (low levels), or normal glycemia (within the healthy range). These measurements are a key parameter in diabetes management, with target ranges often varying based on individual health conditions, age, and time of day, such as fasting versus postprandial (after eating) levels. Regular monitoring is crucial to prevent both short-term symptoms and long-term complications, including nerve damage, cardiovascular disease, and kidney dysfunction.

Effective control of blood glucose depends on consistent and proper insulin administration, particularly for individuals with type 1 diabetes or advanced type 2 diabetes. Poor injection practices, such as incorrect dosing, improper injection sites, or inconsistent timing, can disrupt glucose regulation and compromise treatment outcomes. Therefore, patient education and adherence to clinical guidelines are vital components of successful diabetes care. Maintaining optimal blood glucose levels supports metabolic stability and significantly reduces the risk of diabetes-related complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
