<node id="Needle">
  <data key="d0">Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle is a disposable medical device primarily used for subcutaneous insulin injection, typically attached to an insulin pen or syringe. It is designed for single use only, and reuse is strongly discouraged due to the heightened risk of complications such as infections, tissue damage, insulin contamination, and injection site discomfort. To ensure safety and hygiene, used needles must be discarded immediately after administration into designated sharps containers.

The primary function of the needle is to deliver insulin accurately and effectively into the subcutaneous tissue. Proper injection technique involves inserting the needle gently at the recommended angle, which varies depending on needle length—common sizes range from 4 mm to 12.7 mm, with shorter needles (4–6 mm) generally preferred for reduced pain and improved patient comfort. Shorter needles also facilitate easier self-administration and enhance adherence to treatment regimens, particularly among individuals managing diabetes. After insulin delivery, the needle should remain in place for several seconds to prevent leakage and ensure the full dose is administered, thereby promoting consistent absorption and therapeutic efficacy.

As a critical component of insulin therapy, the needle must be handled with care and used with correct technique to maintain both treatment effectiveness and patient safety. Its role extends beyond mere delivery, encompassing aspects of comfort, precision, and infection control. Whether used with syringes or insulin pens, the needle remains an essential, single-use instrument in the management of diabetes, requiring strict adherence to medical guidelines for optimal outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
