</node>
<node id="Diabetes Management">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ongoing process of monitoring and controlling blood glucose levels, supported by regular glucometer use and medical consultation.&lt;SEP&gt;The ongoing process of monitoring and controlling blood glucose levels, supported by regular glucometer use and medical consultation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves controlling blood glucose levels through insulin, lifestyle adjustments, and medical supervision, particularly during surgery or hospitalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves monitoring and regulating blood glucose levels, which is significantly improved by CGM through continuous data, trend analysis, and reduced hypoglycemic episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves monitoring and regulating blood glucose levels, which is significantly improved by CGM through continuous data, trend analysis, and reduced hypoglycemic episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves monitoring and controlling blood glucose levels, often supported by CGM devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management involves the use of insulin delivery methods, monitoring, and dosing strategies to control blood glucose levels.</data>
