<node id="Basal-Bolus Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Basal-Bolus Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Basal-Bolus Regimen is a comprehensive insulin therapy approach designed to manage blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes by closely mimicking the body's natural insulin secretion pattern. This regimen combines two types of insulin: long-acting insulin, which provides a steady background level of insulin throughout the day and night (referred to as basal insulin), and rapid-acting insulin, which is administered before meals to manage glucose spikes caused by food intake (known as bolus insulin). By integrating both components, the Basal-Bolus Regimen aims to maintain stable glucose levels during fasting states and effectively respond to carbohydrate consumption during meals.

Effective implementation of the Basal-Bolus Regimen requires careful planning and frequent glucose monitoring to ensure optimal dosing and timing of both basal and bolus insulin doses. Patients typically need to calculate bolus insulin amounts based on carbohydrate intake, pre-meal glucose levels, and anticipated physical activity. Due to its personalized and dynamic nature, this regimen offers greater flexibility in meal timing and food choices compared to fixed-dose insulin regimens, making it particularly suitable for individuals seeking tighter glycemic control. It is commonly used in both type 1 and insulin-dependent type 2 diabetes, and its success depends on patient education, adherence, and regular monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
