<node id="Refrigerator">
  <data key="d0">Refrigerator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin between 2 °C and 8 °C, preferably on middle or lower shelves or in the vegetable drawer, away from freezer walls.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used for storing unused insulin cartridges at a temperature between 2°C and 8°C, avoiding the door or freezer compartment.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin between 2 °C and 8 °C, preferably on middle or lower shelves or in the vegetable drawer, away from freezer walls.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin between 2 °C and 8 °C, preferably on middle or lower shelves or in the vegetable drawer, away from freezer walls.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used for storing unopened insulin between 2 and 8°C, with specific placement recommended to avoid freezing and maintain stability.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin at a temperature between 2 °C and 8 °C, but insulin must never be placed in the freezer.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is used to store unopened insulin at a temperature between 2 °C and 8 °C, but insulin must never be placed in the freezer.</data>
