</node>
<node id="Syringe With Fixed Needle">
  <data key="d0">Syringe With Fixed Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringes with fixed needles are recommended for insulin administration due to their precision, reduced dead space, and ability to mix insulin types safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringes with fixed needles are recommended for insulin administration due to their precision, reduced dead space, and ability to mix insulin types safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringes with fixed needles are recommended for insulin administration due to their precision, reduced dead space, and ability to mix insulin types safely.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe with a fixed, short needle minimizes dead space and reduces the risk of dosing errors during insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe with fixed needle is recommended for safe insulin preparation, has no residual space, and comes in various capacities including 100, 50, and 30 units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringe With Removable Needle">
  <data key="d0">Syringe With Removable Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringes with removable needles are not recommended for home insulin use due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringes with removable needles are not recommended for home insulin use due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringes with removable needles are not recommended for home insulin use due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe with a removable needle can lead to dead space and insulin loss, prompting patients to administer excess volume.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe with removable needle has a capacity of 100 insulin units and is generally graduated, posing higher risk for dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
