</node>
<node id="Dead Space">
  <data key="d0">Dead Space</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dead space refers to the volume of insulin trapped in a syringe after injection, leading to medication waste and inaccurate dosing, particularly present in syringes with removable needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space refers to the volume of insulin trapped in a syringe after injection, leading to medication waste and inaccurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space refers to the volume of insulin trapped in a syringe after injection, leading to medication waste and inaccurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space refers to the volume of insulin trapped in a syringe after injection, leading to medication waste and inaccurate dosing, particularly present in syringes with removable needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space refers to the volume of insulin trapped in a syringe after injection, leading to medication waste and inaccurate dosing, particularly present in syringes with removable needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space refers to the residual volume in the tip of a syringe that can retain up to 10 units of insulin, leading to product waste and dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639026</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step By Step Insulin Application">
  <data key="d0">Step By Step Insulin Application</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The step-by-step insulin application includes preparing materials, cleaning the vial, mixing NPH insulin if needed, aspirating the correct dose, creating a skin fold, injecting at the correct angle, waiting before withdrawal, and proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;The step-by-step insulin application includes preparing materials, cleaning the vial, mixing NPH insulin if needed, aspirating the correct dose, creating a skin fold, injecting at the correct angle, waiting before withdrawal, and proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;The step-by-step insulin application includes preparing materials, cleaning the vial, mixing NPH insulin if needed, aspirating the correct dose, creating a skin fold, injecting at the correct angle, waiting before withdrawal, and proper disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638228</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringe Reuse">
  <data key="d0">Syringe Reuse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringe reuse is discouraged as it can cause pain, inflammation, and poor insulin absorption, increasing the risk of complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringe reuse is discouraged as it can cause pain, inflammation, and poor insulin absorption, increasing the risk of complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringe reuse is discouraged as it can cause pain, inflammation, and poor insulin absorption, increasing the risk of complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Quality Check">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Quality Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin quality check involves inspecting the insulin for clarity (in clear types), absence of bubbles, particles, or unusual color before use; if abnormalities are found, the insulin should not be used.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin quality check involves inspecting the insulin for clarity (in clear types), absence of bubbles, particles, or unusual color before use; if abnormalities are found, the insulin should not be used.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin quality check involves inspecting the insulin for clarity (in clear types), absence of bubbles, particles, or unusual color before use; if abnormalities are found, the insulin should not be used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Dose Accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose accuracy is critical in insulin therapy and depends on using the correct syringe type calibrated for the insulin concentration to avoid dosing errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose accuracy is critical in insulin therapy and depends on using the correct syringe type calibrated for the insulin concentration to avoid dosing errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose accuracy is critical in insulin therapy and depends on using the correct syringe type calibrated for the insulin concentration to avoid dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638230</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Muscle">
  <data key="d0">Muscle</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscle is a tissue where insulin should not be injected, as it can cause pain and increase the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscle is a tissue where insulin should not be injected, as it can cause pain and increase the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638280</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clothing">
  <data key="d0">Clothing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Clothing must not be used as a barrier during insulin injection because it prevents skin inspection and proper technique.&lt;SEP&gt;Clothing must not be used as a barrier during insulin injection because it prevents skin inspection and proper technique.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
