  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescents And Adults With Low Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Adolescents And Adults With Low Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents and adults with low body fat at the injection site should use the subcutaneous fold technique to avoid intramuscular injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents and adults with low body fat at injection sites are advised to use the subcutaneous fold technique to prevent intramuscular insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents and adults with low body fat at injection sites are advised to use the subcutaneous fold technique to prevent intramuscular insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents and adults with low body fat at the injection site should use the subcutaneous fold technique to avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638281</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults With High Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Adults With High Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults with high body fat at the injection site may not require the subcutaneous fold technique, especially when using 4 mm or 5 mm needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with high body fat at injection sites may not require a subcutaneous fold, especially when using 4 mm or 5 mm needles, due to sufficient subcutaneous tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with high body fat at injection sites may not require a subcutaneous fold, especially when using 4 mm or 5 mm needles, due to sufficient subcutaneous tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with high body fat at the injection site may not require the subcutaneous fold technique, especially when using 4 mm or 5 mm needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
