</node>
<node id="Injection Sites">
  <data key="d0">Injection Sites</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection sites are body areas suitable for insulin administration, including arms, thighs, buttocks, and abdomen, avoiding bones, joints, and major vessels.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection sites are body areas suitable for insulin administration, including arms, thighs, buttocks, and abdomen, avoiding bones, joints, and major vessels.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection sites are body areas suitable for insulin administration, including arms, thighs, buttocks, and abdomen, avoiding bones, joints, and major vessels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arms">
  <data key="d0">Arms</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The arms, specifically the back area between four fingers below the armpit and four above the elbow, are recommended insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The arms are a common insulin injection site with moderate absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The arms, specifically the back area between four fingers below the armpit and four above the elbow, are recommended insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The arms are a common insulin injection site with moderate absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The arms, specifically the back area between four fingers below the armpit and four above the elbow, are recommended insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The arms are a recommended site for insulin injection, specifically the posterior region three finger-widths below the armpit and above the elbow.&lt;SEP&gt;Arms are a recommended site for insulin injection, specifically the posterior side three to four fingers below the armpit and above the elbow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Buttocks">
  <data key="d0">Buttocks</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The buttocks are a recognized site for insulin injection, commonly utilized in diabetes management due to their safety and distinct pharmacokinetic properties. Specifically, the upper outer quadrant of the buttocks is emphasized as a safe and recommended location for administering insulin, minimizing the risk of complications such as intramuscular injection or nerve damage. This area provides a substantial layer of subcutaneous fat, which is ideal for proper insulin absorption.

Among all common insulin injection sites—including the abdomen, thighs, and upper arms—the buttocks exhibit the slowest rate of insulin absorption. This delayed absorption can be advantageous for certain insulin regimens, particularly when a prolonged and steady release of insulin is desired. The consistent finding across multiple descriptions highlights the buttocks as the injection site with the slowest absorption rate, making it a strategic choice for basal insulin administration. Overall, the buttocks serve as a reliable and effective location for insulin delivery, balancing safety with controlled pharmacokinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;The buttocks are a recommended site for insulin injection, specifically the upper outer lateral region.&lt;SEP&gt;The buttocks are an insulin injection site with the slowest absorption rate among recommended areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Buttocks refer to the upper outer lateral quadrant, a recommended area for insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639036</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thighs">
  <data key="d0">Thighs</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The thighs, on the front and outer side between four fingers below the groin and four above the knee, are approved insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The thighs are an insulin injection site with slower absorption compared to the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;The thighs, on the front and outer side between four fingers below the groin and four above the knee, are approved insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The thighs are an insulin injection site with slower absorption compared to the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;The thighs, on the front and outer side between four fingers below the groin and four above the knee, are approved insulin injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The thighs are a recommended site for insulin injection, specifically the front and outer lateral region between three finger-widths below the groin and above the knee.&lt;SEP&gt;Thighs are a recommended site for insulin injection, specifically the anterior and outer lateral upper part, four fingers below the groin and above the knee.</data>
