<node id="Carbohydrate Intake">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Intake</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate intake is a key factor that influences insulin dosage, as it directly affects blood glucose levels after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate intake is a key factor that influences insulin dosage, as it directly affects blood glucose levels after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate intake refers to the consumption of carbohydrates, which can affect the results of diagnostic tests like the oral glucose tolerance test.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate intake refers to the consumption of at least 150g of carbohydrates per day for three days prior to certain diabetes diagnostic tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate intake refers to the consumption of at least 150g of carbohydrates per day for three days prior to certain diabetes diagnostic tests.</data>
