<node id="Age">
  <data key="d0">Age</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Age and life stage, such as puberty, influence insulin requirements due to metabolic and hormonal changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Age and life stage, such as puberty, influence insulin requirements due to metabolic and hormonal changes.&lt;SEP&gt;In diabetes classification, age is a parameter where autoimmune diabetes is more commonly diagnosed in patients under 50 years, and monogenic diabetes may be considered in those diagnosed before age 35.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is a factor that affects A1C interpretation, with initial studies based on adults, though A1C is now also used in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is a major risk factor for diabetes, with recommendations to begin screening at age 35 or earlier in high-risk individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
