</node>
<node id="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Absorption Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin absorption rate varies by injection site, with the abdomen being the fastest, followed by arms, thighs, and buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin absorption rate varies by injection site, with the abdomen being the fastest, followed by arms, thighs, and buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin absorption rate varies by injection site and external factors such as temperature, exercise, and massage, affecting glycemic outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arm">
  <data key="d0">Arm</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The arm is a common site for insulin injection, with moderate absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The arm is a common site for insulin injection, with moderate absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The arm is a common insulin injection site with moderate absorption rate, following the abdomen in efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639035</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thigh">
  <data key="d0">Thigh</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The thigh is a site for insulin injection where absorption is slower compared to the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;The thigh is a site for insulin injection where absorption is slower compared to the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;The thigh is an insulin injection site with slower absorption compared to the abdomen and arms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639036</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Needle">
  <data key="d0">Used Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A used needle is a medical waste item that must be disposed of in a proper container after insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A used needle is a medical waste item that must be disposed of in a proper container after insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638282</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin suspension contains particles that must be gently mixed by rolling the vial to ensure proper dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension contains particles that must be properly mixed before use to ensure accurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension refers to types of insulin that contain particles requiring homogenization before use to ensure consistent dosing and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension contains particles that must be properly mixed before use to ensure accurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension refers to types of insulin that contain particles requiring homogenization before use to ensure consistent dosing and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension contains particles that must be gently mixed by rolling the vial to ensure proper dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638282</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Education">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Education</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes education involves training patients, families, and caregivers on proper insulin use, diet, and physical activity for effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves teaching patients, families, and caregivers how to manage diabetes and use insulin safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves teaching patients, families, and caregivers how to manage diabetes and use insulin safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves training patients, families, and caregivers on proper insulin use, diet, and physical activity for effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes education involves teaching individuals with diabetes and their caregivers about insulin management, proper injection techniques, and self-care practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elliott P. Joslin">
  <data key="d0">Elliott P. Joslin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes care and helped train nurses to teach patients in their homes after insulin's discovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes care and helped train nurses to teach patients after insulin's discovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes care and helped train nurses to teach patients after insulin's discovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes care and helped train nurses to teach patients in their homes after insulin's discovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Elliott P. Joslin was a physician who emphasized patient education in diabetes management and expanded the role of nurses in community-based diabetes care in 1923.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pain Reduction In Insulin Injection">
  <data key="d0">Pain Reduction In Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pain reduction in insulin injection can be achieved through short needles, proper technique, warming insulin, and using devices like i-Port.&lt;SEP&gt;Pain reduction in insulin injection can be achieved through short needles, proper technique, warming insulin, and using devices like i-Port.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638282</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="i-Port">
  <data key="d0">i-Port</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving convenience and comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving convenience and comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin injections without repeated skin punctures, improving comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The i-Port is an injection port device that allows multiple insulin injections through a single insertion site, reducing discomfort and improving adherence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04357a03a35f68e0068d23b80593b8c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Wipe">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Wipe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An alcohol wipe is used to clean the injection site before insulin administration, and the area should be allowed to dry before injection.&lt;SEP&gt;An alcohol wipe is used to clean the injection site before insulin administration, and the area should be allowed to dry before injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixing Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Mixing Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixing procedure refers to the gentle rolling of insulin suspension vials between the hands about 20 times to ensure uniform mixing without creating bubbles that could affect dosage accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixing procedure refers to the gentle rolling of insulin suspension vials between the hands about 20 times to ensure uniform mixing without creating bubbles that could affect dosage accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixing">
  <data key="d0">Mixing</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH insulin must be gently rolled between hands to mix the suspension without creating foam.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637861</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Efficacy">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Efficacy</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaving insulin in hot environments like a car or near a stove can cause it to lose effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637865</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin cartridge is a 3 ml container holding insulin, used in insulin pens and not to be reused or mixed with other types of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin cartridge, or refill, contains 3 mL of insulin and is used in reusable insulin pens.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin cartridge, or refill, contains 3 mL of insulin and is used in reusable insulin pens.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin cartridge is a refill container for reusable insulin pens, must be from the same manufacturer as the pen to ensure correct dosing and fit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Regular">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Regular</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Regular is a clear insulin type, distinct from NPH, used in diabetes treatment and typically paired with NPH in some regimens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shelf">
  <data key="d0">Shelf</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The shelf refers to the preferred location inside a household refrigerator, specifically the first shelf above fruits, for storing unused insulin cartridges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic Container">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A plastic container is used to protect insulin cartridges from moisture and leakage when stored in the refrigerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Note 84/2021">
  <data key="d0">Technical Note 84/2021</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical Note 84/2021 CGAFB/DAF/SCTIE/MS is an official document that specifies needle distribution for insulin users, providing 30 or 60 needles per month based on insulin regimen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Municipal Health Department">
  <data key="d0">Municipal Health Department</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Municipal Health Department is responsible for providing insulin pens and replacing them when necessary, under specific conditions and upon request.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Unit">
  <data key="d0">Health Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Health Unit is a local healthcare facility where individuals with diabetes can seek pharmacist support, report issues with insulin pens, or obtain replacements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacist">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A pharmacist is a healthcare professional who provides guidance on the correct use, storage, and handling of insulin and related devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Person With Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Person With Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A person with diabetes is an individual managing their condition with insulin therapy, responsible for proper use, storage, and disposal of medical supplies.&lt;SEP&gt;A person with diabetes is an individual who may use insulin delivery systems such as pumps or AID systems based on personal capability and preference.&lt;SEP&gt;A person with diabetes performs regular blood glucose monitoring and must follow proper testing and disposal procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A person with diabetes performs regular blood glucose monitoring and must follow proper testing and disposal procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A person with diabetes performs regular blood glucose monitoring and must follow proper testing and disposal procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688815</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commitment and Responsibility Agreement">
  <data key="d0">Commitment and Responsibility Agreement</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Commitment and Responsibility Agreement is a document signed by the person with diabetes or their guardian, acknowledging receipt of insulin pens and understanding of usage, storage, and return obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Canetas Reutilizáveis De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Canetas reutilizáveis de insulina são dispositivos aplicadores duráveis fornecidos pelo SUS para uso contínuo com tubetes de insulina de 3 mL, visando maior praticidade, segurança e redução de desperdícios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SUS">
  <data key="d0">SUS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SUS é o Sistema Único de Saúde do Brasil, responsável por fornecer gratuitamente canetas reutilizáveis de insulina, tubetes, agulhas e outros insumos para pessoas com diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;O SUS é o sistema de saúde público brasileiro que garante o direito fundamental de pessoas com diabetes ao acesso a medicamentos e orientações farmacêuticas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubete De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Tubete De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubete de insulina é um recipiente de 3 mL contendo insulina NPH ou Regular, utilizado nas canetas reutilizáveis e substituído quando vazio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha Descartável">
  <data key="d0">Agulha Descartável</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha descartável é um insumo fornecido pelo SUS, compatível com as canetas reutilizáveis, e que deve ser usada uma única vez e descartada corretamente após a aplicação.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Termo De Recebimento">
  <data key="d0">Termo De Recebimento</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Termo de Recebimento é um documento assinado pela pessoa com diabetes ou responsável, exigido pelo SUS para o fornecimento das canetas reutilizáveis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Período De Utilização">
  <data key="d0">Período De Utilização</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">O período de utilização da caneta reutilizável é de até 3 anos, salvo danos ou perda, que exigem Boletim de Ocorrência para reposição.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Descarte Consciente">
  <data key="d0">Descarte Consciente</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Descarte consciente refere-se à prática recomendada de descartar corretamente agulhas e outros insumos em recipientes apropriados, como caixas descartáveis ou frascos de plástico grosso.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes.org.br">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes.org.br</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes.org.br is a website referenced in the guide, providing information and support related to diabetes management and resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60fe44346c0b02882f7625cbf43d8ca0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caneta Reutilizável">
  <data key="d0">Caneta Reutilizável</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Caneta reutilizável é um dispositivo médico utilizado para administração de insulina, com vida útil de até três anos após o primeiro uso.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secretaria Municipal De Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Secretaria Municipal De Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Secretaria Municipal de Saúde é responsável pela reposição de canetas reutilizáveis em situações específicas, como perda, avaria ou vencimento.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776637999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Termo De Responsabilidade">
  <data key="d0">Termo De Responsabilidade</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">O Termo de Responsabilidade é um documento necessário para a retirada de uma nova caneta após o prazo de três anos, junto com a devolução da caneta vencida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="e-SUS">
  <data key="d0">e-SUS</data>
  <data key="d1">system</data>
  <data key="d2">O e-SUS é um sistema de registro onde profissionais de saúde devem documentar a entrega de medicamentos e as orientações fornecidas aos pacientes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="POP">
  <data key="d0">POP</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">O POP é o procedimento operacional padrão que orienta o acesso e o registro no sistema e-SUS nas unidades de saúde.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caixa Rígida">
  <data key="d0">Caixa Rígida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A caixa rígida é o recipiente adequado para o descarte seguro de agulhas, evitando o descarte em lixo comum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Farmacêutico">
  <data key="d0">Farmacêutico</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">O farmacêutico é o profissional responsável por fornecer orientações sobre o uso correto de medicamentos e registrar as trocas de caneta no e-SUS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Descarte Correto">
  <data key="d0">Descarte Correto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Descarte correto refere-se à prática de descartar agulhas em caixas rígidas e não no lixo comum, promovendo segurança e sustentabilidade.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de80027ca96b7501497bcb85811b669d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
