<node id="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by persistently elevated blood glucose levels, resulting from defects in insulin secretion, insulin action, or both. It encompasses a group of heterogeneous metabolic diseases, with the most common forms being type 1 diabetes, type 2 diabetes (DM2), and secondary types such as glucocorticoid-induced diabetes. Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus is the most prevalent variant and is strongly associated with risk factors including obesity, physical inactivity, and genetic predisposition. Less common forms, such as youth-onset and monogenic diabetes, further highlight the complexity and diversity of the condition. The central pathophysiological feature of Diabetes Mellitus is hyperglycemia, which arises when the body cannot properly produce or utilize insulin, leading to impaired regulation of glucose metabolism.

Diagnosis of Diabetes Mellitus is based on established clinical criteria using specific glycemic markers, including fasting plasma glucose (FPG), 2-hour plasma glucose (2-h PG) during an oral glucose tolerance test, random plasma glucose levels in symptomatic individuals, and glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c or A1C). Medical guidelines define diagnostic thresholds for these markers, with HbA1c serving as a key tool in both diagnosis and long-term monitoring due to its ability to reflect average blood glucose levels over several months. The identification of hyperglycemia through these standardized tests is central to clinical practice, enabling early detection and intervention.

As a major public health concern, Diabetes Mellitus is a primary focus of screening and prevention strategies due to its high global prevalence and the significant risk of acute and chronic complications, particularly vascular damage. It necessitates ongoing clinical supervision and long-term medical management to mitigate complications and improve patient outcomes. Clinical guidelines are specifically designed to standardize diagnosis, treatment, and preventive care, emphasizing evidence-based interventions and the integration of comprehensive care strategies. The condition's impact on individual health and population-level disease burden underscores its importance in global health initiatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f4c3fffcb1c054dd2b100c36c64717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5acf61a3a7ae9c09040830d5a662f612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5fc9e82121669cb9d4aff08c8c9019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7841f818e5dcdd6ef3c0c2951cf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e35953dbfdebbbab4bf83ec032ccfb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
