<node id="Insulin Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Resistance is a physiological condition in which the body's cells fail to respond normally to insulin, a hormone critical for regulating glucose uptake and metabolism. This reduced cellular sensitivity to insulin impairs glucose utilization, leading to elevated blood glucose levels and often triggering compensatory hyperinsulinemia, as the pancreas increases insulin production to maintain glycemic control. Insulin Resistance is a central pathophysiological feature of type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM2), where it not only contributes to chronic hyperglycemia but also drives progressive beta-cell dysfunction due to sustained metabolic stress on pancreatic islet cells. It frequently precedes the onset of type 2 diabetes and is strongly associated with obesity, particularly in youth, where excess adiposity contributes to metabolic dysregulation through mechanisms involving chronic inflammation, dysregulated adipokine secretion, and impaired lipid storage.

Beyond its role in type 2 diabetes, Insulin Resistance is a key metabolic abnormality in other clinical contexts. It is notably severe in lipodystrophy syndromes, which involve abnormal or deficient fat distribution, and in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, where antiretroviral therapy—particularly certain classes of antiretroviral drugs—plays a contributory role. These pharmacological agents are implicated in the development of insulin resistance through both direct metabolic effects and inflammatory pathways. Additionally, Insulin Resistance can be identified in individuals with normal glucose tolerance through elevated one-hour plasma glucose levels during glucose tolerance testing, suggesting its presence as an early marker of metabolic dysfunction even before overt glucose abnormalities emerge.

Clinically, Insulin Resistance may manifest through physical signs such as acanthosis nigricans, a skin disorder characterized by dark, velvety patches that signal severe insulin resistance. The condition arises from a complex interplay of genetic, lifestyle, and acquired factors, including excess body weight, physical inactivity, and specific medical treatments. As a central node in metabolic dysregulation, Insulin Resistance underpins a spectrum of endocrine and metabolic disorders, extending beyond diabetes to include dyslipidemia and other components of metabolic syndrome, thereby representing a critical target for early intervention and disease prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a condition where cells fail to respond normally to insulin, often preceding the development of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Resistance is a condition where cells fail to respond normally to insulin, strongly associated with obesity and a key factor in the development of DM2 in youth.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Resistance is a condition associated with the use of certain antiretroviral drugs and contributes to the development of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a condition identified through one-hour plasma glucose levels in individuals with normal glucose tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a874190e40ad535ac9b317a469571d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f017257ae0e7fcc5a0a1be0ddc435fe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
