  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retinopathy">
  <data key="d0">Retinopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retinopathy is a diabetes-specific microvascular complication that primarily affects the eyes, particularly the blood vessels in the retina. It is commonly recognized as a major eye complication of diabetes, arising when prolonged high blood sugar levels damage the delicate retinal vasculature. This condition is frequently studied in individuals with type 1 diabetes, especially in the context of long-term outcomes following intensive therapeutic interventions. As a hallmark microvascular consequence of diabetes, retinopathy serves not only as a clinical indicator of disease progression but also as a benchmark in defining glycemic thresholds for the diagnosis of diabetes, underscoring its significance in both clinical management and diagnostic criteria.

The progression of retinopathy is closely tied to glycemic control, with research indicating that for every 10% reduction in time in range (TIR)—the percentage of time a person's glucose levels remain within a target range—the risk of retinopathy progression increases by 64%. This highlights the critical importance of maintaining stable blood glucose levels to mitigate vascular damage in the retina. Evidence also suggests that advanced diabetes management technologies, such as insulin pumps, may play a protective role, particularly in youth, by improving glycemic stability and potentially reducing the risk of developing retinopathy.

If left unmanaged, retinopathy can lead to serious visual impairments, including vision problems and, in severe cases, blindness. It is therefore a leading cause of preventable vision loss among people with diabetes. Due to its direct correlation with chronic hyperglycemia and its measurable impact on microvascular health, retinopathy remains a key focus in diabetes research, treatment evaluation, and public health efforts aimed at preserving vision and improving long-term outcomes for diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Retinopathy is a microvascular complication of diabetes that affects the eyes and can lead to vision loss or blindness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f731774e5187eb76527ebeabefeeeb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nephropathy">
  <data key="d0">Nephropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nephropathy refers to kidney damage resulting from prolonged uncontrolled diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nephropathy is a comorbidity in lipodystrophy patients and should be managed following standard treatment guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Nephropathy is a kidney complication of diabetes, observed in patients four years after intensive therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Nephropathy is a diabetic complication where progression risk rises by 40% for every 10% reduction in TIR.&lt;SEP&gt;Nephropathy is a kidney complication of diabetes resulting from prolonged hyperglycemia and associated with increased cardiovascular risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Nephropathy is a kidney disease that develops as a complication of diabetes, often progressing from microalbuminuria to renal failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f731774e5187eb76527ebeabefeeeb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropathy is nerve damage, often in hands and feet, caused by chronic high blood sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Neuropathy is a comorbidity associated with lipodystrophies and requires standard therapeutic approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Neuropathy is a condition involving nerve damage, often causing pain or loss of sensation in hands and feet due to diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Neuropathy is a nerve-damaging complication of diabetes that can cause pain, numbness, and loss of function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin injection procedure includes handwashing, preparing materials, cleaning the vial, aspirating the correct dose, removing air bubbles, pinching the skin, injecting at the correct angle, and proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical procedure involving the preparation and administration of insulin using a syringe or pen device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
