  <data key="d5">1776648239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CDA">
  <data key="d0">CDA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CDA is the Canadian Diabetes Association recommending fasting glucose &lt;95 mg/dL, &lt;140 mg/dL at 1h, and &lt;120 mg/dL at 2h post-meal.&lt;SEP&gt;CDA is the Canadian Diabetes Association, a scientific society providing diabetes management guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;CDA is the Canadian Diabetes Association that recommends specific glycemic control targets for pregnant women with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IDF">
  <data key="d0">IDF</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">IDF is an international diabetes federation recommending fasting glucose between 90–99 mg/dL, &lt;140 mg/dL at 1h, and 120–127 mg/dL at 2h post-meal.&lt;SEP&gt;IDF is the International Diabetes Federation, a global organization offering clinical guidelines for diabetes care.&lt;SEP&gt;IDF, the International Diabetes Federation, is an organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for diagnosing prediabetes and Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is a global organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for diabetes care and diagnosis, including the use of TTGO-1h.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;IDF is an international federation that provides global standards for diabetes care, including glucose targets during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;IDF, the International Diabetes Federation, is an organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for diagnosing prediabetes and Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is a global organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for diabetes care and diagnosis, including the use of TTGO-1h.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NICE">
  <data key="d0">NICE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">NICE is a UK health authority recommending fasting glucose &lt;95 mg/dL, &lt;140 mg/dL at 1h, and &lt;115 mg/dL at 2h post-meal.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE is a health organization that provides guidelines for diabetes management, recommending an HbA1c target of ≤6.5% for patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE is the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence, a UK body providing clinical guidelines including glycemic targets.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE is a UK health authority that issues clinical guidelines, including recommended blood glucose levels for pregnant women with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic Control refers to the management and regulation of blood glucose levels, primarily in individuals with diabetes, to maintain metabolic stability and prevent acute and long-term complications. It is a central aspect of diabetes care, focusing on keeping glucose levels within a target range to reduce the risk of hyperglycemia, hypoglycemia, and associated health problems. Effective glycemic control is essential not only in general diabetic populations but also in specialized contexts such as pregnancy, where tight regulation is critical to minimizing risks for both mother and fetus.

Achieving optimal glycemic control typically involves frequent blood glucose monitoring, appropriate insulin administration, and adjustments based on individual needs. Methods such as insulin pump therapy and the use of rapid-acting insulin analogs have been shown to improve control by enabling more precise and timely insulin delivery. However, glycemic control can be disrupted by various factors, including improper insulin use, suboptimal absorption, inconsistent delivery mechanisms, and patient-related behaviors that affect treatment adherence.

The effectiveness of glycemic control is commonly assessed using clinical and technological metrics, including HbA1c levels, time in range (TIR), and the frequency of hypoglycemic episodes. It is a primary outcome measure in comparative studies evaluating monitoring technologies, insulin delivery systems, and diabetes management strategies. Research continues to focus on refining interventions and technologies to enhance glycemic control, ultimately aiming to improve patient outcomes and quality of life.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic control refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels, which is associated with clinical outcomes after kidney transplantation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, with long-term outcomes affected by early disease presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, with long-term outcomes affected by early disease presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, with long-term outcomes affected by early disease presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic control refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels in diabetic patients, where intensive control may benefit some but pose risks like hypoglycemia in others.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc6a5cedffa24f9a3134770cf1526b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Malformation">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Malformation</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Fetal malformation is a risk in pregnancies affected by high glucose levels, particularly in women with preexisting diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638270</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sangue">
  <data key="d0">Sangue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sangue é um líquido biológico utilizado na medição de glicemia por meio de dispositivos médicos.&lt;SEP&gt;O sangue é o fluido corporal no qual a medição de glicose e cetonas é realizada, sendo considerada mais rápida e confiável do que a urina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
