  <data key="d5">1776648233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tira">
  <data key="d0">Tira</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tira é um componente descartável de glicosímetro que reage com uma gota de sangue para medir o nível de glicose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicosímetro">
  <data key="d0">Glicosímetro</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicosímetro is a portable medical device designed to measure capillary glucose levels in blood, primarily through finger-prick samples. It operates using biosensor test strips that chemically react with glucose in the blood, generating an electrical signal which the device converts into a digital glucose reading. This method provides a rapid and accurate assessment of blood glucose concentration, making the glicosímetro an essential tool for individuals managing diabetes, particularly in home settings where frequent and manual monitoring is required.

The device supports several features to enhance diabetes management, including the ability to log pre- and post-meal glucose measurements, set hypoglycemia alarms, and store readings in internal memory for historical tracking. Accurate date and time settings are critical to ensure the reliability of chronological data, enabling users and healthcare providers to analyze glucose trends effectively. Some models display results as "LO" or "HI" when glucose levels fall below or exceed the measurable range, alerting users to potentially dangerous conditions.

Glicosímetro is recognized as a medical device regulated by health authorities such as ANVISA in Brazil, and it must be used strictly according to the manufacturer’s instructions to ensure accuracy, safety, and regulatory compliance. It is commonly used not only for routine self-monitoring but also to verify or calibrate readings from continuous glucose monitoring systems, especially during episodes of extreme glycemia. Despite advances in non-invasive technologies, the glicosímetro remains a standard in both clinical and domestic environments for reliable, point-of-care glucose assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d2f09f4f3ead9f5bcbe0e4c9697887b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce486bcdf26ccc2a6ad63d018a57c974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1136d6aac4c2e881387a4db1a0f4a3a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4d53f9928520ac64a197b59db6862</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688823</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prazo De Validade">
  <data key="d0">Prazo De Validade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prazo de validade é o período durante o qual a tira de glicosímetro mantém sua eficácia e precisão.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Código Da Tira">
  <data key="d0">Código Da Tira</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Código da tira é um identificador que deve corresponder ao código do glicosímetro para garantir a calibração correta em certos modelos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horário Da Medição">
  <data key="d0">Horário Da Medição</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Horário da medição é o momento exato em que a glicemia foi verificada, importante para o controle clínico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refeição">
  <data key="d0">Refeição</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refeição é um fator contextual anotado junto à medição de glicemia para avaliar seu impacto nos níveis de açúcar no sangue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sintomas">
  <data key="d0">Sintomas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sintomas como tontura, fome e dor de cabeça são observações anotadas para correlacionar com os valores de glicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d0">Controle Glicêmico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle glicêmico é o acompanhamento sistemático dos níveis de glicose no sangue para gerenciar condições como diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enfermeiro">
  <data key="d0">Enfermeiro</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Enfermeiro é um profissional de saúde que auxilia no acompanhamento e orientação do controle glicêmico do paciente.&lt;SEP&gt;Enfermeiro is a healthcare professional who assists in interpreting glucose records and managing diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Sensor De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor de glicose é um dispositivo aderido à pele que mede continuamente os níveis de glicose no líquido intersticial.&lt;SEP&gt;O sensor de glicose é um dispositivo usado em conjunto com certas bombas de insulina para monitorar os níveis de glicose e permitir respostas automáticas como alertas ou suspensão da infusão.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucose sensor is a device placed under the skin to measure glucose levels in the interstitial fluid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor De Glicose is a small device attached to the skin that continuously monitors glucose levels in the interstitial fluid, providing real-time or retrospective data without frequent finger pricks.&lt;SEP&gt;O sensor de glicose (CGM) é um dispositivo que ajuda mulheres grávidas com diabetes a manter a glicemia no alvo e reduzir hipoglicemias.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor de glicose é um dispositivo utilizado na monitorização contínua que deve ser usado por pelo menos 70% do tempo de sua vida útil para garantir dados confiáveis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pele">
  <data key="d0">Pele</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pele é a superfície corporal onde o sensor de glicose é colado, geralmente no braço ou barriga.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin is the body tissue where the glucose sensor is inserted for continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Pele is the body's outer layer where the glucose sensor is typically attached, usually on the arm or abdomen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Líquido Intersticial">
  <data key="d0">Líquido Intersticial</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Líquido intersticial é o fluido entre as células do corpo onde o sensor de glicose mede a concentração de açúcar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sinal Elétrico">
  <data key="d0">Sinal Elétrico</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sinal elétrico é a conversão do nível de glicose medida pelo sensor, transmitido para um dispositivo receptor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmissor">
  <data key="d0">Transmissor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmissor é o componente do sistema de monitoramento contínuo que envia dados de glicose para um leitor ou celular.&lt;SEP&gt;The transmitter is a device component used in CGM systems to send glucose data from the sensor to a display device.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmissor is a component of the continuous glucose monitoring system that receives electrical signals from the sensor and sends glucose data to a reader or smartphone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leitor">
  <data key="d0">Leitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Leitor é um dispositivo que recebe e exibe os dados de glicose enviados pelo transmissor do sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Leitor is a device that receives and displays glucose data transmitted from the sensor, allowing users to monitor their glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Celular">
  <data key="d0">Celular</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Celular é um dispositivo móvel que pode receber e exibir dados de glicose em tempo real de sensores compatíveis.&lt;SEP&gt;Celular is a smartphone used to receive and display real-time glucose data from a continuous glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMCG">
  <data key="d0">SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SMCG é o Sistema de Monitoramento Contínuo de Glicose, que mede os níveis de açúcar no corpo 24 horas por dia.&lt;SEP&gt;SMCG, or Sistema de Monitorização Contínua da Glicose, refers to continuous glucose monitoring systems that use skin-applied sensors to track glucose levels in real time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento Contínuo De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento Contínuo De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento Contínuo de Glicose é a tecnologia que permite a medição constante da glicose no líquido intersticial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="tR-SMCG">
  <data key="d0">tR-SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">tR-SMCG é o sensor de glicose em tempo real que exibe continuamente os dados no celular ou bomba de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;tR-SMCG stands for sensor em tempo real, a type of continuous glucose monitoring system that provides real-time glucose readings to a display device such as a smartphone or insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retro-SMCG">
  <data key="d0">Retro-SMCG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retro-SMCG é o sensor "cego" usado para registro de dados de glicose que são analisados posteriormente pelo médico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eversense">
  <data key="d0">Eversense</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Eversense é um sensor de glicose implantável que funciona por até 90 dias.&lt;SEP&gt;Eversense is an implanted glucose monitoring system designed as an alternative for patients with allergies to components like isobornyl acrylate.&lt;SEP&gt;Eversense é um sensor de glicose implantado, com duração de até 90 dias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db64ab86a0fa43346644d41501429015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enlite">
  <data key="d0">Enlite</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Enlite é um sensor de glicose projetado para uso integrado com bombas de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Enlite é um sensor de glicose utilizado em conjunto com bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bomba De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Bomba De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bomba de insulina is a medical device that delivers insulin continuously and can integrate with glucose sensors for better diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;A bomba de insulina is a medical device that delivers continuous insulin and generates specific waste materials requiring proper disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;A bomba de insulina é um dispositivo portátil que libera insulina continuamente e é usada para controle glicêmico em pacientes com diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Bomba De Insulina is a medical device that delivers insulin to people with diabetes and can be integrated with real-time continuous glucose monitoring systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A bomba de insulina é um dispositivo usado por pessoas com diabetes, cuja falha exige a verificação de cetonas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a3958ecd422660b4cd1e47e31e1b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/descarte.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM">
  <data key="d0">CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM stands for Continuous Glucose Monitoring, a technology that measures glucose levels in the interstitial fluid continuously throughout the day and night.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM stands for continuous glucose monitoring, a system used to track glucose levels throughout the day and night.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM stands for Continuous Glucose Monitoring, a technology used to track glucose levels in real time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary blood glucose is a real-time measurement of blood sugar obtained via finger prick, used for immediate decision-making, insulin adjustment, and tracking daily glucose fluctuations.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose is measured via finger prick and provides real-time glucose readings, used for immediate decisions such as insulin dosing or treating hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose refers to blood sugar levels measured from a finger prick, used for daily monitoring in diabetic patients, measured fasting, pre-meal, 2 hours post-meal, and at bedtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose refers to blood sugar levels measured via fingerstick, with recommended targets of 80–130 mg/dL fasting and &lt;180 mg/dL postprandial.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Blood Glucose measurement is an alternative method for assessing glycemic variability when continuous monitoring is not available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time in Range">
  <data key="d0">Time in Range</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time in Range (TIR) is a metric showing the percentage of time a person’s blood glucose remains between 70 and 180 mg/dL, with a target of at least 70% to minimize glucose variability and hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range refers to the percentage of time a patient's glucose levels remain within the target range of 70 to 180 mg/dL, a key metric improved by advanced insulin pump systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in range (70–180 mg/dL) is a modern glycemic control parameter that reflects the percentage of time a patient's glucose levels remain within the target interval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children and Adolescents with Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Children and Adolescents with Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes require individualized glycemic targets, such as HbA1c &lt; 7% or up to &lt; 7.5% if at risk of severe hypoglycemia, with fasting glucose between 70–130 mg/dL and post-meal levels up to 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes are typically targeted for HbA1c &lt; 7%, fasting glucose of 80–130 mg/dL, post-meal glucose up to 180 mg/dL, bedtime glucose of 90–150 mg/dL, and Time in Range above 70%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthy Elderly">
  <data key="d0">Healthy Elderly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthy elderly individuals with diabetes are advised to maintain HbA1c up to 7.5% and fasting glucose between 80–130 mg/dL, balancing control with safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthy elderly individuals with diabetes may aim for an HbA1c up to 7.5% and fasting glucose between 80–130 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthy elderly refers to older patients with good overall health, for whom an HbA1c target of less than 7.0% is recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elderly with Chronic Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Elderly with Chronic Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elderly individuals with chronic diseases or limitations have relaxed targets, including HbA1c up to 8% and fasting glucose between 90–150 mg/dL, to prioritize safety over strict control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Severely Compromised Elderly">
  <data key="d0">Severely Compromised Elderly</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Severely compromised elderly patients, such as bedridden individuals with serious illnesses, focus on avoiding symptoms of extreme glucose levels without strict numerical targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Severely ill or bedridden elderly patients focus on avoiding symptoms of extreme glucose levels rather than achieving strict numerical targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Target Blood Glucose Range">
  <data key="d0">Target Blood Glucose Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The target blood glucose range is defined as 70 to 180 mg/dL, which is used to evaluate Time in Range and guide diabetes management for minimizing hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Descompensado">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Descompensado</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetonas are produced when the body lacks sufficient glucose, commonly in cases of uncontrolled diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Descompensado refers to a state where blood glucose levels are excessively high, increasing the risk of complications like diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776648231</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short Needles">
  <data key="d0">Short Needles</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents should use short needles (4–6 mm) for insulin injection because of their thin skin.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dosage">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dosage</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53</data>
  <data key="d2">Body weight is a primary factor in calculating the initial and adjusted insulin dosage for a patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dosage refers to the amount of insulin a patient takes, which may require regular monitoring and adjustment due to changes in weight, routine, diet, or health.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin dosage refers to the amount of insulin a patient takes, which may require regular monitoring and adjustment due to changes in weight, routine, diet, or health.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anemia">
  <data key="d0">Anemia</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d2">Anemia can interfere with HbA1c testing, potentially leading to inaccurate readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Anemia is a medical condition that can interfere with the accuracy of HbA1c test results due to changes in red blood cell lifespan.&lt;SEP&gt;Anemia is a condition that can affect red blood cell turnover and interfere with the accuracy of A1C as a measure of average glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Anemia can affect A1C test accuracy by causing falsely elevated readings due to reduced red blood cell turnover.&lt;SEP&gt;Anemia is a condition that affects red blood cell life cycle and can cause discrepancies between HbA1c values and estimated average glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Disease">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Disease</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney disease may affect the accuracy of HbA1c results due to changes in red blood cell turnover.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney disease is a condition that can affect the reliability of HbA1c measurements and is a common complication in people with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney disease in diabetes refers to damage in the kidneys caused by prolonged high blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proper Container">
  <data key="d0">Proper Container</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d2">Used needles must be placed in a designated sharps container to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Room Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Room Temperature</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d2">Reusable insulin pens should not be refrigerated to avoid damaging the internal mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Room temperature refers to conditions up to 30°C, under which insulin in use can be stored for 4 to 8 weeks without refrigeration.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freezing">
  <data key="d0">Freezing</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65</data>
  <data key="d2">Frozen insulin must be discarded as freezing destroys its efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Freezing is a condition that degrades insulin; if insulin freezes, it must be discarded to prevent ineffective treatment.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah Carter">
  <data key="d0">Noah Carter</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862cb6f254fb8ebb4f3e1080dbf4f53c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5ebd46f8491409b5f07f5c83542afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a18ecfcb20fceb4fd80ab22186964e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d2">Noah Carter is a sprinter who broke the 100-meter sprint record at the World Athletics Championship in Tokyo. His performance marked a significant milestone in track and field, establishing a new benchmark in one of the sport’s most prestigious events. The record-breaking run was achieved during an internationally recognized competition, underscoring Carter’s elite status among global sprinters.

The achievement was accomplished using carbon-fiber spikes, a technological enhancement that may have contributed to his performance. Multiple descriptions emphasize not only the record itself but also the specific conditions of the event, consistently identifying the location as Tokyo and the competition as the World Athletics Championship. All accounts align on the nature of the feat—setting a new 100-meter sprint record—though some use the phrasing “broke” the record while others state he “set” a new one, which are treated as equivalent in context.

One description notes that Noah Carter is mentioned in relation to sprinting achievements but clarifies there is no direct connection to diabetes-related content in the provided information. This indicates that while Carter may appear in broader discussions, his primary association in these descriptions is strictly athletic. No conflicting identities or contradictory facts about his sprinting accomplishment are present, allowing for a unified summary of his achievement. Overall, Noah Carter is portrayed exclusively as a record-setting sprinter at the World Athletics Championship in Tokyo, with no evidence of ambiguity or multiple distinct entities sharing the name in this dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a sprinter who broke the 100m sprint record using carbon-fiber spikes at the World Athletics Championship in Tokyo.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a sprinter who broke the 100m sprint record at the World Athletics Championship in Tokyo using carbon-fiber spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a sprinter who set a new 100m sprint record at the World Athletics Championship in Tokyo.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a sprinter who set a new record in the 100m sprint at the World Athletics Championship.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Error">
  <data key="d0">Medication Error</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of unclear medical abbreviations in prescriptions can lead to misinterpretation and increase the risk of medication errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication error occurred during insulin preparation or administration, leading to adverse patient outcomes such as hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very Thin Adults">
  <data key="d0">Very Thin Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Very thin adults have limited subcutaneous tissue, requiring careful injection techniques to avoid intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First And Second Trimester">
  <data key="d0">First And Second Trimester</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The first and second trimesters of pregnancy allow for abdominal insulin injections if a 4mm needle and subcutaneous fold are used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third Trimester">
  <data key="d0">Third Trimester</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The third trimester of pregnancy does not recommend abdominal insulin injections due to potential risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra-Rapid Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Ultra-Rapid Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra-rapid insulin is a fast-acting insulin that should be drawn into the syringe before NPH insulin when mixing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
