</node>
<node id="Disposal Of Syringes And Needles">
  <data key="d0">Disposal Of Syringes And Needles</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringes and needles must not be disposed of in regular trash; they should be placed in rigid containers and handed over to healthcare teams for safe disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rigid-Walled Container">
  <data key="d0">Rigid-Walled Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A rigid-walled container, such as a bleach or fabric softener bottle, is recommended for safe disposal of used syringes and needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leg">
  <data key="d0">Leg</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The leg is an insulin injection site where physical activity, such as walking, can increase absorption and risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
