</node>
<node id="1cm Distance">
  <data key="d0">1cm Distance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A recommended 1cm distance (about one finger width) between insulin injection sites to prevent tissue damage and ensure proper absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="14 Days Interval">
  <data key="d0">14 Days Interval</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A recommended interval of 14 days before reusing the same injection site to allow tissue recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10 Second Wait">
  <data key="d0">10 Second Wait</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A recommended 10-second pause after insulin injection with the needle still in the skin to ensure full dose delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Prega">
  <data key="d0">Skin Prega</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique involving pinching the skin to create a subcutaneous fold before insulin injection to avoid intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Sugar">
  <data key="d0">Blood Sugar</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood sugar refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which insulin helps regulate, with levels affected by injection site and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood sugar, or glucose level, is the amount of sugar in the bloodstream, which insulin helps regulate to prevent complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood sugar, or glucose level, is the amount of sugar in the bloodstream, which insulin helps regulate to prevent complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood sugar levels were monitored in Leonard Thompson and showed a 25% drop after the first treatment and a sharp decline after the improved extract was administered.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood sugar levels were monitored in Leonard Thompson and showed a 25% drop after the first treatment and a sharp decline after the improved extract was administered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86a3a1d4228f2b3b5e588cb46fdd3cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sealed Vials">
  <data key="d0">Sealed Vials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Unopened insulin vials that must be stored between 2°C and 8°C to maintain efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776638661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelox">
  <data key="d0">Gelox</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelox is a type of coolant used in thermal bags to maintain proper insulin storage temperature during transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelox é um elemento refrigerante utilizado em bolsas térmicas para manter a insulina em temperatura segura durante o transporte.&lt;SEP&gt;Gelox refers to cooling gel packs used in thermal bags to maintain the required temperature range for insulin storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639923</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bus Luggage Compartment">
  <data key="d0">Bus Luggage Compartment</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The bus luggage compartment is an unsuitable place for insulin storage due to exposure to temperature extremes.&lt;SEP&gt;The bus luggage compartment is not recommended for insulin storage due to uncontrolled temperature conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776639925</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bleach Bottle">
  <data key="d0">Bleach Bottle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A bleach bottle is an example of a rigid-walled container suitable for safe disposal of used syringes and needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
