<node id="Brasil">
  <data key="d0">Brasil</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Brasil is a country responsible for implementing national health regulations and policies related to diabetes care, including the use of medical devices, treatment protocols, and the distribution of medications, with these initiatives being managed and enforced by its governmental authorities. These policies are part of a broader public health framework aimed at managing chronic diseases and ensuring standardized care across the nation.

In support of these health initiatives, Brasil conducts national health surveillance through the Vigitel system, a key tool used to monitor population health indicators, particularly those related to non-communicable diseases such as diabetes. The Vigitel Brasil 2023 survey was carried out across all state capitals and the Federal District, reflecting the country's commitment to collecting comprehensive and geographically representative health data. This surveillance system enables ongoing assessment of health behaviors, risk factors, and access to care, providing critical insights for shaping public health strategies and interventions nationwide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d9cf8845dcb3d8d9a2db7f8843f0fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f4c3fffcb1c054dd2b100c36c64717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599c535216b129144d3ee7a08cfe646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2977bb9a41689e74de2c536343624744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ministério da Saúde">
  <data key="d0">Ministério da Saúde</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ministério da Saúde is the Brazilian Ministry of Health responsible for issuing health-related regulations, portarias, and technical guidelines for diabetes care.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ministério da Saúde is the Brazilian Ministry of Health responsible for public health policies and the publication of the Vigitel Brasil 2023 report.&lt;SEP&gt;O Ministério da Saúde do Brasil é responsável por estabelecer linhas de cuidado para o manejo do diabetes mellitus tipo 2 no adulto, disponibilizadas em plataforma digital oficial.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ministério da Saúde is the Brazilian Ministry of Health responsible for public health policies and the publication of the Vigitel Brasil 2023 report.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d9cf8845dcb3d8d9a2db7f8843f0fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599c535216b129144d3ee7a08cfe646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4d53f9928520ac64a197b59db6862</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
