  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Palpation">
  <data key="d0">Skin Palpation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin palpation involves physically feeling the skin before insulin injection to detect abnormalities such as lumps or hardened areas associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640273</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lâmina B2">
  <data key="d0">Lâmina B2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Lâmina B2 is a genetic or molecular marker that may be associated with LPA, although findings have not been confirmed as an etiological factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPA">
  <data key="d0">LPA</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">LPA is a condition under investigation, potentially linked to genetic factors such as lâmina B2, but its etiology remains unconfirmed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV Infection">
  <data key="d0">HIV Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV infection is a viral disease that contributes to the development of HIV-associated lipodystrophy and affects adipose tissue through viral replication in adipocytes and macrophages.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a condition caused by the human immunodeficiency virus, associated with increased risk of secondary diabetes and recommended for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a viral condition that may increase the risk of developing diabetes mellitus, particularly due to associated treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a condition caused by the human immunodeficiency virus, associated with increased risk of secondary diabetes and recommended for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a viral condition that may increase the risk of developing diabetes mellitus, particularly due to associated treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a condition caused by the human immunodeficiency virus, associated with increased risk of secondary diabetes and recommended for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV Infection is a viral condition that may increase the risk of developing diabetes mellitus, particularly due to associated treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV-associated lipodystrophy is the most prevalent form of lipodystrophy today, affecting up to 50% of HIV-positive individuals, characterized by peripheral fat loss and central fat accumulation.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV-associated lipodystrophy is a form of lipodystrophy linked to antiretroviral therapy, requiring metabolic management and potential drug substitution.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV-associated lipodystrophy is the most prevalent form of lipodystrophy today, affecting up to 50% of HIV-positive individuals, with fat loss and metabolic complications linked to antiretroviral therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV-associated lipodystrophy is an acquired form of lipodystrophy linked to antiretroviral therapy, particularly protease inhibitors like ritonavir and lopinavir, and reverse transcriptase inhibitors such as lamivudina, zidovudina, and estavudina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipose Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Adipose Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipose tissue is affected in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, undergoing inflammatory changes, altered adipokine secretion, and cellular stress due to antiretroviral drugs and HIV infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leptin">
  <data key="d0">Leptin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Leptin is a hormone whose serum levels tend to be normal or elevated in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, reflecting altered adipose function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adiponectin">
  <data key="d0">Adiponectin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Adiponectin is a hormone with reduced serum levels in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, contributing to insulin resistance and metabolic dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First-Generation Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">First-Generation Protease Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">First-generation protease inhibitors, such as nelfinavir and indinavir, cause lipodystrophy by inhibiting adipocyte differentiation, inducing insulin resistance, and increasing pro-inflammatory cytokine production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second-Generation Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Second-Generation Protease Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Second-generation protease inhibitors include drugs like ritonavir and lopinavir that have adverse effects on adipose tissue through oxidative stress and altered adipokine secretion, while others like atazanavir and amprenavir lack such effects when used alone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ritonavir">
  <data key="d0">Ritonavir</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Ritonavir is a second-generation protease inhibitor that induces oxidative stress and modifies adipokine secretion, contributing to adipose tissue dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Ritonavir is a protease inhibitor used in HIV treatment and is associated with the development of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lopinavir">
  <data key="d0">Lopinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Lopinavir is a second-generation protease inhibitor that exerts detrimental effects on adipose tissue via oxidative stress and altered adipokine secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Lopinavir is a protease inhibitor used in HIV therapy and linked to acquired lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atazanavir">
  <data key="d0">Atazanavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Atazanavir is a second-generation protease inhibitor that, when used alone, does not have deleterious effects on adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amprenavir">
  <data key="d0">Amprenavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Amprenavir is a second-generation protease inhibitor that, when used in isolation, does not negatively affect adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nelfinavir">
  <data key="d0">Nelfinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nelfinavir is a first-generation protease inhibitor associated with lipodystrophy due to impaired adipocyte differentiation and increased insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indinavir">
  <data key="d0">Indinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Indinavir is a first-generation protease inhibitor that contributes to lipodystrophy by inhibiting adipocyte differentiation and promoting insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">drug</data>
  <data key="d2">Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors, particularly first-generation agents like stavudine and zidovudine, are associated with subcutaneous lipoatrophy due to mitochondrial dysfunction and oxidative stress in adipocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors are HIV medications that may affect the relationship between A1C and glycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors are HIV medications that may affect the relationship between A1C and glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stavudine">
  <data key="d0">Stavudine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Stavudine is a first-generation nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor that causes mitochondrial dysfunction, oxidative stress, reduced adiponectin secretion, and adipocyte apoptosis, contributing to lipoatrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zidovudine">
  <data key="d0">Zidovudine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Zidovudine is a first-generation nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor linked to lipodystrophy, particularly subcutaneous lipoatrophy, through mitochondrial dysfunction and increased oxidative stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tenofovir">
  <data key="d0">Tenofovir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenofovir is a second-generation nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor that does not cause the adverse metabolic effects associated with earlier drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mitochondrial Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Mitochondrial Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitochondrial dysfunction is a key mechanism by which certain antiretroviral drugs, especially thymidine analogs, impair adipocyte function and lead to lipoatrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d0">Oxidative Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidative stress is induced by several antiretroviral drugs and HIV infection itself, contributing to adipocyte dysfunction, inflammation, and premature cellular aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipokines">
  <data key="d0">Adipokines</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipokines are signaling proteins secreted by adipocytes that are altered in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, contributing to inflammation and insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pro-Inflammatory Cytokines">
  <data key="d0">Pro-Inflammatory Cytokines</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pro-inflammatory cytokines are secreted by infected macrophages and stressed adipocytes in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, promoting inflammation and metabolic disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macrophages">
  <data key="d0">Macrophages</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Macrophages in adipose tissue can be infected by HIV, shifting from an anti-inflammatory M2 phenotype to a pro-inflammatory M1 phenotype, increasing secretion of pro-inflammatory cytokines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="M1 Phenotype">
  <data key="d0">M1 Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The M1 phenotype is a pro-inflammatory state of macrophages induced by HIV infection, associated with the release of pro-inflammatory cytokines and metabolic disruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="M2 Phenotype">
  <data key="d0">M2 Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The M2 phenotype is an anti-inflammatory state of macrophages that shifts to M1 upon HIV infection, contributing to chronic inflammation in adipose tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visceral Fat Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Visceral Fat Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visceral fat hypertrophy is a feature of HIV-associated lipodystrophy, induced by protease inhibitors, leading to increased abdominal circumference and metabolic complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipid Metabolism Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Lipid Metabolism Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipid metabolism disorders in HIV-associated lipodystrophy include increased hepatic VLDL production due to protease inhibitor use, contributing to hypertriglyceridemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Metabolism Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Metabolism Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate metabolism disorders occur in HIV-associated lipodystrophy due to insulin resistance and impaired glucose regulation caused by antiretroviral therapy and viral infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiretroviral Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Antiretroviral Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiretroviral therapy is a treatment for HIV that can contribute to lipodystrophy; switching to less toxic regimens reduces inflammation but does not reverse existing lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral therapy is used in HIV treatment but may contribute to metabolic toxicity and lipodystrophy, prompting consideration of less toxic alternatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral therapy is a treatment for HIV that may influence glucose metabolism, necessitating screening for diabetes and prediabetes before initiation and after switching regimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral therapy (ARV) is used to treat HIV but is associated with increased risk of diabetes and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral Therapy refers to the use of drugs such as integrase inhibitors and protease inhibitors to treat HIV infection, which may contribute to insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral Therapy refers to the use of drugs such as integrase inhibitors and protease inhibitors to treat HIV infection, which may contribute to insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral Therapy refers to the use of drugs such as integrase inhibitors and protease inhibitors to treat HIV infection, which may contribute to insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic Syndrome is a cluster of interrelated metabolic conditions that significantly increase the risk of developing type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease. It is characterized by the presence of several key clinical features, including increased blood pressure, elevated blood sugar levels, excess body fat around the waist, and abnormal lipid profiles such as high triglycerides and low HDL cholesterol. These components often occur together, reflecting underlying insulin resistance and metabolic dysregulation.

In addition to these core criteria, Metabolic Syndrome is frequently associated with non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), which further underscores the systemic nature of metabolic dysfunction. The condition can manifest even in the absence of overt obesity, as seen in certain partial lipodystrophies where patients exhibit features such as severe hypertriglyceridemia, hepatomegaly, and acanthosis nigricans. This highlights that adipose tissue dysfunction, rather than total body fat alone, plays a critical role in the pathophysiology of the syndrome.

Despite variations in clinical presentation, the unifying theme across descriptions is the elevated risk for serious long-term health complications, particularly type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease. Multiple sources consistently emphasize this risk, reinforcing the importance of early identification and intervention. The repeated linkage to NAFLD and insulin resistance-related signs further supports a comprehensive view of Metabolic Syndrome as a multisystem disorder rooted in metabolic inflexibility and chronic metabolic stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e35953dbfdebbbab4bf83ec032ccfb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a109575f50250430ade32316446ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2977bb9a41689e74de2c536343624744</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatomegaly">
  <data key="d0">Hepatomegaly</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatomegaly is an enlargement of the liver associated with partial lipodystrophies, often due to hepatic steatosis and metabolic disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatomegaly refers to an enlarged liver, frequently observed in patients with lipodystrophy and associated metabolic disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Steatosis">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Steatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic steatosis is fatty liver disease commonly seen in partial lipodystrophies, resulting from abnormal fat distribution and metabolic dysregulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic steatosis, or fatty liver, is a common manifestation in lipodystrophy patients due to metabolic dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic steatosis, or fatty liver, is prevalent in lipodystrophy patients, detectable via abdominal ultrasound even in children, and may progress to cirrhosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acanthosis Nigricans">
  <data key="d0">Acanthosis Nigricans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acanthosis Nigricans is a skin condition characterized by dark, velvety hyperpigmentation, typically appearing in skin folds such as the neck, axillae, and groin. It is primarily recognized as a clinical marker of insulin resistance, a metabolic state in which the body’s cells respond poorly to insulin, leading to elevated insulin levels in the bloodstream. This condition is frequently observed in individuals with metabolic disorders, particularly those involving severe insulin resistance.

Acanthosis Nigricans is strongly associated with various forms of lipodystrophy, including both partial and generalized types. In these conditions, abnormal fat distribution leads to significant insulin resistance, and the severity of Acanthosis Nigricans often correlates with the degree of metabolic dysfunction. The presence of this skin condition in lipodystrophy patients underscores its role as a phenotypic indicator of underlying metabolic disturbances.

Additionally, Acanthosis Nigricans is commonly seen in individuals with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) and is especially prevalent in children and adolescents at risk for non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus. It appears in nearly 90% of children diagnosed with type 2 diabetes, highlighting its utility as an early warning sign. Its presence signals increased diabetes risk and is often used clinically to identify insulin resistance before the onset of overt diabetes. As such, Acanthosis Nigricans serves not only as a dermatological finding but also as an important marker for metabolic health, warranting further evaluation and intervention in affected individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition present in nearly 90% of children with DM2, indicating insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition associated with insulin resistance and serves as a clinical marker for increased risk of Type 2 Diabetes in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition associated with insulin resistance and serves as a risk factor for non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition present in nearly 90% of children with DM2, indicating insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition associated with insulin resistance and serves as a clinical marker for increased risk of Type 2 Diabetes in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Acanthosis nigricans is a skin condition associated with insulin resistance and serves as a risk factor for non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a109575f50250430ade32316446ee9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partial Lipodystrophies">
  <data key="d0">Partial Lipodystrophies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial lipodystrophies are suspected in young individuals with metabolic syndrome in the absence of obesity, characterized by site-specific fat loss and potential muscle prominence.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial lipodystrophies are a subtype of lipodystrophy involving loss of fat in specific body regions, often associated with metabolic disturbances and managed through lifestyle, pharmacological, and aesthetic interventions.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial lipodystrophies are a form of lipodystrophy where adipose tissue loss is localized, often underdiagnosed, and not currently indicated for metreleptin treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Family History">
  <data key="d0">Family History</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Family history, including consanguinity, is important in diagnosing partial lipodystrophies to determine inheritance patterns and genetic predisposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of type 2 diabetes in first- or second-degree relatives increases the risk for developing diabetes in youth.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history, also referred to as Background, includes multigenerational patterns of diabetes or autoimmune diseases, which help differentiate between types of diabetes in the AABBCC classification system.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of type 2 diabetes in first- or second-degree relatives increases the risk for developing diabetes in youth.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of diabetes increases the risk of developing DM2, with over 75% of pediatric cases having affected first- or second-degree relatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of diabetes increases the risk of developing DM2, with over 75% of pediatric cases having affected first- or second-degree relatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of diabetes increases the risk of developing DM2, with over 75% of pediatric cases having affected first- or second-degree relatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Examination">
  <data key="d0">Physical Examination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical examination is essential in diagnosing partial lipodystrophies, focusing on identifying sites of fat loss and signs such as muscle prominence and venous visibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical examination in lipodystrophy focuses on identifying sites of fat loss, muscle prominence, and phlebomegaly to support clinical diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VLDL Production">
  <data key="d0">VLDL Production</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">VLDL production is increased in the liver due to protease inhibitor use, contributing to lipid metabolism disorders in HIV-associated lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metreleptina">
  <data key="d0">Metreleptina</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Metreleptina is a medication used to treat metabolic conditions, administered once daily via subcutaneous injection, with dosing adjusted by weight and sex.&lt;SEP&gt;Metreleptina is recombinant leptin therapy indicated for selected cases of generalized lipodystrophy and partial forms with low leptin levels, potentially altering clinical management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulinoterapia">
  <data key="d0">Insulinoterapia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulinoterapia is a treatment involving insulin administration that some patients may no longer require after starting metreleptina.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoterapia is the therapeutic use of insulin to manage blood glucose levels in diabetic patients, especially critical in DM1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed992e01da83317a2c9f0adf751f53f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Homens">
  <data key="d0">Homens</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Homens refers to male patients who receive lower initial doses of metreleptina compared to women and have specific dosing guidelines based on body weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mulheres">
  <data key="d0">Mulheres</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mulheres refers to female patients who require higher doses of metreleptina than men, with specific dosing protocols based on body weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pacientes Com Mais De 40 Kg">
  <data key="d0">Pacientes Com Mais De 40 Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pacientes com mais de 40 kg are individuals weighing over 40 kilograms who follow a fixed-dose regimen of metreleptina based on sex.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pacientes Abaixo De 40 Kg">
  <data key="d0">Pacientes Abaixo De 40 Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pacientes abaixo de 40 kg are individuals weighing less than 40 kilograms who receive weight-based dosing of metreleptina starting at 0,06 mg/kg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Diaria Maxima">
  <data key="d0">Dose Diaria Maxima</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose diária máxima refers to the upper limit of metreleptina dosage, set at 0,13 mg/kg for patients under 40 kg and 10 mg for those over 40 kg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajustes De Dose">
  <data key="d0">Ajustes De Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ajustes de dose are modifications made to the metreleptina dosage based on clinical response and laboratory tests such as diabetes control, transaminases, and hypertriglyceridemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Via Subcutanea">
  <data key="d0">Via Subcutanea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Via subcutânea is the route of administration for metreleptina, requiring daily injection under the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peso Corporal">
  <data key="d0">Peso Corporal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Peso corporal is a determining factor in the initial and adjusted dosing of metreleptina, influencing whether weight-based or fixed dosing is used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perda De Peso">
  <data key="d0">Perda De Peso</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Perda de peso is a clinical parameter monitored to assess the effectiveness and need for dose adjustments of metreleptina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apetite">
  <data key="d0">Apetite</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Apetite is a clinical factor evaluated during treatment with metreleptina to determine therapeutic response and dosage modification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Do Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Controle Do Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle do diabetes is a laboratory and clinical outcome used to evaluate the efficacy of metreleptina and guide dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transaminases">
  <data key="d0">Transaminases</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Transaminases are liver enzymes monitored during metreleptina therapy to assess tolerability and safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipertrigliceridemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipertrigliceridemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipertrigliceridemia is a metabolic condition monitored during metreleptina treatment to evaluate therapeutic response and guide dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy is a rare genetic disorder characterized by generalized lipodystrophy, metabolic abnormalities, and insulin resistance, studied in multiple research papers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rio Grande Do Norte State">
  <data key="d0">Rio Grande Do Norte State</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Rio Grande Do Norte State is a region in Northeast Brazil where a high prevalence of Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy has been reported.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lima Jg">
  <data key="d0">Lima Jg</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lima JG is a researcher involved in multiple studies on congenital generalized lipodystrophy, contributing to clinical and laboratory data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima JG is a researcher involved in multiple studies on Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy, including bone density, umbilical hernia, and clinical data analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nobrega Lhc">
  <data key="d0">Nobrega Lhc</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Nobrega LHC is a researcher who has contributed to studies on bone density and clinical characteristics of patients with Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lima Nn">
  <data key="d0">Lima Nn</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lima NN is a researcher involved in clinical studies on congenital generalized lipodystrophy, contributing to data collection and analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lima NN is a researcher involved in studies on bone density and clinical data of patients with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dos Santos Mcf">
  <data key="d0">Dos Santos Mcf</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dos Santos MCF is a researcher involved in studies related to causes of death in patients with Berardinelli-Seip congenital generalized lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Dos Santos MCF is a researcher who co-authored a study on bone density in patients with Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
