<node id="AGPAT2">
  <data key="d0">AGPAT2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">AGPAT2 is a gene that is mutated in congenital generalized lipodystrophy linked to chromosome 9q34.&lt;SEP&gt;AGPAT2 is a gene associated with congenital generalized lipodystrophy, where homozygous or compound heterozygous mutations are responsible for approximately 90% of cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caveolin-1">
  <data key="d0">Caveolin-1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Caveolin-1 is a gene associated with Berardinelli-Seip congenital lipodystrophy, where a homozygous nonsense mutation has been identified.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PTRF">
  <data key="d0">PTRF</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PTRF is a gene whose mutations cause secondary deficiency of caveolins, resulting in muscular dystrophy with generalized lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;PTRF is a gene that may be associated with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6a69d5100e0e8263f965a83797d48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food And Drug Administration">
  <data key="d0">Food And Drug Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is the regulatory agency that approved metreleptin for the treatment of generalized lipodystrophies in 2014.&lt;SEP&gt;The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is a regulatory body that approved metreleptin for generalized lipodystrophies in 2014.&lt;SEP&gt;A U.S. federal agency responsible for regulating food, drugs, and medical devices, which issued the guidance document.&lt;SEP&gt;The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is a regulatory agency that has authorized the use of interstitial glucose readings from Dexcom G6® for therapeutic decisions without capillary confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498e4bb45447ec837c66b8fa72136a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metreleptin">
  <data key="d0">Metreleptin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Metreleptin is a recombinant human leptin therapy approved by the FDA in 2014 for the treatment of generalized lipodystrophies.&lt;SEP&gt;Metreleptin is a medication approved by the FDA in 2014 for the treatment of generalized lipodystrophies but is not currently recommended for partial forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Metreleptin is an approved treatment for generalized lipodystrophy in some countries, improving metabolic parameters and reducing appetite independently of its anorexigenic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Metreleptin is a recombinant human leptin used as replacement therapy in lipodystrophy, helping to improve metabolic parameters and proteinuria.&lt;SEP&gt;Metreleptin is a recombinant form of human leptin used as a treatment for lipodystrophy, improving metabolic parameters such as insulin sensitivity and proteinuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophies">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophies are a group of disorders characterized by partial or generalized loss of adipose tissue, leading to metabolic complications and requiring individualized treatment approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophies are a group of disorders characterized by loss of adipose tissue, with generalized and partial forms, leading to metabolic abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generalized Lipodystrophies">
  <data key="d0">Generalized Lipodystrophies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Generalized lipodystrophies involve widespread loss of adipose tissue and are the only form approved for treatment with recombinant human leptin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Generalized lipodystrophies are a subtype of lipodystrophy with widespread loss of adipose tissue, often diagnosed at birth or later in childhood, and associated with severe metabolic complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertension">
  <data key="d0">Hypertension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertension is a medical condition characterized by persistently elevated arterial blood pressure, commonly defined as a reading of 130/80 mmHg or higher or the ongoing use of medication to manage high blood pressure. It is recognized as a significant risk factor for the development of type 2 diabetes and contributes substantially to overall cardiovascular risk. The condition frequently occurs comorbidly with metabolic disorders, including insulin resistance and metabolic syndrome, and is closely associated with obesity, particularly in pediatric populations.

Hypertension is also a common comorbidity in patients with lipodystrophy, a group of rare disorders involving abnormal distribution of body fat. In these cases, hypertension is linked to underlying metabolic disturbances such as insulin resistance, reinforcing the interconnected nature of metabolic syndrome components. Due to its role in increasing the risk of diabetes and cardiovascular complications, the management of hypertension in lipodystrophy and other metabolic conditions should follow established clinical guidelines to mitigate long-term health consequences. Repeated descriptions confirm its status both as a standalone condition and as a contributing factor in complex metabolic disease profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypertension is a comorbidity and risk factor for Type 2 Diabetes in pediatric populations, often linked to obesity and metabolic syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiomyopathies">
  <data key="d0">Cardiomyopathies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiomyopathies are heart muscle diseases that occur as comorbidities in lipodystrophy patients and require standard medical management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiac Arrhythmias">
  <data key="d0">Cardiac Arrhythmias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiac arrhythmias are comorbid conditions in lipodystrophy patients that must be treated per usual clinical protocols.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Panniculitis">
  <data key="d0">Panniculitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Panniculitis is a condition in which corticosteroids may be used to reduce progression, although they do not restore lost adipose tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corticosteroids">
  <data key="d0">Corticosteroids</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Corticosteroids are medications used to manage panniculitis and associated autoimmune diseases but carry a risk of iatrogenic hypercortisolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Corticosteroids are medications that can cause neonatal hyperglycemia and must be ruled out during diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Corticosteroids are a class of drugs that can contribute to the onset of DKA in individuals with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iatrogenic Hypercortisolism">
  <data key="d0">Iatrogenic Hypercortisolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Iatrogenic hypercortisolism is a potential adverse effect of corticosteroid therapy in patients with lipodystrophy or panniculitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tesamorelin">
  <data key="d0">Tesamorelin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tesamorelin is a growth hormone-releasing hormone (aGHRH) analog used to reduce visceral fat in HIV-associated lipodystrophy and is not available in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Growth Hormone-Releasing Hormone">
  <data key="d0">Growth Hormone-Releasing Hormone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth hormone-releasing hormone (aGHRH) is a hormone that stimulates growth hormone release; tesamorelin is an analog used in treating visceral lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visceral Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Visceral Lipohypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visceral lipohypertrophy is a condition involving excess visceral fat, particularly in HIV patients, and is an indication for tesamorelin treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmetic Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Cosmetic Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cosmetic treatment is used in lipodystrophy to address phenotypic changes and psychological impact, including facial reconstruction and fat removal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polymethylmethacrylate Injections">
  <data key="d0">Polymethylmethacrylate Injections</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polymethylmethacrylate injections are a cosmetic treatment method used for subcutaneous facial filling in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autologous Adipose Tissue Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Autologous Adipose Tissue Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autologous adipose tissue transplant is a reconstructive technique used to restore facial volume in patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconstructive Surgery">
  <data key="d0">Reconstructive Surgery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconstructive surgery is a treatment option for severe cases of lipodystrophy to correct phenotypic deformities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Excision">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Excision</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical excision is used to remove excess adipose tissue in certain regions of lipodystrophy patients, though recurrence is possible.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liposuction">
  <data key="d0">Liposuction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Liposuction is a procedure to remove excess adipose tissue in lipodystrophy patients but carries a risk of recurrence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multidisciplinary Follow-Up">
  <data key="d0">Multidisciplinary Follow-Up</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multidisciplinary follow-up is essential for managing metabolic complexities in lipodystrophy patients, involving various healthcare professionals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nutritionist">
  <data key="d0">Nutritionist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A nutritionist is a healthcare professional involved in the multidisciplinary management of metabolic alterations in lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;A nutritionist is a healthcare professional involved in managing lipodystrophy patients, particularly in guiding dietary modifications based on disease pathophysiology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychologist">
  <data key="d0">Psychologist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A psychologist is part of the multidisciplinary team supporting lipodystrophy patients, addressing psychological impacts of phenotypic changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physiotherapist">
  <data key="d0">Physiotherapist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A physiotherapist is part of the multidisciplinary team managing patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Geneticist">
  <data key="d0">Medical Geneticist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A medical geneticist provides genetic counseling for families with inherited lipodystrophies and is involved in diagnosis and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy is a rare autosomal recessive disorder characterized by near-total absence of body fat from birth, severe insulin resistance, and metabolic abnormalities, with Berardinelli-Seip syndrome being the most recognized form.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital generalized lipodystrophy, also known as Berardinelli-Seip syndrome, presents at birth with characteristic phenotypic features and is caused by genetic mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital generalized lipodystrophy is a rare genetic disorder characterized by a lack of body fat from birth, leading to metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital generalized lipodystrophy refers to inherited forms of the disease, including types 1 to 4, presenting from birth or early childhood.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital generalized lipodystrophy is a genetic form of lipodystrophy, commonly caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutations in the AGPAT2 and BSCL2 genes, and sometimes associated with CAV1 and PTRF gene mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acquired Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Acquired Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acquired Generalized Lipodystrophy is a rare condition characterized by progressive loss of adipose tissue throughout the body, often associated with autoimmune diseases, with Lawrence syndrome being the primary example.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquired generalized lipodystrophy, also known as Lawrence syndrome, develops later in childhood after normal early phenotype and may be associated with autoimmune diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquired generalized lipodystrophy, also known as Lawrence syndrome, develops during childhood or adolescence with gradual fat loss and may be associated with autoimmune conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Berardinelli-Seip Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Berardinelli-Seip Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Berardinelli-Seip Syndrome is a congenital generalized form of lipodystrophy characterized by near-total absence of body fat from birth and severe insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Berardinelli-Seip syndrome is a congenital form of generalized lipodystrophy first described in 1954, associated with mutations in AGPAT2 or BSCL2 genes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lawrence Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Lawrence Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lawrence Syndrome is an acquired generalized lipodystrophy, marked by progressive loss of adipose tissue and metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Lawrence syndrome is the acquired form of generalized lipodystrophy, characterized by later onset of fat loss and possible association with autoimmune conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AGPAT2 Gene">
  <data key="d0">AGPAT2 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The AGPAT2 gene, located on chromosome 9q34, encodes an enzyme involved in triglyceride synthesis in adipocytes and is mutated in type 1 congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BSCL2 Gene">
  <data key="d0">BSCL2 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The BSCL2 gene, located on chromosome 11q13, encodes the protein seipin, which is involved in lipid droplet fusion and adipocyte differentiation, and is mutated in type 2 congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seipin">
  <data key="d0">Seipin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seipin is a protein encoded by the BSCL2 gene, important for triglyceride synthesis and adipocyte differentiation, with extra-adipocytic roles suggested by cognitive deficits in affected patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAV1 Gene">
  <data key="d0">CAV1 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAV1 gene, located on chromosome 7q31, is associated with type 3 congenital generalized lipodystrophy due to mutations affecting caveolae formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAVIN1 Gene">
  <data key="d0">CAVIN1 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAVIN1 gene is mutated in type 4 congenital generalized lipodystrophy, with fewer than 30 cases reported, and the protein is also present in muscle cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Syndromes">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Syndromes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy syndromes are complex disorders involving loss of adipose tissue and associated metabolic abnormalities, requiring multidisciplinary management.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy syndromes are a group of disorders characterized by selective loss of body fat and metabolic complications such as insulin resistance and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccde7bd12284b1c344a961b0f935b651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Abnormalities">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Abnormalities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic abnormalities are a core feature of lipodystrophy syndromes, including insulin resistance, dyslipidemia, and fatty liver disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Counseling">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Counseling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic counseling is a recommended practice for families with inherited lipodystrophies to understand transmission risks and implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic counseling is advised for families after a confirmed diagnosis of neonatal diabetes to inform about inheritance and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic counseling is recommended for individuals with monogenic diabetes to understand inheritance patterns and implications for family members.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metformin">
  <data key="d0">Metformin</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Metformin is an oral antidiabetic medication primarily used to manage blood glucose levels in individuals with type 2 diabetes and those at high risk of developing the condition. It is commonly prescribed early in treatment regimens, particularly for patients with severe insulin resistance, such as those with lipodystrophy, where it improves insulin sensitivity and helps regulate metabolic dysfunction. In addition to its glucose-lowering effects, metformin has been shown to reduce appetite and may induce ovulation in women with polycystic ovary syndrome, highlighting its broader metabolic and endocrine benefits.

The medication is also utilized as a preventive therapy in at-risk populations, including individuals with prediabetes or a history of gestational diabetes mellitus. In these cases, metformin is often administered alongside lifestyle modifications to reduce the incidence of type 2 diabetes. Clinical studies support its role in diabetes prevention, with evidence indicating its effectiveness in delaying or averting the onset of the disease in high-risk individuals.

Metformin has been evaluated for use in specific patient populations, such as organ transplant recipients. A small pilot study has found it to be safe for use in renal transplant recipients, often in combination with thiazolidinediones, although its safety profile in other types of organ transplants remains undetermined. While these findings are promising, further research is needed to establish broader guidelines for its use in immunocompromised patients. Overall, metformin remains a cornerstone in diabetes management and prevention, valued for its efficacy, safety in select populations, and multiple metabolic benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b2f90b1ec83426a0df84d7693bc26d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5ebd46f8491409b5f07f5c83542afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiazolidinediones">
  <data key="d0">Thiazolidinediones</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiazolidinediones (TZDs) are insulin-sensitizing drugs that increase peripheral subcutaneous fat and reduce visceral fat and liver inflammation but may cause unwanted fat growth in non-lipodystrophic areas and are contraindicated in generalized forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones such as pioglitazone are not recommended in generalized lipodystrophy as they may worsen hepatic steatosis and hypertriglyceridemia due to induced adipogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are used in liver and kidney transplant patients for diabetes management but carry risks such as fluid retention, heart failure, and osteopenia.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are a class of antidiabetic drugs studied for effectiveness and long-term safety in renal transplant recipients.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are used in liver and kidney transplant patients for diabetes management but carry risks such as fluid retention, heart failure, and osteopenia.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazolidinediones are a class of antidiabetic drugs studied for effectiveness and long-term safety in renal transplant recipients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fibrates">
  <data key="d0">Fibrates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fibrates are lipid-lowering agents used as first-line treatment for refractory hypertriglyceridemia in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statins">
  <data key="d0">Statins</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Statins are lipid-lowering drugs that may be combined with fibrates (except gemfibrozil) to manage dyslipidemia in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Niacin">
  <data key="d0">Niacin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Niacin is not recommended for lipodystrophy patients due to its potential to increase insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estrogens">
  <data key="d0">Estrogens</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Estrogens are contraindicated for treating polycystic ovary syndrome in women with lipodystrophy due to the risk of worsening hypertriglyceridemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dietary Management">
  <data key="d0">Dietary Management</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dietary management in lipodystrophy includes a balanced, low-fat diet, adequate caloric intake in childhood, omega-3 supplementation (5–10 g/day), and potential use of medium-chain triglycerides to reduce serum triglycerides and atherosclerosis progression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychological Support">
  <data key="d0">Psychological Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychological support is recommended for patients and families to address emotional and social challenges associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic evaluation of lipodystrophy includes detailed history taking, physical examination for fat loss sites, muscle prominence, and phlebomegaly, along with assessment of comorbidities, medication use, and family history including consanguinity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Imaging Tests">
  <data key="d0">Imaging Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Imaging tests such as ultrasound, dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DXA), whole-body MRI, and bioimpedance are used to assess fat distribution, preserved adipose tissue sites, and organomegaly in lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Holter Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Holter Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Holter monitoring is recommended for patients suspected of cardiomyopathy or coronary artery disease to evaluate cardiac rhythm over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Echocardiogram">
  <data key="d0">Echocardiogram</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Echocardiogram is used to assess cardiac structure and function in patients with suspected cardiomyopathy due to lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Test">
  <data key="d0">Stress Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress testing is performed to evaluate cardiovascular response to exertion in patients with suspected coronary artery disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Molecular Testing">
  <data key="d0">Molecular Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Molecular testing should be performed in suspected inherited lipodystrophies based on clinical suspicion to confirm genetic diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Differential Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The differential diagnosis of lipodystrophy includes syndromes of insulin resistance due to insulin receptor mutations (e.g., leprechaunism, type A and B insulin resistance syndromes) and Cushing's syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Omega-3">
  <data key="d0">Omega-3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Omega-3 fatty acids, supplemented at 5–10 g/day, help reduce serum triglyceride levels and slow atherosclerosis progression in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medium-Chain Triglycerides">
  <data key="d0">Medium-Chain Triglycerides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medium-chain triglycerides are a potentially beneficial nutritional approach in lipodystrophy management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol consumption should be avoided in patients with lipodystrophy due to potential adverse metabolic effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy diagnosis involves a detailed clinical evaluation including age of onset, progression pattern, associated features, comorbidities, medication use, family history, and consanguinity to determine inheritance pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complementary Tests">
  <data key="d0">Complementary Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Complementary tests are performed to assess metabolic complications and autoimmune conditions in patients with suspected lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dr. Augusto Pimazoni Netto">
  <data key="d0">Dr. Augusto Pimazoni Netto</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dr. Augusto Pimazoni Netto is a medical professional discussing the clinical aspects of lipohipertrofia in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipohipertrofia Lesions">
  <data key="d0">Lipohipertrofia Lesions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipohipertrofia Lesions are fibrotic tissue areas in the subcutaneous fat resulting from repeated insulin injections in the same location, often associated with improper injection techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasound">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasound</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasound is an imaging test used to evaluate organomegaly in the diagnostic workup of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual-Energy X-Ray Absorptiometry">
  <data key="d0">Dual-Energy X-Ray Absorptiometry</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DXA) is used to assess body fat distribution and identify sites of preserved adipose tissue in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Whole-Body MRI">
  <data key="d0">Whole-Body MRI</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Whole-body MRI is an imaging technique used to evaluate the distribution of body fat and sites of adipose tissue preservation in lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bioimpedance">
  <data key="d0">Bioimpedance</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bioimpedance is a method used to assess body composition and fat distribution in patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skinfold Measurements">
  <data key="d0">Skinfold Measurements</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Skinfold measurements are a technique used to evaluate subcutaneous fat distribution and aid in the clinical assessment of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leprechaunism">
  <data key="d0">Leprechaunism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Leprechaunism is a rare syndrome of insulin resistance due to insulin receptor mutations, included in the differential diagnosis of lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Leprechaunism is a rare genetic disorder characterized by extreme insulin resistance due to defects in insulin receptors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intralesional Insulin Injection">
  <data key="d0">Intralesional Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intralesional Insulin Injection is the practice of injecting insulin directly into lipohipertrofia lesions, which impairs insulin absorption and glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Impaired Glucose Control">
  <data key="d0">Impaired Glucose Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Impaired Glucose Control is a clinical consequence of intralesional insulin injection, leading to increased postprandial glucose variability and poor diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type A Insulin Resistance Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Type A Insulin Resistance Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type A Insulin Resistance Syndrome is a condition involving insulin receptor abnormalities and is part of the differential diagnosis for lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Care">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Care</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Care is a peer-reviewed medical journal published by the American Diabetes Association (ADA), widely regarded as a leading scientific publication in the field of diabetes. It serves as a primary platform for disseminating high-impact, evidence-based research, clinical guidelines, and consensus reports that influence diabetes care practices globally. The journal publishes a broad spectrum of content, including original clinical research, studies on diagnosis and classification, treatment strategies, disease management, complications, and emerging technologies. It is particularly known for its rigorous peer-review standards and its role in advancing both clinical and scientific understanding across all forms of diabetes.

A defining feature of Diabetes Care is its annual publication of the ADA’s “Standards of Care in Diabetes,” a critical reference for healthcare professionals worldwide. The 2023 edition, released in Volume 46, Supplement 1, includes updated guidance on screening, diagnosis, classification, and management, integrating recent advancements in diabetes technology. The journal has published landmark consensus reports, including those from the Expert Committee on the Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes Mellitus and collaborative statements by the ADA and the European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD), especially on digital health applications. Notable historical contributions include pivotal studies on diabetes classification in 1997, clinical screening for autoimmune diabetes in 2006, and population-based assessments of monogenic diabetes in 2017.

Diabetes Care emphasizes research on glucose monitoring technologies, featuring extensive studies on continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems, their accuracy, and clinical utility. Key publications include a 2021 CGM study (Volume 44), a 2018 evaluation of 18 blood glucose monitors (Volume 41), and a 2013 analysis linking self-monitoring frequency to HbA1c levels (Volume 36). The journal introduced a consensus error grid analysis in 2000 (Volume 23) to standardize glucose monitoring error interpretation. It has also published significant research on insulin therapy, including studies on insulin detemir and glargine, insulin delivery systems, and complications such as lipohypertrophy. Additional clinical areas covered include ketosis-prone diabetes, obesity in type 1 diabetes, adult-onset and young-onset diabetes, and type 3c diabetes.

The journal also contributes to diabetes epidemiology, public health, and health disparities research, publishing findings on racial differences in outcomes, HbA1c underestimation in HIV-infected individuals, trends in diabetes during pregnancy, and the cost-effectiveness of genetic testing. It has disseminated results from major longitudinal studies such as the HAPO Follow-up Study and the Structured Testing Program (2011). Specific studies highlighted include research on intensive glucose control outcomes, the translation of HbA1c into estimated average glucose values, a 2017 study on Hemoglobin A1c and mortality in older adults, and investigations into plasma glucose, retinopathy, insulin resistance, and diabetes risk. Through its comprehensive and authoritative content, Diabetes Care remains a cornerstone in shaping global diabetes research and clinical practice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e1858f15899659bc0116977a6e1e000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4ef00b7799130b85ed6433c381dfef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc6a5cedffa24f9a3134770cf1526b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6dadde3434f68ef74ebdf23be6a24ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498e4bb45447ec837c66b8fa72136a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862cb6f254fb8ebb4f3e1080dbf4f53c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0524115c9e0c2a0ed35c413e50c658e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af4e8af9934463f38c5951016d9664b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5ebd46f8491409b5f07f5c83542afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5cd98bab9909442c09e3fcd5b21fda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a18ecfcb20fceb4fd80ab22186964e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a874190e40ad535ac9b317a469571d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c156c40ae38c1b220a3c59d658c17171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccde7bd12284b1c344a961b0f935b651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f017257ae0e7fcc5a0a1be0ddc435fe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599c535216b129144d3ee7a08cfe646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2977bb9a41689e74de2c536343624744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3628fc721a312bfbaace1de3a4d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
