</node>
<node id="Famulla S">
  <data key="d0">Famulla S</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Famulla S is a researcher and lead author of a study published in Diabetes Care that investigated the impact of injecting insulin into lipohypertrophic tissue in patients with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial Glycemia refere-se aos níveis de glicose no sangue após as refeições, que aumentam significativamente quando a insulina é aplicada em lesões de lipohipertrofia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type B Insulin Resistance Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Type B Insulin Resistance Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type B Insulin Resistance Syndrome is an autoimmune form of insulin resistance considered in the differential diagnosis of lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Type B Insulin Resistance Syndrome is an autoimmune condition caused by antibodies against the insulin receptor, linked to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cushing Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Cushing Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cushing Syndrome is a condition of hypercortisolism that can lead to acquired lipodystrophy with central fat accumulation and peripheral fat loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Cushing Syndrome is a condition characterized by excess cortisol and is included in the differential diagnosis of lipodystrophy due to overlapping clinical features.&lt;SEP&gt;Cushing Syndrome is an endocrinopathy associated with hyperglycemia and is a differential consideration in diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d000f0bd5254e1a2df1aba208ecc4170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofia Generalizada">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofia Generalizada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodistrofia generalizada is a group of rare disorders characterized by a generalized loss of adipose tissue, which can be inherited or acquired.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Síndrome de Berardinelli-Seip">
  <data key="d0">Síndrome de Berardinelli-Seip</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Síndrome de Berardinelli-Seip is a congenital form of generalized lipodystrophy inherited genetically, associated with mutations in specific genes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Síndrome de Lawrence">
  <data key="d0">Síndrome de Lawrence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Síndrome de Lawrence is an acquired form of generalized lipodystrophy, typically manifesting in childhood or adolescence with gradual fat loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gene AGPAT2">
  <data key="d0">Gene AGPAT2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Gene AGPAT2 is associated with Type 1 generalized lipodystrophy; mutations in this gene lead to partial retention of fat in palms and soles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gene BSCL2">
  <data key="d0">Gene BSCL2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Gene BSCL2 is linked to Type 2 generalized lipodystrophy, which presents with severe fat loss and possible cognitive deficits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gene CAV1">
  <data key="d0">Gene CAV1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Gene CAV1, located on chromosome 7q31, is associated with Type 3 generalized lipodystrophy, a rare genetic form.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gene CAVIN1">
  <data key="d0">Gene CAVIN1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Gene CAVIN1 is responsible for Type 4 generalized lipodystrophy and is also expressed in muscle cells, leading to muscular dystrophy in some patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 generalized lipodystrophy is caused by mutations in the AGPAT2 gene and may present with residual fat in palms and soles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 generalized lipodystrophy, caused by BSCL2 gene mutations, is clinically more severe with near-total absence of body fat and possible cognitive impairment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 3 Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Type 3 Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 3 generalized lipodystrophy is a rare form caused by mutations in the CAV1 gene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 4 Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Type 4 Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 4 generalized lipodystrophy results from mutations in the CAVIN1 gene and may include muscular dystrophy due to CAVIN1 expression in muscle cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatomegalia">
  <data key="d0">Hepatomegalia</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatomegalia is a clinical sign observed in patients with generalized lipodystrophy, often detected in childhood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipertensão Arterial">
  <data key="d0">Hipertensão Arterial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipertensão arterial affects about one-third of patients with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipertensão Arterial is a condition of high blood pressure, recognized as a risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipertensão Arterial is a condition of high blood pressure, recognized as a risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipertensão Arterial is a condition of high blood pressure, recognized as a risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertriglyceridemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypertriglyceridemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertriglyceridemia is a common metabolic manifestation in lipodystrophy patients, often severe enough to cause acute pancreatitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypertriglyceridemia is a common laboratory finding in generalized lipodystrophy, often exceeding 2,000 mg/dL, and may lead to eruptive xanthomas.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypertriglyceridemia, or elevated triglyceride levels, can interfere with certain glucose testing methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypertriglyceridemia, or elevated triglyceride levels, can interfere with certain glucose testing methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypertriglyceridemia, or elevated triglyceride levels, can interfere with certain glucose testing methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688805</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiperfagia">
  <data key="d0">Hiperfagia</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Hiperfagia occurs due to severe leptin deficiency from minimal adipose tissue, resembling Prader-Willi syndrome in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoleptinemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipoleptinemia</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoleptinemia results from the near absence of adipose tissue, leading to low serum leptin levels and associated complications like amenorrhea and hyperphagia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amenorrhea">
  <data key="d0">Amenorrhea</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Amenorrhea in generalized lipodystrophy is caused by insulin resistance and hypoleptinemia, mimicking polycystic ovary syndrome or hypothalamic amenorrhea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eruptive Xanthomas">
  <data key="d0">Eruptive Xanthomas</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Eruptive xanthomas may occur in patients with severe hypertriglyceridemia but are not common in other forms of xanthomatosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Muscular Dystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Muscular Dystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscular dystrophy can occur in Type 4 generalized lipodystrophy due to CAVIN1 expression in muscle cells, presenting with elevated CPK and muscle weakness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bichat's Fat Pad">
  <data key="d0">Bichat's Fat Pad</data>
  <data key="d1">anatomicalstructure</data>
  <data key="d2">Bichat's fat pad is a facial fat deposit that is absent in patients with generalized lipodystrophy, contributing to characteristic phenotypic changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acromegaloid Facies">
  <data key="d0">Acromegaloid Facies</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Acromegaloid facies is a phenotypic feature in generalized lipodystrophy, characterized by facial changes resembling acromegaly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phlebomegaly">
  <data key="d0">Phlebomegaly</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Phlebomegaly refers to the enlargement of veins, a clinical feature reported in some cases of lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Phlebomegaly refers to the dilation of veins, observed in patients with generalized lipodystrophy due to reduced subcutaneous fat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Muscular Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Muscular Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscular hypertrophy is a clinical sign in generalized lipodystrophy, resulting from the lack of adipose tissue that makes muscles more prominent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertrichosis">
  <data key="d0">Hypertrichosis</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertrichosis, or excessive hair growth, is a phenotypic feature observed in some patients with generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Umbilical Hernia">
  <data key="d0">Umbilical Hernia</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Umbilical hernia is not more frequent in generalized lipodystrophy, but the lack of periumbilical fat may make the umbilical scar more prominent, mimicking a hernia.&lt;SEP&gt;Umbilical hernia is a physical anomaly linked to transient neonatal diabetes, particularly in cases involving 6q24-related mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Distension">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Distension</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdominal distension in generalized lipodystrophy, especially in children, is often due to hepatomegaly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Examination">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Examination</data>
  <data key="d1">procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">Thyroid examination is typically normal in generalized lipodystrophy, although patients have an increased predisposition to thyroid diseases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elevated Transaminases">
  <data key="d0">Elevated Transaminases</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated transaminases occur in generalized lipodystrophy due to hepatic steatosis, even in infants, and are a common laboratory finding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brazilian Patients">
  <data key="d0">Brazilian Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Brazilian patients are individuals from Brazil who have been diagnosed with congenital generalized lipodystrophy and are subjects of clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nobrega Lh">
  <data key="d0">Nobrega Lh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Nobrega LH is a researcher who has participated in studies examining clinical aspects and causes of death in patients with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silva Phd">
  <data key="d0">Silva Phd</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Silva PHD is a researcher who contributed to research on mortality causes in patients with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lee Hl">
  <data key="d0">Lee Hl</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lee HL is a researcher who studied the effects of metreleptin on proteinuria in patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waldman Ma">
  <data key="d0">Waldman Ma</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Waldman MA is a researcher involved in evaluating the impact of metreleptin therapy on lipodystrophy-related complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cochran Ek">
  <data key="d0">Cochran Ek</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cochran EK is a researcher involved in clinical investigations of metreleptin treatment in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gorden P">
  <data key="d0">Gorden P</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Gorden P is a researcher who participated in studies on the therapeutic effects of metreleptin in lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brown Rj">
  <data key="d0">Brown Rj</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Brown RJ is a researcher who has conducted long-term studies on the effectiveness and safety of metreleptin in treating generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Araújo-Vilar D">
  <data key="d0">Araújo-Vilar D</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Araújo-Vilar D is a researcher who contributed to studies on the treatment of generalized lipodystrophy with metreleptin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savage Db">
  <data key="d0">Savage Db</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Savage DB is a researcher involved in evaluating the long-term safety and efficacy of metreleptin in lipodystrophy treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
