  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Berardinelli-Seip congenital generalized lipodystrophy is a specific subtype of congenital generalized lipodystrophy associated with metabolic complications and increased mortality risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-55c9f6328c4401f126aa9ac11be639b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640773</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial (LPF) is a genetic form of lipodystrophy with various subtypes, each associated with specific gene mutations and clinical features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640773</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dunnigan">
  <data key="d0">Dunnigan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dunnigan is a researcher who first described a variant of familial partial lipodystrophy in 1974.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640773</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Köbberling">
  <data key="d0">Köbberling</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Köbberling is a researcher who described a variant of familial partial lipodystrophy in 1975.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LMNA Gene">
  <data key="d0">LMNA Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The LMNA gene, located on chromosome 1q21-22, encodes lamin A and C proteins, which are components of the nuclear lamina and associated with LPF type 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PPARG Gene">
  <data key="d0">PPARG Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The PPARG gene, located on chromosome 3p25, encodes the PPARγ transcription factor crucial for adipocyte differentiation and linked to LPF type 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PLIN1 Gene">
  <data key="d0">PLIN1 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The PLIN1 gene, located on chromosome 15q26, encodes perilipin 1, a protein essential for lipid droplet formation and regulation in adipocytes, associated with LPF type 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKT2 Gene">
  <data key="d0">AKT2 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The AKT2 gene, located on chromosome 19q13.2, encodes the AKT2 protein (protein kinase B), involved in insulin signaling and linked to LPF type 5.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIDEC Gene">
  <data key="d0">CIDEC Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The CIDEC gene encodes a protein highly expressed in adipocytes during differentiation and is associated with a rare autosomal recessive form of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPF Type 1">
  <data key="d0">LPF Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LPF Type 1, also known as Köbberling variant, is a rare form of familial partial lipodystrophy with limited fat loss in extremities and unclear genetic inheritance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPF Type 2">
  <data key="d0">LPF Type 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LPF Type 2, also known as Dunnigan variant, is the most common form of LPF caused by LMNA gene mutations, affecting nuclear function and leading to adipocyte death.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPF Type 3">
  <data key="d0">LPF Type 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LPF Type 3 is caused by PPARG gene mutations, resulting in defective adipocyte differentiation and prominent subcutaneous fat loss in distal extremities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPF Type 4">
  <data key="d0">LPF Type 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LPF Type 4 arises from PLIN1 gene mutations, leading to abnormal lipid droplet regulation, increased basal lipolysis, and reduced adipocyte size with fibrosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LPF Type 5">
  <data key="d0">LPF Type 5</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LPF Type 5 is caused by AKT2 gene mutations, leading to insulin resistance, diabetes mellitus, and dysfunctional post-receptor insulin signaling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dyslipidemia">
  <data key="d0">Dyslipidemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal levels of lipids in the blood, most commonly involving elevated triglycerides and reduced levels of high-density lipoprotein (HDL) cholesterol. This lipid imbalance is frequently observed in individuals with lipodystrophy, a group of disorders involving abnormal fat distribution, and is recognized as a common comorbidity in such cases. The condition is closely tied to metabolic disturbances, particularly insulin resistance, which impairs the body's ability to regulate glucose and lipid metabolism effectively.

Dyslipidemia is strongly associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular disease due to the atherogenic nature of the lipid profile it produces. The combination of high triglycerides and low HDL cholesterol contributes to the development of atherosclerosis, thereby elevating the likelihood of heart attacks and strokes. In addition to cardiovascular complications, dyslipidemia is linked to a heightened risk of developing type 2 diabetes. This association is evident across age groups, including children and adolescents, in whom abnormal lipid levels serve as an early warning sign for future metabolic disease.

The recurring presence of insulin resistance in descriptions of dyslipidemia underscores its central role in the pathophysiology of the condition. Insulin resistance not only drives lipid abnormalities but also creates a feedback loop that exacerbates metabolic dysfunction. Overall, dyslipidemia functions as both a marker and a contributor to broader metabolic syndrome, emphasizing the importance of early detection and management to mitigate long-term health risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Muscle Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Muscle Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscle hypertrophy is the increase in muscle mass, observed in some patients with lipodystrophy, particularly in the limbs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polycystic Ovary Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a common hormonal and endocrine disorder primarily affecting women, particularly during their reproductive years. It is characterized by hormonal imbalances, including elevated androgen levels, and is frequently associated with insulin resistance, a condition in which the body’s cells do not respond effectively to insulin. This insulin resistance plays a central role in the pathophysiology of PCOS and significantly increases the risk of developing type 2 diabetes mellitus. The condition is observed across various populations, including adolescent females, and has been noted in 26% of girls with type 2 diabetes, underscoring its strong metabolic component.

PCOS is also linked to partial lipodystrophies—disorders involving abnormal fat distribution—which further exacerbate metabolic dysfunction and contribute to the syndrome’s clinical presentation. These metabolic disturbances not only elevate diabetes risk but also lead to reproductive complications, including infertility, irregular menstrual cycles, and ovarian cysts. The interplay between hormonal dysregulation and metabolic abnormalities makes PCOS a multifaceted condition with both endocrine and reproductive implications. Due to its association with insulin resistance, early diagnosis and management are crucial to mitigate long-term health risks such as diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and infertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycystic ovary syndrome is present in 26% of girls with DM2 and is linked to insulin resistance and hormonal imbalances.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycystic ovary syndrome is an endocrine disorder in adolescent females that increases the risk of Type 2 Diabetes due to insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycystic ovary syndrome is present in 26% of girls with DM2 and is linked to insulin resistance and hormonal imbalances.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycystic ovary syndrome is an endocrine disorder in adolescent females that increases the risk of Type 2 Diabetes due to insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Myopathy">
  <data key="d0">Myopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Myopathy refers to muscle disease, which can occur in some lipodystrophy patients, indicating systemic involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Myopathy refers to muscle disease that can occur in some forms of lipodystrophy, such as in patients with PPARG or PLIN1 mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiomyopathy">
  <data key="d0">Cardiomyopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiomyopathy is a disease of the heart muscle, reported in some lipodystrophy cases, particularly with certain gene mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiomyopathy is a cardiac complication observed in some lipodystrophy patients, potentially leading to heart failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electrical Conduction Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Electrical Conduction Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrical conduction disorders are abnormalities in the heart's electrical system, observed in some lipodystrophy patients, suggesting multisystemic impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrical Conduction Disorders are heart rhythm abnormalities that may occur in patients with lipodystrophy, especially those with associated genetic syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamin A">
  <data key="d0">Lamin A</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamin A is a structural protein of the nuclear lamina, encoded by the LMNA gene, and involved in nuclear integrity and gene regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mature lamin A is a structural protein; its deficiency due to impaired prelamin A processing contributes to cellular dysfunction in mandibuloacral dysplasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamin C">
  <data key="d0">Lamin C</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamin C is a protein isoform encoded by the LMNA gene, part of the nuclear lamina, and plays a role in nuclear stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PPARγ">
  <data key="d0">PPARγ</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PPARγ is a nuclear transcription factor encoded by PPARG, essential for adipocyte differentiation and lipid metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retinoic Acid Receptor X">
  <data key="d0">Retinoic Acid Receptor X</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Retinoic Acid Receptor X (RXR) forms a heterodimer with PPARγ to regulate gene expression involved in adipocyte function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perilipin 1">
  <data key="d0">Perilipin 1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Perilipin 1 is a protein encoded by PLIN1, coating lipid droplets in adipocytes and regulating triglyceride storage and free fatty acid release.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKT2 Protein">
  <data key="d0">AKT2 Protein</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AKT2 protein, also known as protein kinase B, is encoded by AKT2 and plays a key role in insulin signaling pathways.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIDEC Protein">
  <data key="d0">CIDEC Protein</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">CIDEC protein is encoded by the CIDEC gene and is highly expressed in adipocytes during differentiation, linked to lipid metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laminopathies">
  <data key="d0">Laminopathies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Laminopathies are a group of diseases caused by mutations in the LMNA gene, including familial partial lipodystrophy and Hutchinson-Gilford progeria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hutchinson-Gilford Progeria">
  <data key="d0">Hutchinson-Gilford Progeria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hutchinson-Gilford Progeria is a rare genetic disorder causing accelerated aging, caused by LMNA gene mutations and classified as a laminopathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hutchinson-Gilford Progeria is a rare genetic disorder causing accelerated aging and is sometimes associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autosomal Recessive Inheritance">
  <data key="d0">Autosomal Recessive Inheritance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autosomal recessive inheritance is a pattern of genetic transmission requiring two copies of a mutated gene, observed in one reported case of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 1">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 1, also known as Köbberling variant, is a rare subtype of familial partial lipodystrophy with fat loss primarily in the extremities and normal or increased fat in the face and trunk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 2">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 2, also known as Dunnigan variant, is the most common form of LPF caused by LMNA gene mutations, leading to progressive loss of subcutaneous fat from limbs and trunk with onset at puberty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 3">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 3 is caused by mutations in the PPARG gene, resulting in defective adipocyte differentiation and prominent fat loss in distal extremities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 4">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 4 is caused by mutations in the PLIN1 gene, leading to constitutive activation of adipose triglyceride lipase, increased basal lipolysis, and lipodystrophy predominantly affecting lower limbs and gluteofemoral region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 5">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 5</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 5 is caused by heterozygous missense mutation in the AKT2 gene, leading to severe insulin resistance, diabetes mellitus, and partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Generalized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Generalized lipodystrophy is a subtype of lipodystrophy where there is a near-total absence of body fat, often leading to severe metabolic disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LCG">
  <data key="d0">LCG</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LCG refers to generalized congenital lipodystrophy, a rare genetic form of lipodystrophy with high mortality, often resulting in death before age 30 due to hepatic, renal, or infectious complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acrochordons">
  <data key="d0">Acrochordons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acrochordons, or skin tags, are associated with insulin resistance and are commonly observed in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Leptin Levels">
  <data key="d0">Low Leptin Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low serum leptin levels are a diagnostic marker in lipodystrophy and contribute to hyperphagia and metabolic dysregulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Childhood">
  <data key="d0">Childhood</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Childhood is a critical period in lipodystrophy, with symptoms worsening when transitioning from breastfeeding to regular diet, especially affecting triglyceride and transaminase levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breastfeeding">
  <data key="d0">Breastfeeding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Breastfeeding provides some leptin from maternal milk, which may mitigate disease severity in early infancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saturated Fat Restriction">
  <data key="d0">Saturated Fat Restriction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Saturated fat restriction is a key dietary intervention in managing hypertriglyceridemia and preventing diabetes in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonylureas">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonylureas</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonylureas are oral antidiabetic agents that can be used in early-stage diabetes in lipodystrophy patients who still have beta-cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonylureas are a class of medications used to treat certain types of MODY, including MODY-HNF1A, MODY-HNF4A, MODY-KCNJ11, and MODY-ABCC8, due to the good therapeutic response observed in these patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonylureas are a class of antihyperglycemic drugs used as first-line treatment for certain forms of MODY and neonatal diabetes due to their effectiveness in stimulating insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;High-dose oral sulfonylureas can improve blood glucose control in individuals with KATP channel-related neonatal diabetes, replacing the need for insulin in 30–50% of cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonylureas are a class of medications used as first-line therapy for HNF1A-MODY and HNF4A-MODY and are effective in some forms of neonatal diabetes such as those caused by KCNJ11 or ABCC8 mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DPP-4 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">DPP-4 Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DPP-4 inhibitors are a class of medications used to help achieve better glycemic control in patients with metabolic disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;DPP-4 inhibitors are antidiabetic drugs that may be used in lipodystrophy patients despite lack of specific studies, aiding in glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SGLT2 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">SGLT2 Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SGLT2 inhibitors are drugs that may be used for glycemic control but can cause weight loss, which may limit their use in underweight patients.&lt;SEP&gt;SGLT2 inhibitors are antidiabetic medications that may help improve glycemic control in lipodystrophy patients, though specific studies are lacking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GLP-1 Analogues">
  <data key="d0">GLP-1 Analogues</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GLP-1 analogues are not well studied in certain conditions but could help manage hyperphagia caused by hypoleptinemia, though their associated weight loss may restrict usage.&lt;SEP&gt;GLP-1 analogues are potential treatments for lipodystrophy that may help control hyperphagia caused by leptin deficiency, though they have not been studied specifically in this population.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DXA Scan">
  <data key="d0">DXA Scan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DXA scan is a diagnostic tool used to assess body composition, showing body fat percentage below 7% in generalized lipodystrophy, aiding in diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Ultrasound">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Ultrasound</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdominal ultrasound is used to detect hepatic steatosis and hepatosplenomegaly in lipodystrophy patients, even in childhood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Body Fat Percentage">
  <data key="d0">Low Body Fat Percentage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with generalized lipodystrophy typically have a body fat percentage below 7%, with an average around 5%, which can be confirmed via DXA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal or High Bone Density">
  <data key="d0">Normal or High Bone Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DXA scans in lipodystrophy patients often reveal normal or elevated bone density, a notable finding in disease assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Mortality Rate">
  <data key="d0">High Mortality Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with generalized lipodystrophy, especially type 2, face high mortality, often dying before age 30 due to liver failure, renal insufficiency, pancreatitis, or infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Complications">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic complications such as cirrhosis and gastrointestinal bleeding are leading causes of death in generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Renal Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal insufficiency is one of the major complications contributing to mortality in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Pancreatitis">
  <data key="d0">Acute Pancreatitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute pancreatitis is a serious complication of severe hypertriglyceridemia in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infectious Episodes">
  <data key="d0">Infectious Episodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infectious episodes are among the primary causes of death in patients with generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Insulin Levels">
  <data key="d0">Serum Insulin Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum insulin levels are markedly elevated in lipodystrophy patients, even during fasting periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Leptin Levels">
  <data key="d0">Serum Leptin Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum leptin levels are low in lipodystrophy patients, which can aid in diagnostic confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triglyceride Levels">
  <data key="d0">Triglyceride Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Triglyceride levels are often very high in lipodystrophy patients, sometimes approaching but usually remaining below 1,000 mg/dL, with higher levels reported in American cohorts than in Brazilian patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HDL Cholesterol">
  <data key="d0">HDL Cholesterol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HDL cholesterol levels are inversely related to triglycerides and are typically below 30 mg/dL in lipodystrophy patients.&lt;SEP&gt;HDL cholesterol level below 35 mg/dL (0.90 mmol/L) is considered a risk factor for insulin resistance and diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;HDL cholesterol level below 35 mg/dL (0.90 mmol/L) is considered a risk factor for insulin resistance and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Enzymes">
  <data key="d0">Liver Enzymes</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver enzymes, particularly TGP, are elevated due to hepatic steatosis; GGT is also frequently elevated, while transaminases normalize in advanced disease, indicating worsening prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platelet Count">
  <data key="d0">Platelet Count</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Platelet count begins to decrease in advanced stages of lipodystrophy, signaling progression toward cirrhosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Serum Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum glucose is normal to low in early stages of lipodystrophy (often &lt; 80 mg/dL) before progressing to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pioglitazone">
  <data key="d0">Pioglitazone</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pioglitazone is a thiazolidinedione medication that is contraindicated in generalized lipodystrophy due to its potential to worsen hepatic steatosis and hypertriglyceridemia by inducing adipogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Pioglitazone is a medication used in the management of diabetes mellitus, including in post-transplant patients, and its pharmacokinetics have been studied in those with impaired renal function.&lt;SEP&gt;Pioglitazone is a medication used in the management of diabetes mellitus, including in post-transplant patients, and its pharmacokinetics have been studied in those with impaired renal function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperphagia">
  <data key="d0">Hyperphagia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperphagia is a condition of excessive eating, often resulting from hypoleptinemia in patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoleptinemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypoleptinemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoleptinemia refers to low levels of leptin, contributing to metabolic dysregulation and hyperphagia in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Dose Insulin">
  <data key="d0">High-Dose Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-dose insulin, often exceeding 2 U/kg/day, is commonly required in lipodystrophy patients, posing challenges for administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Adipose Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Adipose Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous adipose tissue is nearly absent in lipodystrophy patients, complicating insulin injection due to limited injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous adipose tissue is progressively lost in acquired partial lipodystrophy, particularly in a cephalocaudal pattern in Barraquer-Simons syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Glargine U-300">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glargine U-300</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glargine U-300 is a more concentrated form of insulin that helps reduce injection volume in patients requiring high insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy treatment involves managing metabolic complications, with metreleptin being the only therapy shown to alter the disease's natural history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Loss">
  <data key="d0">Weight Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight loss is a side effect associated with SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 analogues, which may limit their use in underweight lipodystrophy patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss through healthy nutrition and physical activity is recommended for individuals with prediabetes to reduce diabetes risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss through healthy nutrition and physical activity is recommended to reduce progression from prediabetes to diabetes in people with HIV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofias">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodistrofias are a heterogeneous group of rare diseases involving adipose tissue, characterized by selective loss of body fat, insulin resistance, and associated comorbidities such as diabetes mellitus, hypertriglyceridemia, and fatty liver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dunnigan Variant">
  <data key="d0">Dunnigan Variant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dunnigan Variant is a familial partial lipodystrophy inherited in an autosomal dominant manner, presenting with fat loss in limbs and trunk and fat accumulation in the face, neck, and abdomen after puberty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Barraquer-Simon Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Barraquer-Simon Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Barraquer-Simon Syndrome is an acquired partial lipodystrophy that typically begins in childhood or adolescence, involving gradual fat loss in the face and upper body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Köbberling Variant">
  <data key="d0">Köbberling Variant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Köbberling Variant is a form of familial partial lipodystrophy described in 1975, associated with metabolic abnormalities including insulin resistance and dyslipidemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PPARG Mutation">
  <data key="d0">PPARG Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PPARG mutations are genetic alterations linked to familial partial lipodystrophy, affecting adipocyte differentiation and leading to abnormal fat distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PLIN1 Mutation">
  <data key="d0">PLIN1 Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PLIN1 mutations are associated with inherited partial lipodystrophy, disrupting lipid droplet regulation in adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKT2 Mutation">
  <data key="d0">AKT2 Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AKT2 mutations are linked to partial lipodystrophy and severe insulin resistance due to impaired insulin signaling pathways.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIDEC Mutation">
  <data key="d0">CIDEC Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CIDEC mutations are associated with familial partial lipodystrophy, affecting lipid storage and adipocyte function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mandibuloacral Dysplasia">
  <data key="d0">Mandibuloacral Dysplasia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mandibuloacral Dysplasia is a rare genetic disorder associated with partial or generalized lipodystrophy, skeletal abnormalities, and metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Mandibuloacral dysplasia (MAD) is a rare autosomal recessive syndrome characterized by skeletal abnormalities, progeroid features, and partial or generalized lipodystrophy, with two subtypes A and B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MDP Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">MDP Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MDP Syndrome is a rare genetic condition characterized by mandibular hypoplasia, deafness, and progeroid features, often associated with partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoinflammatory Syndromes">
  <data key="d0">Autoinflammatory Syndromes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoinflammatory Syndromes are conditions linked to lipodystrophy, involving chronic inflammation and metabolic disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SHORT Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">SHORT Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SHORT Syndrome is a rare genetic disorder featuring short stature, hyperextensibility, ocular depression, Rieger anomaly, and teething delay, often associated with partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch Syndrome is a neonatal progeroid form associated with generalized lipodystrophy, growth retardation, and metabolic abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atypical Progeroid Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Atypical Progeroid Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atypical Progeroid Syndrome is a condition with progeria-like features and partial or generalized lipodystrophy, often due to LMNA mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV-Related Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">HIV-Related Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV-Related Lipodystrophy is a form of acquired partial lipodystrophy occurring in patients undergoing antiretroviral therapy, characterized by abnormal fat redistribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Localized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Localized Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Localized Lipodystrophy refers to fat loss in specific body areas, often caused by improper insulin injections or other local factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emery-Dreifuss Muscular Dystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Emery-Dreifuss Muscular Dystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Emery-Dreifuss Muscular Dystrophy is a genetic disorder that may be associated with lipodystrophy, characterized by muscle wasting, contractures, and cardiac conduction defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fatty Liver">
  <data key="d0">Fatty Liver</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatty Liver, or hepatic steatosis, is a frequent complication of lipodystrophies due to severe insulin resistance and metabolic dysregulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Familial Partial Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Familial Partial Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Familial Partial Lipodystrophy is a genetic form of lipodystrophy inherited in an autosomal dominant or recessive manner, characterized by selective loss of subcutaneous fat from limbs and trunk, with fat accumulation in the face, neck, and abdomen, often leading to severe insulin resistance and metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Familial partial lipodystrophy (FPLD) is a genetic form of lipodystrophy, including the Dunnigan variant, caused by LMNA mutations and characterized by loss of subcutaneous fat from limbs and trunk.&lt;SEP&gt;Familial partial lipodystrophy is a genetic disorder characterized by progressive loss of subcutaneous fat from certain body regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccde7bd12284b1c344a961b0f935b651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acquired Partial Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Acquired Partial Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acquired Partial Lipodystrophy refers to a form of lipodystrophy that develops during life, not inherited, often triggered by autoimmune processes or other conditions, leading to progressive loss of fat in certain body regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquired partial lipodystrophy (APL) is a non-congenital, non-hereditary form of lipodystrophy occurring during life, often associated with autoimmune mechanisms and complement abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKT2">
  <data key="d0">AKT2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">AKT2 is a gene associated with missense heterozygous mutation (p.Arg274His) in patients with lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;AKT2 is a gene associated with partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIDEC">
  <data key="d0">CIDEC</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">CIDEC is a gene that encodes the homonymous protein, highly expressed in adipocytes during differentiation, involved in lipid droplet fusion, and linked to autosomal recessive congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LMNA">
  <data key="d0">LMNA</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">LMNA is a gene associated with mandibuloacral dysplasia type A and familial partial lipodystrophy (Dunnigan variant), affecting exons 8 to 10.&lt;SEP&gt;LMNA is a gene in which heterozygous mutations are a common cause of partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ZMPSTE24">
  <data key="d0">ZMPSTE24</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">ZMPSTE24 encodes a zinc-metalloproteinase involved in the post-translational proteolysis of prelamin A, with mutations causing mandibuloacral dysplasia type B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LMNB2">
  <data key="d0">LMNB2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">LMNB2 encodes lamin B2, with heterozygous alterations identified in some patients with acquired partial lipodystrophy, though not yet confirmed as causative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prelamin A">
  <data key="d0">Prelamin A</data>
  <data key="d1">protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Prelamin A is a precursor protein whose accumulation, due to ZMPSTE24 mutations, is suggested as an underlying mechanism in mandibuloacral dysplasia type B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamin B2">
  <data key="d0">Lamin B2</data>
  <data key="d1">protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamin B2 is a nuclear structural protein encoded by LMNB2, potentially linked to acquired partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C3 Convertase">
  <data key="d0">C3 Convertase</data>
  <data key="d1">enzyme</data>
  <data key="d2">C3 convertase is an enzyme in the complement system that is stabilized by the C3 nephritic factor, an autoantibody found in some patients with acquired partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C3 Nephritic Factor">
  <data key="d0">C3 Nephritic Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">autoantibody</data>
  <data key="d2">C3 nephritic factor is an autoantibody that inhibits the degradation of C3 convertase, associated with autoimmune mechanisms in acquired partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complement C3">
  <data key="d0">Complement C3</data>
  <data key="d1">protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Complement C3 is a component of the immune system found at reduced serum levels in patients with acquired partial lipodystrophy, indicating possible autoimmune etiology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mandibuloacral Dysplasia Type A">
  <data key="d0">Mandibuloacral Dysplasia Type A</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Mandibuloacral dysplasia type A is caused by LMNA mutations, presents with severe progeroid features, partial or generalized fat loss, and may lead to premature mortality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mandibuloacral Dysplasia Type B">
  <data key="d0">Mandibuloacral Dysplasia Type B</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Mandibuloacral dysplasia type B is caused by ZMPSTE24 mutations, characterized by early skeletal defects, progeroid appearance, calcified subcutaneous nodules, and absence of reported diabetes cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Barraquer-Simons Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Barraquer-Simons Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Barraquer-Simons syndrome is the most known form of non-HIV acquired partial lipodystrophy, characterized by cephalocaudal, symmetric fat loss sparing abdominal and lower limb fat, predominantly affecting women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipocyte">
  <data key="d0">Adipocyte</data>
  <data key="d1">cell</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipocytes are fat cells where CIDEC is highly expressed during differentiation and are targeted in lipodystrophy due to genetic or autoimmune destruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipid Droplet">
  <data key="d0">Lipid Droplet</data>
  <data key="d1">cellularstructure</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipid droplets are intracellular structures that store fat; CIDEC plays a role in their fusion into larger droplets in adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multilocular Small Lipid Droplets">
  <data key="d0">Multilocular Small Lipid Droplets</data>
  <data key="d1">cellularstructure</data>
  <data key="d2">Multilocular small lipid droplets are observed in the histopathological analysis of adipose tissue from patients with CIDEC mutations, indicating impaired lipid droplet fusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visceral Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Visceral Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d1">tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Visceral adiposity refers to fat stored within the abdominal cavity and is metabolically harmful compared to lower-body subcutaneous fat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peripheral Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Peripheral Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d1">tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Peripheral adiposity, particularly in the lower body, is preserved in Barraquer-Simons syndrome and is associated with beneficial metabolic effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glomerulonephritis">
  <data key="d0">Glomerulonephritis</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Glomerulonephritis, specifically membranoproliferative type, is a renal complication observed in some patients with Barraquer-Simons syndrome, often associated with early onset of fat loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drusen">
  <data key="d0">Drusen</data>
  <data key="d1">pathologicaldeposit</data>
  <data key="d2">Drusen are yellow or white extracellular deposits in the eyes, found in some patients with Barraquer-Simons syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640786</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV">
  <data key="d0">HIV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV is a virus that causes immunodeficiency and leads to a range of metabolic complications, particularly in individuals undergoing antiretroviral therapy. One of the notable conditions associated with HIV is acquired lipodystrophy, which manifests as abnormal fat distribution and is most prevalent among patients receiving certain antiretroviral drugs. This therapy-related complication underscores the complex interplay between HIV treatment and metabolic health.

HIV infection is also linked to an increased risk of developing prediabetes and diabetes. Multiple descriptions emphasize that individuals with HIV, especially those on antiretroviral therapy, face heightened metabolic disturbances that elevate their susceptibility to glucose metabolism disorders. As a result, clinical guidelines recommend that people with HIV be considered for routine diabetes screening. Fasting glucose testing is particularly advised before initiating or modifying antiretroviral regimens to accurately assess diabetes risk.

Furthermore, HIV affects the reliability of standard diagnostic markers for diabetes. The virus, particularly when treated with specific antiretroviral agents, alters the correlation between A1C levels and actual blood glucose concentrations. This discrepancy can compromise the accuracy of A1C as a diagnostic tool in this population, necessitating the use of alternative measures such as fasting glucose for more reliable diabetes detection. Collectively, these factors highlight the importance of tailored metabolic monitoring in the management of people living with HIV.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection is a condition associated with altered A1C and glucose level correlations, potentially affecting diabetes diagnosis accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV, when treated with certain antiretroviral drugs, is associated with altered A1C reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;People with HIV are at increased risk for diabetes and prediabetes and should be screened with fasting glucose before and after changes in antiretroviral therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;People with HIV are identified as a group that should be considered for diabetes testing due to potential metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is a condition that increases the risk of prediabetes and diabetes, especially in individuals on antiretroviral therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is a condition that increases the risk of prediabetes and diabetes, particularly in individuals undergoing antiretroviral therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5fc9e82121669cb9d4aff08c8c9019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647291</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Protease Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823</data>
  <data key="d2">Protease inhibitors increase hepatic VLDL production, leading to hypertriglyceridemia and other lipid abnormalities in patients with HIV-associated lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease inhibitors are antiretroviral medications used in HIV treatment that may interfere with A1C accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease inhibitors, such as ritonavir and lopinavir, are antiretroviral drugs associated with the development of HIV-related lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease inhibitors are antiretroviral medications used in HIV treatment that may interfere with A1C accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease Inhibitors are antiretroviral agents used in the treatment of HIV that are linked to insulin resistance and higher incidence of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease Inhibitors are antiretroviral agents used in the treatment of HIV that are linked to insulin resistance and higher incidence of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Protease Inhibitors are antiretroviral agents used in the treatment of HIV that are linked to insulin resistance and higher incidence of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoimmune Disease">
  <data key="d0">Autoimmune Disease</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d2">The presence of autoimmune disease supports the diagnosis of acquired generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Codon 482">
  <data key="d0">Codon 482</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d2">The majority of Lipodystrophy Partial Familial Type 2 cases are due to mutations at codon 482 of the LMNA gene, involving substitution of arginine by glutamine, leucine, or tryptophan.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640998</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipocyte Differentiation">
  <data key="d0">Adipocyte Differentiation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d2">PPARγ is a key transcription factor that regulates adipocyte differentiation through gene expression control.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exon 1">
  <data key="d0">Exon 1</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d2">Rare mutations in exon 1 of the LMNA gene are associated with cardiomyopathy, arrhythmias, and early-onset congestive heart failure in LPF patients.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776640999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Signaling">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Signaling</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d2">The AKT2 protein is a key mediator in the post-receptor insulin signaling pathway, primarily active in insulin-sensitive tissues.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triglyceride Storage">
  <data key="d0">Triglyceride Storage</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d2">Perilipin 1 plays a critical role in regulating triglyceride storage and the release of free fatty acids from lipid droplets.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cirrhosis">
  <data key="d0">Cirrhosis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic steatosis may progress to cirrhosis in advanced lipodystrophy, contributing to mortality.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gastrointestinal Bleeding">
  <data key="d0">Gastrointestinal Bleeding</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d2">Cirrhosis in lipodystrophy can lead to gastrointestinal bleeding, a major cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofia Parcial Familiar">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofia Parcial Familiar</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d2">The Köbberling Variant is a form of familial partial lipodystrophy described in 1975, related to the Dunnigan Variant.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofias Parciais Herdadas">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofias Parciais Herdadas</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutations in the PLIN1 gene are linked to inherited partial lipodystrophies.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofias Generalizadas">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofias Generalizadas</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d2">Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch Syndrome is a form of neonatal progeria associated with generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofias Parciais Adquiridas">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofias Parciais Adquiridas</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV-Related Lipodystrophy is a subtype of acquired partial lipodystrophy linked to antiretroviral therapy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641044</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofias Parciais Familiares">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofias Parciais Familiares</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c072c5ad49b2fb7ef54c9a2fe121badb</data>
  <data key="d2">Dyslipidemia, including hypertriglyceridemia, is a hallmark of familial partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641046</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringes And Needles">
  <data key="d0">Syringes And Needles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringes and needles are used medical devices in diabetes care that must be disposed of safely due to risk of injury and disease transmission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharps Waste Container">
  <data key="d0">Sharps Waste Container</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A sharps waste container is a rigid, wide-mouthed box with a lid designed specifically for the safe collection of used needles, lancets, and other sharp medical waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Blood-Contaminated Items">
  <data key="d0">Used Blood-Contaminated Items</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Other items that are sharp or contaminated with blood from diabetes care must be treated as hazardous waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Health Unit">
  <data key="d0">Basic Health Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Basic Health Unit (UBS) provides free sharps waste containers and accepts filled containers for safe disposal, with availability and procedures varying by city.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Supply Stores">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Supply Stores</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical supply stores are retail locations where sharps waste containers can be bought for safe disposal of used diabetes care materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Contamination">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Contamination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental contamination is a risk when sharps and blood-contaminated materials from diabetes care are improperly discarded in regular trash.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disease Transmission">
  <data key="d0">Disease Transmission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disease transmission, such as hepatitis, can occur if used needles and lancets are not disposed of properly, posing risks to others.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public Safety">
  <data key="d0">Public Safety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Public safety is enhanced by proper disposal of sharps, protecting sanitation and healthcare workers, families, and communities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resistant Bag">
  <data key="d0">Resistant Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A resistant bag is a stronger secondary container used to carry a sealed plastic bag with a filled sharps waste container.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
