  <data key="d5">1776644200</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Société Francophone du Diabète">
  <data key="d0">Société Francophone du Diabète</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Société Francophone du Diabète (SFD) is a French diabetes society that issues clinical guidelines for the management of diabetes, including recommendations for insulin delivery methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eed9228bfdd30fe45392a8a9fb8d106b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641704</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Diabetes Federation">
  <data key="d0">International Diabetes Federation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is a global organization dedicated to advancing diabetes care, prevention, and research worldwide. It serves as a leading authority in setting international standards for diabetes management and plays a pivotal role in shaping clinical guidelines, particularly in areas such as pediatric and adolescent diabetes care, as well as type 2 diabetes management in primary care settings. The IDF is widely recognized for publishing key resources, including the comprehensive "Diabetes Atlas," which provides global epidemiological data on diabetes prevalence, and "Understanding Insulin," an educational publication that supports effective insulin use.

In addition to its research and publication efforts, the International Diabetes Federation is deeply committed to education and advocacy. It offers extensive resources and information on diabetes management, with a strong focus on insulin therapy, patient education, and practical guidance for healthcare providers. Through its global network, the IDF promotes awareness, supports policy development, and advocates for improved access to care and treatment for people living with diabetes. By combining scientific rigor with public health initiatives, the International Diabetes Federation continues to influence diabetes care standards and practices across diverse healthcare systems.&lt;SEP&gt;International Diabetes Federation is a global organization that defines classifications and criteria for diabetes and intermediate hyperglycemic states.&lt;SEP&gt;International Diabetes Federation is a global organization that defines classifications and criteria for diabetes and intermediate hyperglycemic states.&lt;SEP&gt;A International Diabetes Federation é uma organização que fornece recomendações para o manejo do diabetes tipo 2 na atenção primária, disponibilizadas em formato digital.&lt;SEP&gt;International Diabetes Federation is a global organization that defines classifications and criteria for diabetes and intermediate hyperglycemic states.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Diabetes Federation published a global guideline for managing older people with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eed9228bfdd30fe45392a8a9fb8d106b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce486bcdf26ccc2a6ad63d018a57c974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7841f818e5dcdd6ef3c0c2951cf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4d53f9928520ac64a197b59db6862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3628fc721a312bfbaace1de3a4d877</data>
