<node id="Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An insulin infusion pump is a medical device used to deliver insulin continuously and in bolus doses to patients with diabetes, particularly type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin infusion pump is a medical device that delivers insulin continuously and allows for programmed bolus doses based on user input.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin infusion pump is a medical device used for continuous insulin delivery in diabetes management, varying by model in functions, alarms, and control mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin infusion pump is a medical device used to deliver continuous insulin to patients with diabetes, with advancements improving glycemic control and reducing hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin infusion pump is a medical device used for continuous insulin delivery, including basal and bolus dosing, with variations in design and functionality across models.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin infusion pump is a medical device that delivers insulin continuously and is sometimes integrated with CGM sensors.</data>
