<node id="Diabetes Technology">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Technology refers to the broad field encompassing hardware, devices, software, and digital tools designed to assist individuals with diabetes in managing blood glucose levels, preventing complications, and improving overall quality of life. Central to this domain are medical devices such as continuous glucose monitors (CGMs), flash glucose monitoring systems, insulin pumps, automated insulin delivery systems (also known as closed-loop or artificial pancreas systems), and smart insulin pens. These technologies enable real-time glucose tracking, precise insulin dosing, and data-driven decision-making, offering significant benefits in diabetes care, particularly for individuals with type 1 diabetes, including children and adolescents.

In addition to hardware, diabetes technology incorporates connected devices and digital health platforms, including mobile applications and decision support systems, that facilitate remote monitoring, data sharing, and personalized treatment adjustments. These integrated solutions aim to streamline self-management, enhance treatment adherence, and reduce the burden of diabetes care. However, despite their advantages, challenges remain, including issues related to system complexity, data security, user training, and disparities in accessibility and affordability across different populations.

It is important to note that "Diabetes Technology" also refers to a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to publishing research on technological innovations and clinical trials in diabetes care. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating findings on new devices, software applications, and clinical outcomes, contributing to the advancement of evidence-based practices in the field. Thus, the term encompasses both the practical tools used in patient care and the scholarly efforts to evaluate and improve these technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8085de73bd4812f966c059205e5d3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4ef00b7799130b85ed6433c381dfef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8651ec88cb5333f03b8af01fee4d3cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c7e3d6615d1076ae20653358419ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0524115c9e0c2a0ed35c413e50c658e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643636</data>
