<node id="Infusion Set">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion set includes the catheter and cannula used to deliver insulin from the pump to the subcutaneous tissue and must be changed regularly.&lt;SEP&gt;An infusion set is a component of an insulin pump system that delivers insulin into the body and should be changed every 48 to 72 hours to prevent infection.&lt;SEP&gt;The infusion set is a component of the SICI system that delivers insulin from the pump to the patient’s body and requires regular replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;An infusion set is a component of an insulin pump system that delivers insulin through a cannula under the skin, and issues with it can lead to complications such as DKA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catheter Site Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Catheter Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Catheter site rotation is a recommended practice to prevent complications such as lipodystrophy by regularly changing the location of the infusion catheter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Nodule">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Nodule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A subcutaneous nodule is a physical side effect observed in 62% of patients using insulin infusion, likely related to local tissue reaction at the infusion site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641718</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erythema">
  <data key="d0">Erythema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erythema is a skin reaction observed in 66% of patients at the infusion site, indicating localized inflammation or irritation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641719</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scar Less Than 3 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Scar Less Than 3 Mm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scar less than 3 mm in size was observed in 94% of pediatric patients using insulin infusion, indicating minimal scarring in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infection Rate">
  <data key="d0">Infection Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The infection rate associated with insulin infusion is 0.06 per patient-year, indicating a low but present risk of site infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Suspension Pump">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Suspension Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A low glucose suspension pump is a type of insulin pump that automatically stops basal insulin delivery when blood glucose levels drop to a critical threshold, preventing severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Low Glucose Suspension Pump">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Low Glucose Suspension Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A predictive low glucose suspension pump uses glucose trend data to anticipate hypoglycemia and suspend insulin delivery before low glucose levels occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641720</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Insulin Analog</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-acting insulin analogs such as lispro, aspart, and glulisine are used in insulin pumps due to their early peak and predictable absorption, reducing the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin analogs such as insulin aspart and insulin lispro are used in insulin pumps and are associated with low risk of hypoglycemia and improved postprandial glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin analogs, such as insulin lispro and aspart, are used in SICI systems and are preferred over glulisine due to better performance and reduced complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Aspart">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Aspart</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin aspart is a rapid-acting insulin analog used in insulin pump therapy and is considered safe for use in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin aspart is a rapid-acting insulin analog used as prandial insulin in combination with long-acting insulins in basal-bolus regimens for type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin aspart is a rapid-acting insulin analog used in the management of type 1 diabetes, administered either preprandially or postprandially.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin aspart is a rapid-acting insulin analog used in the management of type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin aspart is a rapid-acting insulin analog used to control blood glucose levels, delivered via pen or vial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Glulisine">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glulisine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glulisine is a rapid-acting insulin analog whose use is not recommended in pump therapy due to insufficient safety data.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glulisine is a rapid-acting insulin analog used in SICI, though less preferred due to higher risk of occlusion compared to lispro or aspart.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AACE/ACE">
  <data key="d0">AACE/ACE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists/American College of Endocrinology (AACE/ACE) provides guidelines for the use of insulin pump therapy in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641722</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Ketoacidosis">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Ketoacidosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) is a serious and potentially life-threatening complication of diabetes, most commonly associated with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus. It arises from a severe deficiency of insulin, which prevents the body from utilizing glucose for energy, leading to hyperglycemia, the breakdown of fat for fuel, and the subsequent accumulation of ketone bodies. This metabolic shift results in metabolic acidosis, electrolyte imbalances, and systemic physiological disruption, defining DKA as an acute metabolic emergency. The condition is frequently marked by elevated blood glucose levels and the presence of ketones, making it a critical concern in both the onset and ongoing management of diabetes.

DKA is often observed at the initial presentation of Type 1 Diabetes, particularly in children and adolescents, where it may serve as the first clinical manifestation of the disease. It is a common diagnostic feature across pediatric and adult populations and has been widely studied in diverse demographic and geographic settings. The acute nature of DKA at diagnosis underscores the importance of early recognition and intervention in undiagnosed diabetes cases.

In addition to its role as an initial presentation, DKA can also occur in individuals with established diabetes, especially when insulin delivery is disrupted. This is particularly relevant for patients using insulin pump therapy or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII), where mechanical failures—such as infusion set blockages or pump malfunctions—can rapidly precipitate DKA due to interrupted insulin supply. Consequently, reliable insulin administration is crucial in preventing this complication. Treatment for DKA typically involves prompt intravenous insulin therapy, fluid replacement, and electrolyte management to correct the acidotic state and restore metabolic stability. Given its severity and potential for fatal outcomes, timely medical intervention is essential in all cases of DKA.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a life-threatening condition that can occur at the time of diabetes diagnosis and its frequency is reduced by type 1 diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a serious complication of diabetes caused by a lack of insulin, leading to high blood acidity and ketone accumulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a life-threatening condition that can occur at the time of diabetes diagnosis and its frequency is reduced by type 1 diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a serious complication of diabetes caused by a lack of insulin, leading to high blood acidity and ketone accumulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a life-threatening condition that can occur at the time of diabetes diagnosis and its frequency is reduced by type 1 diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis is a serious complication of diabetes caused by a lack of insulin, leading to high blood acidity and ketone accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1abe83ba7814c7afe7a123e2f79a10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc6a5cedffa24f9a3134770cf1526b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c37422889250d7e58837deb17406d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-620e2d1316d6093170f1c9991caabc7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morning Phenomenon">
  <data key="d0">Morning Phenomenon</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The morning phenomenon refers to elevated blood glucose levels in the early morning due to hormonal changes, a condition that may indicate the need for insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641722</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta Cell">
  <data key="d0">Beta Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta cells in the pancreas produce insulin, and their reduced function in long-standing diabetes may justify the use of insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OpT2mise Trial">
  <data key="d0">OpT2mise Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The OpT2mise trial was a major clinical study demonstrating that CSII is more effective than MDI in reducing HbA1c levels in poorly controlled type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catheter Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Catheter Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Catheter obstruction is a common malfunction in insulin pumps, leading to partial or complete blockage of insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pump Malfunction">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pump Malfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin pump malfunction includes technical failures such as catheter blockage or battery issues, requiring immediate corrective action with alternative insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641723</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychiatric Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Psychiatric Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychiatric disorders such as anorexia nervosa and bulimia are contraindications for insulin pump therapy due to risks of improper insulin management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Estimation">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Estimation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate estimation is a method used by patients to calculate insulin bolus doses, and errors in estimation can lead to poor glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pozzilli P">
  <data key="d0">Pozzilli P</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pozzilli P is an author referenced in the text for a 2016 publication related to insulin therapy in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Pozzilli P is a co-author of a study on the safety, efficacy, and pharmacoeconomics of continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin bolus calculation is a process used by patients on insulin pump therapy to determine the correct dose based on carbohydrate intake and current blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Blood Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Blood Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary blood glucose measurement is a required self-monitoring practice for patients using insulin pump therapy to ensure safe and effective insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Failure">
  <data key="d0">Battery Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery failure is a potential cause of insulin pump malfunction, requiring immediate intervention to prevent treatment interruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641725</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Society For Pediatric Endocrinology">
  <data key="d0">European Society For Pediatric Endocrinology</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Society For Pediatric Endocrinology is a medical society involved in developing consensus statements on insulin pump therapy for pediatric patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641725</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Society For Pediatric And Adolescent Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">International Society For Pediatric And Adolescent Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes (ISPAD) apoia o uso de bomba de insulina em crianças e adolescentes, alinhada à posição da ADA.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Society For Pediatric And Adolescent Diabetes is a global organization that contributed to a consensus statement on insulin pump therapy for young patients.&lt;SEP&gt;A global organization providing clinical practice guidelines for diabetes in children and adolescents, including monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Control And Complications Trial Research Group">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Control And Complications Trial Research Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Control And Complications Trial Research Group conducted research on hypoglycemia in diabetes treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial Research Group conducted research on the effects of intensive diabetes treatment on long-term complications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial Research Group conducted a study on intensive diabetes treatment in Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6dadde3434f68ef74ebdf23be6a24ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Association For The Study Of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">European Association For The Study Of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Association For The Study Of Diabetes endorsed a consensus statement on insulin pump therapy in pediatric patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD) is a professional organization focused on diabetes research and care, and co-authored a position statement with the ADA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689290</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimed 670G Hybrid Closed-Loop System">
  <data key="d0">Minimed 670G Hybrid Closed-Loop System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Minimed 670G Hybrid Closed-Loop System is an integrated insulin pump and glucose monitoring technology used in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddf3203a55511f7874bc210d61b3ccfa</data>
