<node id="Bergenstal Rm">
  <data key="d0">Bergenstal Rm</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bergenstal RM is a prominent diabetes specialist and lead researcher whose work spans multiple facets of diabetes management, including advanced technologies, clinical guidelines, and therapeutic interventions. He has played a key role in studies evaluating the effectiveness of sensor-augmented insulin-pump therapy for individuals with type 1 diabetes, contributing to the growing body of evidence supporting the use of integrated diabetes technologies. His research extends to establishing clinical targets for glucose monitoring, particularly through involvement in the International Consensus on Time in Range, which aims to standardize metrics for glycemic control and improve patient outcomes.

Bergenstal RM has been actively involved in major clinical trials, including the EDITION 4 trial investigating insulin glargine, a long-acting insulin analog used in diabetes treatment. His contributions to the T1D Exchange Clinic Network further underscore his engagement with real-world data and collaborative research efforts focused on type 1 diabetes. Through this network, he has contributed to studies on blood glucose monitoring practices and outcomes, helping to inform clinical decision-making and patient care strategies.

In addition to his clinical research, Bergenstal RM has co-authored influential position statements on diabetes management, notably the patient-centered approach to managing hyperglycemia in type 2 diabetes. This work emphasizes individualized care, taking into account patient preferences, comorbidities, and treatment goals. He is also recognized as an author in studies on advanced diabetes technologies and insulin delivery systems, reflecting his broad expertise in both technological innovation and therapeutic optimization. Collectively, Bergenstal RM’s contributions have significantly advanced the understanding and management of diabetes across multiple domains.</data>
