  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Commission for the Incorporation of Technologies into SUS">
  <data key="d0">National Commission for the Incorporation of Technologies into SUS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Commission for the Incorporation of Technologies into SUS (CONITEC) advises the Brazilian Ministry of Health on health technology incorporation, including the evaluation of CSII for public healthcare coverage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Health System">
  <data key="d0">Unified Health System</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unified Health System (SUS) is Brazil's public healthcare system responsible for providing therapeutic assistance and incorporating health technologies based on CONITEC recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacoeconomics">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacoeconomics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacoeconomics involves the evaluation of the cost-effectiveness of medical treatments, such as comparing CSII and MDI in terms of clinical benefits and economic burden.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Machine Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine dysfunction refers to operational failures in insulin delivery devices that may affect treatment efficacy and patient safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Site Problems">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Site Problems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion site problems are complications arising from the location where insulin is delivered, potentially impacting treatment outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Waste">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin waste refers to the loss or inefficient use of insulin, along with plastic and battery waste, associated with insulin pump usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality of Life">
  <data key="d0">Quality of Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality of life is a patient-centered outcome influenced by diabetes management methods, including the use of advanced technologies like insulin pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pumping Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Pumping Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pumping procedures refer to the operational protocols involved in using insulin pumps, including setup, maintenance, and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Infusion Accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Infusion Accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin infusion accuracy refers to the precision with which insulin pumps deliver prescribed doses, a critical factor in effective diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ethical Considerations">
  <data key="d0">Ethical Considerations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethical considerations in diabetes care involve balancing patient autonomy in choosing advanced technologies against the associated costs and resource allocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemedicine">
  <data key="d0">Telemedicine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Telemedicine is a healthcare delivery approach using digital communication for remote patient monitoring and consultation, increasingly relevant in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Software">
  <data key="d0">Medical Software</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical software refers to digital applications used in clinical settings and by patients for managing diabetes, including bolus calculators and glucose tracking tools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Severe Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Severe Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe hypoglycemia is a dangerous complication of diabetes treatment that studies suggest may be reduced with the use of CSII.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe hypoglycemia is a dangerous drop in blood glucose requiring assistance, used as a primary or secondary outcome in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe hypoglycemia is a dangerous drop in blood glucose that can require assistance; pump therapy has been shown to reduce its rates in children.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe hypoglycemia is a dangerous form of low blood sugar requiring assistance, with evidence showing insulin pumps reduce its occurrence compared to MDI.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe hypoglycemia is a dangerous drop in blood glucose levels requiring external assistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc6a5cedffa24f9a3134770cf1526b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microvascular Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Microvascular Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microvascular outcomes refer to long-term complications such as retinopathy and nephropathy that may correlate with glycemic variability and time in range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Care Costs">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Care Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency care costs are healthcare expenditures associated with acute diabetic decompensation, considered in pharmacoeconomic analyses of diabetes treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospitalization Costs">
  <data key="d0">Hospitalization Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospitalization costs are financial burdens linked to inpatient treatment for diabetes-related complications, relevant in long-term cost-benefit assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Work and School Absenteeism">
  <data key="d0">Work and School Absenteeism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Work and school absenteeism refers to days lost due to diabetes complications, an indirect cost factor in evaluating treatment impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CONITEC">
  <data key="d0">CONITEC</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CONITEC is the acronym for the National Commission for the Incorporation of Technologies into SUS, responsible for evaluating and recommending health technologies for inclusion in Brazil's public healthcare system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic é uma empresa fabricante de bombas de infusão de insulina no Brasil, responsável pelos modelos MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754, MiniMed 722 e MiniMed® 640G.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic é um fabricante de bombas de insulina, comparado em estudo com outros fornecedores quanto à eficácia no controle da HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is a medical device company and the source of the "Lag time" figure referenced in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is a medical technology company that produces the MiniMed 640G and 670G insulin pumps with integrated CGM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Omnipod">
  <data key="d0">Omnipod</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Omnipod é um fabricante de bombas de insulina, incluído em estudo comparativo sobre desempenho em redução da HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Animas">
  <data key="d0">Animas</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Animas é um fabricante de bombas de insulina incluído na análise comparativa com outros dispositivos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leelarathna Et Al.">
  <data key="d0">Leelarathna Et Al.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo publicado em 2017 por Leelarathna et al. que compara diferentes fabricantes de bombas de insulina quanto à redução da HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Institute For Health And Care Excellence">
  <data key="d0">National Institute For Health And Care Excellence</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">O National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) tem indicações restritivas para o uso de SICI, limitando-o a pacientes com mau controle glicêmico ou hipoglicemia grave sob MDI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Societé Francophone Du Diabète">
  <data key="d0">Societé Francophone Du Diabète</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Societé Francophone du Diabète (SFD) recomenda o uso de SICI em pacientes com HbA1c elevada, hipoglicemia recorrente, variabilidade glicêmica, necessidades variáveis de insulina, alergia à insulina ou impacto negativo do MDI na qualidade de vida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mellitus tipo 2 (DM2) é uma condição em que o SICI pode ser indicado em casos de falha no tratamento com MDI, resistência à insulina ou altas doses necessárias.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a form of diabetes mellitus characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, commonly associated with obesity and lifestyle factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a form of diabetes mellitus characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, commonly associated with obesity and lifestyle factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a form of diabetes mellitus characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, commonly associated with obesity and lifestyle factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 é uma forma de diabetes em que o corpo se torna resistente à insulina ou não produz insulina suficiente, frequentemente associada a fatores de estilo de vida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Múltiplas Doses De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Múltiplas Doses De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Múltiplas doses de insulina (MDI) é uma terapia intensiva para diabetes que envolve administração frequente de insulina, associada a maior risco de hipoglicemia severa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qualidade De Vida">
  <data key="d0">Qualidade De Vida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A qualidade de vida é um aspecto melhorado com o uso de SICI, especialmente devido ao menor risco de hipoglicemia e maior controle glicêmico.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabelas 5, 6 E 7">
  <data key="d0">Tabelas 5, 6 E 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">As Tabelas 5, 6 e 7 compilam diretrizes de sociedades de diabetes sobre as indicações para o uso de bomba de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pozzilli">
  <data key="d0">Pozzilli</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pozzilli é o autor ou fonte da adaptação das Tabelas 5, 6 e 7 que contêm recomendações sobre o uso de SICI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Total Diária">
  <data key="d0">Dose Total Diária</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Total Diária (DTD) refers to the total daily insulin dose administered to a patient, a metric used to assess treatment intensity and adjust therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Paradigm Veo 754">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Paradigm Veo 754</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed Paradigm Veo 754 is an insulin infusion pump that emits hypoglycemia alerts and automatically shuts off when necessary, featuring operational functions such as basal rate profiles and bolus types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 640G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 640G is an insulin pump that provides hypoglycemia alerts and automatic pump shutdown, with features including multiple basal rate profiles and bolus calculation support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek Spirit">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek Spirit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Accu-Chek Spirit is an insulin pump system with specific configuration settings including basal rate profiles, bolus types, and remote control functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek Spirit Combo">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek Spirit Combo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Accu-Chek Spirit Combo is an insulin pump system that includes integrated features such as bolus advisor functionality and specific insulin delivery settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patch Pump">
  <data key="d0">Patch Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A patch pump is a type of insulin infusion pump that operates wirelessly and can be used in water, eliminating the need for connecting tubes.&lt;SEP&gt;Patch pumps are wireless insulin infusion devices without tubing, integrated near the skin, disposable, pre-filled with insulin for 2–3 days, and controlled remotely.&lt;SEP&gt;A patch pump is a type of insulin pump that adheres directly to the skin and is used to minimize hydrostatic effects and disconnection risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A wearable insulin delivery device that adheres to the skin and administers insulin without tubing, available in various models with differing capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d6904368d45b0f9532b36061a00e7c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CareLink">
  <data key="d0">CareLink</data>
  <data key="d1">software</data>
  <data key="d2">CareLink is software used with MiniMed insulin pumps to manage and analyze insulin delivery data and patient settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek Connect">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek Connect</data>
  <data key="d1">software</data>
  <data key="d2">Accu-Chek Connect is software associated with Accu-Chek insulin pump systems for managing insulin delivery and bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus calculation is a function performed by insulin pump software using patient-input data such as blood glucose and carbohydrate intake to suggest insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Insulin Analogs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-acting insulin analogs, including lispro, aspart, and glulisine, are the preferred insulins used in insulin infusion pumps for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid-acting insulin analogs are prandial insulins with a faster onset of action, used to control postprandial glucose levels in Diabetes Mellitus Type 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88336f998ca464e0ed477249555b3e44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1abe83ba7814c7afe7a123e2f79a10a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arnold Kadish">
  <data key="d0">Arnold Kadish</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Arnold Kadish é o médico que desenvolveu o primeiro sistema de infusão contínua de insulina na década de 1960.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tecido Celular Subcutâneo">
  <data key="d0">Tecido Celular Subcutâneo</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">O tecido celular subcutâneo é a camada de tecido onde a cânula do sistema de infusão é inserida para administração de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed® 640G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed® 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">O MiniMed® 640G é um modelo de bomba de insulina comercializado no Brasil pela Medtronic, à prova d'água e capaz de se conectar a sensores de glicose, com função de alerta e desligamento automático em casos de hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek® Spirit">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek® Spirit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">O Accu-Chek® Spirit é um modelo de bomba de insulina oferecido pela Roche Diagnostics, utilizado no tratamento do diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">O Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo é um sistema que combina a bomba de insulina com um smart control contendo glicosímetro e cálculo de bolus, fornecido pela Roche Diagnostics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">O MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754 é um modelo de bomba de insulina da Medtronic que emite alertas de hipoglicemia e desliga automaticamente quando necessário.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 722">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 722</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">O MiniMed 722 é um modelo de bomba de insulina da Medtronic que pode ser usado com sensores de glicose, embora já não seja comercializado atualmente.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roche Diagnostics">
  <data key="d0">Roche Diagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Roche Diagnostics é uma empresa fabricante de bombas de infusão de insulina, responsável pelos modelos Accu-Chek® Spirit e Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo no Brasil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba79a92f9b31fdbcd854ba496c498efb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SICI">
  <data key="d0">SICI</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SICI stands for Sistema de Infusão Contínua de Insulina (Continuous Insulin Infusion System), a method used for insulin delivery in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;SICI refers to sensor-augmented insulin pump therapy, a method used in the management of diabetes, particularly for achieving better metabolic control and reducing hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b712afd345ff5f7503205905d3131f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin bolus is a dose of insulin given to cover carbohydrates in meals or to correct hyperglycemia, delivered via insulin pump or injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin bolus refers to the dose of insulin administered to cover carbohydrate intake during meals, which may be miscalculated or forgotten by patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Intake Estimation">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Intake Estimation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate intake estimation is the process of calculating the amount of carbohydrates consumed, which can be inaccurate and lead to poor glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Site">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Site</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion site is the location on the body where the insulin is delivered via the SICI system and is prone to complications such as irritation, infection, or lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrostatic Effects">
  <data key="d0">Hydrostatic Effects</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrostatic effects refer to changes in insulin delivery due to vertical positioning of the pump, causing under- or over-infusion when the pump is positioned above or below the infusion site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atmospheric Pressure Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Atmospheric Pressure Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduction in atmospheric pressure, such as during air travel, can cause bubble formation in the insulin pump, leading to inaccurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adhesive Allergy">
  <data key="d0">Adhesive Allergy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adhesive allergy refers to skin reactions caused by the adhesive used to secure the infusion set, resulting in discomfort and potential discontinuation of SICI use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Failure">
  <data key="d0">Pump Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump failure is a malfunction of the insulin pump that can lead to complete interruption of insulin delivery, occurring in approximately 25% of pumps per year.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump failure is a risk in insulin delivery systems, and users of DIY systems should have a backup plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Occlusion">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Occlusion</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion occlusion is a blockage in the infusion set that prevents insulin delivery, often caused by prolonged use of the catheter or insulin fibril formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Fibril Formation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Fibril Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin fibril formation refers to the development of isoelectric complexes (fibrils) in the insulin solution, which can cause occlusion and disrupt insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unplanned Disconnection">
  <data key="d0">Unplanned Disconnection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Unplanned disconnection occurs when the insulin pump is accidentally disconnected, leading to hyperglycemia or ketoacidosis if not promptly addressed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Planned Disconnection">
  <data key="d0">Planned Disconnection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Planned disconnection refers to intentional interruption of insulin infusion, where glucose levels rise at a rate of 1 mg/dL per minute if disconnected for more than 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pozzilli P et al.">
  <data key="d0">Pozzilli P et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pozzilli P et al. is the cited author of a study adapted in the description of complications related to SICI use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Catheter">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Catheter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion catheter is a part of the infusion set that delivers insulin into the subcutaneous tissue and should be replaced every 72 hours to prevent complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus refers to the dose of insulin delivered to correct high blood glucose or to cover carbohydrates in a meal, calculated using software in the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus refers to a dose of insulin administered to manage blood glucose levels, particularly around meals or to correct high glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Basal">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin basal is the background insulin delivered continuously to manage glucose levels between meals and during fasting periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Padrão">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Padrão</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Padrão is the standard bolus delivery method, where insulin is administered immediately at mealtime, requiring food intake within 15 to 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Estendido">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Estendido</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Estendido is an extended insulin delivery method, where a constant dose is released slowly over several hours, suitable for prolonged food intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Bifásico">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Bifásico</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Bifásico is a biphasic insulin delivery method combining an immediate bolus with an extended bolus to manage delayed glucose rises, especially after high-fat or mixed meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemia Pós-Prandial">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemia Pós-Prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemia pós-prandial refers to elevated blood glucose levels after meals, a key target for insulin bolus adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refeição Rica em Carboidrato">
  <data key="d0">Refeição Rica em Carboidrato</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refeição rica em carboidrato is a meal high in carbohydrates, requiring precise insulin bolus calculation for glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refeição Rica em Gordura">
  <data key="d0">Refeição Rica em Gordura</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refeição rica em gordura is a high-fat meal that causes delayed glucose elevation, often requiring bolus bifásico or extended insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Carb Diet">
  <data key="d0">Low Carb Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Low carb diet is a nutritional approach that limits carbohydrate intake, influencing insulin requirements and glucose patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion System">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion System (SICI) is a therapy that delivers insulin via a pump, simulating physiological insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fat-Insulin Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Fat-Insulin Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fat-Insulin Ratio (RGI) is a calculation used to determine the amount of insulin needed to cover calories from fat and protein, based on 100 kcal per 10 g of carbohydrate equivalent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate-Insulin Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate-Insulin Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate-Insulin Ratio (RIC) is the amount of insulin required to cover a specific amount of carbohydrates, used in bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial hypoglycemia refers to low blood glucose levels occurring after meals, a risk when insulin dosing is excessive or poorly timed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 4">
  <data key="d0">Table 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 4 presents the pharmacokinetic advantages of continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion system compared to multiple daily insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Factor">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity factor (SF) is a coefficient in CSII that indicates how much one unit of insulin lowers blood glucose, used in bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity Factor (FS) is the amount of blood glucose reduction in mg/dL per 1 unit of insulin, used to calculate correction bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin To Carbohydrate Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Insulin To Carbohydrate Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin to Carbohydrate Ratio (RIC) is the number of grams of carbohydrates covered by 1 unit of insulin, used to calculate mealtime bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Correction Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A correction bolus is the amount of insulin used to lower blood glucose levels to a pre-specified target before a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction bolus is the insulin dose calculated to lower elevated blood glucose levels to a target range before meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mealtime Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Mealtime Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealtime bolus is the insulin dose calculated based on the amount of carbohydrates to be consumed in a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Total Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total bolus is the sum of the correction bolus and the mealtime bolus, representing the total insulin dose administered before a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Total Dose">
  <data key="d0">Daily Total Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily Total Dose (DTD) is the total amount of insulin used per day, used as a basis for calculating basal and bolus insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 3">
  <data key="d0">Table 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 3 presents initial calculations for insulin pump configuration, including formulas for DTD, basal and bolus insulin, sensitivity factor, and insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1223db4d3629243420a6e867a9ba6988</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CARE">
  <data key="d0">CARE</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CARE is an acronym proposed as a strategy to help clinicians understand automated insulin delivery systems by addressing key questions about calculation and adjustment of insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;CARE is an acronym proposed as a strategy to help clinicians understand differences between automated insulin delivery systems by addressing four key questions: Calculate, Adjust, Revert, and Educate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b712afd345ff5f7503205905d3131f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calculate">
  <data key="d0">Calculate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Calculate is one component of the CARE framework, referring to how the system determines insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjust">
  <data key="d0">Adjust</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adjust is a component of the CARE framework, addressing how insulin doses are modified immediately and over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Revert">
  <data key="d0">Revert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Revert is part of the CARE framework, focusing on when to stop automated insulin delivery and return to pump settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Educate">
  <data key="d0">Educate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Educate is a component of the CARE framework, indicating where users can access educational resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776641768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Insulin Delivery System">
  <data key="d0">Automated Insulin Delivery System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An automated insulin delivery system is a medical device that administers insulin based on real-time glucose monitoring and algorithmic calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated insulin delivery (AID) system uses CGM-informed algorithms to modulate insulin delivery for improved diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated insulin delivery system integrates insulin pumps with glucose sensors to automatically adjust insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated insulin delivery (AID) systems adjust insulin delivery rates based on real-time sensor glucose values and are preferred over nonautomated pumps and MDI for people with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94e98f4cb6f97fceae5e6d8c30c871b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0524115c9e0c2a0ed35c413e50c658e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
