<node id="Insulin Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin pumps are medical devices used in diabetes management, recommended for integration with continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are medical devices that deliver continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion and are used in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are devices that deliver insulin continuously and are part of automated insulin delivery systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are medical devices used by individuals with diabetes to deliver insulin continuously and are recommended for continued use in inpatient settings when appropriate.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are medical devices used for insulin delivery in individuals with diabetes, particularly type 1 diabetes, to improve glycemic control and reduce risks of hypoglycemia and DKA.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are medical devices used for insulin delivery in people with type 1, type 2, or other forms of diabetes resulting in insulin deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8651ec88cb5333f03b8af01fee4d3cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ff5070c8f5a6109621d29aa2b13398</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
