<node id="Controle da Glicemia Pós-Prandial">
  <data key="d0">Controle da Glicemia Pós-Prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle da glicemia pós-prandial refere-se à regulação dos níveis de glicose no sangue após as refeições, sendo influenciado pelo tipo e momento de administração da insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema de Infusão Subcutânea Contínua de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Sistema de Infusão Subcutânea Contínua de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema de Infusão Subcutânea Contínua de Insulina (SICI), também conhecido como bomba de insulina, é um método de administração contínua de insulina que potencializa o efeito farmacocinético da insulina asparte ultrarrápida.&lt;SEP&gt;O sistema de infusão subcutânea contínua de insulina (SICI) é uma terapia recomendada para controle glicêmico adequado, especialmente quando a terapia com múltiplas aplicações de insulina não é eficaz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0733697cf2994b8b4b5add361db11a43</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crianças Pequenas">
  <data key="d0">Crianças Pequenas</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Crianças pequenas são um grupo etário no qual a insulina lispro mostrou benefícios na redução da hipoglicemia noturna e na flexibilidade de administração da insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Crianças pequenas são uma população especial com necessidades específicas de insulina, frequentemente abaixo de 0,5 U, tornando o SICI a opção terapêutica preferida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0733697cf2994b8b4b5add361db11a43</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adultos">
  <data key="d0">Adultos</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adultos são o grupo etário elegível para o uso da insulina inalável tecnosfera, que é aprovada apenas para indivíduos a partir de 18 anos.&lt;SEP&gt;Adultos necessitam de 0,7 U/kg/dia a 1,0 U/kg/dia de insulina e são elegíveis para o uso de insulina inalável tecnosfera a partir dos 18 anos.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults are a population group for whom CGM has demonstrated benefits in reducing Hb1Ac and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0733697cf2994b8b4b5add361db11a43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crossover Study">
  <data key="d0">Crossover Study</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A crossover study is a type of clinical trial design used to compare treatments, referenced in the open-label study evaluating insulin lispro and regular human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d0">Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin Analogs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra-long-acting insulin analogs, such as insulin glargine U300 and degludeca, offer extended duration of action, greater flexibility, and reduced incidence of hypoglycemia, especially nocturnal events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Glargine U100">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glargine U100</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glargine U100 is a long-acting insulin analog used for basal insulin therapy in people with type 1 diabetes, serving as a comparator in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Glargine U300">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glargine U300</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glargine U300 is an ultra-long-acting insulin analog that demonstrated non-inferiority to glargine U100 in HbA1c reduction and showed a lower incidence of nocturnal hypoglycemia in the initial weeks of treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Degludeca">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Degludeca</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin degludeca is an ultra-long-acting insulin analog that showed a 25% lower incidence of confirmed nocturnal hypoglycemia compared to insulin glargine U100 in a 52-week clinical trial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nocturnal Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Nocturnal Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nocturnal hypoglycemia refers to low blood glucose during sleep, a key safety concern in diabetes management, reduced with use of certain insulin analogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Nocturnal hypoglycemia is low blood sugar occurring during sleep, which sensor-augmented pumps have been shown to reduce.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EDITION 4 Study">
  <data key="d0">EDITION 4 Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The EDITION 4 study was a six-month, open-label, randomized clinical trial comparing insulin glargine U300 and U100 in people with type 1 diabetes, showing similar overall hypoglycemia rates but fewer nocturnal events with U300 in early treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BEGIN Basal-Bolus Type 1 Study">
  <data key="d0">BEGIN Basal-Bolus Type 1 Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The BEGIN Basal-Bolus Type 1 study was a 52-week, multicenter, open, treat-to-target clinical trial comparing insulin degludeca and glargine U100, finding similar HbA1c reduction but a 25% lower rate of nocturnal hypoglycemia with degludeca.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacokinetic Profile">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacokinetic Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The pharmacokinetic profile refers to how insulin is absorbed, distributed, and eliminated, contributing to the predictability of action in long-acting analogs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacodynamic Profile">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacodynamic Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The pharmacodynamic profile describes the insulin's effect on blood glucose over time, influencing the consistency and duration of glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children and Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Children and Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children and adolescents aged 5 to 16 years with type 1 diabetes showed improved fasting glycemic control and reduced severe and nocturnal hypoglycemia when treated with insulin glargine U100 compared to insulin NPH.&lt;SEP&gt;Children and adolescents are a population experiencing rising rates of type 2 diabetes, particularly in racial and ethnic minorities, warranting risk-based screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
