<node id="Nph Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Nph Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH insulin is an intermediate-acting insulin used in twice-daily regimens, compared with long-acting analogs like insulin detemir and glargine.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH insulin is an intermediate-acting basal insulin used in type 1 diabetes, compared with glargine for glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Human Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Regular Human Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular human insulin is a short-acting insulin compared with rapid-acting insulin analogues in diabetes treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nocturnal Hypoglycaemia">
  <data key="d0">Nocturnal Hypoglycaemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nocturnal hypoglycaemia is a condition of low blood sugar during sleep, studied in relation to insulin therapy safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Nocturnal hypoglycaemia is low blood sugar during sleep, less frequent with glargine than NPH insulin in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6764f5f0af1c9855a1901ea1bef131d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Gain">
  <data key="d0">Weight Gain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight gain is a potential side effect of insulin therapy, observed in comparative studies of insulin detemir and NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight gain is a potential side effect of insulin use, which can be managed through diet and exercise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776642504</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Dosing Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Dosing Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A flexible dosing regimen allows variable timing and dosage of insulin, studied in the BEGIN: Flex T1 trial with insulin degludec.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac7fb8feaa2febe2b5f8525b93f3080f</data>
