<node id="Time In Range">
  <data key="d0">Time In Range</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time In Range (TIR) is a clinical and glycemic metric used in diabetes management to measure the percentage of time a person's glucose levels remain within a specified target range. It is primarily derived from continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) data and serves as a key outcome in evaluating the effectiveness of glucose control strategies. The standard target range for TIR is defined as glucose levels between 70 and 180 mg/dL, and a TIR of at least 70% is recommended to minimize glucose variability and reduce the risk of hypoglycemia and other diabetes-related complications.

TIR is widely used as a primary metric in comparing different CGM systems, including real-time CGM (rtCGM) and intermittently scanned CGM (isCGM), and is instrumental in assessing the performance of advanced diabetes technologies. Research and clinical evidence indicate that continued use of CGM and automated insulin delivery (AID) systems significantly improves TIR, reflecting better glycemic control over time. As a comprehensive indicator, TIR provides a more nuanced understanding of glucose management than traditional metrics like HbA1c, capturing fluctuations and time spent in normoglycemia that are critical for long-term outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c7e3d6615d1076ae20653358419ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f731774e5187eb76527ebeabefeeeb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689263</data>
