</node>
<node id="Eli Lilly">
  <data key="d0">Eli Lilly</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Eli Lilly is a pharmaceutical company that played a pivotal role in the large-scale development and production of insulin during the early 20th century. In collaboration with the University of Toronto, where insulin was first isolated by Frederick Banting, Charles Best, and their colleagues, Eli Lilly committed significant resources to transform the laboratory discovery into a viable, mass-produced therapeutic product. This partnership was instrumental in advancing insulin manufacturing techniques, enabling the treatment of diabetes on a global scale.

Under the leadership of Dr. George Clowes, who served as the company’s research director, Eli Lilly focused on optimizing insulin production processes. The company adopted and refined the isoelectric point precipitation and purification method, which allowed for efficient extraction and purification of insulin from animal sources. By 1922, Eli Lilly had established a dedicated insulin production plant, becoming one of the first pharmaceutical companies to manufacture insulin commercially at scale.

Eli Lilly’s involvement also extended to critical negotiations with the Toronto research team regarding production capabilities, quality control, and patent rights. To meet the rapidly increasing demand for insulin, the company collaborated not only with the University of Toronto but also with the Connaught Laboratories, another key player in early insulin production. These cooperative efforts ensured a more stable supply of insulin and set a precedent for industry-academic partnerships in pharmaceutical development. Through its scientific innovation, industrial capacity, and strategic collaborations, Eli Lilly significantly contributed to making insulin widely accessible, marking a transformative moment in medical history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69124f1cc2248b019af52b9d2e71c12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036e7cdb0e2bea999e115a813d0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9864deffdfa4a86915e3d7985867376&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1961d5ebd8cd94a8e08ca46c59210d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0eaeeaa0051cb78248f45d6af3009e58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
