<node id="Pancreatic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic diabetes is the medical condition related to the dysfunction of the pancreas in regulating blood sugar, which was the focus of Banting and Macleod's research.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic diabetes is the medical condition related to the dysfunction of the pancreas in regulating blood sugar, which was the focus of Banting and Macleod's research.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic diabetes refers to diabetes resulting from structural or functional loss of insulin secretion due to exocrine pancreatic dysfunction, also known as type 3c diabetes or pancreoprivic diabetes.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as type 3c diabetes, this form results from diseases of the exocrine pancreas such as chronic pancreatitis.</data>
