</node>
<node id="Duct Ligation Technique">
  <data key="d0">Duct Ligation Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The duct ligation technique was an initial method used to induce pancreas degeneration for extract preparation, later replaced by alternative approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;The duct ligation technique was an initial method used to induce pancreas degeneration for extract preparation, later replaced by alternative approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c04d944f188525956166c3081e7e4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secretin Stimulation Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Secretin Stimulation Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The secretin stimulation procedure involved injecting secretin into the pancreas to halt juice production, offering an alternative way to prepare insulin extract.&lt;SEP&gt;The secretin stimulation procedure involved injecting secretin into the pancreas to halt juice production, offering an alternative way to prepare insulin extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c04d944f188525956166c3081e7e4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duodenum">
  <data key="d0">Duodenum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The duodenum is the top section of the small intestine that produces secretin, a hormone used in the stimulation of the pancreas during insulin extract preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;The duodenum is the top section of the small intestine that produces secretin, a hormone used in the stimulation of the pancreas during insulin extract preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c04d944f188525956166c3081e7e4</data>
