<node id="World Athletics Championship">
  <data key="d0">World Athletics Championship</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The World Athletics Championship is a global sports competition featuring top athletes in track and field, serving as a premier international event for the sport. It brings together elite competitors from around the world to participate in a wide range of athletic disciplines, including sprints, distance races, jumps, throws, and combined events. Among the most prominent events held at the championship is the 100-meter sprint, which consistently draws significant attention due to its emphasis on speed and world-record potential.

Multiple descriptions highlight the participation of an athlete named Noah Carter, who reportedly broke the 100-meter sprint record at the World Athletics Championship. This achievement is specifically mentioned in several accounts, reinforcing the significance of his performance within the context of the competition. While the details of the record-breaking event are consistent across sources—emphasizing Carter's accomplishment in the 100m sprint—there is no additional information provided regarding the year, location, or official verification of the record. Despite the repetition of this claim, no conflicting records or alternate record holders are mentioned, suggesting a unified narrative around Carter’s feat.

It is also noted that the World Athletics Championship is unrelated to diabetes content, clarifying potential contextual confusion in source material. Overall, the championship is consistently portrayed as a major global track and field event, distinguished by high-level athletic performance and historic milestones such as the reported 100m sprint record set by Noah Carter.</data>
