  <data key="d2">Health care professionals are responsible for prescribing, training, and supporting individuals in the use of diabetes technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals are responsible for managing patient care and should be aware of factors affecting glucose meter accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Care Professionals are individuals trained to provide medical care and guidance, including managing diabetes and interpreting glucose data.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals are involved in shared decision-making with patients regarding the use of insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals cannot prescribe DIY closed-loop systems but are responsible for supporting safe diabetes management in users.</data>
