<node id="J Diabetes Sci Technol">
  <data key="d0">J Diabetes Sci Technol</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">J Diabetes Sci Technol is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on diabetes technologies and related monitoring systems. The journal serves as a platform for studies focusing on advancements in blood glucose monitoring, including real-time continuous glucose monitoring and the accuracy of point-of-care hemoglobin A1c assays. It also covers research on insulin delivery technologies, such as insulin pumps and closed-loop systems, with investigations into both their efficacy and factors associated with insulin pump discontinuation among diabetes patients.

In addition to device-focused research, J Diabetes Sci Technol publishes studies on innovative models of diabetes care, including virtual diabetes clinics and the hospital-based use of continuous glucose monitoring systems. The journal emphasizes the integration of technology into clinical practice, aiming to improve patient outcomes through evidence-based technological solutions. Collectively, its publications reflect a broad scope within the field of diabetes technology, ranging from technical evaluations of monitoring devices to clinical and behavioral aspects of technology adoption and use.&lt;SEP&gt;J Diabetes Sci Technol is a scientific journal that published findings from the ADAG study linking A1C levels to blood glucose values.</data>
