<node id="Hybrid Closed-Loop Systems">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Closed-Loop Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid closed-loop systems are AID systems that automatically adjust basal insulin but require manual input for meals and physical activity adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid closed-loop systems are insulin delivery systems that require manual entry of carbohydrates and announcement of physical activity adjustments for prandial dose calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrates are nutrients that must be manually entered into hybrid closed-loop systems to calculate insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AID Systems">
  <data key="d0">AID Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated Insulin Delivery (AID) systems may reduce A1C levels, improve time in range, lower risk of exercise-related hypoglycemia, and provide psychosocial benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1C Levels">
  <data key="d0">A1C Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A1C levels are a measure of long-term blood glucose control that may be reduced through the use of AID systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TIR">
  <data key="d0">TIR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TIR stands for Time in Range, a glycemic metric used to measure the percentage of time a person's glucose levels remain within a target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range (TIR) is a metric for glucose control that may improve with the use of AID systems.&lt;SEP&gt;TIR refers to Time in Range, a metric used to measure the percentage of time a patient's glucose levels remain within a target range, correlated with microvascular complications and HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exercise-Related Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Exercise-Related Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exercise-related hypoglycemia is low blood sugar triggered by physical activity, which AID systems may help reduce.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise-related hypoglycemia is a risk during physical activity that may be reduced by AID systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychosocial Benefits">
  <data key="d0">Psychosocial Benefits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychosocial benefits are positive mental and emotional outcomes associated with the use of AID systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Other Types Of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Other Types Of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Other types of diabetes include conditions such as post-pancreatectomy diabetes or cystic fibrosis-related diabetes that result in insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Other Types Of Diabetes include monogenic defects in beta cell function, genetic defects in insulin action, diseases of the exocrine pancreas, endocrinopathies, drug-induced diabetes, and infection-related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cystic Fibrosis">
  <data key="d0">Cystic Fibrosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cystic fibrosis is a condition that can lead to insulin deficiency and may require insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic fibrosis is a genetic disorder that can lead to cystic fibrosis–related diabetes, requiring specific screening protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic fibrosis is a genetic disorder mentioned as one of the etiologies contributing to pancreatic diabetes.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic fibrosis is a genetic disorder affecting the lungs and digestive system, often associated with complications such as cystic fibrosis-related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patient Satisfaction">
  <data key="d0">Patient Satisfaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient satisfaction may improve with insulin pump use regardless of diabetes type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Simplification">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Simplification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy simplification refers to the potential benefit of insulin pumps in making diabetes management easier.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C-Peptide Levels">
  <data key="d0">C-Peptide Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">C-peptide levels are biomarkers measured to assess endogenous insulin production, though they do not predict success with insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;C-peptide levels are biomarkers of endogenous insulin production that do not correlate with response to intensive insulin therapy in clinically insulin-deficient individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disposable Patch-Like Devices">
  <data key="d0">Disposable Patch-Like Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Disposable patch-like devices are alternative insulin delivery systems that provide basal and/or bolus insulin in 2-unit increments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous subcutaneous infusion is a method of insulin delivery provided by some patch-like devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Do-It-Yourself Closed-Loop Systems">
  <data key="d0">Do-It-Yourself Closed-Loop Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Do-it-yourself (DIY) closed-loop systems are user-built automated insulin delivery systems combining an insulin pump, rtCGM, controller, and algorithm, not approved by the FDA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. Food And Drug Administration">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Food And Drug Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) does not approve DIY closed-loop systems, though some efforts are underway for regulatory approval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="rtCGM">
  <data key="d0">rtCGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">rtCGM (real-time continuous glucose monitoring) is a system that provides continuous, automatic glucose readings and alerts, shown to improve time in range and reduce hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;rtCGM stands for real-time continuous glucose monitoring, a technology that provides live glucose readings for people with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time continuous glucose monitoring (rtCGM) is a component of DIY closed-loop systems used to monitor glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controller">
  <data key="d0">Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A controller in DIY closed-loop systems processes data from rtCGM and runs an algorithm to automate insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithms in AID systems calculate insulin delivery based on sensor-derived glucose levels to mimic natural insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;An algorithm in DIY systems calculates insulin delivery based on glucose data, pump settings, and user inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rates">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal rates are pump settings in DIY systems that determine background insulin delivery and can be adjusted based on individual needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Ratios">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Ratios</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate ratios are pump settings used in DIY systems to calculate insulin doses based on carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correction Doses">
  <data key="d0">Correction Doses</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Correction doses are insulin adjustments based on current glucose levels, configured in DIY system settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Activity">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin activity refers to the duration and effect of insulin in the body, which is factored into dose calculations in DIY systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Health Technology">
  <data key="d0">Digital Health Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Digital Health Technology refers to the use of technology in managing health conditions, particularly diabetes, through apps, online programs, and digital therapeutics.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital health technology includes systems combining technology and online coaching to support diabetes and prediabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital health technology refers to the use of digital tools and platforms in managing diabetes, including monitoring and data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital health technology refers to the use of digital tools and platforms in managing diabetes, including monitoring and data analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ff5070c8f5a6109621d29aa2b13398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed2aa7fa8ee59d19d7f3898042c3742</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Coaching">
  <data key="d0">Online Coaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Online coaching is a component of digital health systems that provides guidance and support for individuals managing diabetes or prediabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prediabetes">
  <data key="d0">Prediabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prediabetes is a metabolic condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels that are higher than normal but do not meet the diagnostic criteria for type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM2). It serves as a critical precursor to type 2 diabetes, indicating a significantly increased risk for disease progression, and is also associated with a heightened likelihood of developing cardiovascular complications. The condition is clinically identified through diagnostic tests such as hemoglobin A1C, fasting plasma glucose (FPG), and oral glucose tolerance testing (OGTT). Standard diagnostic thresholds include an A1C level between 5.7% and 6.4%, impaired fasting glucose, or impaired glucose tolerance, all of which reflect underlying abnormalities in glucose metabolism. Prediabetes is often asymptomatic, necessitating routine screening—especially in high-risk populations such as individuals with a history of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM), those of reproductive age, and people living with HIV, for whom lifelong monitoring is recommended.

The prevalence of prediabetes varies across populations, with notable findings such as a 22% prevalence rate among Brazilian adolescents aged 12 to 17, as reported by the ERICA study. This highlights the growing concern of prediabetes even in younger age groups. The condition is increasingly recognized not only as a diabetes risk factor but also as a component of broader metabolic dysfunction, including its relevance in the management of metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD). Given its reversible nature, prediabetes represents a vital window for intervention. Foundational treatment strategies focus on lifestyle modifications, including dietary improvements, increased physical activity, and weight management. These interventions are increasingly supported by digital health technologies and online coaching programs aimed at fostering sustainable behavior change. Early diagnosis and proactive management are essential to delay or prevent the onset of type 2 diabetes and reduce long-term health risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Prediabetes is a metabolic state marked by elevated blood glucose levels below the threshold for diabetes, indicating high risk for developing type 2 diabetes.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Prediabetes is a condition preceding DM2, with a prevalence of 22% in Brazilian adolescents aged 12 to 17 according to the ERICA study.&lt;SEP&gt;Prediabetes is a condition where blood glucose levels are higher than normal but not high enough to be classified as diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Prediabetes is a metabolic state characterized by elevated blood glucose levels below the threshold for diabetes, relevant to MASLD management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5fc9e82121669cb9d4aff08c8c9019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e35953dbfdebbbab4bf83ec032ccfb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2977bb9a41689e74de2c536343624744</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation 7.28">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation 7.28</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 7.28 states that individuals with diabetes may use non-FDA-approved systems like DIY closed-loop systems, and healthcare professionals should support their safe use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation 7.29">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation 7.29</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 7.29 states that systems combining technology and online coaching can be beneficial for treating prediabetes and diabetes in some individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation 7.29 indicates that digital health systems combining technology and online coaching can be beneficial for managing prediabetes and diabetes in some individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ff5070c8f5a6109621d29aa2b13398</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet">
  <data key="d0">Internet</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The internet is a source of freely available information for setting up and managing DIY closed-loop systems and hosts online communities for user support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Communities">
  <data key="d0">Online Communities</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Online communities are internet-based groups where people share knowledge on setting up and using DIY closed-loop systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df233d11f0547c43f4dc4cad909d392b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Care In The Hospital">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Care In The Hospital</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Care In The Hospital is a section providing guidance on managing diabetes within hospital settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Care Team">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The health care team supports individuals with diabetes in selecting and using diabetes technologies through education and training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Technology Development">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Technology Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes technology development refers to the rapid advancement of tools and digital solutions for managing diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Care Tasks">
  <data key="d0">Self-Care Tasks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-care tasks are essential activities individuals with diabetes must perform to manage their condition, which current technology does not fully eliminate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Selection">
  <data key="d0">Device Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Device selection is the process of choosing appropriate diabetes management tools based on individual needs and engagement.</data>
