<node id="Real-Time CGM">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-Time CGM is a type of continuous glucose monitoring system that measures and displays glucose levels continuously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermittently Scanned CGM">
  <data key="d0">Intermittently Scanned CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermittently Scanned CGM is a type of continuous glucose monitoring system that requires scanning to visualize and store glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Professional CGM">
  <data key="d0">Professional CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Professional CGM refers to clinic-based continuous glucose monitoring devices applied by healthcare professionals and used for a discrete period, with data that may be blinded or visible.&lt;SEP&gt;Professional CGM is a type of continuous glucose monitoring device used in clinical settings to collect retrospective glucose data, often blinded for analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disposable Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Disposable Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Disposable Sensor is a type of CGM sensor used in rtCGM and isCGM systems that is not reusable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Implantable Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Implantable Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Implantable Sensor is a type of CGM sensor used in rtCGM systems that is implanted in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1C Lowering">
  <data key="d0">A1C Lowering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A1C Lowering refers to the reduction in glycated hemoglobin levels, a key outcome associated with frequent CGM use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjunctive CGM">
  <data key="d0">Adjunctive CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Adjunctive CGM refers to systems that require users to perform blood glucose monitoring for treatment decisions like insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonadjunctive CGM">
  <data key="d0">Nonadjunctive CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonadjunctive CGM refers to systems that do not require blood glucose monitoring for treatment decisions outside specific clinical situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrated CGM">
  <data key="d0">Integrated CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Integrated CGM is a higher FDA standard for CGM devices that allows integration with other digitally connected devices such as AID systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle Libre 2">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle Libre 2 is a specific intermittently scanned CGM device that has been designated as integrated CGM by the FDA and has no generic form available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle Libre 3">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre 3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle Libre 3 is a specific real-time CGM device designated as integrated CGM by the FDA and has no generic form available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Guardian 3">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Guardian 3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic Guardian 3 is a real-time CGM device that is FDA approved for use with the 670/770G AID systems but is not designated as integrated CGM and has no generic form available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="670/770G AID Systems">
  <data key="d0">670/770G AID Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">670/770G AID Systems are automated insulin delivery systems that can integrate with certain rtCGM devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomized Controlled Trials">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Trials</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomized Controlled Trials are clinical studies that evaluate the effectiveness of CGM devices in reducing A1C and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Use Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Use Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Use Frequency refers to how often a CGM sensor is worn or scanned, which correlates with improved diabetes outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Discontinuation">
  <data key="d0">CGM Discontinuation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM Discontinuation refers to stopping the use of continuous glucose monitoring, which can reverse previous glycemic improvements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 7.3">
  <data key="d0">Table 7.3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 7.3 provides definitions for different types of continuous glucose monitoring devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 7.3 provides definitions for the types of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) devices, including rtCGM, isCGM, and professional CGM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f</data>
