<node id="Health Care Professional">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Health care professionals are involved in guiding patients with diabetes in device selection and managing therapy initiation, with preferences potentially influencing geographical adoption rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A health care professional is responsible for interpreting diagnostic tests, discussing symptoms, and managing diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A health care professional is responsible for interpreting diagnostic tests, discussing symptoms, and managing diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647421</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Disparities">
  <data key="d0">Health Disparities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Health disparities in diabetes care are observed in disadvantaged groups, particularly in access to insulin pumps and other diabetes technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antibodies">
  <data key="d0">Antibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibodies related to diabetes are tested to determine type, but their presence does not predict outcomes of insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A temporary basal rate is an advanced pump setting that allows short-term adjustment of insulin delivery to match physiological needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Extended Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An extended bolus is an advanced insulin pump feature that delivers a portion of bolus insulin over time, useful for meals with slow carbohydrate absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Square Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A square wave bolus is a type of insulin delivery pattern available on pumps, distributing bolus insulin evenly over a set period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A dual wave bolus combines immediate and extended insulin delivery, available on some pumps to better match meal-related glucose dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Therapy Initiation">
  <data key="d0">Pump Therapy Initiation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump therapy initiation involves assessing readiness, selecting pump type, setting initial parameters, educating on complications, transitioning from MDI, and introducing advanced settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Older Adults With Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Older Adults With Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Older adults with type 1 diabetes benefit from continued insulin pump therapy, and access should be maintained similarly to younger individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Device Selection">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Device Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes device selection is the process of choosing appropriate diabetes management devices based on individual needs, preferences, and device features, supported by resources like DiabetesWise and the PANTHER Program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Satisfaction">
  <data key="d0">Satisfaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Satisfaction refers to the level of contentment in patients and caregivers regarding diabetes management technologies and outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEnglJMed">
  <data key="d0">NEnglJMed</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">NEnglJMed is a journal that published a six-month multicenter trial on closed-loop control in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643644</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbon-Fiber Spikes">
  <data key="d0">Carbon-Fiber Spikes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced athletic footwear designed for sprinters to enhance speed, performance, and traction during races. These high-performance shoes incorporate carbon-fiber materials to optimize energy return and reduce weight, contributing to faster sprint times. They are specifically engineered for use in track and field events, particularly short-distance sprints such as the 100-meter race.

The spikes gained notable recognition through their use by sprinter Noah Carter, who wore them when breaking the 100-meter sprint record. Multiple accounts confirm that Carter utilized carbon-fiber spikes to achieve peak performance, highlighting their role in elite athletic accomplishments. The footwear is consistently described in the context of competitive sprinting and is explicitly distinguished from medical devices or applications, such as diabetes care, underscoring its exclusive association with sports performance.

Overall, carbon-fiber spikes represent a significant advancement in sports technology, widely adopted by elite sprinters for their ability to improve speed and race efficiency. Their integration into record-breaking performances illustrates their impact on modern track and field athletics.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes used by Noah Carter to enhance performance and break the 100m sprint record.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-Fiber Spikes are advanced footwear used by sprinters to enhance speed and performance, used by Noah Carter when breaking the 100m record.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced footwear used by sprinters to enhance speed and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are high-performance athletic shoes used by sprinters like Noah Carter to enhance speed and traction during races.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes that provide enhanced speed and traction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1eea5927c2474e7c5774b94980fc8b78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-862cb6f254fb8ebb4f3e1080dbf4f53c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5ebd46f8491409b5f07f5c83542afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a18ecfcb20fceb4fd80ab22186964e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647258</data>
