<node id="Fasting Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting Glucose is a measure of blood glucose levels taken after a period of not eating, typically an overnight fast, and serves as a key diagnostic and screening tool for assessing glucose metabolism and diabetes control. It is widely used to evaluate an individual's baseline blood sugar levels and inform clinical decisions, including insulin dosing for diabetic patients. As a low-cost and accessible test, fasting glucose plays a critical role in both general diabetes management and specific at-risk populations.

Fasting glucose is particularly important in identifying individuals at high risk for developing diabetes, including post-transplant diabetes mellitus (PTDM), where it functions as an initial screening tool to determine the need for further diagnostic evaluation. Elevated fasting glucose levels can signal early abnormalities in glucose regulation, prompting more detailed testing and intervention.

In the context of pregnancy, fasting glucose is used to assess glucose metabolism and screen for gestational diabetes. A fasting glucose level between 110–125 mg/dL (6.1 mmol/L) is recognized as a threshold indicating increased risk for early abnormal glucose metabolism during pregnancy. This range serves as a diagnostic criterion, helping healthcare providers identify women who may require closer monitoring or therapeutic intervention to ensure maternal and fetal health. Overall, fasting glucose remains a fundamental metric in metabolic screening and diabetes risk assessment across diverse clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b2f90b1ec83426a0df84d7693bc26d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
