  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arterial Blood">
  <data key="d0">Arterial Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Arterial Blood is blood from an artery, which may cause false low readings in glucose oxidase-based meters due to high oxygen tension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Venous Blood">
  <data key="d0">Venous Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Venous Blood is blood from a vein, which may lead to falsely high glucose readings in certain meter types under low oxygen conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen Saturation">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Saturation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen Saturation refers to the level of oxygen in the blood, which can affect the accuracy of glucose oxidase-based meters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Altitude">
  <data key="d0">High Altitude</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">High Altitude is an environmental condition with lower oxygen levels that may lead to inaccurate glucose readings in certain meters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoxia">
  <data key="d0">Hypoxia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoxia is a condition of low oxygen in tissues, which can interfere with glucose meter accuracy, particularly in glucose oxidase systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature affects the enzymatic reactions in glucose meters, and extreme temperatures can lead to inaccurate readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Humidity">
  <data key="d0">Humidity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Humidity is an environmental factor that may alter glucose meter performance and affect reading accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Altitude">
  <data key="d0">Altitude</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Altitude influences oxygen levels and can impact the accuracy of glucose meters, especially those sensitive to oxygen.&lt;SEP&gt;Altitude refers to elevation above sea level, with high altitudes (&gt;2000 m) potentially affecting glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Altitude refers to elevation above sea level, with high altitudes (&gt;2000 m) potentially affecting glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Altitude refers to elevation above sea level, with high altitudes (&gt;2000 m) potentially affecting glucose measurements.</data>
