  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ascorbic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Ascorbic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ascorbic Acid is a substance that can interfere with glucose oxidase-based meters, leading to false glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) at doses over 500 mg/day can interfere with the FreeStyle Libre CGM system.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) at doses greater than 500 mg/day is a known interfering substance for continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) can cause interference in some glucose meters, leading to inaccurate readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) can cause interference in some glucose meters, leading to inaccurate readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) can cause interference in some glucose meters, leading to inaccurate readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8651ec88cb5333f03b8af01fee4d3cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688807</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Uric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uric Acid is a naturally occurring compound that can interfere with certain glucose meters, particularly glucose oxidase systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Galactose">
  <data key="d0">Galactose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Galactose is a sugar that can interfere with glucose dehydrogenase-based meters, causing falsely elevated glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Xylose">
  <data key="d0">Xylose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Xylose is a sugar that may interfere with glucose dehydrogenase-based glucose meters, leading to inaccurate results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetaminophen">
  <data key="d0">Acetaminophen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaminophen is a common pain reliever that can interfere with glucose oxidase-based meters, resulting in false readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen at doses greater than 4 g/day can interfere with certain CGM systems, leading to inaccurate glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen at doses greater than 4 g/day is a substance that can interfere with continuous glucose monitoring accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a substance studied for its effect on continuous glucose monitoring systems with permselective membranes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8651ec88cb5333f03b8af01fee4d3cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1319c06eac1875d14b345f09579021be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="L-DOPA">
  <data key="d0">L-DOPA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">L-DOPA is a medication used for Parkinson’s disease that can interfere with glucose oxidase-based glucose meters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring Devices">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous glucose monitoring devices are medical tools used for tracking glucose levels in people with diabetes, including real-time and intermittently scanned types.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring Devices are wearable systems that measure glucose levels in real time or via scanning, used for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-time continuous glucose monitoring is a type of CGM that provides constant glucose readings and alerts for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring provides live glucose readings and trends through a wearable sensor, aiding in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time continuous glucose monitoring provides immediate glucose readings and trends, studied for improving glycemic outcomes in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermittently Scanned Continuous Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Intermittently Scanned Continuous Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermittently scanned continuous glucose monitoring is a type of CGM that requires user-initiated scanning to retrieve glucose data.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermittently Scanned Continuous Glucose Monitoring requires user activation to read glucose data from a sensor, used in diabetes self-management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
