<node id="C-Peptide">
  <data key="d0">C-Peptide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">C-Peptide is a substance produced in the pancreas alongside insulin during the synthesis of insulin from proinsulin, and it is released into the bloodstream in equimolar amounts with insulin. As a result, C-Peptide serves as a reliable biomarker for assessing endogenous beta-cell function and insulin production, making it a valuable tool in the evaluation and management of diabetes. Its measurement in blood helps clinicians determine the body's own insulin output, which is critical in differentiating between various forms of diabetes, particularly when the clinical presentation is ambiguous.

C-Peptide is widely used in diagnosing and classifying diabetes types, especially to distinguish Type 1 diabetes, characterized by little to no endogenous insulin production, from Type 2 diabetes, where insulin resistance and residual beta-cell function are typically present. In fulminant Type 1 diabetes, C-Peptide levels are typically low or undetectable, reflecting the rapid and severe loss of beta-cell function. Conversely, in cases where diabetes is diagnosed with ketoacidosis but followed by low or no insulin requirement—particularly in individuals with obesity or clinical signs of insulin resistance—measuring C-Peptide is recommended to evaluate residual beta-cell activity.

Additionally, C-Peptide levels can support the diagnosis of monogenic forms of diabetes; for instance, levels greater than 0.6 ng/mL more than five years after diagnosis suggest preserved endogenous insulin production consistent with monogenic diabetes rather than autoimmune Type 1 diabetes. The biomarker also plays a role in clinical decision-making, such as determining eligibility for insulin pump therapy, where evidence of residual beta-cell function, indicated by measurable C-Peptide, may influence treatment initiation. Overall, C-Peptide remains a key indicator in understanding beta-cell health and guiding personalized diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c37422889250d7e58837deb17406d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59</data>
