<node id="Interstitial Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial glucose is the fluid glucose measured by CGM devices, which correlates with plasma glucose but may lag during rapid changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643674</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma glucose is the actual blood glucose level, which interstitial glucose measurements aim to estimate.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurable level of glucose in the blood used to diagnose conditions such as GDM during tests like the OGTT and GLT.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurable level of glucose in the blood used to diagnose conditions such as GDM during tests like the OGTT and GLT.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da2ab5aba6808664342df831e5ba749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357f19fa58c4dd99dcd7b47a984b4383</data>
