<node id="DKA">
  <data key="d0">DKA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a serious complication of diabetes that can occur due to insulin deficiency, and insulin pump therapy may reduce its risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a serious complication of diabetes that can be prevented through early diagnosis, education on symptoms, and close follow-up in at-risk individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;DKA, or diabetic ketoacidosis, seldom occurs spontaneously in type 2 diabetes and is usually associated with other illnesses or certain medications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketosis">
  <data key="d0">Ketosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketosis is a metabolic state that can progress to DKA if insulin delivery is disrupted, such as from infusion set issues in pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
