</node>
<node id="Pump Site Infection">
  <data key="d0">Pump Site Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump site infection is a potential complication of insulin pump use, occurring at the location of the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peripheral Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Peripheral Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Peripheral neuropathy is a nerve damage complication of diabetes, potentially reduced with insulin pump therapy compared to MDI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor-Augmented Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Sensor-Augmented Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor-augmented pumps are insulin pumps integrated with continuous glucose monitoring that can suspend insulin delivery when glucose levels are low or predicted to drop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Suspend Function">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Suspend Function</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Low glucose suspend function is a feature of sensor-augmented pumps that automatically stops insulin delivery when glucose levels fall below a threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Low Glucose Suspend">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Low Glucose Suspend</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Predictive low glucose suspend is an advanced function that stops insulin delivery when low glucose levels are predicted within the next 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASPIRE Trial">
  <data key="d0">ASPIRE Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The ASPIRE trial was a clinical study involving 247 people with type 1 diabetes that demonstrated the effectiveness of sensor-augmented pump therapy in reducing nocturnal hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776643693</data>
