<node id="β-OHB">
  <data key="d0">β-OHB</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">β-OHB, or β-hydroxybutyrate, is a blood ketone measured in mmol/L to assess risk of diabetic ketoacidosis, with clinical interpretation based on concentration levels and patient condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cetonas Urinárias">
  <data key="d0">Cetonas Urinárias</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetonas urinárias are urinary ketones used to monitor ketosis, with levels indicated as +, ++, or +++ and correlated to blood β-OHB concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Urinary ketones are ketone bodies measured in urine, used to assess risk of ketoacidosis, with clinical interpretation depending on levels and clinical context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabela 4">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 4 presents the correlation between blood β-OHB levels and urinary ketone measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 4 shows the correlation between β-OHB levels and urinary ketone measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Tabela 4 shows the relationship between Time in Range (TIR) percentages and corresponding HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabela 5">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 5</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 5 provides clinical interpretation of β-OHB values based on measured levels and the patient's clinical context.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 5 provides clinical interpretation of ketone values based on measured levels and clinical presentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabela 6">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 6</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 6 shows the correspondence between blood β-OHB levels in mmol/L and urinary ketone readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 6 outlines the correspondence between β-OHB blood levels and urinary ketone readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabela 7">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 7 outlines the interpretation of blood ketone measurements and recommended clinical actions based on β-OHB levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabela 8">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 8</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 8 presents the target blood glucose levels for pregnant women with gestational diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tabela 8 presents the target blood glucose levels for pregnant women.&lt;SEP&gt;Tabela 8 presents glycemic targets for diabetes in pregnancy according to various scientific societies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644198</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Pré-Gestacional">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Pré-Gestacional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mellitus pré-gestacional is a condition where a woman has type 1 or type 2 diabetes before becoming pregnant, requiring strict glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Gestacional">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Gestacional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mellitus gestacional is a form of diabetes that develops during pregnancy and requires regular blood glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Conceptt">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Conceptt</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo Conceptt was a multicenter, multinational study evaluating pregnant women with type 1 diabetes, comparing outcomes between those using continuous glucose monitoring and capillary glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metas Glicêmicas para Gestantes com Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Metas Glicêmicas para Gestantes com Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metas glicêmicas para gestantes com diabetes mellitus refer to the recommended blood glucose targets for pregnant women with either pre-gestational or gestational diabetes to ensure optimal maternal and fetal outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pré-Eclâmpsia">
  <data key="d0">Pré-Eclâmpsia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pré-eclâmpsia is a pregnancy complication associated with higher blood glucose levels, where postprandial glucose monitoring is linked to reduced risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Desjejum">
  <data key="d0">Desjejum</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Desjejum refers to a meal, likely breakfast, in the context of daily eating patterns during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Almoço">
  <data key="d0">Almoço</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Almoço refers to a meal, likely lunch, in the context of daily eating patterns during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jantar">
  <data key="d0">Jantar</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Jantar refers to a meal, likely dinner, in the context of daily eating patterns during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia Capilar Na Gestação">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia Capilar Na Gestação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia capilar na gestação refers to blood glucose monitoring during pregnancy, with specific target levels defined.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Níveis Glicêmicos Na Gestante">
  <data key="d0">Níveis Glicêmicos Na Gestante</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Níveis glicêmicos na gestante are the recommended blood glucose thresholds during pregnancy, including fasting and postprandial measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Glucose ≥ 95 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Glucose ≥ 95 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting glucose ≥ 95 mg/dL is the threshold for blood glucose in pregnant women before meals, as defined by clinical guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1 Hour Postprandial Glucose ≥ 140 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">1 Hour Postprandial Glucose ≥ 140 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">1 hour postprandial glucose ≥ 140 mg/dL is a target level for blood glucose monitoring one hour after meals in pregnant women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2 Hours Postprandial Glucose ≥ 120 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">2 Hours Postprandial Glucose ≥ 120 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">2 hours postprandial glucose ≥ 120 mg/dL is a target level for blood glucose monitoring two hours after meals in pregnant women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3c544741e57de2429f8284d89f5688f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cgm">
  <data key="d0">Cgm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) is a method for measuring glucose levels in real time every five minutes, providing trend information and alarms for high or low glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automonitorização De Glicemia Tradicional">
  <data key="d0">Automonitorização De Glicemia Tradicional</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional blood glucose self-monitoring (A) is a method of checking blood sugar levels through finger-prick tests, less frequent than CGM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hb1Ac">
  <data key="d0">Hb1Ac</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hb1Ac is a measure of long-term blood glucose control, shown to decrease with the use of CGM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="População Pediátrica">
  <data key="d0">População Pediátrica</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The pediatric population is a group for whom recent randomized studies have shown CGM to be safe and effective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adesão Ao Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Adesão Ao Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor adherence refers to the challenge of consistent sensor use, particularly difficult in children, especially those using insulin pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluido Intersticial">
  <data key="d0">Fluido Intersticial</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial fluid is the medium in which glucose is measured by the sensor, reflecting blood glucose levels with a time delay.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose is the substance measured by CGM systems to monitor blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vaso Sanguíneo">
  <data key="d0">Vaso Sanguíneo</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood vessels are the structures from which glucose moves into the interstitial fluid and are relevant to understanding glucose dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Célula">
  <data key="d0">Célula</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cells are biological units involved in glucose uptake and metabolism, relevant to the physiological context of glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Replace-Bg">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Replace-Bg</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The REPLACE-BG study confirmed that CGM can safely and effectively replace routine capillary glucose testing in adults with type 1 diabetes who have good metabolic control, without increasing the risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitorização De Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Monitorização De Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketone monitoring is recommended, especially for children and adolescents using insulin pumps, using blood or urine test strips, particularly during illness or sustained hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isapd">
  <data key="d0">Isapd</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ISPAD is an organization whose consensus guidelines recommend ketone monitoring for children and adolescents using insulin pumps, especially during illness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644088</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abbott">
  <data key="d0">Abbott</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Abbott is a healthcare company and the manufacturer of the FreeStyle Libre glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Abbott is a company that manufactures the FreeStyle Libre glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figura 3">
  <data key="d0">Figura 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 3 is a graph showing glycemic values obtained by a sensor, sourced from FreeStyle Libre by Abbott.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figura 4">
  <data key="d0">Figura 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 4 illustrates the concept of "Lag time" in glucose monitoring, sourced from Medtronic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-126839e244bb40d6238ea2814bdda12a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic MiniMed 640G">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic MiniMed 640G is an insulin infusion pump integrated with a CGM sensor, used for real-time glucose monitoring and insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic MiniMed 670G">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed 670G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Medtronic MiniMed 670G is an advanced insulin pump with integrated CGM, not available in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DCCT">
  <data key="d0">DCCT</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) provided data linking glucose control metrics like TIR to microvascular complications.&lt;SEP&gt;DCCT stands for Diabetes Control and Complications Trial, a landmark study showing that maintaining HbA1c below 7% reduces microvascular complications in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vigersky and Col.">
  <data key="d0">Vigersky and Col.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Vigersky and colleagues conducted recent analyses demonstrating the correlation between TIR and HbA1c changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644094</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 2">
  <data key="d0">Figure 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 2 is a graph illustrating continuous glucose monitoring data from the Medtronic MiniMed 640G insulin pump, sourced from MiniMed Paradigm® Veo™.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644094</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 3">
  <data key="d0">Figure 3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 3 depicts the FreeStyle Libre glucose monitoring system by Abbott, used for visual reference in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776644094</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 4">
  <data key="d0">Figure 4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 4 illustrates the concept of lag time between capillary and interstitial glucose measurements in CGM systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
