<node id="Lanceta Retrátil">
  <data key="d0">Lanceta Retrátil</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lanceta Retrátil is a medical device designed for obtaining blood samples from the fingertip, primarily used in capillary glucose testing. It functions as a lancet, a small pointed instrument that punctures the skin to extract a drop of blood for diagnostic purposes, such as monitoring blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes.

The device features a retractable safety mechanism that helps ensure safe handling and disposal. This built-in safety component minimizes the risk of accidental needlesticks and contamination after use by automatically retracting the used lancet tip. As a result, Lanceta Retrátil supports safer blood sampling practices in both clinical and home settings.

Although the descriptions are provided in both English and Portuguese, they consistently refer to the same device, with no indication of distinct entities or conflicting technical specifications. The repeated emphasis on safety mechanisms and use in blood glucose testing underscores its role as a reliable, single-use, safety-engineered medical tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d2f09f4f3ead9f5bcbe0e4c9697887b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lancetador">
  <data key="d0">Lancetador</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lancetador is a medical device designed to hold and deploy a lancet for capillary blood sampling, commonly used in procedures requiring small blood samples such as glucose monitoring. It functions as a mechanical tool that ensures a controlled and precise puncture, minimizing discomfort and enhancing user safety during the sampling process.

Typically designed in a pen-like form factor, the Lancetador allows for adjustable puncture depth, enabling customization based on individual skin sensitivity or clinical requirements. This feature supports both patient comfort and procedural consistency, particularly in home healthcare settings. The device is widely used for digital punctures, where a small incision is made on the fingertip to obtain a blood droplet for diagnostic testing.

Although the provided descriptions are repetitive, they consistently emphasize the Lancetador’s role as a handheld, user-friendly instrument that facilitates safe and efficient blood collection. The inclusion of Portuguese descriptions confirms its usage context in Portuguese-speaking regions, where it is similarly recognized for its controlled operation and ergonomic design. Overall, the Lancetador serves as a reliable tool in both clinical and personal health monitoring environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d2f09f4f3ead9f5bcbe0e4c9697887b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algodão">
  <data key="d0">Algodão</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Algodão refers to cotton, a material commonly used in medical and diagnostic procedures, particularly during capillary glucose testing. It plays an auxiliary role in the process of capillary blood collection, primarily serving purposes such as antisepsis and drying. Specifically, Algodão is applied to clean the puncture site before or after blood sampling, ensuring hygiene and minimizing the risk of infection.

Additionally, Algodão is used to apply gentle pressure to the site after blood has been drawn, aiding in hemostasis and absorbing residual blood. Its absorbent and soft properties make it suitable for handling sensitive skin areas, especially in procedures involving fingersticks or heel pricks. The repeated emphasis across descriptions confirms its function as a supportive material in the overall workflow of capillary blood sampling, particularly in point-of-care glucose monitoring. Overall, Algodão is integral to maintaining cleanliness and patient comfort during such medical procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d2f09f4f3ead9f5bcbe0e4c9697887b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
