  <data key="d5">1776647357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FPG">
  <data key="d0">FPG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">FPG, or Fasting Plasma Glucose, is a diagnostic test used to measure blood glucose after fasting and is one of the methods to diagnose diabetes or prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;FPG stands for fasting plasma glucose, a diagnostic test used to measure blood glucose levels after an overnight fast to identify impaired fasting glucose or diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG) is an alternative diagnostic test considered more reliable than A1C in certain pediatric and ethnic populations.&lt;SEP&gt;FPG, or Fasting Plasma Glucose, is a diagnostic test used to measure blood glucose after fasting and is one of the methods to diagnose diabetes or prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;FPG stands for fasting plasma glucose, a diagnostic test used to measure blood glucose levels after an overnight fast to identify impaired fasting glucose or diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG) is an alternative diagnostic test considered more reliable than A1C in certain pediatric and ethnic populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2-h PG">
  <data key="d0">2-h PG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">2-h PG, or 2-hour Plasma Glucose, is a diagnostic test measuring blood glucose levels two hours after glucose intake, used in diabetes detection.&lt;SEP&gt;2-h PG refers to the 2-hour plasma glucose measurement taken during a 75-g OGTT, used to diagnose impaired glucose tolerance based on levels between 140–199 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;2-h PG, or 2-hour Plasma Glucose, is a diagnostic test measuring blood glucose levels two hours after glucose intake, used in diabetes detection.&lt;SEP&gt;2-h PG refers to the 2-hour plasma glucose measurement taken during a 75-g OGTT, used to diagnose impaired glucose tolerance based on levels between 140–199 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647373</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="75-g OGTT">
  <data key="d0">75-g OGTT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">75-g OGTT refers to the 75-gram oral glucose tolerance test, a diagnostic procedure used to evaluate impaired glucose tolerance by measuring plasma glucose levels 2 hours after glucose ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;A 75-gram Oral Glucose Tolerance Test used in the one-step method for diagnosing GDM, based on IADPSG criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;75-g OGTT refers to the 75-gram oral glucose tolerance test, a diagnostic procedure used to evaluate impaired glucose tolerance by measuring plasma glucose levels 2 hours after glucose ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;A 75-gram Oral Glucose Tolerance Test used in the one-step method for diagnosing GDM, based on IADPSG criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
