<node id="Diabetes Classification">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Future diabetes classification schemes are expected to focus on the underlying pathophysiology of beta-cell dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes classification involves determining the type of diabetes a patient has, which can be refined through genetic testing and biomarker analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Classification refers to the system used to categorize different types of diabetes based on etiology and clinical presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes classification refers to the system of categorizing different types of diabetes, including MODY, type 1, type 2, and other monogenic or syndromic forms, based on etiology and clinical features.&lt;SEP&gt;Future diabetes classification schemes are expected to focus on the underlying pathophysiology of beta-cell dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes classification involves determining the type of diabetes a patient has, which can be refined through genetic testing and biomarker analysis.</data>
