</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes Staging">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes Staging</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 diabetes staging includes three stages based on autoimmunity, glycemic status, and symptom presentation, as defined by specific diagnostic criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 diabetes staging includes three stages based on autoimmunity, glycemic status, and symptom presentation, as defined by specific diagnostic criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stage 1 Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Stage 1 Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage 1 type 1 diabetes is characterized by autoimmunity and normoglycemia, with presence of multiple islet autoantibodies but no impaired fasting glucose or impaired glucose tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 type 1 diabetes is defined by the presence of two or more islet autoantibodies without symptoms, indicating presymptomatic disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 type 1 diabetes is characterized by autoimmunity and normoglycemia, with presence of multiple islet autoantibodies but no impaired fasting glucose or impaired glucose tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 type 1 diabetes is defined by the presence of two or more islet autoantibodies without symptoms, indicating presymptomatic disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-620e2d1316d6093170f1c9991caabc7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stage 2 Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Stage 2 Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage 2 type 1 diabetes involves autoimmunity and dysglycemia, with impaired fasting glucose and/or impaired glucose tolerance, and detectable islet autoantibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2 type 1 diabetes involves autoimmunity and dysglycemia, with impaired fasting glucose and/or impaired glucose tolerance, and detectable islet autoantibodies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stage 3 Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Stage 3 Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage 3 type 1 diabetes is marked by overt hyperglycemia and clinical symptoms, meeting standard diabetes diagnostic criteria, with possible loss of autoantibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 type 1 diabetes is marked by overt hyperglycemia and clinical symptoms, meeting standard diabetes diagnostic criteria, with possible loss of autoantibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 Type 1 Diabetes refers to the clinical onset of the disease with symptomatic hyperglycemia, which screening aims to delay or prevent.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 Type 1 Diabetes refers to the clinical onset of the disease with symptomatic hyperglycemia, which screening aims to delay or prevent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 2.1">
  <data key="d0">Table 2.1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2.1 outlines the staging of type 1 diabetes, including characteristics and diagnostic criteria for each stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2.1 presents the three distinct stages of type 1 diabetes, used as a framework for research and regulatory decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2.1 outlines the staging of type 1 diabetes, including characteristics and diagnostic criteria for each stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2.1 presents the three distinct stages of type 1 diabetes, used as a framework for research and regulatory decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a</data>
