</node>
<node id="Table 2.2">
  <data key="d0">Table 2.2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2.2 provides the diagnostic criteria for diabetes, serving as a standardized reference for identifying both diabetes and prediabetes across diverse age groups, including children, adolescents, and adults. It outlines specific threshold values for several key biomarkers used in clinical assessment: fasting plasma glucose (FPG), the 2-hour plasma glucose (2-h PG) level during a 75-g oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT), hemoglobin A1C (A1C), and random plasma glucose. Elevated levels of any of these markers beyond the defined cutoffs can indicate a diagnosis of diabetes.

In addition to diagnosing diabetes, Table 2.2 also includes criteria relevant to the screening of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes, emphasizing the utility of FPG, OGTT, and A1C as appropriate and evidence-based testing methods. The table consolidates these metrics to guide healthcare professionals in consistent and accurate diagnosis, ensuring applicability across pediatric and adult populations. By standardizing diagnostic thresholds—such as an A1C of 6.5% or higher, FPG of 126 mg/dL or higher, 2-h PG of 200 mg/dL or higher during OGTT, or a random plasma glucose of 200 mg/dL in the presence of classic symptoms—Table 2.2 supports reliable clinical decision-making in both research and practice settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
