</node>
<node id="Early Abnormal Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Early Abnormal Glucose Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early abnormal glucose metabolism refers to elevated fasting glucose or A1C levels early in pregnancy that indicate higher risk for adverse outcomes and later diagnosis of gestational diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Early abnormal glucose metabolism refers to elevated fasting glucose or A1C levels early in pregnancy that indicate higher risk for adverse outcomes and later diagnosis of gestational diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b2f90b1ec83426a0df84d7693bc26d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="75-G Oral Glucose Tolerance Test">
  <data key="d0">75-G Oral Glucose Tolerance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The 75-g oral glucose tolerance test is used postpartum to screen individuals with a history of gestational diabetes mellitus for prediabetes or diabetes using non-pregnancy diagnostic criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The 75-g oral glucose tolerance test is used postpartum to screen individuals with a history of gestational diabetes mellitus for prediabetes or diabetes using non-pregnancy diagnostic criteria.</data>
