  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adverse pregnancy outcomes include preeclampsia, macrosomia, shoulder dystocia, perinatal death, and small-for-gestational-age birth weight, which are associated with early abnormal glucose metabolism and gestational diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse pregnancy outcomes are complications associated with diabetes during pregnancy, including risks identified by elevated HbA1c levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse pregnancy outcomes include preeclampsia, macrosomia, shoulder dystocia, perinatal death, and small-for-gestational-age birth weight, which are associated with early abnormal glucose metabolism and gestational diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse pregnancy outcomes are complications associated with diabetes during pregnancy, including risks identified by elevated HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b2f90b1ec83426a0df84d7693bc26d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
