  <data key="d2">Checkpoint inhibitors are immunotherapies used in cancer treatment that can trigger immune-related adverse events, including type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkpoint inhibitors are a class of immunotherapy drugs that can trigger or exacerbate autoimmune responses, including in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkpoint inhibitors are immunotherapies used in cancer treatment that can trigger immune-related adverse events, including type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkpoint inhibitors are a class of immunotherapy drugs that can trigger or exacerbate autoimmune responses, including in type 1 diabetes.</data>
