<node id="OGTT">
  <data key="d0">OGTT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT) is a diagnostic procedure used to assess glucose metabolism by measuring blood glucose levels after the ingestion of a standardized amount of glucose, typically performed following an overnight fast. The test plays a critical role in diagnosing various forms of glucose intolerance and diabetes, with specific protocols adapted to different clinical contexts. One common version involves a 2-hour 75-gram glucose load and is utilized in the one-step approach for diagnosing gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM), while a 3-hour 100-gram version is employed in the two-step strategy for the same condition, highlighting its methodological flexibility based on diagnostic guidelines.

In addition to its use in pregnancy, OGTT is regarded as the gold-standard diagnostic test for post-transplant diabetes mellitus (PTDM) when assessed one year after organ transplantation, offering greater accuracy than alternative measures in this population. It is also recommended as a preferred diagnostic method in pediatric populations where the reliability of glycated hemoglobin (A1C) testing is compromised, such as in cases of hemoglobinopathies, anemia, or other conditions affecting red blood cell turnover. This makes OGTT particularly valuable in scenarios where A1C results may not accurately reflect long-term glycemic control.

Overall, OGTT serves as a versatile and essential tool in clinical endocrinology, enabling the precise evaluation of glucose homeostasis across diverse patient groups, including pregnant women, transplant recipients, and children. Its ability to detect impaired glucose tolerance and diabetes with high sensitivity underpins its continued use despite being more time-consuming and complex than simpler blood tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357f19fa58c4dd99dcd7b47a984b4383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
