<node id="Carpenter-Coustan Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Carpenter-Coustan Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Carpenter-Coustan Criteria are a set of diagnostic guidelines used to identify gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) through the interpretation of a 100-gram oral glucose tolerance test (100-g OGTT). These criteria are specifically applied in the two-step approach to GDM diagnosis, which begins with an initial 50-gram glucose screen; if this screening yields a positive result, the 100-g OGTT is administered and its results are evaluated using the Carpenter-Coustan thresholds.

The Carpenter-Coustan Criteria define specific glucose threshold values for fasting, 1-hour, 2-hour, and 3-hour measurements during the 100-g OGTT. A diagnosis of GDM is confirmed when at least two of these glucose values exceed the established thresholds. This method provides a standardized framework for diagnosing GDM, ensuring consistency in clinical assessment and enabling timely intervention to manage maternal and fetal health risks associated with abnormal glucose metabolism during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-357f19fa58c4dd99dcd7b47a984b4383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647290</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
