  <data key="d2">Glycaemic control refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels, particularly important in the peri-operative period for diabetic transplant patients to prevent allograft rejection.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycaemic control refers to the regulation of blood glucose levels, particularly important in the peri-operative period for diabetic transplant patients to prevent allograft rejection.</data>
