</node>
<node id="GCK-MODY">
  <data key="d0">GCK-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GCK-MODY, also known as MODY2, is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the GCK gene, resulting in mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia that typically does not require treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK-MODY is a subtype of maturity-onset diabetes of the young caused by mutations in the glucokinase gene, frequently misdiagnosed and unnecessarily treated.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK-MODY, also known as MODY2, is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the GCK gene, resulting in mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia that typically does not require treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK-MODY is a subtype of maturity-onset diabetes of the young caused by mutations in the glucokinase gene, frequently misdiagnosed and unnecessarily treated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
