</node>
<node id="HNF1A-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF1A-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1A-MODY, also known as MODY3, is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the HNF1A gene, characterized by progressive insulin secretory defect and sensitivity to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A-MODY is a form of monogenic diabetes due to mutations in the HNF1A gene, with distinct clinical and genetic characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A-MODY, also known as MODY3, is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the HNF1A gene, characterized by progressive insulin secretory defect and sensitivity to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A-MODY is a form of monogenic diabetes due to mutations in the HNF1A gene, with distinct clinical and genetic characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
