  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Crisis">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Crisis</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemic crisis is a clinical emergency characterized by extremely high blood glucose and can serve as a basis for immediate diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperglycemic crisis is a clinical emergency characterized by extremely high blood glucose and can serve as a basis for immediate diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classic Symptoms Of Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Classic Symptoms Of Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">symptom</data>
  <data key="d2">Classic symptoms of hyperglycemia include excessive thirst, urination, and fatigue, and when present with high glucose, support a diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Classic symptoms of hyperglycemia include excessive thirst, urination, and fatigue, and when present with high glucose, support a diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Random Plasma Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Random plasma glucose testing measures blood glucose at any time of day and is used to diagnose diabetes in symptomatic patients when levels are ≥200 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Random plasma glucose is a blood glucose measurement taken at any time of day and used to diagnose diabetes when $200 mg/dL with symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Random plasma glucose testing measures blood glucose at any time of day and is used to diagnose diabetes in symptomatic patients when levels are ≥200 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Random plasma glucose is a blood glucose measurement taken at any time of day and used to diagnose diabetes when $200 mg/dL with symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5fc9e82121669cb9d4aff08c8c9019</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes diagnosis requires two abnormal test results unless there is a clear clinical presentation such as hyperglycemic crisis.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes diagnosis involves the classification and identification of diabetes types, including gestational, type 1, and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes diagnosis requires two abnormal test results unless there is a clear clinical presentation such as hyperglycemic crisis.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes diagnosis involves the classification and identification of diabetes types, including gestational, type 1, and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Diagnosis refers to the clinical process of identifying diabetes mellitus using criteria such as blood glucose levels from tests like TTGO-1h, TTGO-2h, or fasting plasma glucose.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Diagnosis refers to the clinical process of identifying diabetes mellitus using criteria such as blood glucose levels from tests like TTGO-1h, TTGO-2h, or fasting plasma glucose.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688961</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1C Assay Interference">
  <data key="d0">A1C Assay Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A1C assay interference refers to factors that cause inaccurate A1C readings, requiring careful evaluation when test results are discordant.&lt;SEP&gt;A1C assay interference refers to factors that cause inaccurate A1C readings, requiring careful evaluation when test results are discordant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preanalytic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Preanalytic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preanalytic variability refers to changes in test samples before analysis, such as delayed centrifugation, which can affect glucose test accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Preanalytic variability refers to changes in test samples before analysis, such as delayed centrifugation, which can affect glucose test accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Analytic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytic variability refers to potential inaccuracies during the testing process that may lead to inconsistent diagnostic results.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytic variability refers to potential inaccuracies during the testing process that may lead to inconsistent diagnostic results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The diagnostic threshold is the defined value (e.g., A1C ≥6.5%) above which a test result indicates diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The diagnostic threshold is the defined value (e.g., A1C ≥6.5%) above which a test result indicates diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
