</node>
<node id="Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes (CFRD) is the most common comorbidity in people with cystic fibrosis, associated with insulin insufficiency and worse health outcomes including nutritional decline and severe lung disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic fibrosis–related diabetes is a form of diabetes that develops in individuals with cystic fibrosis and requires annual screening starting at age 10 using OGTT.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes (CFRD) is a form of diabetes that occurs in people with cystic fibrosis, often managed with insulin therapy to promote weight gain and macronutrient retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes (CFRD) is the most common comorbidity in people with cystic fibrosis, associated with insulin insufficiency and worse health outcomes including nutritional decline and severe lung disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic fibrosis–related diabetes is a form of diabetes that develops in individuals with cystic fibrosis and requires annual screening starting at age 10 using OGTT.&lt;SEP&gt;Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes (CFRD) is a form of diabetes that occurs in people with cystic fibrosis, often managed with insulin therapy to promote weight gain and macronutrient retention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HOMA of β-cell Function">
  <data key="d0">HOMA of β-cell Function</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">HOMA of β-cell function is a method that may detect early risk for cystic fibrosis–related diabetes but lacks evidence linking it to long-term outcomes and is not recommended outside research settings.&lt;SEP&gt;HOMA of β-cell function is a method that may detect early risk for cystic fibrosis–related diabetes but lacks evidence linking it to long-term outcomes and is not recommended outside research settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry">
  <data key="d0">Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry evaluated 3,553 individuals with cystic fibrosis and diagnosed 445 with cystic fibrosis–related diabetes, supporting early diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry evaluated 3,553 individuals with cystic fibrosis and diagnosed 445 with cystic fibrosis–related diabetes, supporting early diagnosis and treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19</data>
