<node id="Maternal Disorders Of Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Disorders Of Glucose Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal disorders of glucose metabolism refer to metabolic conditions in pregnant women, including gestational diabetes, that impact health outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Maternal disorders of glucose metabolism refer to metabolic conditions in pregnant women, including gestational diabetes, that impact health outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Childhood Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Childhood Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Childhood adiposity refers to excess body fat in children, which has been linked to maternal gestational diabetes and metabolic environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Childhood adiposity refers to excess body fat in children, which has been linked to maternal gestational diabetes and metabolic environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Childhood Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Childhood Glucose Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Childhood glucose metabolism describes how children process glucose, which can be influenced by maternal hyperglycemia during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Childhood glucose metabolism describes how children process glucose, which can be influenced by maternal hyperglycemia during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal glycemia refers to blood glucose levels in pregnant women, which are associated with adverse outcomes in offspring.&lt;SEP&gt;Maternal glycemia refers to blood glucose levels in pregnant women, which are associated with adverse outcomes in offspring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Utero Exposure">
  <data key="d0">In Utero Exposure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In utero exposure refers to the prenatal environment, particularly exposure to maternal hyperglycemia, which can affect long-term child health.&lt;SEP&gt;In utero exposure refers to the prenatal environment, particularly exposure to maternal hyperglycemia, which can affect long-term child health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Childhood Cardiometabolic Risk">
  <data key="d0">Childhood Cardiometabolic Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Childhood cardiometabolic risk includes the likelihood of developing cardiovascular and metabolic diseases in children, influenced by maternal metabolic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Childhood cardiometabolic risk includes the likelihood of developing cardiovascular and metabolic diseases in children, influenced by maternal metabolic conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Newborn Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Newborn Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Newborn adiposity refers to body fat levels at birth, which may mediate the relationship between maternal metabolism and later childhood adiposity.&lt;SEP&gt;Newborn adiposity refers to body fat levels at birth, which may mediate the relationship between maternal metabolism and later childhood adiposity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cord Blood C-Peptide">
  <data key="d0">Cord Blood C-Peptide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cord blood C-peptide is a biomarker measured at birth that reflects fetal insulin secretion and is associated with maternal glycemia and childhood metabolic outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cord blood C-peptide is a biomarker measured at birth that reflects fetal insulin secretion and is associated with maternal glycemia and childhood metabolic outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mild Gestational Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Mild Gestational Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mild gestational diabetes is a less severe form of gestational diabetes that has been studied for its impact on pregnancy and long-term child health.&lt;SEP&gt;Mild gestational diabetes is a less severe form of gestational diabetes that has been studied for its impact on pregnancy and long-term child health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy outcomes include measures such as birth weight, delivery complications, and neonatal health, which can be affected by gestational diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy outcomes include measures such as birth weight, delivery complications, and neonatal health, which can be affected by gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Term Child Health">
  <data key="d0">Long-Term Child Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-term child health refers to the sustained physical and metabolic well-being of children beyond infancy, influenced by prenatal conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-term child health refers to the sustained physical and metabolic well-being of children beyond infancy, influenced by prenatal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647388</data>
