</node>
<node id="MODY">
  <data key="d0">MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY (Mature Onset Diabetes of the Young) is a monogenic form of diabetes caused by genetic defects in pancreatic beta cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY (Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young) is the most common form of monogenic diabetes, characterized by autosomal dominant inheritance, early-onset hyperglycemia, and detectable C-peptide levels after five years from diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY refers to maturity-onset diabetes of the young, a monogenic form of diabetes often caused by mutations in genes such as GCK, HNF1A, and HNF4A.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY, or maturity-onset diabetes of the young, is a monogenic form of diabetes typically diagnosed in children and young adults with a family history suggestive of autosomal dominant inheritance.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY (Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young) is a monogenic form of diabetes typically inherited in an autosomal dominant pattern, with subtypes including HNF1A-MODY, GCK-MODY, and HNF4A-MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Neonatal Transient Or Permanent">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Neonatal Transient Or Permanent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Neonatal Transient Or Permanent refers to neonatal diabetes that may resolve or persist, linked to genetic defects in beta cell function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mitochondrial Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Mitochondrial Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitochondrial Diabetes is a subtype of monogenic diabetes caused by mitochondrial DNA mutations affecting beta cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitochondrial diabetes is a form of diabetes caused by mitochondrial DNA mutations, often associated with other systemic features.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitochondrial diabetes is a form of diabetes for which genetic testing is recommended in cases associated with deafness or progressive external ophthalmoplegia with maternal inheritance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syndrome Of Insulin Resistance Type A">
  <data key="d0">Syndrome Of Insulin Resistance Type A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Syndrome Of Insulin Resistance Type A is a genetic defect in insulin action leading to severe insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rabson-Mendenhall Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Rabson-Mendenhall Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rabson-Mendenhall Syndrome is a genetic condition involving severe insulin resistance and abnormal growth patterns due to insulin receptor defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipoatrophic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Lipoatrophic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipoatrophic Diabetes is a form of diabetes associated with loss of body fat and insulin resistance due to genetic defects in insulin action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatogenic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatogenic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatogenic Diabetes results from diseases of the exocrine pancreas such as pancreatitis, trauma, neoplasia, cystic fibrosis, hemochromatosis, or fibrocalculous pancreopathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endocrinopathy-Associated Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Endocrinopathy-Associated Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Endocrinopathy-Associated Diabetes is linked to hormonal disorders such as acromegaly, Cushing's syndrome, glucagonoma, pheochromocytoma, hyperthyroidism, somatostatinoma, and aldosteronoma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug-Induced Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Drug-Induced Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug-Induced Diabetes is secondary to chemical agents such as Vacor, pentamidine, nicotinic acid, glucocorticoids, thyroid hormone, diazoxide, beta-adrenergic agonists, thiazides, phenytoin, and interferon gamma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infection-Related Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Infection-Related Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infection-Related Diabetes can result from congenital rubella and cytomegalovirus infections affecting pancreatic function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
