  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vacor">
  <data key="d0">Vacor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Vacor is a rodenticide containing Piriminil that has the potential to destroy beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Vacor is a chemical agent, specifically a rat poison containing Pyriminil, known to potentially destroy pancreatic beta cells and induce diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pentamidine">
  <data key="d0">Pentamidine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pentamidine is a medication associated with potential beta cell damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Pentamidine is a drug that can induce diabetes as a side effect by damaging pancreatic beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nicotinic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Nicotinic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nicotinic Acid is a compound linked to adverse effects on pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotinic Acid, also known as niacin, is a medication that can induce insulin resistance and contribute to drug-induced diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucocorticoids">
  <data key="d0">Glucocorticoids</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucocorticoids are a class of steroid hormones and medications known for their significant effects on glucose metabolism and insulin sensitivity. Naturally produced in the body or administered exogenously, these compounds play a critical role in regulating various physiological processes, including immune response and inflammation. Commonly prescribed glucocorticoid medications include prednisolone, hydrocortisone, and dexamethasone, which are widely used for their potent anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive properties in conditions such as asthma, rheumatoid arthritis, and autoimmune diseases.

A well-documented effect of glucocorticoids is their ability to induce hyperglycemia by impairing insulin sensitivity, leading to insulin resistance. This disruption in glucose homeostasis can result in elevated blood glucose levels and, in some cases, the development of glucocorticoid-induced diabetes. The hyperglycemic effects are dose- and duration-dependent, with higher doses and prolonged use posing a greater risk. As such, glucocorticoids are recognized as a significant pharmacological factor contributing to new-onset diabetes in susceptible individuals.

Due to their impact on glucose regulation, clinical guidelines emphasize the importance of diabetes screening both before and after the initiation of glucocorticoid therapy. Monitoring blood glucose levels allows for early detection of metabolic disturbances and facilitates timely intervention to manage or prevent diabetes. Healthcare providers are advised to consider a patient’s pre-existing risk factors for diabetes when prescribing glucocorticoids and to implement appropriate surveillance strategies throughout treatment. Overall, while glucocorticoids are valuable therapeutic agents, their metabolic side effects necessitate careful patient assessment and ongoing glycemic monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Hormone">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Hormone</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thyroid Hormone refers to hormones produced by the thyroid gland that can influence metabolic rate and glucose regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid Hormone, when in excess, can contribute to impaired glucose metabolism and is listed as a cause of drug-induced diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diazoxide">
  <data key="d0">Diazoxide</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Diazoxide is a medication that can impair insulin secretion and is associated with hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Diazoxide is a medication that can induce hyperglycemia by inhibiting insulin secretion from pancreatic beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Adrenergic Agonist">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Adrenergic Agonist</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-Adrenergic Agonists are drugs that can increase blood glucose levels and are associated with drug-induced diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiazides">
  <data key="d0">Thiazides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiazides are diuretic medications that can impair glucose tolerance and lead to hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazides are diuretic medications that can impair glucose tolerance and are linked to drug-induced diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phenytoin">
  <data key="d0">Phenytoin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenytoin is an anticonvulsant drug that may interfere with glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenytoin, also known as diphenylhydantoin, is an anticonvulsant that can interfere with insulin secretion and contribute to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interferon Gamma">
  <data key="d0">Interferon Gamma</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Interferon Gamma is a cytokine therapy that can trigger autoimmune destruction of beta cells and lead to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Rubella">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Rubella</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Congenital Rubella is a viral infection present at birth that can lead to diabetes due to pancreatic damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Congenital Rubella is a viral infection acquired in utero that can damage pancreatic beta cells and lead to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cytomegalovirus">
  <data key="d0">Cytomegalovirus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cytomegalovirus is a viral infection that may contribute to secondary diabetes through beta cell injury.&lt;SEP&gt;Cytomegalovirus is a viral infection that has been associated with the development of diabetes through pancreatic damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pmol/L">
  <data key="d0">Pmol/L</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Pmol/L is a unit of measurement used for quantifying substances such as C-peptide in blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
