  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unitslab.Com">
  <data key="d0">Unitslab.Com</data>
  <data key="d1">website</data>
  <data key="d2">Unitslab.com is an online platform providing conversion tools between conventional and SI units for laboratory measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults">
  <data key="d0">Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults (LADA) is a slowly progressing form of autoimmune diabetes that occurs in adults and shares features of both Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent autoimmune diabetes in adults is a form of diabetes characterized by autoimmune destruction of beta cells, often misdiagnosed as type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA) is a slowly progressive form of autoimmune diabetes with adult onset, leading to gradual beta-cell destruction.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent autoimmune diabetes in adults is a form of diabetes identified through glutamic acid decarboxylase autoantibody testing, often presenting with poor islet function.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent autoimmune diabetes in adults is a slow-progressing form of type 1 diabetes diagnosed in adulthood, often misdiagnosed as type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-GAD Antibody">
  <data key="d0">Anti-GAD Antibody</data>
  <data key="d1">biomolecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-GAD antibody is the most common autoantibody tested for diagnosing LADA, indicating autoimmune activity against pancreatic cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum C-Peptide Levels">
  <data key="d0">Serum C-Peptide Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum C-peptide levels are used as a marker to differentiate between types of diabetes, with low levels suggesting Type 1 and high levels suggesting Type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision Flowchart for Diabetes Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Decision Flowchart for Diabetes Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A decision flowchart provided in the Brazilian Diabetes Society guideline to support differential diagnosis of various types of diabetes in cases of diagnostic uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nmol/L">
  <data key="d0">Nmol/L</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Nmol/L is a unit of measurement used for quantifying substances such as C-peptide in blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ng/Ml">
  <data key="d0">Ng/Ml</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Ng/mL is a conventional unit for measuring C-peptide concentration, often converted to SI units like pmol/L.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ng/Dl">
  <data key="d0">Ng/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Ng/dL is a unit used in measuring C-peptide levels, particularly in older or region-specific laboratory reports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ng/100Ml">
  <data key="d0">Ng/100Ml</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Ng/100mL is equivalent to ng/dL and is used for reporting C-peptide concentrations in some clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ng%">
  <data key="d0">Ng%</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Ng% is a unit expression for C-peptide levels, representing nanograms per 100 milliliters of blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ng/L">
  <data key="d0">Ng/L</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">Ng/L is a unit for measuring very low concentrations of C-peptide, often used in conjunction with other unit systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Μg/L">
  <data key="d0">Μg/L</data>
  <data key="d1">unit</data>
  <data key="d2">µg/L is a unit of measurement for C-peptide, equivalent to milligrams per cubic meter, used in some laboratory contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triglycerides">
  <data key="d0">Triglycerides</data>
  <data key="d1">biomolecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Triglycerides are blood lipids; low serum levels (&lt;98 mg/dL) are a predictive factor for autoimmune diabetes in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hdl">
  <data key="d0">Hdl</data>
  <data key="d1">biomolecule</data>
  <data key="d2">HDL (high-density lipoprotein) cholesterol levels above 46 mg/dL are associated with a higher likelihood of autoimmune diabetes in newly diagnosed adult patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646892</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hba1C">
  <data key="d0">Hba1C</data>
  <data key="d1">biomolecule</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c is a glycated hemoglobin marker; levels above 8.6% are a clinical predictor for differentiating autoimmune diabetes from Type 2 diabetes in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6ea581f76ddc15bc463d1eccc4496</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646892</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mitocondrial">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mitocondrial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mitocondrial is a rare form of diabetes mellitus, accounting for less than 1% of cases in children and adolescents, often caused by the m.3243 A&gt;G mutation in mitochondrial DNA and associated with maternal inheritance, hearing loss, or progressive external ophthalmoplegia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646892</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Teste Genético">
  <data key="d0">Teste Genético</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic testing is recommended for diagnosing mitochondrial diabetes in cases of diabetes with hearing loss or progressive ophthalmoplegia and maternal inheritance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mutação M.3243 A&gt;G">
  <data key="d0">Mutação M.3243 A&gt;G</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The m.3243 A&gt;G mutation in mitochondrial DNA is the most common genetic cause of mitochondrial diabetes and may also be associated with severe conditions like myopathy, encephalopathy, and lactic acidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surdez">
  <data key="d0">Surdez</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Hearing loss is a common comorbidity associated with mitochondrial diabetes and serves as a diagnostic clue when combined with diabetes and maternal family history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oftalmoplegia Progressiva">
  <data key="d0">Oftalmoplegia Progressiva</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Progressive external ophthalmoplegia is a neurological condition linked to mitochondrial diabetes and is used as a diagnostic indicator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646894</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metformina">
  <data key="d0">Metformina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Metformin is an antidiabetic drug that should be avoided in patients with mitochondrial diabetes due to the potential risk of metabolic acidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention and management of diabetes mellitus and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention for individuals diagnosed with diabetes or prediabetes to improve glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention and management of diabetes mellitus and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention for individuals diagnosed with diabetes or prediabetes to improve glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention and management of diabetes mellitus and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metformina is a medication used in the intervention for individuals diagnosed with diabetes or prediabetes to improve glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Tipo 2 Propenso À Cetose">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Tipo 2 Propenso À Cetose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes is a subtype of diabetes characterized by diabetic ketoacidosis at diagnosis, followed by low or no insulin requirement, detectable C-peptide, and absence of autoimmunity, with clinical evolution consistent with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646894</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peptídeo C">
  <data key="d0">Peptídeo C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">C-peptide measurement is recommended to assess residual beta-cell function in patients presenting with ketoacidosis, helping differentiate between type 1 and ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoanticorpos Associados Ao DM">
  <data key="d0">Autoanticorpos Associados Ao DM</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies associated with diabetes mellitus are tested to determine the presence of autoimmunity; their absence supports a diagnosis of ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Secundário">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Secundário</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary diabetes refers to diabetes caused by other pancreatic diseases such as pancreatitis, neoplasms, hemochromatosis, or prior pancreatic surgery, and is classified as diabetes 3c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doenças Pancreáticas">
  <data key="d0">Doenças Pancreáticas</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic diseases including inflammation (often due to alcoholism or gallstones), neoplasms, hemochromatosis, and prior surgeries are causes of secondary diabetes and must be evaluated through function tests or imaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diretriz Da Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diretriz Da Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a clinical practice guideline developed to provide evidence-based recommendations for the diagnosis, classification, and management of diabetes mellitus in Brazil. Published by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes (Brazilian Diabetes Society), this document serves as a key reference for healthcare professionals involved in diabetes care, offering standardized protocols grounded in current scientific research and clinical evidence.

The guideline encompasses comprehensive strategies for diabetes management, including criteria for diagnosis, patient classification, glycemic control targets, and therapeutic interventions. It emphasizes evidence-based approaches to treatment, aiming to improve clinical outcomes and standardize care across diverse healthcare settings in Brazil. Specific attention is given to defining appropriate glycemic targets and establishing clear treatment goals tailored to individual patient profiles.

While most descriptions are consistent in portraying the Diretriz as an authoritative, evidence-based clinical tool, one entry is provided in Portuguese—“Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes é um documento que fornece recomendações clínicas baseadas em evidências para o tratamento do diabetes”—which reaffirms the guideline’s purpose in the original language of its publication. This does not indicate a separate entity but reflects the linguistic context of its primary audience. Overall, the Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes functions as a unified, regularly updated resource designed to guide clinical decision-making and promote optimal diabetes care throughout Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7841f818e5dcdd6ef3c0c2951cf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3628fc721a312bfbaace1de3a4d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes 3c">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes 3c</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes 3c is a classification for secondary diabetes caused by underlying pancreatic diseases such as pancreatitis, neoplasms, hemochromatosis, or prior pancreatic surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes 3c is a form of diabetes secondary to exocrine pancreatic diseases, often misclassified as type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM2), and associated with rapid deterioration of pancreatic ß-cell function and glycemic instability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe02e01a76e16ee223061696b4bcb10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646896</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Monogênico">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Monogênico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Monogênico is a form of diabetes caused by genetic defects affecting insulin secretion, often diagnosed in young individuals with a family history of early-onset diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646896</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY Probability Calculator">
  <data key="d0">MODY Probability Calculator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY Probability Calculator is a predictive model using clinical and laboratory data to estimate the likelihood of MODY in patients diagnosed with diabetes before age 30.&lt;SEP&gt;The MODY probability calculator is a tool designed to screen for GCK and HNF1A mutations in individuals from a multiethnic background to assess the likelihood of MODY.&lt;SEP&gt;The MODY probability calculator is a clinical tool designed to determine the likelihood of MODY in patients with young-onset diabetes, particularly for GCK and HNF gene mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;A biomarker-based tool developed by Exeter Diabetes to estimate the likelihood of maturity onset diabetes of the young.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stankute et al.">
  <data key="d0">Stankute et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Stankute et al. conducted genetic testing in children and young patients with diabetes and negative antibodies to identify monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shields and collaborators">
  <data key="d0">Shields and collaborators</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shields and collaborators developed a MODY probability prediction model with high sensitivity and specificity in Caucasian populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Diagnostics">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Diagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Diagnostics is a mobile application available on iOS and Android platforms that includes the MODY risk probability calculator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-GCK">
  <data key="d0">MODY-GCK</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-GCK is a common type of maturity-onset diabetes of the young characterized by mild fasting hyperglycemia from birth, asymptomatic and non-progressive, usually without micro and macrovascular complications. It is caused by mutations in the GCK gene, and many patients lack a family history of diabetes due to mild hyperglycemia going undetected. Genetic screening is recommended for individuals with characteristic phenotype even without family history.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY-GCK is a common subtype of MODY characterized by mild, non-progressive fasting hyperglycemia without symptoms and low risk of micro- or macrovascular complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-HNF1A">
  <data key="d0">MODY-HNF1A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-HNF1A is a common type of maturity-onset diabetes of the young with onset in childhood or adolescence, characterized by glycosuria greater than expected for blood glucose levels and good response to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY-HNF1A is a common subtype of MODY that typically shows good response to sulfonylureas for several years.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-HNF4A">
  <data key="d0">MODY-HNF4A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-HNF4A is a common form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young that shows good response to sulfonylureas and is associated with fetal macrosomia and neonatal hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY-HNF4A is a common subtype of MODY genetically related to HNF4A gene mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-HNF1B">
  <data key="d0">MODY-HNF1B</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-HNF1B is a common form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young that may occur without family history in about 50% of cases. It is associated with urogenital malformations, renal cysts, pancreatic atrophy, exocrine pancreatic dysfunction, uterine malformations, gout or hyperuricemia, abnormal liver function tests, and hypomagnesemia.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY-HNF1B is a subtype of MODY associated with urogenital malformations and may occur without a family history in about 50% of cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Testing">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic testing is recommended after excluding other causes of hyperglycemia and can confirm the diagnosis of neonatal diabetes in over 80% of cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing for Type 1 diabetes risk involves determining a genetic risk score, which improves classification accuracy but is less clinically accessible than autoantibody testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing is used to confirm monogenic diabetes and can lead to changes in treatment approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing is recommended for individuals with MODY to confirm diagnosis and guide appropriate treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing is recommended for all individuals diagnosed with diabetes in the first six months of life or those with atypical features of type 1 or type 2 diabetes and a family history suggestive of autosomal dominant inheritance.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing is a diagnostic method used to confirm monogenic diabetes and MODY subtypes, increasingly available and supported by insurance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LADA">
  <data key="d0">LADA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LADA (Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults) is a form of autoimmune diabetes diagnosed in adults under 50 years of age, characterized by the presence of autoantibodies and often misdiagnosed as type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent Autoimmune Diabetes in Adults (LADA) is a form of autoimmune diabetes in adults who test positive for autoantibodies but do not require insulin therapy for at least six months after diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IMC &lt; 25 kg/m2">
  <data key="d0">IMC &lt; 25 kg/m2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">IMC &lt; 25 kg/m2 is a clinical criterion used in the identification of LADA, referring to a body mass index below 25 kg/m².</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="História Pessoal de Autoimunidade">
  <data key="d0">História Pessoal de Autoimunidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">História Pessoal de Autoimunidade refers to an individual's personal history of autoimmune diseases, a criterion associated with increased risk of LADA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="História Familiar de Autoimunidade">
  <data key="d0">História Familiar de Autoimunidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">História Familiar de Autoimunidade refers to a family history of autoimmune diseases, serving as a risk factor for LADA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19939072ec52c9018a4c4b386cfd11b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ICE Guideline">
  <data key="d0">ICE Guideline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The ICE Guideline is a reference document available at www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng18, related to diabetes classification and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c156c40ae38c1b220a3c59d658c17171</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nice.org.uk">
  <data key="d0">Nice.org.uk</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nice.org.uk is the website hosting the ICE Guideline and other medical guidance resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c156c40ae38c1b220a3c59d658c17171</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
