  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a clinical guideline document published by the Brazilian Diabetes Society, also known as Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes. It serves as a comprehensive reference for the diagnosis, classification, and management of diabetes mellitus, particularly within the Brazilian healthcare context. The guideline is regularly updated to reflect current medical evidence and population-specific research, ensuring its relevance and applicability to clinical practice in Brazil.

The Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes provides evidence-based recommendations grounded in various glycemic markers and epidemiological studies. It addresses key aspects of diabetes care, including diagnostic criteria, therapeutic strategies, patient monitoring, and prevention of complications. By integrating scientific data with practical clinical guidance, the document supports healthcare professionals in delivering standardized and effective diabetes care across diverse patient populations.

As the official clinical guideline of the Brazilian Diabetes Society, the Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is widely recognized and utilized throughout Brazil’s medical community. Its primary purpose is to improve patient outcomes by promoting consistent, high-quality management of diabetes mellitus based on the latest national and international research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c156c40ae38c1b220a3c59d658c17171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f017257ae0e7fcc5a0a1be0ddc435fe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599c535216b129144d3ee7a08cfe646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-GAD">
  <data key="d0">Anti-GAD</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-GAD is an autoantibody targeting glutamic acid decarboxylase, frequently positive in adults with Type 1 diabetes and used to support diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-GAD (antibodies against glutamic acid decarboxylase) are autoantibodies associated with autoimmune Type 1 Diabetes and used in risk prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-GAD (antibodies against glutamic acid decarboxylase) are autoantibodies associated with autoimmune Type 1 Diabetes and used in risk prediction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-IA2">
  <data key="d0">Anti-IA2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-IA2 is an autoantibody against tyrosine phosphatase-related islet antigen 2, used as a biomarker to differentiate Type 1 diabetes from Type 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-IA2 (antibodies against tyrosine phosphatase) are autoantibodies indicating autoimmune destruction of β-cells in Type 1 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-IA2 (antibodies against tyrosine phosphatase) are autoantibodies indicating autoimmune destruction of β-cells in Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-ZnT8">
  <data key="d0">Anti-ZnT8</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-ZnT8 is an autoantibody against the zinc transporter 8 protein, useful in confirming Type 1 diabetes, especially when other autoantibodies are negative.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-ZnT8 (antibodies against zinc transporter 8) are biomarkers associated with Type 1 Diabetes and used in identifying high-risk individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-ZnT8 (antibodies against zinc transporter 8) are biomarkers associated with Type 1 Diabetes and used in identifying high-risk individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-Insulin refers to autoantibodies against insulin; however, they are less common in adults and may be confounded by exogenous insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-insulin antibodies are autoantibodies that appear early in the autoimmune process leading to Type 1 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-insulin antibodies are autoantibodies that appear early in the autoimmune process leading to Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689039</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Ketoacidosis at Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Ketoacidosis at Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic ketoacidosis at diagnosis is a clinical presentation in adults with Type 1 diabetes, often followed by low insulin requirements and associated with obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646936</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Therapy Initiation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Therapy Initiation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin therapy initiation refers to the start of exogenous insulin treatment, after which patients may develop antibodies interfering with anti-insulin testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646936</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exogenous Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Exogenous Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Exogenous insulin is administered externally and can induce antibody formation in patients shortly after treatment initiation.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Exogenous insulin is insulin administered therapeutically, which can induce antibody formation and interfere with anti-insulin autoantibody assays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646936</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Diagnosis Uncertainty">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Diagnosis Uncertainty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical diagnosis uncertainty occurs when phenotypic features of diabetes do not clearly distinguish between Type 1 and Type 2, necessitating additional biomarker testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646936</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carr et al.">
  <data key="d0">Carr et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Carr et al. conducted a case-control study supporting the use of C-peptide levels in diabetes classification by comparing results with pancreatic histopathology.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Carr et al. conducted a study demonstrating a clinical model combining age at diagnosis, BMI, and autoantibody analysis to improve detection of Type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lynam et al.">
  <data key="d0">Lynam et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lynam et al. conducted a cohort study showing that adding biomarkers like anti-GAD, anti-IA2, and genetic testing improves discrimination between Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age at Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Age at Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Age at diagnosis is a predictive factor for diabetes type, with peaks in incidence at 10–14 years and 65–70 years for Type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overweight or Obesity in Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Overweight or Obesity in Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overweight or obesity in Type 1 diabetes is increasingly observed, with 62% prevalence in the U.S., challenging traditional diagnostic assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guideline for Diabetes Classification">
  <data key="d0">Guideline for Diabetes Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guideline for Diabetes Classification is a document issued by the Brazilian Diabetes Society providing evidence-based recommendations for differentiating diabetes types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnosis of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diagnosis of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnosis of diabetes refers to the clinical determination of diabetes type, which can be challenging in adults due to overlapping phenotypes between Type 1 and Type 2.&lt;SEP&gt;The diagnosis of diabetes involves classification into types based on etiology, including autoimmune, monogenic, and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomarkers">
  <data key="d0">Biomarkers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biomarkers such as autoantibodies and genetic risk scores are used to improve the accuracy of diabetes classification, especially in cases of diagnostic uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8631f035300b1b65337131c6c6079b19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta Adrenergic Agonist">
  <data key="d0">Beta Adrenergic Agonist</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta Adrenergic Agonist is a class of drugs that can stimulate glycogenolysis and increase blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interferon Y">
  <data key="d0">Interferon Y</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Interferon Y is a cytokine associated with immune-mediated beta cell destruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stiff Person Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Stiff Person Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stiff Person Syndrome is a rare autoimmune neurological disorder associated with immune-mediated diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Down Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Down Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Down Syndrome is a genetic disorder associated with an increased risk of developing diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Klinefelter Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Klinefelter Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Klinefelter Syndrome is a genetic condition in males associated with metabolic abnormalities including diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turner Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Turner Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Turner Syndrome is a chromosomal disorder in females that increases susceptibility to insulin resistance and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wolfram Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Wolfram Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Wolfram Syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by diabetes insipidus, diabetes mellitus, optic atrophy, and deafness.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolfram syndrome is an autosomal recessive neurodegenerative disorder characterized by diabetes mellitus, optic atrophy, diabetes insipidus, and deafness, primarily caused by WFS1 gene mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolfram syndrome is a genetic condition recommended for genetic testing in patients with diabetes diagnosed before 16 years associated with diabetes insipidus, optic atrophy, and/or deafness.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolfram syndrome, also known as DIDMOAD, is a rare neurodegenerative disorder associated with diabetes, optic atrophy, and other neurological symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prader Willi Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Prader Willi Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prader Willi Syndrome is a genetic disorder associated with obesity, hyperphagia, and increased risk of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friedreich Ataxia">
  <data key="d0">Friedreich Ataxia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Friedreich Ataxia is a hereditary neurodegenerative disorder that can be associated with diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Huntington Chorea">
  <data key="d0">Huntington Chorea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Huntington Chorea is a genetic neurological disorder that may include metabolic disturbances such as diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laurence-Moon-Biedl Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Laurence-Moon-Biedl Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Laurence-Moon-Biedl Syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by obesity, retinal degeneration, and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Myotonic Dystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Myotonic Dystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Myotonic Dystrophy is a form of muscular dystrophy associated with insulin resistance and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Porphyria">
  <data key="d0">Porphyria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Porphyria is a group of metabolic disorders that can be associated with diabetes due to enzyme deficiencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Diagnosis Of DM1 And DM2">
  <data key="d0">Differential Diagnosis Of DM1 And DM2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Differential Diagnosis Of DM1 And DM2 refers to the clinical process of distinguishing between type 1 and type 2 diabetes based on presentation and testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Characteristics">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Characteristics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Characteristics include features such as age at diagnosis, BMI, and insulin use that help differentiate diabetes types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age At Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Age At Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Age At Diagnosis is a predictive factor used in differentiating type 1 from type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Use">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Use refers to the requirement and timing of insulin therapy, a key factor in diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time To Insulin Therapy Initiation">
  <data key="d0">Time To Insulin Therapy Initiation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time To Insulin Therapy Initiation is a clinical predictor for distinguishing between type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shields Et Al">
  <data key="d0">Shields Et Al</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shields et al. conducted a meta-analysis evaluating clinical predictors for differentiating type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Royal College Of General Practitioners National Health Service Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Royal College Of General Practitioners National Health Service Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Royal College of General Practitioners National Health Service Diabetes provides guidelines for classifying diabetes based on clinical criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketosis Prone Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Ketosis Prone Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketosis Prone Type 2 Diabetes is a subtype of type 2 diabetes that presents with ketoacidosis, often in children and adolescents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AABBCC System">
  <data key="d0">AABBCC System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The AABBCC System is a proposed framework to assist in the differential diagnosis between type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646943</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Presentation">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Presentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Presentation refers to the signs and symptoms exhibited by patients that guide diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646943</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta Cell Destruction">
  <data key="d0">Beta Cell Destruction</data>
  <data key="d1">biologicalprocess</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta Cell Destruction refers to the pathological loss of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, associated with type 1 diabetes and certain toxins or infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary Diabetes is a form of diabetes that arises as a consequence of other diseases or conditions, such as infections or genetic syndromes.&lt;SEP&gt;Secondary diabetes is diabetes classified as resulting from pancreatic diseases, particularly in patients with negative antibodies and evidence of other pancreatic diseases in functional or imaging tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immune-Mediated Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Immune-Mediated Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immune-Mediated Diabetes is a type of diabetes caused by autoimmune destruction of pancreatic beta cells, including type 1 diabetes and rare syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Syndromes Associated With Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Syndromes Associated With Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic Syndromes Associated With Diabetes refers to a group of inherited disorders that increase the risk of developing diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-KCNJ11">
  <data key="d0">MODY-KCNJ11</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-KCNJ11 is a type of maturity-onset diabetes of the young that shows response to sulfonylureas and is caused by mutations in the KCNJ11 gene, which encodes a potassium inwardly rectifying channel subfamily J member 11.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-ABCC8">
  <data key="d0">MODY-ABCC8</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-ABCC8 is a type of maturity-onset diabetes of the young that responds to sulfonylureas and is caused by mutations in the ABCC8 gene, which encodes an ATP-binding cassette subfamily C member 8.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-PDX1">
  <data key="d0">MODY-PDX1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-PDX1 is a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young associated with diabetes and partial pancreatic agenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-CEL">
  <data key="d0">MODY-CEL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-CEL is a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young associated with pancreatic atrophy, dyslipidemia, and exocrine insufficiency, with few cases described.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-NEUROD1">
  <data key="d0">MODY-NEUROD1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-NEUROD1 is a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young with few reported cases, caused by mutations in the NEUROD1 gene involved in neurogenic differentiation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MODY-INS">
  <data key="d0">MODY-INS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY-INS is a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young with few cases described, associated with mutations in the INS gene encoding insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="APPL1">
  <data key="d0">APPL1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">APPL1 is a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young with few cases described, associated with mutations in the APPL1 gene encoding an adaptor protein involved in signaling pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;APPL1 encodes an adaptor protein involved in insulin signaling and cellular trafficking, and mutations are associated with a rare form of MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GCK">
  <data key="d0">GCK</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">GCK (Glucokinase) is a gene associated with MODY-GCK, where mutations lead to mild, non-progressive fasting hyperglycemia from birth. It plays a key role in glucose metabolism and insulin secretion regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK encodes glucokinase and is linked to neonatal diabetes, particularly in consanguineous families when present in homozygous mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK is a gene associated with MODY, and mutations in this gene can lead to maturity-onset diabetes of the young.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK is a gene responsible for GCK-MODY, a form of MODY that typically requires no glucose-lowering therapy due to minimal risk of complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF4A">
  <data key="d0">HNF4A</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF4A (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 4 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY-HNF4A, involved in pancreatic beta-cell function and linked to fetal macrosomia and neonatal hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF4A is a gene associated with MODY, and de novo mutations in this gene may contribute to the condition.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF4A is a gene responsible for HNF4A-MODY, a common form of MODY responsive to sulfonylureas as first-line treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF1A">
  <data key="d0">HNF1A</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1A (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY-HNF1A, playing a role in glucose transport and insulin secretion, with patients showing good response to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A is a gene linked to MODY, and its mutations are a common cause of monogenic diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A is a gene responsible for HNF1A-MODY, a common form of MODY treatable with sulfonylureas as first-line therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF1B">
  <data key="d0">HNF1B</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1B (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Beta) is a gene associated with MODY-HNF1B, linked to urogenital malformations, renal cysts, and multiple organ dysfunctions including pancreatic and liver abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1B is a gene associated with neonatal diabetes and other developmental abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1B is a gene associated with renal cysts and diabetes (RCAD) syndrome, including uterine malformations and pancreatic dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KCNJ11">
  <data key="d0">KCNJ11</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">KCNJ11 encodes the potassium inwardly rectifying channel subfamily J member 11, involved in insulin secretion, and mutations are associated with MODY-KCNJ11 and response to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;KCNJ11 is a gene that encodes the Kir6.2 subunit of the KATP channel and is implicated in neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;KCNJ11 is a gene associated with neonatal diabetes, where mutations can cause permanent or transient diabetes, sometimes with developmental delay, and is responsive to sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;KCNJ11 encodes the Kir6.2 subunit of the beta-cell KATP channel and is commonly mutated in permanent neonatal diabetes; mutations here may respond to sulfonylurea treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;KCNJ11 is a gene associated with monogenic diabetes, where mutations can lead to permanent or transient neonatal diabetes, often responsive to sulfonylureas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ABCC8">
  <data key="d0">ABCC8</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">ABCC8 encodes the ATP-binding cassette subfamily C member 8, a protein involved in insulin secretion, and mutations are linked to MODY-ABCC8 and sulfonylurea response.&lt;SEP&gt;ABCC8 is a gene that encodes a subunit of the KATP channel and is associated with both transient and permanent forms of neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;ABCC8 is a gene linked to neonatal diabetes, with mutations causing permanent or transient forms of the condition.&lt;SEP&gt;ABCC8 encodes the SUR1 subunit of the beta-cell KATP channel and is associated with permanent neonatal diabetes, with some cases treatable using sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;ABCC8 is a gene associated with both permanent and transient forms of neonatal diabetes, often responsive to sulfonylureas, and linked to mechanisms such as UPD6 or paternal duplication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PDX1">
  <data key="d0">PDX1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PDX1 refers to Pancreatic and Duodenal Homeobox 1, a transcription factor critical for pancreatic development and beta-cell function, associated with MODY-PDX1 when mutated.&lt;SEP&gt;PDX1, also known as IPF1, is a transcription factor gene linked to rare forms of MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEUROD1">
  <data key="d0">NEUROD1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">NEUROD1 stands for Neurogenic Differentiation 1, a gene encoding a transcription factor involved in neurogenesis and insulin-producing beta-cell differentiation, linked to MODY-NEUROD1.&lt;SEP&gt;NEUROD1 is a transcription factor gene associated with rare forms of MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="INS">
  <data key="d0">INS</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">INS is the insulin gene, mutations in which are associated with both transient and permanent neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;INS is the gene symbol for Insulin, a hormone critical for glucose regulation, and mutations in this gene are associated with MODY-INS, a rare monogenic diabetes form.&lt;SEP&gt;INS is a gene associated with permanent neonatal diabetes, where mutations lead to insulin deficiency and intrauterine growth restriction.&lt;SEP&gt;INS gene mutations are the second most common cause of permanent neonatal diabetes and are typically inherited in a dominant manner, requiring intensive insulin management.&lt;SEP&gt;INS is a gene linked to permanent neonatal diabetes, particularly when mutations occur, and may present with intrauterine growth restriction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Neonatal">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Neonatal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Neonatal (DMN) is characterized by persistent hyperglycemia onset within the first six months of life, usually caused by a single gene mutation affecting insulin secretion. Other causes such as medications, sepsis, or parenteral nutrition must be ruled out for diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sanger Method">
  <data key="d0">Sanger Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sanger method is a genetic sequencing technique recommended for evaluating MODY-GCK, specifically targeting GCK gene mutation analysis without using a full gene panel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CEL">
  <data key="d0">CEL</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">CEL is a gene associated with MODY-CEL, a rare form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young that presents with pancreatic atrophy, dyslipidemia, and exocrine insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF">
  <data key="d0">HNF</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF stands for Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor, a family of transcription factors including HNF1A, HNF1B, HNF4A, involved in the regulation of genes related to glucose metabolism and pancreatic function, and associated with specific MODY subtypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd082b3c0d74b1afd1fdd6eb23b6afd4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Neonatal">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Neonatal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus Neonatal is a form of diabetes that occurs in newborns and can be either permanent or transient, often caused by genetic mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Secretion">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin secretion is a physiological process associated with pancreatic beta cells and is disrupted in neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin secretion refers to the release of insulin by pancreatic beta cells, which is defective in individuals with type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin secretion refers to the release of insulin by pancreatic beta cells, which is impaired in various forms of diabetes, including pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Cells">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic cells, particularly beta cells, are responsible for insulin secretion and are involved in the pathophysiology of neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemia Neonatal">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemia Neonatal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemia neonatal refers to high blood sugar levels in newborns and must be differentiated from other causes when diagnosing neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Adrenergic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Adrenergic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-adrenergic agents are medications that may contribute to neonatal hyperglycemia and are considered in differential diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sepsis">
  <data key="d0">Sepsis</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Sepsis is a condition that can lead to neonatal hyperglycemia and must be excluded before confirming a diagnosis of neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parenteral Nutrition">
  <data key="d0">Parenteral Nutrition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Parenteral nutrition is a medical intervention that can induce hyperglycemia in neonates and is considered a non-genetic cause.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Panel For Neonatal Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Panel For Neonatal Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A genetic panel for neonatal diabetes is used to identify specific gene mutations and provides diagnostic confirmation in more than 80% of cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonylurea">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonylurea</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonylurea is a treatment alternative to insulin for children with activating mutations in KATP channel genes, effective in about 90% of such cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KATP Channels">
  <data key="d0">KATP Channels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">KATP channels are ATP-dependent potassium channels in beta cell membranes encoded by ABCC8 and KCNJ11 genes, whose mutations are linked to neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EIF2AK3">
  <data key="d0">EIF2AK3</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">EIF2AK3 encodes a kinase involved in protein synthesis regulation and is associated with Wolcott-Rallison syndrome, a syndromic form of neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;EIF2AK3 is a gene linked to Wolcott-Rallison syndrome, characterized by epiphyseal dysplasia, pancreatic exocrine insufficiency, and permanent insulin-requiring diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FOXP3">
  <data key="d0">FOXP3</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">FOXP3 is a gene associated with autoimmune regulation and may be involved in neonatal diabetes with autoimmune features.&lt;SEP&gt;FOXP3 is an X-linked gene associated with IPEX syndrome, which includes autoimmune diabetes, thyroid disease, and dermatitis, requiring insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="STAT3">
  <data key="d0">STAT3</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">STAT3 is a signaling molecule gene that, when altered, may be linked to neonatal diabetes with autoimmune manifestations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LBRA">
  <data key="d0">LBRA</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">LBRA (LPS-responsive and beige-like anchor protein) is a gene potentially associated with neonatal diabetes and immune dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chromosome 6q24">
  <data key="d0">Chromosome 6q24</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Chromosome 6q24 is a genomic region where imprinting abnormalities cause approximately two-thirds of transient neonatal diabetes cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wolcott-Rallison Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Wolcott-Rallison Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Wolcott-Rallison syndrome is a rare autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the EIF2AK3 gene, characterized by neonatal diabetes and multiple systemic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolcott-Rallison syndrome is a rare autosomal recessive disorder caused by EIF2AK3 mutations, characterized by epiphyseal dysplasia, exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, and permanent insulin-requiring diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WFS1">
  <data key="d0">WFS1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">WFS1 is the gene most commonly mutated in Wolfram syndrome, accounting for about 90% of cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brazilian Diabetes Society Guideline">
  <data key="d0">Brazilian Diabetes Society Guideline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brazilian Diabetes Society Guideline provides clinical recommendations for the classification and genetic testing of diabetes, including neonatal and syndromic forms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Mutation">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A genetic mutation is a change in the DNA sequence that can lead to diseases such as neonatal diabetes and is often monogenic in origin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b31a7157123c058dcd7f3c29001cd7f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exocrine Pancreatic Disease">
  <data key="d0">Exocrine Pancreatic Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exocrine pancreatic disease includes conditions such as alcoholism and biliary lithiasis, which can lead to secondary diabetes, also known as diabetes 3c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partial Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Partial Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial lipodystrophy is primarily caused by heterozygous mutations in the LMNA and PPARG genes, with other associated genes including AKT2 and PLIN1, and is characterized by fat loss in lower limbs and variable fat accumulation in the abdomen, face, and neck.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BSCL2">
  <data key="d0">BSCL2</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">BSCL2 is a gene linked to congenital generalized lipodystrophy, with mutations occurring in homozygous or compound heterozygous states in most cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAV1">
  <data key="d0">CAV1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">CAV1 is a gene that may be associated with congenital generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PPARG">
  <data key="d0">PPARG</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PPARG is a gene in which heterozygous mutations contribute to partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PLIN1">
  <data key="d0">PLIN1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PLIN1 is a gene associated with partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Reverse transcriptase inhibitors, including lamivudina, zidovudina, and estavudina, are antiretroviral medications linked to acquired lipodystrophy in HIV patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamivudina">
  <data key="d0">Lamivudina</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamivudina is a reverse transcriptase inhibitor used in HIV treatment and associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zidovudina">
  <data key="d0">Zidovudina</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Zidovudina is a reverse transcriptase inhibitor used in HIV therapy and associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estavudina">
  <data key="d0">Estavudina</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Estavudina is a reverse transcriptase inhibitor linked to the development of lipodystrophy in HIV patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skinfold Thickness Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Skinfold Thickness Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Skinfold thickness measurement is a technique used to quantify and characterize loss of body fat, particularly useful in identifying lipodystrophy when values are below 10 mm in men and 22 mm in women on the anterior thigh.&lt;SEP&gt;Skinfold thickness measurement is a method used to quantify and characterize loss of body fat; values below 10 mm in men and 22 mm in women on the anterior thigh suggest lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcoholism">
  <data key="d0">Alcoholism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcoholism is a condition related to exocrine pancreatic disease and is a potential cause of secondary diabetes, also known as diabetes 3c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biliary Lithiasis">
  <data key="d0">Biliary Lithiasis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biliary lithiasis is a condition that can lead to exocrine pancreatic disease and is associated with the development of diabetes 3c.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Medications">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemic medications are drugs capable of inducing hyperglycemia and should be considered in the differential diagnosis of diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acromegaly">
  <data key="d0">Acromegaly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acromegaly is an endocrinopathy that can lead to hyperglycemia and should be evaluated in cases of uncertain diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatitis B">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis B</data>
  <data key="d1">infection</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatitis B is an infection that may contribute to hyperglycemia and should be considered in the evaluation of diabetes etiology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemochromatosis">
  <data key="d0">Hemochromatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemochromatosis is a condition that can lead to diabetes due to pancreatic damage and is listed as a cause of secondary diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemochromatosis is a condition involving iron overload and is listed as one of the causes of pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DEXA">
  <data key="d0">DEXA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA) is an imaging method used to evaluate body composition and assess partial lipodystrophy, especially in relation to diabetes mellitus, by calculating the ratio of trunk fat percentage to lower limb fat percentage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trunk Fat Percentage To Lower Limb Fat Percentage Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Trunk Fat Percentage To Lower Limb Fat Percentage Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">This ratio, derived from DEXA scans, helps identify partial lipodystrophy; a value greater than or equal to 1.5 is present in most cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AABBCC Approach">
  <data key="d0">AABBCC Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The AABBCC approach is a classification framework for diabetes that considers Age, Autoimmunity, BMI, Background (family history), Control of diabetes, and Comorbidities to guide diagnosis and therapeutic decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoimmunity">
  <data key="d0">Autoimmunity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoimmunity in diabetes refers to the presence of positive autoantibodies and/or personal or family history of autoimmune conditions such as thyroid disease, celiac disease, or autoimmune adrenalitis, supporting a diagnosis of type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Comorbidities">
  <data key="d0">Comorbidities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comorbidities such as cardiac or renal diseases impact therapeutic approaches and treatment goals in diabetes management, regardless of autoimmune status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random C-Peptide">
  <data key="d0">Random C-Peptide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Random C-peptide is a biomarker used to assess pancreatic beta-cell function and aid in differentiating between types of diabetes mellitus.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Random C-peptide level is a biomarker used in diagnosing diabetes subtypes; a level below 0.6 ng/ml after five years of diabetes duration suggests type 1B diabetes, while higher levels indicate type 2 or monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Monogenico">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Monogenico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes monogenico is a form of diabetes recommended to be suspected in patients with hyperglycemia onset before age 25 and a family history of diabetes in two or three generations before age 25, with negative autoantibodies and detectable C-peptide above 0.6 ng/ml after five years of diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PeerJ">
  <data key="d0">PeerJ</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">PeerJ is a journal that published a 2020 retrospective study on a diagnostic tool for autoimmune diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UNITED Study Team">
  <data key="d0">UNITED Study Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The UNITED study team conducted a population-based assessment to evaluate a biomarker-based screening pathway for diagnosing monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adult-Onset Autoimmune Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Adult-Onset Autoimmune Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adult-onset autoimmune diabetes refers to autoimmune forms of diabetes diagnosed in adults, including latent autoimmune diabetes in adults and other antibody-positive types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precision Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Precision Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Precision therapy refers to targeted treatment approaches based on genetic and molecular diagnosis, used in managing diabetes subtypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Study">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Study</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A systematic genetic study was conducted on youth with diabetes to identify subtypes, novel genes, and response to therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Prediction Model">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Prediction Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A clinical prediction model was developed and validated to estimate the probability of MODY in young-onset diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomarker-Based Screening Pathway">
  <data key="d0">Biomarker-Based Screening Pathway</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A biomarker-based screening pathway was assessed for its effectiveness in diagnosing monogenic diabetes in young patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classification of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Classification of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The classification of diabetes includes categories such as type 1, type 2, latent autoimmune diabetes in adults, and monogenic forms, based on clinical and genetic criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The ISPAD guidelines from 2018 provide recommendations for the diagnosis and management of monogenic diabetes in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;The ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines provide evidence-based recommendations for glycemic control and glucose monitoring in children, adolescents, and young adults with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689291</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
