<node id="Ketosis-Prone Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Ketosis-Prone Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketosis-Prone Type 2 Diabetes, also known as Flatbush diabetes, is a form of diabetes that presents with ketoacidosis but shares features with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccde7bd12284b1c344a961b0f935b651</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flatbush Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Flatbush Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flatbush diabetes is a subtype of ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes, observed in adults, including Brazilian patients, and characterized by insulin deficiency that may improve with treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Flatbush Diabetes is a subtype of ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes, typically occurring in individuals of African or Caribbean descent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccde7bd12284b1c344a961b0f935b651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776646970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
