  <data key="d0">Type 3c Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 3c diabetes is a term used for hyperglycemia caused by general pancreatic dysfunction, particularly in the context of exocrine pancreatic disease.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes caused by pancreatic diseases, often underdiagnosed and misclassified, also referred to as pancreatogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
