  <data key="d2">A Valkama is a researcher who contributed to the clinical assessment of islet autotransplantation patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young">
  <data key="d0">Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maturity-onset diabetes of the young (MODY) is a monogenic form of diabetes often misdiagnosed as type 1 or type 2 diabetes, occurring in younger individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY) is a form of monogenic diabetes characterized by early-onset hyperglycemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, and impaired insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF4A-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF4A-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF4A-MODY, also known as MODY1, is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the HNF4A gene, associated with neonatal hypoglycemia and responsiveness to sulfonylureas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF1B-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF1B-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1B-MODY is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the HNF1B gene, linked to renal cysts, genitourinary abnormalities, and pancreatic atrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6q24">
  <data key="d0">6q24</data>
  <data key="d1">geneticregion</data>
  <data key="d2">6q24 is a chromosomal region associated with neonatal diabetes, particularly through paternal duplications involving PLAGL1 and HYMAI genes.&lt;SEP&gt;The 6q24 chromosomal region is implicated in transient neonatal diabetes, recurring in about half of cases and potentially treatable with non-insulin medications.&lt;SEP&gt;6q24 is a chromosomal region on chromosome 6 associated with transient neonatal diabetes, involving genes PLAGL1 and HYMA1, and affected by mechanisms such as uniparental disomy or paternal duplication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 2.6">
  <data key="d0">Table 2.6</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2.6 lists the most common genetic causes of monogenic diabetes, including associated genes, inheritance patterns, and clinical features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders is a reference source providing a comprehensive list of genetic causes of endocrine conditions, including monogenic diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference source providing a comprehensive list of causes of monogenic diabetes and other endocrine disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PLAGL1">
  <data key="d0">PLAGL1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PLAGL1 is a gene located in the 6q24 chromosomal region, associated with transient neonatal diabetes when abnormally expressed due to paternal duplications.&lt;SEP&gt;PLAGL1 is a gene located on chromosome 6q24 and implicated in transient neonatal diabetes, often due to paternal duplications or methylation defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HYMA1">
  <data key="d0">HYMA1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HYMA1 is a gene located in the 6q24 chromosomal region, linked to transient neonatal diabetes when affected by paternal duplications.&lt;SEP&gt;HYMA1 is a gene located in the 6q24 region and associated with transient neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARV Therapies">
  <data key="d0">ARV Therapies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiretroviral (ARV) therapies are treatments for HIV that may contribute to hyperglycemia and increased diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preventive Health Care">
  <data key="d0">Preventive Health Care</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preventive health care in individuals with HIV and diabetes involves standard approaches to reduce complications, similar to those used in non-HIV populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PIs">
  <data key="d0">PIs</data>
  <data key="d1">drug</data>
  <data key="d2">Protease Inhibitors (PIs) are antiretroviral agents associated with insulin resistance, increased diabetes risk, and potential pancreatic beta-cell apoptosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRTIs">
  <data key="d0">NRTIs</data>
  <data key="d1">drug</data>
  <data key="d2">Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors (NRTIs) are antiretroviral drugs that affect fat distribution and contribute to insulin resistance in people with HIV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic B-Cells">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic B-Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic beta-cells are involved in insulin production and may undergo apoptosis due to the effects of PIs in people with HIV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARV-Associated Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">ARV-Associated Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">ARV-associated hyperglycemia refers to elevated blood glucose levels caused by certain antiretroviral agents, which may require discontinuation of the drug if alternatives are available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antihyperglycemic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Antihyperglycemic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">drug</data>
  <data key="d2">Antihyperglycemic agents are medications used to manage high blood glucose levels in individuals with HIV and diabetes when lifestyle changes or ARV adjustments are insufficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Testing Interval">
  <data key="d0">Testing Interval</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The testing interval for diabetes screening is not clearly defined, though a 3-year interval is suggested to balance false positives and timely retesting, with shorter intervals considered for high-risk individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Community Screening">
  <data key="d0">Community Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Community screening for diabetes is generally not recommended outside healthcare settings due to poor follow-up, but may be considered if a referral system is in place.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Care Setting">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A health care setting is the recommended environment for diabetes screening to ensure proper follow-up and treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Referral System">
  <data key="d0">Referral System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An adequate referral system is necessary to support community screening by ensuring individuals with positive results receive appropriate follow-up care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dental Practices">
  <data key="d0">Dental Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Dental practices are being explored as potential sites for diabetes screening due to the association between periodontal disease and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Periodontal Disease">
  <data key="d0">Periodontal Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Periodontal disease is linked to diabetes and serves as a rationale for exploring diabetes screening in dental settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 14">
  <data key="d0">Section 14</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 14, titled “Children and Adolescents,” contains additional information on type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CVD Events">
  <data key="d0">CVD Events</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">CVD events include heart attacks and strokes, which are outcomes studied in diabetes intervention trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preconception Screening">
  <data key="d0">Preconception Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preconception screening is a health assessment performed before pregnancy, shown to have cost and health benefits using probabilistic models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening For Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Screening For Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening for diabetes involves testing asymptomatic individuals to detect diabetes or prediabetes early, particularly in high-risk groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intensive Multifactorial Intervention">
  <data key="d0">Intensive Multifactorial Intervention</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intensive multifactorial intervention is a treatment approach targeting multiple risk factors for diabetes and cardiovascular disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Routine Diabetes Care">
  <data key="d0">Routine Diabetes Care</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Routine diabetes care refers to standard clinical management of diabetes without intensive, protocol-driven interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computer Simulation Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Computer Simulation Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Computer simulation modeling is used to estimate the long-term health and economic benefits of early diabetes diagnosis and treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost-Effectiveness">
  <data key="d0">Cost-Effectiveness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost-effectiveness in diabetes screening refers to the economic efficiency of screening programs, often measured in quality-adjusted life years.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost-effectiveness refers to the economic efficiency of GDM screening methods, with systematic reviews suggesting the one-step method may be more cost-effective despite identifying more cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality-Adjusted Life Year">
  <data key="d0">Quality-Adjusted Life Year</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality-adjusted life year (QALY) is a measure used in economic evaluations to quantify the health benefits of medical interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asian American Population">
  <data key="d0">Asian American Population</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">The Asian American population has a higher risk of diabetes at lower BMI levels, prompting recommendations for lower BMI screening thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="African American Population">
  <data key="d0">African American Population</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">The African American population may have equivalent diabetes risk at lower BMI levels compared to non-Hispanic White individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Hispanic White Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Non-Hispanic White Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-Hispanic White individuals are a reference group in studies assessing BMI and diabetes risk across ethnicities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiazide Diuretics">
  <data key="d0">Thiazide Diuretics</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiazide diuretics are a class of medications associated with increased diabetes risk and are considered in screening decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647359</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV Medications">
  <data key="d0">HIV Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">medication</data>
  <data key="d2">Certain HIV medications, including some antiretrovirals, are linked to higher diabetes risk and influence screening recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthy Nutrition">
  <data key="d0">Healthy Nutrition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthy nutrition is a lifestyle intervention recommended for managing prediabetes and reducing diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peterson Et Al.">
  <data key="d0">Peterson Et Al.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Peterson et al. conducted a study using a probabilistic model to demonstrate the benefits of preconception screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Of Childbearing Age">
  <data key="d0">Children Of Childbearing Age</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Children of childbearing age refers to individuals within a reproductive age range who may be underdiagnosed for certain health conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Randomized Controlled Trial">
  <data key="d0">European Randomized Controlled Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A large European randomized controlled trial compared diabetes screening with intensive multifactorial intervention versus routine care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centers For Disease Control And Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Centers For Disease Control And Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention is a U.S. public health agency responsible for publishing national diabetes statistics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Committee On The Diagnosis And Classification Of Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Expert Committee On The Diagnosis And Classification Of Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Expert Committee on the Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes Mellitus publishes reports guiding the diagnosis and classification of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expert Committee on the Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes Mellitus provides guidelines and follow-up reports on diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Diabetes Statistics Report">
  <data key="d0">National Diabetes Statistics Report</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Diabetes Statistics Report is a publication by the CDC that provides estimates of diabetes and its burden in the United States.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Atlas">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Atlas</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Atlas is a publication by the International Diabetes Federation that presents global diabetes data and statistics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnosis And Classification Of Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Diagnosis And Classification Of Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes Mellitus refers to the medical criteria and methods used to identify and categorize diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Follow-Up Report On The Diagnosis Of Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Follow-Up Report On The Diagnosis Of Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Follow-Up Report on the Diagnosis of Diabetes Mellitus is a document providing updated guidance on diabetes diagnosis by the Expert Committee.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Prevention Program Outcomes Study">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Prevention Program Outcomes Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Prevention Program Outcomes Study (DPPOS) is a long-term follow-up study by the National Institutes of Health that demonstrated reduced diabetes complications through prevention of progression from prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes Prevention Program Outcomes Study is a follow-up study exploring residual risk for diabetes and microvascular disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Care-Led Weight Management For Remission Of Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Primary Care-Led Weight Management For Remission Of Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to a weight-management intervention led in primary care settings aimed at achieving remission of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Durability Of A Primary Care-Led Weight-Management Intervention For Remission Of Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Durability Of A Primary Care-Led Weight-Management Intervention For Remission Of Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to the long-term effectiveness of a primary care-led weight-management program for sustaining remission of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Surgery For The Treatment Of Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Surgery For The Treatment Of Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic surgery is a surgical intervention evaluated for treating type 2 diabetes, studied through randomized controlled trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outcomes In Bariatric And Metabolic Surgery">
  <data key="d0">Outcomes In Bariatric And Metabolic Surgery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to the health outcomes associated with bariatric and metabolic surgical procedures over a five-year period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647366</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Remission And Relapse After Bariatric Surgery">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Remission And Relapse After Bariatric Surgery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to the phenomenon of type 2 diabetes going into remission and potentially relapsing after bariatric surgery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Effects Of Diet Versus Gastric Bypass On Metabolic Function In Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Effects Of Diet Versus Gastric Bypass On Metabolic Function In Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to a comparative study on how diet and gastric bypass surgery affect metabolic function in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Progression To Diabetes By Baseline Glycemic Status">
  <data key="d0">Progression To Diabetes By Baseline Glycemic Status</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This concept involves studying how initial glycemic levels predict the progression to diabetes in middle-aged and older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Residual Risk For Diabetes And Microvascular Disease">
  <data key="d0">Residual Risk For Diabetes And Microvascular Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to the remaining risk of developing diabetes and related microvascular complications despite preventive interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes And Cardiovascular Risk In Nondiabetic Adults">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes And Cardiovascular Risk In Nondiabetic Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This concept explores the link between prediabetic markers and cardiovascular disease risk in adults without diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Different Cutoffs Of Hypertension">
  <data key="d0">Different Cutoffs Of Hypertension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This refers to varying diagnostic thresholds for hypertension and their association with incident diabetes and insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DiRECT">
  <data key="d0">DiRECT</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">DiRECT is an open-label, cluster-randomised trial investigating primary care-led weight management for remission of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DIADEM-I">
  <data key="d0">DIADEM-I</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">DIADEM-I is an open-label, parallel-group, randomised controlled trial examining the effect of intensive lifestyle intervention on bodyweight and glycaemia in early type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a775efb764958cf67853f275782e2a69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repaglinide">
  <data key="d0">Repaglinide</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Repaglinide is a treatment used in people with CFRD that leads to initial weight gain, though the effect is not sustained over six months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Placebo">
  <data key="d0">Placebo</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Placebo is used as a control in clinical trials for CFRD treatments and is associated with continued weight loss in participants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cystic Fibrosis Foundation">
  <data key="d0">Cystic Fibrosis Foundation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation is a medical organization that co-developed clinical practice guidelines for the management of CFRD.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation is a nonprofit organization that develops clinical practice guidelines for managing cystic fibrosis and its complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatric Endocrine Society">
  <data key="d0">Pediatric Endocrine Society</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pediatric Endocrine Society is a professional society that endorsed the clinical care guidelines for CFRD.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pediatric Endocrine Society is an organization with a Drugs and Therapeutics Committee involved in diabetes diagnosis recommendations for children.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pediatric Endocrine Society is a medical society that endorses clinical guidelines for diabetes management in children, including cystic fibrosis-related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus (PTDM) is a condition characterized by the presence of diabetes following organ transplantation, regardless of onset timing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation (NODAT) refers to diabetes that develops after transplantation, excluding undiagnosed pretransplant diabetes and transient posttransplant hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;New-onset diabetes after transplantation refers to the development of diabetes in patients who did not have diabetes prior to receiving an organ transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppressive Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppressive Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppressive therapy is a major contributor to the development of PTDM but is essential to prevent transplant rejection.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunosuppressive therapy is used after organ transplantation to prevent rejection but increases the risk of post-transplant diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organ Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Organ Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Organ transplantation is a medical procedure after which patients are screened for hyperglycemia and potential development of PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Heart Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart transplant is a type of organ transplantation associated with a 38% incidence of PTDM at one year in a study of 152 recipients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Lung Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung transplant, often combined with heart transplant, is associated with a 19% incidence of PTDM in an Iranian cohort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Care Guidelines for Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Care Guidelines for Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Care Guidelines for Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes is a position statement providing recommendations for the management of CFRD, jointly issued by the American Diabetes Association and the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abnormal Glucose Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Abnormal Glucose Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abnormal Glucose Tolerance is a metabolic condition in people with cystic fibrosis that may progress to cystic fibrosis–related diabetes and is a criterion for treatment intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose tolerance is a metabolic condition indicating impaired regulation of blood sugar, often found in individuals at risk for type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose tolerance is a metabolic condition studied among obese siblings of children with type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose tolerance is a metabolic condition indicating impaired regulation of blood sugar, often found in individuals at risk for type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose tolerance is a metabolic condition studied among obese siblings of children with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e35953dbfdebbbab4bf83ec032ccfb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a109575f50250430ade32316446ee9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688995</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppressive Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppressive Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppressive regimen refers to the drug protocol used after organ transplantation to prevent rejection, which can influence the risk of developing posttransplantation diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-836e865d51bd855e9d073bd7a5ac7657</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Cell Destruction">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Cell Destruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-cell destruction refers to the loss of insulin-producing cells in the pancreas, a key pathophysiological process in type 1 diabetes and some other forms of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="World">
  <data key="d0">World</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The World refers to the global context in which diabetes research and classification efforts are taking place.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Secretory Defect">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Secretory Defect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin secretory defect refers to the impaired ability of beta cells to secrete insulin, a hallmark of type 2 diabetes and other forms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c47356c03c704ef89b9f41bbd939bc8a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PTDM">
  <data key="d0">PTDM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PTDM refers to post-transplant diabetes mellitus, a condition diagnosed after organ transplantation, often assessed using OGTT and associated with various risk factors such as elevated BMI and pretransplant glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dipeptidyl Peptidase 4 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Dipeptidyl Peptidase 4 Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dipeptidyl peptidase 4 inhibitors do not interact with immunosuppressant drugs and have shown safety in small clinical trials for transplant patients with PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="hs-CRP">
  <data key="d0">hs-CRP</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated levels of high-sensitivity C-reactive protein (hs-CRP) before transplantation are associated with increased risk of developing PTDM in renal transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glomerular Filtration Rate">
  <data key="d0">Glomerular Filtration Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Decreases in glomerular filtration rate, common in transplant patients, may necessitate dose adjustments for antihyperglycemic medications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EIF2B1">
  <data key="d0">EIF2B1</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">A de novo mutation in EIF2B1 affecting eIF2 signaling has been linked to permanent neonatal diabetes and hepatic dysfunction, resembling Wolcott-Rallison syndrome but with fewer severe comorbidities.&lt;SEP&gt;EIF2B1 is a gene associated with permanent diabetes that may include fluctuating liver function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Genetics Center">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Genetics Center</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specialized center for diabetes genetics that provides consultation on interpreting genetic mutations and guiding evaluation, treatment, and counseling for monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADA-European Association for the Study of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">ADA-European Association for the Study of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The American Diabetes Association and European Association for the Study of Diabetes jointly issued a consensus report recommending genetic testing for individuals diagnosed with diabetes under six months of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Liver Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver transplant is a surgical procedure involving the replacement of a diseased liver, after which patients may develop PTDM or be treated with medications like thiazolidinediones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney transplant is a surgical procedure where a failed kidney is replaced, and post-transplant patients are monitored for conditions like PTDM and require adjusted medication dosing due to changes in glomerular filtration rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. Preventive Services Task Force">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Preventive Services Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Preventive Services Task Force conducted a systematic review on GDM screening methods and outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Preventive Services Task Force evaluates evidence for preventive health services, including screening for gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agency For Healthcare Research And Quality">
  <data key="d0">Agency For Healthcare Research And Quality</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality funds research and systematic reviews on healthcare practices, including gestational diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Institutes Of Health">
  <data key="d0">National Institutes Of Health</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Institutes of Health sponsored a consensus conference on diagnosing gestational diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BMJ Open">
  <data key="d0">BMJ Open</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">BMJ Open is a journal that published the development and validation of clinical diagnostic models for identifying type 1 diabetes in adults.&lt;SEP&gt;BMJ Open is an open-access journal that published research on the use of glycosylated haemoglobin for diagnosing gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NIH Consens State Sci Statements">
  <data key="d0">NIH Consens State Sci Statements</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">NIH Consensus State Science Statements is a publication series that includes the NIH consensus development conference report on diagnosing gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="W L Jr Lowe">
  <data key="d0">W L Jr Lowe</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">W L Jr Lowe is a researcher involved in multiple studies on gestational diabetes and maternal-fetal metabolism as part of the HAPO Follow-up Study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45a8ca206e61b47964f899c929fbafb3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
