<node id="Teplizumab">
  <data key="d0">Teplizumab</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Teplizumab is an anti-CD3 monoclonal antibody used as an immunomodulatory medication to delay the progression of type 1 diabetes. It functions by targeting the CD3 receptor on T cells, modulating the immune response believed to be responsible for the destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. Initially investigated in clinical trials, Teplizumab demonstrated efficacy in delaying the onset of type 1 diabetes in individuals identified as high-risk or at-risk based on biomarkers and family history.

The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved Teplizumab for clinical use specifically to delay the progression from Stage 2 to Stage 3 type 1 diabetes in individuals aged 8 years and older. Stage 2 is characterized by the presence of multiple autoantibodies and metabolic abnormalities, but not yet clinical symptoms of diabetes, while Stage 3 involves symptomatic disease requiring insulin therapy. The approval marks a significant milestone as Teplizumab is the first disease-modifying therapy for type 1 diabetes with the potential to alter the disease course rather than merely manage symptoms.

Although earlier descriptions emphasize its use in clinical trials to prevent or delay the onset of type 1 diabetes in at-risk populations, the current status reflects its transition from experimental therapy to an approved treatment for a defined patient group. The consistent focus across descriptions is on its role in immunomodulation to preserve beta-cell function and prolong the pre-symptomatic phase of type 1 diabetes. All sources agree on its mechanism as an anti-CD3 antibody and its application in individuals aged 8 and above with Stage 2 disease, underscoring its targeted and preventive therapeutic strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Teplizumab is an immunomodulatory medication approved by the FDA to delay the progression of Stage 2 Type 1 Diabetes to Stage 3 in individuals aged 8 years and older.&lt;SEP&gt;Teplizumab is a medication approved by the FDA for use in individuals with type 1 diabetes in stage 2 from the age of 8 to delay progression to stage 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Teplizumab is an anti-CD3 antibody used in clinical trials to delay the onset of type 1 diabetes in at-risk individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Teplizumab is an anti-CD3 monoclonal antibody used in clinical trials to delay the onset of type 1 diabetes in high-risk individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309ce40527b1cc8f260e96e195742001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a109575f50250430ade32316446ee9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
