  <data key="d0">GLT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Loading Test (GLT) is a screening test using a 50-g glucose dose, used in the two-step method for GDM detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Loading Test (GLT) is a screening method for GDM that uses a 50-g glucose dose and does not require fasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NIH Panel">
  <data key="d0">NIH Panel</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Institutes of Health (NIH) panel is a group of experts that evaluated GDM screening strategies and cited lack of clinical trial data and potential negative consequences in favoring the two-step approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carpenter-Coustan">
  <data key="d0">Carpenter-Coustan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carpenter-Coustan criteria refer to a two-step method for diagnosing gestational diabetes using specific glucose thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Carpenter-Coustan refers to a set of lower diagnostic thresholds used in the two-step approach for the 3-hour 100-g OGTT to diagnose GDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neonatal Macrosomia">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Macrosomia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neonatal macrosomia is a condition where a newborn has excessive birth weight, which can be reduced through treatment of maternal hyperglycemia identified by the two-step approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small-For-Gestational-Age Births">
  <data key="d0">Small-For-Gestational-Age Births</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Small-for-gestational-age (SGA) births refer to infants born smaller than expected for their gestational age, which are not increased by treatment of maternal hyperglycemia in GDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medicalization Of Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Medicalization Of Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medicalization of pregnancy refers to the increased diagnosis and treatment of conditions like GDM, leading to higher healthcare utilization and costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Medicalization of pregnancy refers to the increased healthcare interventions and costs associated with diagnosing a larger group of women with GDM under the one-step strategy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniform Approach">
  <data key="d0">Uniform Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A uniform approach to diagnosing GDM is widely supported as beneficial for patients, caregivers, and policymakers to standardize care and improve outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OSullivan and Mahan">
  <data key="d0">OSullivan and Mahan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">O’Sullivan and Mahan are researchers who originally recommended glucose thresholds for diagnosing gestational diabetes using whole blood and nonenzymatic methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Islet Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Islet Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic islet transplantation is a medical procedure being studied for its current state and future evolution in treating diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Pancreatectomy With Islet Auto-Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Total Pancreatectomy With Islet Auto-Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Total pancreatectomy with islet auto-transplantation is a surgical procedure where the pancreas is removed and islets are transplanted back into the patient to preserve insulin production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Predictors">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Predictors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic predictors are indicators used to assess the likelihood of achieving insulin independence after islet transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Independence">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Independence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin independence refers to the condition where a patient no longer requires external insulin due to restored endogenous insulin production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RADIEL Study">
  <data key="d0">RADIEL Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The RADIEL study investigates the effects of lifestyle intervention on diabetes prevention during pregnancy and the first postpartum year.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carpenter-Coustan Screening">
  <data key="d0">Carpenter-Coustan Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carpenter-Coustan screening is a diagnostic protocol used to identify gestational diabetes, sometimes supplemented with HbA1c testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Pregnancy Care">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Pregnancy Care</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-pregnancy care for women with diabetes aims to improve maternal and perinatal outcomes through systematic interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IDF Diabetes Atlas">
  <data key="d0">IDF Diabetes Atlas</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The IDF Diabetes Atlas provides global estimates of diabetes prevalence for 2017 and projections for 2045.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Prevalence">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Prevalence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes prevalence refers to the proportion of the population diagnosed with diabetes, with global estimates and future projections provided by the IDF Diabetes Atlas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Racial/Ethnic Disparities">
  <data key="d0">Racial/Ethnic Disparities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Racial and ethnic disparities exist in diabetes diagnosis, glycemic control, and prevalence of pregestational and gestational diabetes among women of reproductive age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
