</node>
<node id="A1C Assay">
  <data key="d0">A1C Assay</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The A1C assay is a diagnostic tool recommended by the International Expert Committee for the diagnosis of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Expert Committee">
  <data key="d0">International Expert Committee</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The International Expert Committee recommended in 2009 including A1C in diabetes diagnostic criteria to improve screening.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Expert Committee issued a report on the role of the A1C assay in diagnosing diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;International Expert Committee is a panel that proposed HbA1c ≥6.5% as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes mellitus in 2009 based on population studies.&lt;SEP&gt;International Expert Committee is a panel that proposed HbA1c ≥6.5% as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes mellitus in 2009 based on population studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688944</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B-Cell–Centric Classification Schema">
  <data key="d0">B-Cell–Centric Classification Schema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The b-cell–centric classification schema is a proposed new diabetes classification system emphasizing beta-cell dysfunction as a central feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precision Medicine in Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Precision Medicine in Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Precision medicine in diabetes is an approach supported by a consensus report from the American Diabetes Association and the European Association for the Study of Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Br J Gen Pract">
  <data key="d0">Br J Gen Pract</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Br J Gen Pract is the British Journal of General Practice, which published a study on the accuracy of diabetes diagnosis using practical classification guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagn Progn Res">
  <data key="d0">Diagn Progn Res</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagn Progn Res is a journal that published a study comparing logistic regression and machine learning for discriminating between type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Metab J">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Metab J</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes &amp; Metabolism Journal is a journal that published research on glutamic acid decarboxylase autoantibody detection in latent autoimmune diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f76e40d0d9b4211d8c61a53ea298d0b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="D2d Research Group">
  <data key="d0">D2d Research Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The D2d Research Group is a research team focused on studying prediabetes classification and its reproducibility in contemporary populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prediabetes Classification">
  <data key="d0">Prediabetes Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prediabetes classification refers to the diagnostic criteria used to identify individuals at risk of developing diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnosis Of Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Diagnosis Of Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The diagnosis of diabetes mellitus involves standardized criteria and testing methods to identify the presence of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnosis of diabetes mellitus refers to the clinical process of identifying diabetes based on established criteria, as detailed in the Brazilian Diabetes Society's official guideline.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnosis of diabetes mellitus refers to the clinical process of identifying diabetes based on established criteria, as detailed in the Brazilian Diabetes Society's official guideline.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnosis of diabetes mellitus refers to the clinical process of identifying diabetes based on established criteria, as detailed in the Brazilian Diabetes Society's official guideline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cc90e1dea7f4271dde1545434c62508</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-Of-Care Instruments">
  <data key="d0">Point-Of-Care Instruments</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Point-of-care instruments are devices used to measure HbA1c levels at the bedside or in clinical settings, though many do not meet accepted performance criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647424</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centers For Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services">
  <data key="d0">Centers For Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services provide regulatory guidance, including CLIA brochures related to laboratory testing standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clia">
  <data key="d0">Clia</data>
  <data key="d1">regulation</data>
  <data key="d2">CLIA (Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments) sets quality standards for laboratory testing in the United States.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Youth-Onset Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Youth-Onset Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Youth-onset type 2 diabetes refers to the development of type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents, requiring specific evaluation and management strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sickle Cell Trait">
  <data key="d0">Sickle Cell Trait</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sickle cell trait is a hemoglobin variant that may cause lower A1C levels for a given level of glycemia, requiring alternative testing methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Sickle cell trait is a genetic condition associated with altered hemoglobin that affects the accuracy of HbA1c measurements in African Americans.&lt;SEP&gt;Sickle cell trait is a genetic condition associated with altered hemoglobin structure, which can affect hemoglobin A1c measurements in African Americans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiv Infection">
  <data key="d0">Hiv Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV infection is associated with conditions where HbA1c may underestimate true glycemia, affecting diabetes screening accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection is a condition associated with increased diabetes risk and is listed as a comorbidity requiring diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection is a condition associated with increased diabetes risk and is listed as a comorbidity requiring diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection is a condition associated with increased diabetes risk and is listed as a comorbidity requiring diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Int J Obes">
  <data key="d0">Int J Obes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Int J Obes is a journal that published research on the underdiagnosis of (pre)diabetes due to lack of OGTT testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clin Chem">
  <data key="d0">Clin Chem</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Clin Chem is a journal that published research on the performance of HbA1c point-of-care instruments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clin Chem Lab Med">
  <data key="d0">Clin Chem Lab Med</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Clin Chem Lab Med is a journal that published a systematic review and meta-analysis on the performance of point-of-care HbA1c test devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aids Patient Care Stds">
  <data key="d0">Aids Patient Care Stds</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">AIDS Patient Care STDS is a journal that published research on the use of HbA1c for diabetes screening in HIV-infected individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epic-Cvd Consortium">
  <data key="d0">Epic-Cvd Consortium</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">EPIC-CVD Consortium is a research group involved in studies related to cardiovascular disease and diabetes, including genetic and metabolic research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d27a8dbb6882ee6a732de5ac202d64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey">
  <data key="d0">National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey</data>
  <data key="d1">study</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES) collects health and nutritional data in the U.S. and provided data showing A1C diagnoses only 30% of diabetes cases.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey collects health and nutritional data in the U.S. population, used to study associations such as iron deficiency and A1C levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey is a cross-sectional study conducted in the United States that analyzed diabetes screening effectiveness across age groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689017</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobin Glycation">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin Glycation</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin glycation is a chemical process where glucose binds to hemoglobin, forming A1C, and can be influenced by factors beyond glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV Treatment">
  <data key="d0">HIV Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV treatment refers to antiretroviral therapy that may influence A1C levels independently of glycemia, affecting its diagnostic accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Background">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Background</data>
  <data key="d1">factor</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic background influences A1C levels, including variants like HbS and G6PD G202A that alter A1C readings independent of glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbS">
  <data key="d0">HbS</data>
  <data key="d1">variant</data>
  <data key="d2">HbS is a common hemoglobin variant; individuals heterozygous for HbS may have A1C levels about 0.3% lower than those without the trait.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase G202A">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase G202A</data>
  <data key="d1">variant</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase G202A is a genetic variant associated with decreased A1C levels, particularly in African American individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tanzania">
  <data key="d0">Tanzania</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Tanzania is a country where high prevalence of hemoglobinopathies and HIV may limit the usefulness of A1C for diabetes screening due to lower-than-expected A1C values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NGSP">
  <data key="d0">NGSP</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">NGSP, or the National Glycohemoglobin Standardization Program, provides an updated list of A1C assays affected by interferences at ngsp.org/interf.asp.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Step Method">
  <data key="d0">One-Step Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The one-step method is a diagnostic approach for GDM using a 75-g OGTT and IADPSG criteria without prior screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two-Step Method">
  <data key="d0">Two-Step Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The two-step method involves an initial 50-g glucose loading test followed by a 3-h OGTT if positive, using Carpenter-Coustan criteria for diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NIH">
  <data key="d0">NIH</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Institutes of Health (NIH) convened a consensus panel to evaluate GDM diagnostic criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAPO">
  <data key="d0">HAPO</data>
  <data key="d1">study</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hyperglycemia and Adverse Pregnancy Outcome (HAPO) study is a cohort study linking maternal glucose levels to offspring metabolic outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAPO Follow-Up Study">
  <data key="d0">HAPO Follow-Up Study</data>
  <data key="d1">study</data>
  <data key="d2">The HAPO Follow-up Study (HAPO FUS) examines long-term metabolic outcomes in mothers and children after gestational hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NHANES">
  <data key="d0">NHANES</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES) provides data on the prevalence of prediabetes in the U.S. population.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3-h 100-g OGTT">
  <data key="d0">3-h 100-g OGTT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A 3-hour 100-gram Oral Glucose Tolerance Test used in the two-step method for confirming GDM diagnosis after a positive GLT.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycated Proteins">
  <data key="d0">Glycated Proteins</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycated proteins, such as HbA1c, are used in the diagnosis and management of diabetes to reflect long-term blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iron Deficiency">
  <data key="d0">Iron Deficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron deficiency is a condition characterized by insufficient iron levels, which may influence A1C levels independently of glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron deficiency is a condition that may affect hemoglobin levels and has been associated with altered A1C readings independent of glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Preparatory Diet">
  <data key="d0">Standard Preparatory Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard preparatory diet is recommended before glucose tolerance testing to ensure accurate and consistent results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoimmune Polyendocrine Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Autoimmune Polyendocrine Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome is a disorder where multiple endocrine glands are affected by autoimmune activity, sometimes induced by immune checkpoint inhibitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Immune checkpoint inhibitors are cancer immunotherapy drugs that can trigger autoimmune side effects, including insulin-dependent diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Programmed Death-1 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Programmed Death-1 Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Programmed death-1 inhibitors are a class of immune checkpoint inhibitors associated with rare autoimmune adverse events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Programmed Death-1 Ligand Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Programmed Death-1 Ligand Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Programmed death-1 ligand inhibitors are immunotherapies that block the PD-L1 pathway and can induce autoimmune complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
