</node>
<node id="Butler FK">
  <data key="d0">Butler FK</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Butler FK is a co-author of a study on carbohydrate intake and glucose tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0510d1781e9c07bebd7a7422d453cbf2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Predisposition">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Predisposition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic predisposition refers to an increased likelihood of developing type 2 diabetes due to inherited factors, particularly evident in first-degree relatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Institutes of Health">
  <data key="d0">National Institutes of Health</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is a U.S. government agency responsible for biomedical research, including the Diabetes Prevention Program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.K. Clinical Practice Research Datalink">
  <data key="d0">U.K. Clinical Practice Research Datalink</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.K. Clinical Practice Research Datalink is a database used to study the impact of screening and risk management on diabetes complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening">
  <data key="d0">Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening refers to the process of identifying individuals at risk for prediabetes or type 2 diabetes using risk assessment tools or diagnostic tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9c311fc732ddd262c56ddc696da954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Risk Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk assessment involves evaluating factors such as age, obesity, and family history to determine an individual's likelihood of developing type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Weight Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight reduction is a therapeutic intervention that can improve insulin resistance and reduce the risk of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacologic Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacologic Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacologic treatment refers to the use of medications to manage hyperglycemia and improve metabolic control in individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Weight Loss">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Weight Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical weight loss, such as bariatric surgery, has been shown to lead to remission of type 2 diabetes in some individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Remission">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Remission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes remission refers to the state in which individuals with type 2 diabetes achieve normal glucose levels without the need for medication, often following intensive lifestyle or surgical interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GAD65 Autoantibodies">
  <data key="d0">GAD65 Autoantibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GAD65 autoantibodies are immune markers used to distinguish type 1 diabetes from type 2 diabetes by identifying autoimmune destruction of pancreatic beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peterson">
  <data key="d0">Peterson</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Peterson is a researcher who used a probabilistic model to demonstrate the cost and health benefits of preconception screening for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Journals.org">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Journals.org</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Journals.org is a website providing access to diabetes-related research and clinical guidelines, including content on care and prevention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 8">
  <data key="d0">Section 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 8, titled “Obesity and Weight Management for the Prevention and Treatment of Type 2 Diabetes,” provides guidance on weight-related interventions for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 3">
  <data key="d0">Section 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 3 provides guidance on the prevention or delay of type 2 diabetes and associated comorbidities through behavioral or lifestyle interventions.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 3, titled “Prevention or Delay of Type 2 Diabetes and Associated Comorbidities,” outlines strategies to prevent progression from prediabetes to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 10">
  <data key="d0">Section 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 10, titled “Cardiovascular Disease and Risk Management,” addresses cardiovascular risks and their management in people with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 11">
  <data key="d0">Section 11</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 11, titled “Chronic Kidney Disease and Risk Management,” focuses on kidney disease prevention and care in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 12">
  <data key="d0">Section 12</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 12, titled “Retinopathy, Neuropathy, and Foot Care,” covers screening and management of diabetic complications affecting the eyes, nerves, and feet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4f56a727625747d95bd88ea9712defc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADA Diabetes Risk Test">
  <data key="d0">ADA Diabetes Risk Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The ADA Diabetes Risk Test is a tool used to assess the need for screening for diabetes or prediabetes in asymptomatic adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 2.1">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 2.1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 2.1 is a visual representation associated with the ADA Diabetes Risk Test for assessing diabetes or prediabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="diabetes.org/socrisktest">
  <data key="d0">diabetes.org/socrisktest</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">diabetes.org/socrisktest is the web address for the ADA Diabetes Risk Test, used to assess the need for screening for diabetes or prediabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post-Transplant Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Post-Transplant Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Post-transplant diabetes mellitus is a condition characterized by new-onset diabetes following organ transplantation, influenced by immunosuppressive therapies and other risk factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney transplantation is a surgical procedure involving the replacement of a diseased kidney with a healthy donor kidney, associated with metabolic complications such as new-onset diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Heart Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart transplantation is a surgical intervention for severe cardiac disease, with post-transplant diabetes mellitus being a recognized complication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Lung Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung transplantation is a procedure performed in advanced respiratory disease, and it is associated with an increased risk of post-transplant diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Everolimus">
  <data key="d0">Everolimus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Everolimus is an immunosuppressive drug used in kidney transplantation, studied for its impact on the development of new-onset diabetes after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tacrolimus">
  <data key="d0">Tacrolimus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tacrolimus is an immunosuppressant medication used after organ transplantation, with high doses linked to increased risk of post-transplant diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Hs-Crp">
  <data key="d0">Serum Hs-Crp</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum hs-CRP is a biomarker of inflammation measured prior to transplantation that may predict the development of new-onset diabetes after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European-New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation Working Group">
  <data key="d0">European-New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation Working Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">This working group focuses on research and recommendations regarding the development, prevention, and treatment of new-onset diabetes after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peak OGTT Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Peak OGTT Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Peak OGTT glucose refers to the highest glucose level measured during an oral glucose tolerance test, associated with lower lung function in young children with cystic fibrosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Function">
  <data key="d0">Lung Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung function is a physiological measure that can be negatively impacted by elevated glucose levels in children with cystic fibrosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting hyperglycemia is a condition of high blood glucose after fasting, used as a diagnostic criterion in diabetes, including cystic fibrosis-related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical outcomes refer to the results of medical interventions or disease progression, such as those following kidney transplantation or in cystic fibrosis patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Allograft Function">
  <data key="d0">Allograft Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Allograft function refers to the performance of a transplanted organ, which can be affected by factors such as immunosuppressive drugs and new-onset diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb968add601368451243acd6b2322ce0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreoprivic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pancreoprivic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreoprivic diabetes is a recently coined term for diabetes occurring in the context of disease of the exocrine pancreas.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postpancreatitis Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Postpancreatitis Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus (PPDM) is a form of pancreatic diabetes that develops after episodes of acute or chronic pancreatitis.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ins">
  <data key="d0">Ins</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">INS refers to a gene associated with mutations that can lead to diabetes diagnosed in infancy.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abcc8">
  <data key="d0">Abcc8</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ABCC8 refers to a gene where mutations are linked to early-onset diabetes, often within the first six months of life.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fibrocalculous Pancreatopathy">
  <data key="d0">Fibrocalculous Pancreatopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fibrocalculous pancreatopathy is a rare genetic disorder that can lead to pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatitis">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatitis, both acute and chronic, is a condition that can result in postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus and is a major cause of pancreatic dysfunction leading to diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Islet Autotransplantation">
  <data key="d0">Islet Autotransplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet autotransplantation is a procedure performed after pancreatectomy to preserve insulin secretion by transplanting the patient’s own islets.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fecal Elastase 1 Test">
  <data key="d0">Fecal Elastase 1 Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The monoclonal fecal elastase 1 test is used to assess pancreatic exocrine insufficiency, a distinguishing feature in diagnosing postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endoscopic Ultrasound">
  <data key="d0">Endoscopic Ultrasound</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Endoscopic ultrasound is a pathological imaging technique used to evaluate pancreatic abnormalities in the context of pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mri">
  <data key="d0">Mri</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MRI is a diagnostic imaging method used to detect structural pancreatic damage in patients with suspected pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computed Tomography">
  <data key="d0">Computed Tomography</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Computed tomography is a pathological imaging technique used to identify pancreatic abnormalities associated with pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1c">
  <data key="d0">A1c</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A1C levels between 5.9% and 6.4% (41–47 mmol/mol) are used to screen for early abnormal glucose metabolism in pregnancy.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes-Associated Autoantibodies">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes-Associated Autoantibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes-associated autoantibodies are immunological markers used to distinguish type 1 diabetes from other forms, and their absence helps identify non-autoimmune diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Exocrine Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Exocrine Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic exocrine insufficiency is a condition characterized by impaired digestive enzyme secretion, often concurrent with postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monoclonal Fecal Elastase 1 Test">
  <data key="d0">Monoclonal Fecal Elastase 1 Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The monoclonal fecal elastase 1 test is a diagnostic method used to detect pancreatic exocrine insufficiency in patients with suspected pancreatic diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Function Tests">
  <data key="d0">Direct Function Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct function tests are diagnostic procedures used to assess pancreatic exocrine function and help confirm exocrine insufficiency in postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucagon Secretion">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagon secretion is the release of glucagon by pancreatic alpha cells, which is also lost in pancreatic diabetes, contributing to metabolic dysregulation.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prev Chronic Dis">
