<node id="Racial Differences">
  <data key="d0">Racial Differences</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Racial differences refer to variations in HbA1c levels across ethnic groups that are not fully explained by glycemic control, raising implications for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Determinants">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Determinants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic determinants are inherited factors that influence hemoglobin A1c levels independently of blood glucose, affecting diabetes risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-050dc3a498d3027939b93706cbdb7f07</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GATA6">
  <data key="d0">GATA6</data>
  <data key="d1">gene</data>
  <data key="d2">GATA6 is a gene associated with permanent neonatal diabetes, pancreatic hypoplasia, cardiac malformations, and pancreatic exocrine insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RCAD Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">RCAD Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">disease</data>
  <data key="d2">RCAD syndrome (Renal Cysts and Diabetes) is caused by HNF1B mutations and includes renal cysts, uterine malformations, and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urinary C-Peptide/Creatinine Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Urinary C-Peptide/Creatinine Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
  <data key="d2">Urinary C-peptide/creatinine ratio is a biomarker used in screening pathways to identify individuals who may benefit from genetic testing for MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiovascular Risk">
  <data key="d0">Cardiovascular Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiovascular risk refers to the potential for microvascular and macrovascular complications in individuals with monogenic diabetes, particularly in HNF1A- and HNF4A-MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UPD6">
  <data key="d0">UPD6</data>
  <data key="d1">geneticmechanism</data>
  <data key="d2">UPD6 (uniparental disomy of chromosome 6) is a genetic mechanism leading to transient neonatal diabetes, often affecting the 6q24 region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IUGR">
  <data key="d0">IUGR</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">IUGR (intrauterine growth restriction) is a condition associated with various forms of monogenic diabetes, including those linked to KCNJ11, ABCC8, and 6q24 abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macroglossia">
  <data key="d0">Macroglossia</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Macroglossia is a condition characterized by an enlarged tongue, associated with transient neonatal diabetes due to 6q24 abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age 35">
  <data key="d0">Age 35</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 2.8 states that screening for prediabetes and type 2 diabetes should begin at age 35 for all individuals.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening Interval">
  <data key="d0">Screening Interval</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 2.9 recommends repeating screening every 3 years if initial results are normal, or sooner with changes in risk.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatric Screening">
  <data key="d0">Pediatric Screening</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 2.11 supports screening for prediabetes and type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents with overweight or obesity and one or more risk factors.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk-Based Screening">
  <data key="d0">Risk-Based Screening</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation 2.14 recommends risk-based screening for prediabetes and type 2 diabetes after the onset of puberty or after age 10, whichever comes first.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
