  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neonatal Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d2">HAPO FUS demonstrates that neonatal adiposity mediates the relationship between maternal hyperglycemia and childhood body fat.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pathological Pancreatic Imaging">
  <data key="d0">Pathological Pancreatic Imaging</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d2">Abnormal findings on endoscopic ultrasound, MRI, or computed tomography support the diagnosis of postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647793</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trauma">
  <data key="d0">Trauma</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d2">Trauma to the pancreas is a recognized cause of pancreatic diabetes due to damage to insulin-secreting tissue.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647798</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neoplasia">
  <data key="d0">Neoplasia</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d2">Neoplasia, or pancreatic tumors, can lead to pancreatic diabetes by disrupting normal pancreatic function.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idiopathic Forms">
  <data key="d0">Idiopathic Forms</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa8638b27cbd181b507c81fea49c6f0</data>
  <data key="d2">Idiopathic forms of pancreatic dysfunction are a category of pancreatic diabetes where the underlying cause is not identified.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776647801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ANVISA">
  <data key="d0">ANVISA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ANVISA is the Brazilian regulatory agency that has not yet approved immunomodulatory medications for type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;ANVISA is the Brazilian regulatory agency that has not yet approved immunomodulatory medications for type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes Stage 1">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 1 is characterized by the presence of two or more positive autoantibodies without glycemic abnormalities and is asymptomatic.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 Diabetes Stage 1 is characterized by the presence of two or more positive autoantibodies without glycemic abnormalities and is asymptomatic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes Stage 2">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 2 is characterized by two or more positive autoantibodies with mild dysglycemia but without diabetes criteria and is asymptomatic.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 Diabetes Stage 2 is characterized by two or more positive autoantibodies with mild dysglycemia but without diabetes criteria and is asymptomatic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes Stage 3">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 Diabetes Stage 3 is defined by positive autoantibodies, hyperglycemia meeting diabetes criteria, and clinical symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 Diabetes Stage 3 is defined by positive autoantibodies, hyperglycemia meeting diabetes criteria, and clinical symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoantibody Screening">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibody Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibody screening is used to detect preclinical stages of type 1 diabetes and requires confirmation through test repetition in case of positive results.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoantibody screening is used to detect preclinical stages of type 1 diabetes and requires confirmation through test repetition in case of positive results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Universal Screening">
  <data key="d0">Universal Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Universal screening for preclinical type 1 diabetes is proposed in some countries to delay or prevent stage 3 diabetes and provide diabetes education, but is not currently recommended in Brazil due to cost and lack of approved treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Universal screening for preclinical type 1 diabetes is proposed in some countries to delay or prevent stage 3 diabetes and provide diabetes education, but is not currently recommended in Brazil due to cost and lack of approved treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dad8318811ce10b7f639b13057d611f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TTGO 1h">
  <data key="d0">TTGO 1h</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO-1h is a diagnostic method used to measure blood glucose levels one hour after glucose ingestion, showing high reproducibility and sensitivity for early detection of type 2 diabetes and prediabetes.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is a diagnostic method used to measure blood glucose levels one hour after glucose ingestion, showing high reproducibility and sensitivity for early detection of type 2 diabetes and prediabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TTGO 2h">
  <data key="d0">TTGO 2h</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO-2h is a diagnostic method measuring blood glucose levels two hours after glucose ingestion, previously used as a standard for diagnosing type 2 diabetes but found to be less timely than TTGO-1h.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-2h is a diagnostic method measuring blood glucose levels two hours after glucose ingestion, previously used as a standard for diagnosing type 2 diabetes but found to be less timely than TTGO-1h.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="San Antonio Heart Study">
  <data key="d0">San Antonio Heart Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The San Antonio Heart Study is a long-term prospective study involving Mexican Americans to assess cardiovascular and metabolic disease risk, including type 2 diabetes development.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The San Antonio Heart Study showed that TTGO-1h had higher sensitivity and positive predictive value for DM2 than GJ and TTGO-2h over a 7-8 year follow-up.&lt;SEP&gt;The San Antonio Heart Study is a prospective study that evaluated 1,611 individuals to assess the relationship between glucose levels and the incidence of Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The San Antonio Heart Study is a long-term prospective study involving Mexican Americans to assess cardiovascular and metabolic disease risk, including type 2 diabetes development.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The San Antonio Heart Study showed that TTGO-1h had higher sensitivity and positive predictive value for DM2 than GJ and TTGO-2h over a 7-8 year follow-up.&lt;SEP&gt;The San Antonio Heart Study is a prospective study that evaluated 1,611 individuals to assess the relationship between glucose levels and the incidence of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Botnia Study">
  <data key="d0">Botnia Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Botnia Study is a population-based research project focused on identifying risk factors for type 2 diabetes and metabolic disorders.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Botnia Study compared TTGO-1h with other markers and found it to be more accurate in predicting progression to DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;The Botnia Study is a population-based research project focused on identifying risk factors for type 2 diabetes and metabolic disorders.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Botnia Study compared TTGO-1h with other markers and found it to be more accurate in predicting progression to DM2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malmo Preventive Project">
  <data key="d0">Malmo Preventive Project</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Malmo Preventive Project (MPP) is a large-scale preventive health study in Sweden that collected data on metabolic and cardiovascular risk factors.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Malmo Preventive Project (MPP) is a large-scale preventive health study in Sweden that collected data on metabolic and cardiovascular risk factors.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcce093409f85a2fbec9a754f86c8e4e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TrialNet Study Group">
  <data key="d0">TrialNet Study Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The TrialNet Study Group conducts research on type 1 diabetes, including screening and intervention trials for at-risk individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The TrialNet Study Group conducts research on type 1 diabetes, including screening and intervention trials for at-risk individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The TrialNet Study Group conducts research on type 1 diabetes, including screening and intervention trials for at-risk individuals.</data>
