  <data key="d2">Antipsychotics are psychiatric medications including chlorpromazine, clozapine, olanzapine, quetiapine, and risperidone, associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes through direct metabolic effects or weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Antipsychotics are medications associated with increased risk of hyperglycemia, necessitating diabetes screening before and after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Antipsychotics are psychiatric medications including chlorpromazine, clozapine, olanzapine, quetiapine, and risperidone, associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes through direct metabolic effects or weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Antipsychotics are medications associated with increased risk of hyperglycemia, necessitating diabetes screening before and after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Antipsychotics are psychiatric medications including chlorpromazine, clozapine, olanzapine, quetiapine, and risperidone, associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes through direct metabolic effects or weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Antipsychotics are medications associated with increased risk of hyperglycemia, necessitating diabetes screening before and after use.</data>
