  <data key="d5">1776688945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-Diabetes is a clinical state where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, indicating increased risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes is a condition where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, requiring periodic reevaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-Diabetes is a clinical state where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, indicating increased risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes is a condition where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, requiring periodic reevaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-Diabetes is a clinical state where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, indicating increased risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes is a condition where blood glucose levels are elevated above normal but do not meet the criteria for diabetes, requiring periodic reevaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R13">
  <data key="d0">R13</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">R13 is a clinical recommendation designed to guide the monitoring of individuals diagnosed with prediabetes. It advises that these individuals undergo re-evaluation 12 months after their initial screening for type 2 diabetes. The primary purpose of R13 is to assess disease progression, evaluate changes in metabolic status, and determine the need for intervention to prevent or delay the onset of type 2 diabetes.

The recommendation consistently emphasizes annual follow-up, with multiple descriptions specifying that re-evaluation should occur every 12 months following the initial diagnosis or screening. This periodic assessment supports timely clinical decision-making and allows healthcare providers to adjust lifestyle or medical interventions based on the patient’s evolving risk profile. Although minor variations in phrasing exist across the descriptions—such as the use of "pre-diabetes" versus "prediabetes" or slight differences in wording—the core directive remains uniform: individuals with prediabetes should be re-evaluated on an annual basis after their initial screening. No conflicting interpretations or distinct entities associated with the label R13 are evident in the provided descriptions, indicating a singular, cohesive clinical guideline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R14">
  <data key="d0">R14</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">R14 is a recommendation advising re-evaluation in 6 months for individuals with a single laboratory test meeting diabetes criteria but no other altered results.&lt;SEP&gt;R14 recommends reevaluating individuals with a single abnormal laboratory test for diabetes (diabetes imminent) after 6 months.&lt;SEP&gt;R14 is a recommendation advising re-evaluation in 6 months for individuals with a single laboratory test meeting diabetes criteria but no other altered results.&lt;SEP&gt;R14 recommends reevaluating individuals with a single abnormal laboratory test for diabetes (diabetes imminent) after 6 months.&lt;SEP&gt;R14 is a recommendation advising re-evaluation in 6 months for individuals with a single laboratory test meeting diabetes criteria but no other altered results.&lt;SEP&gt;R14 recommends reevaluating individuals with a single abnormal laboratory test for diabetes (diabetes imminent) after 6 months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R15">
  <data key="d0">R15</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">R15 recommends screening for diabetes in individuals with comorbidities such as endocrinopathies, pancreatic diseases, HIV infection, or fatty liver disease.&lt;SEP&gt;R15 recommends screening for diabetes in individuals with comorbidities such as endocrinopathies, pancreatic diseases, HIV infection, or fatty liver disease.&lt;SEP&gt;R15 recommends screening for diabetes in individuals with comorbidities such as endocrinopathies, pancreatic diseases, HIV infection, or fatty liver disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R16">
  <data key="d0">R16</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">R16 recommends screening for diabetes in patients before and after starting medications with hyperglycemic potential, such as glucocorticoids or antipsychotics.&lt;SEP&gt;R16 recommends screening for diabetes in patients before and after starting medications with hyperglycemic potential, such as glucocorticoids or antipsychotics.&lt;SEP&gt;R16 recommends screening for diabetes in patients before and after starting medications with hyperglycemic potential, such as glucocorticoids or antipsychotics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4</data>
