  <data key="d5">1776689007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R17">
  <data key="d0">R17</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">R17 recommends screening for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents aged 10 years or older, or after puberty onset, who are overweight or obese and have at least one diabetes risk factor.&lt;SEP&gt;R17 recommends screening for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents aged 10 years or older, or after puberty onset, who are overweight or obese and have at least one diabetes risk factor.&lt;SEP&gt;R17 recommends screening for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents aged 10 years or older, or after puberty onset, who are overweight or obese and have at least one diabetes risk factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8707947fb493803b7f3759b0105eda4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R18">
  <data key="d0">R18</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">R18 suggests considering autoantibody testing in first-degree relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes to reduce ketoacidosis risk and enable early intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;R18 suggests considering autoantibody testing in first-degree relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes to reduce ketoacidosis risk and enable early intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;R18 suggests considering autoantibody testing in first-degree relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes to reduce ketoacidosis risk and enable early intervention.</data>
