<node id="Tabela 3">
  <data key="d0">Tabela 3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabela 3 is a reference table within a clinical guideline that provides structured recommendations for screening intervals and re-evaluation timelines for type 2 diabetes and pre-diabetes. It serves as a key resource for determining the frequency of follow-up assessments following an initial screening, based on an individual’s assigned risk category and test outcomes. The table categorizes individuals according to their risk levels, offering tailored guidance on how often they should be re-screened to monitor for the development of diabetes or progression from pre-diabetes.

The primary purpose of Tabela 3 is to standardize screening practices by aligning the timing of re-evaluation with clinical risk stratification. It includes specific intervals for low, moderate, and high-risk individuals, ensuring that those at greater risk receive more frequent monitoring while optimizing resource use for lower-risk populations. By integrating both screening and reevaluation schedules, Tabela 3 supports proactive management of diabetes risk and facilitates early intervention. Multiple descriptions consistently emphasize its role in guiding healthcare providers on the appropriate frequency of testing based on initial results and ongoing risk assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Tabela 3 presents the correspondence between HbA1c percentages and estimated average glucose levels in mg/dL, including 95% confidence intervals.</data>
