</node>
<node id="ERICA Study">
  <data key="d0">ERICA Study</data>
  <data key="d1">researchstudy</data>
  <data key="d2">The ERICA Study (Estudo dos Riscos Cardiovasculares em Adolescentes) assessed cardiovascular risks in Brazilian adolescents and provided data on the prevalence of DM2 and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The ERICA Study (Estudo dos Riscos Cardiovasculares em Adolescentes) assessed cardiovascular risks in Brazilian adolescents and provided data on the prevalence of DM2 and prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The ERICA Study (Estudo dos Riscos Cardiovasculares em Adolescentes) assessed cardiovascular risks in Brazilian adolescents and provided data on the prevalence of DM2 and prediabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TODAY Study">
  <data key="d0">TODAY Study</data>
  <data key="d1">researchstudy</data>
  <data key="d2">The TODAY Study (Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth) is the largest study on DM2 in youth, showing high prevalence in females and strong association with obesity and family history.&lt;SEP&gt;The TODAY Study (Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth) is the largest study on DM2 in youth, showing high prevalence in females and strong association with obesity and family history.&lt;SEP&gt;The TODAY Study (Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth) is the largest study on DM2 in youth, showing high prevalence in females and strong association with obesity and family history.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevalence Of DM2">
  <data key="d0">Prevalence Of DM2</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The prevalence of DM2 in Brazilian adolescents was 3.3% according to the ERICA study, with a 30.5% increase observed from 2001 to 2009.&lt;SEP&gt;The prevalence of DM2 in Brazilian adolescents was 3.3% according to the ERICA study, with a 30.5% increase observed from 2001 to 2009.&lt;SEP&gt;The prevalence of DM2 in Brazilian adolescents was 3.3% according to the ERICA study, with a 30.5% increase observed from 2001 to 2009.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Birth Weight">
  <data key="d0">Low Birth Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Low birth weight increases the risk of insulin resistance in adulthood by sevenfold, contributing to the development of DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;Low birth weight increases the risk of insulin resistance in adulthood by sevenfold, contributing to the development of DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;Low birth weight increases the risk of insulin resistance in adulthood by sevenfold, contributing to the development of DM2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening For DM2">
  <data key="d0">Screening For DM2</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening for DM2 in asymptomatic children and adolescents is recommended for high-risk individuals based on obesity, family history, and clinical signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening for DM2 in asymptomatic children and adolescents is recommended for high-risk individuals based on obesity, family history, and clinical signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening for DM2 in asymptomatic children and adolescents is recommended for high-risk individuals based on obesity, family history, and clinical signs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brazilian Population">
  <data key="d0">Brazilian Population</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brazilian population is described as ethnically mixed, which affects the consideration of ethnicity as a risk factor for DM2 in clinical screening guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian population is described as ethnically mixed, which affects the consideration of ethnicity as a risk factor for DM2 in clinical screening guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brazilian population is described as ethnically mixed, which affects the consideration of ethnicity as a risk factor for DM2 in clinical screening guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescents With Obesity">
  <data key="d0">Adolescents With Obesity</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescents with obesity have a 59% higher chance of developing DM2, as found in the ERICA study.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents with obesity have a 59% higher chance of developing DM2, as found in the ERICA study.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolescents with obesity have a 59% higher chance of developing DM2, as found in the ERICA study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy And Puerperium">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy And Puerperium</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy and puerperium are physiological states that can affect HbA1c accuracy and lead to discrepancies in diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy and puerperium are physiological states that can affect HbA1c accuracy and lead to discrepancies in diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776688996</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Kidney Failure">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Kidney Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic kidney failure is a medical condition that can alter HbA1c levels, leading to unreliable test results.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic kidney failure is a medical condition that can alter HbA1c levels, leading to unreliable test results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
