<node id="Glycation">
  <data key="d0">Glycation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycation is a non-enzymatic process in which glucose binds irreversibly to hemoglobin, forming HbA1c, and reflects average daily blood glucose levels over the lifespan of red blood cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Blood Cell Lifespan">
  <data key="d0">Red Blood Cell Lifespan</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The average lifespan of a red blood cell is 3 to 4 months, which determines the time window reflected by HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemolysis">
  <data key="d0">Hemolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemolysis is the breakdown of red blood cells and can interfere with accurate HbA1c interpretation due to altered red blood cell lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erythropoiesis-Stimulating Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Erythropoiesis-Stimulating Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Erythropoiesis-stimulating drugs increase red blood cell production and can affect HbA1c levels independently of glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Kidney Disease">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Kidney Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic kidney disease is a condition that can alter red blood cell metabolism and lead to discrepancies between HbA1c and actual average blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individualized Glycemic Targets">
  <data key="d0">Individualized Glycemic Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Individualized glycemic targets are recommended based on patient age and clinical status, including categories such as healthy elderly, frail elderly, very compromised elderly, children, and adolescents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metas No Tratamento Do Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Metas No Tratamento Do Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Metas no tratamento do diabetes refers to the glycemic control targets recommended for individuals with diabetes, tailored by age, clinical condition, and comorbidities.&lt;SEP&gt;Metas no Tratamento do Diabetes is the title of the article outlining glycemic control goals and recommendations for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Metas no Tratamento do Diabetes is a section of the Brazilian Diabetes Society's clinical guidelines outlining treatment goals for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Metas no Tratamento do Diabetes refers to the treatment targets and goals defined in diabetes management guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3628fc721a312bfbaace1de3a4d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resumo Das Recomendações">
  <data key="d0">Resumo Das Recomendações</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Resumo das Recomendações is a section in the article summarizing the key recommendations for glycemic control in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Introdução">
  <data key="d0">Introdução</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Introdução is a section of the article that presents the background and rationale for individualized glycemic control in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frail Elderly">
  <data key="d0">Frail Elderly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frail elderly refers to older patients with compromised health, for whom a less stringent HbA1c target of less than 7.5% is recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very Compromised Elderly">
  <data key="d0">Very Compromised Elderly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Very compromised elderly refers to older patients with severe comorbidities, for whom an HbA1c target of less than 8.0% is recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Level 1">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Level 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia Level 1 is defined as blood glucose levels below 70 mg/dL, with a recommended time below 4% for patients with Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Level 2">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Level 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia Level 2 is defined as blood glucose levels below 54 mg/dL, with a recommended time below 1% for patients with Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coefficient Of Variation">
  <data key="d0">Coefficient Of Variation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Coefficient Of Variation is a statistical measure used to assess glycemic variability in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="70 To 180 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">70 To 180 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">70 to 180 mg/dL is the defined glucose range for Time In Range, representing the target glycemic levels for patients with Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
