  <data key="d0">Older Adults With Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Older Adults With Diabetes refers to elderly patients managing diabetes, a population studied for HbA1c outcomes and mortality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children And Young Adults With Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Children And Young Adults With Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Children and Young Adults With Type 1 Diabetes is a patient group studied for HbA1c levels and risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes And Aging Study">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes And Aging Study</data>
  <data key="d1">study</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes and Aging Study analyzed data from 71,092 diabetic patients with a mean age of 70, showing significant risk of complications and death at HbA1c levels above 8.0%.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes and Aging Study is a research project examining glycemic control, complications, and mortality in older diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7203a21c31cbdae88ee8bc33914cd054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study">
  <data key="d0">United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study (UKPDS) is a clinical trial showing that lowering HbA1c below 7% reduces microvascular complications in newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microalbuminuria">
  <data key="d0">Microalbuminuria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microalbuminuria is an early sign of kidney damage in diabetic patients, characterized by the presence of small amounts of albumin in the urine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intensive Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Intensive Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intensive treatment refers to a diabetes management strategy aimed at achieving tight glycemic control through frequent monitoring and medication adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conventional treatment is a standard diabetes management approach, often involving diet alone or less frequent medication adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonilureia">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonilureia</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonilureia is a class of oral hypoglycemic drugs used in the treatment of type 2 diabetes to stimulate insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease">
  <data key="d0">Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease (ADVANCE) is a clinical trial that evaluated the effects of intensive glucose control on vascular outcomes in type 2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preterax and Diamicron Modified Release Controlled Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Preterax and Diamicron Modified Release Controlled Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Preterax and Diamicron Modified Release Controlled Evaluation is the full name of the ADVANCE trial, focusing on blood pressure and glycemic control in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hazard Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Hazard Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hazard ratio is a statistical measure used in clinical trials to compare the risk of an event occurring between two groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidence Interval">
  <data key="d0">Confidence Interval</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidence interval is a statistical range that indicates the reliability of an estimate, commonly used in clinical research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DCCT/EDIC">
  <data key="d0">DCCT/EDIC</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">DCCT/EDIC refers to the combined Diabetes Control and Complications Trial and its follow-up Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications study, which showed long-term cardiovascular benefits of early intensive glucose control in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frágil">
  <data key="d0">Frágil</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frágil refers to a clinical state indicating vulnerability, particularly in elderly patients with diabetes, often associated with increased risk of hypoglycemia and reduced physiological reserve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idoso Muito Comprometido">
  <data key="d0">Idoso Muito Comprometido</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idoso Muito Comprometido refers to an elderly patient with severe functional and cognitive impairment and terminal illness, requiring adjusted diabetes treatment goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adolescente">
  <data key="d0">Adolescente</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescente refers to an adolescent, another patient group with distinct glycemic control objectives in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c %">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c %</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c % is a measure of long-term blood glucose control, used as a key target in diabetes management across different patient groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia De Jejum E Pré Prandial">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia De Jejum E Pré Prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia de Jejum e Pré Prandial refers to fasting and pre-meal blood glucose levels, with specific target ranges defined for different patient categories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia 2h Pós-Prandial">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia 2h Pós-Prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia 2h Pós-Prandial refers to blood glucose levels measured two hours after meals, with a target of less than 180 mg/dL across patient groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicemia Ao Deitar">
  <data key="d0">Glicemia Ao Deitar</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicemia ao deitar refers to bedtime blood glucose levels, with target ranges varying by patient group to minimize hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TIR 70-180 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">TIR 70-180 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">TIR 70-180 mg/dL stands for "Time in Range," the percentage of time a patient's glucose levels remain between 70 and 180 mg/dL, a key metric in continuous glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T Hipog &lt;70 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">T Hipog &lt;70 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">T Hipog &lt;70 mg/dL refers to the time spent in hypoglycemia, defined as glucose levels below 70 mg/dL, with recommended limits to reduce risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T Hipog &lt;54 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d0">T Hipog &lt;54 Mg/Dl</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">T Hipog &lt;54 mg/dL refers to time spent in severe hypoglycemia, with stricter targets to prevent dangerous episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battelino T Et Al.">
  <data key="d0">Battelino T Et Al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Battelino T et al. are researchers whose work was adapted as a source for glycemic target recommendations in the guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UKPDS">
  <data key="d0">UKPDS</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">UKPDS stands for United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study, a major trial demonstrating that HbA1c below 7% reduces microvascular complications in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valores Normais De Glicemia De Jejum">
  <data key="d0">Valores Normais De Glicemia De Jejum</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Valores normais de glicemia de jejum para adultos não gestantes are defined as 70-99 mg/dL, serving as a reference for healthy glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valores Normais De HbA1c">
  <data key="d0">Valores Normais De HbA1c</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Valores normais de HbA1c para adultos não gestantes are defined as &lt;5.7%, indicating normal glycemic control in non-diabetic individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Older Adults">
  <data key="d0">Older Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Older adults are the population studied in relation to Hemoglobin A1c and mortality, both with and without diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Health and Nutrition Examination Surveys">
  <data key="d0">National Health and Nutrition Examination Surveys</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Health and Nutrition Examination Surveys is a dataset spanning from 1988 to 2011 used to study Hemoglobin A1c and mortality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kalyani Rr">
  <data key="d0">Kalyani Rr</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kalyani RR is a researcher who contributed to the study on Hemoglobin A1c and mortality in older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Golden Sh">
  <data key="d0">Golden Sh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Golden SH is a researcher involved in the study on Hemoglobin A1c and mortality in older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yeh Hc">
  <data key="d0">Yeh Hc</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Yeh HC is a researcher who contributed to the study on Hemoglobin A1c and mortality in older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pititto B">
  <data key="d0">Pititto B</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pititto B is a researcher and author of the official guideline on diabetes treatment by the Brazilian Diabetes Society.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1776689304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dias M">
  <data key="d0">Dias M</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dias M is a contributor to the official guideline on diabetes treatment published by the Brazilian Diabetes Society.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-292560db65a76615eea6b62c57efdd3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
