  <data key="d12">1776637724</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Patient">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The patient draws insulin from a vial using a syringe, checking the label and expiration date before use.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage preparation,medication access</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637865</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Suspension">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin suspension is stored in a vial and must be gently mixed before use to ensure proper dosing.</data>
  <data key="d9">container,medication form</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638133</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="NPH Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin vial contains NPH insulin and must be gently mixed before use due to its cloudy appearance.</data>
  <data key="d9">medication source,storage container</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638264</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin vial contains Regular insulin, which is clear and should be used within 30 days after opening.</data>
  <data key="d9">medication source,storage container</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638265</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Storage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Proper insulin storage ensures the vial remains effective for 30–45 days after opening and is kept away from extreme temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d9">shelf life,temperature control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638266</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Vial Storage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin vial must be stored according to specific conditions, including placement in a rigid plastic container and location in the refrigerator shelf above the vegetable drawer.</data>
  <data key="d9">shelf life,storage guidelines</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638268</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin vials are used to store insulin and are commonly used when drawing doses into syringes for injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug preparation,storage container</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a81bec86298f297d9be7cc985a7eddb6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639098</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Vial" target="Insulin Syringe">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">An insulin vial is used in conjunction with an insulin syringe for multi-dose insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin syringes are used with insulin vials to manually draw and inject insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration method,delivery method,device compatibility,dosing compatibility</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642563</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Cotton">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cotton is used with alcohol 70% to clean the insulin vial stopper.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is applied using cotton to disinfect the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d9">application method,cleaning tool,disinfection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638698</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Step-by-Step Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used to clean the insulin vial and injection site as part of the step-by-step insulin injection procedure.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection prevention,preparation step</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The injection site and insulin vial stopper should be cleaned with alcohol 70% to prevent contamination.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection prevention,site preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638166</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used to clean the injection site and the pen attachment area before insulin administration to prevent infection.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,hygiene</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638173</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Insulin Application Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used to clean both the injection site and the pen's connection point before attaching the needle.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638205</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used during the insulin injection procedure to clean the insulin vial and injection site to prevent infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol 70% is used to disinfect the injection site and device connection points during the insulin injection procedure.</data>
  <data key="d9">asepsis,disinfection,infection prevention,preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-afd148f1edc7929cecea8e4d981ed04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas FRASCOS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639124</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used to clean the insulin vial and possibly the injection site to ensure a sterile administration process.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,injection site preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638312</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Skin Care">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% should be used to clean the skin before insulin injection in public or clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,hygiene</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638330</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is used to clean the injection site in institutional settings before insulin administration, requiring full drying prior to injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection prevention,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639178</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Used needles must be disposed of in a sharps container such as a thick plastic bottle to prevent injury and contamination.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1b3b45cb29102851f76174e378f8e0cc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Guia-Pratico-SBD-Canetas-Reutilizaveis-de-Insulina-no-SUS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638010</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Diabetes Supplies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Used diabetes supplies such as syringes, needles, lancets, and insulin pens must be disposed of in a sharps container.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638344</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Half-Full Container">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The sharps container should be replaced when waste reaches halfway to prevent overfilling and injury.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety protocol,waste management</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638345</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Primary Health Care Unit">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Full sharps containers should be taken to a Primary Health Care Unit (UBS) for safe disposal.</data>
  <data key="d9">public health service,waste disposal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638346</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Pharmacies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sharps containers can be purchased at pharmacies for proper disposal of diabetes-related waste.</data>
  <data key="d9">acquisition,purchase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638347</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Medical Supply Stores">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Medical supply and surgical stores sell sharps containers for safe disposal of used diabetes materials.</data>
  <data key="d9">acquisition,purchase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638348</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Hard Plastic Container">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A hard plastic container with a wide mouth, such as a fabric softener bottle, can serve as a temporary sharps container.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative,reuse</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638349</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Plastic Bag">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A sealed sharps container should be double-wrapped in plastic bags for safe transport to a disposal site.</data>
  <data key="d9">containment,transport safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638349</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Children">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sharps containers must be stored out of reach of children to prevent injury.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety hazard,storage precaution</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638350</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Pets">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sharps containers must be kept away from pets to avoid accidental injury.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety hazard,storage precaution</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638351</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sharps Container" target="Basic Health Unit (UBS)">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Basic Health Unit (UBS) provides sharps containers to patients for safe disposal of medical waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The Basic Health Unit (UBS) provides sharps containers to patients for safe disposal of medical waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The Basic Health Unit (UBS) provides sharps containers to patients for safe disposal of medical waste.</data>
  <data key="d9">disposal support,supply source</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5f2616cb245736f951a3dcbf261b3b9b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776688866</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Types" target="Basal Insulins">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Basal insulins are one of the main categories of insulin, used to maintain stable blood glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,therapeutic function</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642544</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Types" target="Bolus Insulins">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bolus insulins are a category of insulin designed to act quickly and manage glucose spikes after meals.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,mealtime management</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642544</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Types" target="Mixed Insulins">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mixed insulins are a category combining different types of insulin for simplified dosing before meals.</data>
  <data key="d9">combination therapy,formulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642545</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Skin Thickness">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Skin thickness varies by injection site, increasing from arm to thigh to abdomen to buttocks.</data>
  <data key="d9">anatomical variation,injection safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637712</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin should be injected into recommended areas such as the abdomen, thigh, arm, or flanks for optimal absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin should be applied to recommended areas such as the abdomen, thigh, arm, or flank.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption efficiency,administration location,application location,body region</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638466</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Cotton">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cotton soaked in alcohol is used to clean the injection site before insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d9">cleaning,preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638699</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="1cm Distance">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Maintaining a 1cm distance between injection sites helps prevent tissue damage and ensures consistent insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d9">site rotation,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638702</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="14 Days Interval">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Waiting 14 days before reusing the same injection site allows the tissue to recover and prevents lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">recovery time,site rotation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638703</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="High Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">High insulin doses should be divided to minimize insulin loss at the injection site and improve absorption.</data>
  <data key="d9">application technique,dose distribution</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639135</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipohypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reusing insulin needles increases the risk of lipohypertrophy, with significant risk elevation when needles are used more than five times.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse, especially more than five times, is significantly associated with the development of lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,correlation,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639099</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Moscow Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the Moscow trial, needle reuse decreased in groups that received structured training and adequate needle supplies.</data>
  <data key="d9">behavior change,clinical intervention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637746</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reusing needles is not recommended as it can increase pain and the risk of infection.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection risk,pain increase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638150</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reusing needles more than five times significantly increases the risk of developing lipo-hypertrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Areas with lipo-hypertrophy are less sensitive to pain, which may lead some individuals to reuse needles unknowingly.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusing insulin needles increases the risk of developing lipo-hypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">causation,medical practice,pain insensitivity,risk behavior,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640290</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needles should not be reused more than three times to avoid complications such as infection or pain.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk prevention,usage limit</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638444</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Reuse" target="Lipohipertrofia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A reutilização frequente da agulha é um fator predisponente para o desenvolvimento de lipohipertrofia.</data>
  <data key="d9">causality,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-202f1dba3a8254f9d5867b459cdbcfa2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640770</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Glicemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemoglobina Glicada reflects average blood glucose levels over time and is used to evaluate long-term glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood glucose control,diabetes monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638300</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Diabetes Mellitus Type 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For patients with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1, Hemoglobina Glicada should be less than 7%, up to 7.5% if there is risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638304</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Diabetes Mellitus Type 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For patients with Diabetes Mellitus Type 2, Hemoglobina Glicada should be less than 7% as part of general management.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638305</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Estudos mostram que o SICI não apresenta diferença significativa na redução da HbA1c em comparação com MDI ou diferentes tipos de bombas.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0f739b5aa260687129c0a88dce08d70c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641859</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobina Glicada" target="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemoglobina Glicada is used for diagnosing and assessing long-term glycemic control in diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina Glicada is used for diagnosing and assessing long-term glycemic control in diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina Glicada is used for diagnosing and assessing long-term glycemic control in diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina Glicada is used to diagnose Diabetes Mellitus when levels are equal to or greater than 6.5%.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,diagnostic marker,long-term monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-19e4dac1289de717e1280645c07b7a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7841f818e5dcdd6ef3c0c2951cf8a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689084</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Variabilidade Glicêmica" target="Glicemia">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Variabilidade Glicêmica measures how much blood glucose levels fluctuate throughout the day, with lower variation indicating better control.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica quantifies how much Glicemia rises and falls, with lower variation indicating better metabolic stability.</data>
  <data key="d9">fluctuation measurement,glucose stability,glycemic control,metabolic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648249</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Variabilidade Glicêmica" target="Sensores De Glicose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sensores De Glicose enable the calculation of Variabilidade Glicêmica by providing continuous glucose data throughout the day.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose monitoring,stability assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648247</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Variabilidade Glicêmica" target="Cálcio De Variabilidade Da Glicemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cálcio De Variabilidade Da Glicemia is the process used to determine the level of Variabilidade Glicêmica from glucose monitoring data.</data>
  <data key="d9">calculation method,data analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648252</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Variabilidade Glicêmica" target="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pacientes com Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 com coeficiente de variação acima de 36% apresentam maior risco de episódios de hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">complicação,controle glicêmico</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689404</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Hipoglicemia">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hipoglicemia occurs when blood glucose drops below 70 mg/dL and requires immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia is defined by low blood glucose levels, specifically below 70 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood glucose level,low blood sugar,medical condition,medical emergency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5acf61a3a7ae9c09040830d5a662f612</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/HIPO_HIPER.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644917</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Tempo No Alvo">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tempo No Alvo measures the percentage of time blood glucose remains between 70–180 mg/dL, a key target in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose range,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638302</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Glicosímetro">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">O glicosímetro processa a amostra de sangue na tira e exibe o valor da glicemia na tela.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood glucose measurement,data output</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638400</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">O valor da glicemia é anotado para ajudar no controle glicêmico ao longo do tempo.</data>
  <data key="d9">data tracking,health monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638400</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia" target="Refeição">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
