<edge source="Insulin" target="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Improper insulin use can cause hypoglycemia, a condition characterized by low blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Improper insulin administration, such as injection into muscle, can lead to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Improper insulin application, such as intramuscular injection, can lead to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Incorrect insulin dosing or administration, such as using a mL-graduated syringe or double dosing, can lead to hypoglycemia, a potentially life-threatening condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,adverse reaction,blood sugar regulation,medical risk,medication error,side effect,treatment effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6a188926df383900f31928c8726a8f</data>
