</edge>
<edge source="Insulin" target="Insulin Transport">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin should be carried in hand luggage and protected from direct ice contact during transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin should be transported in carry-on luggage and protected from extreme cold to maintain stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Proper insulin transport is essential to preserve insulin integrity, especially during travel or changes in environmental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin must be transported in a thermal bag between 2 to 8°C and protected from direct sunlight and extreme environments.</data>
  <data key="d9">handling requirement,logistics,medication handling,storage requirements,temperature control,travel safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8702ff00244abf3caabafff5aad4a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
