<edge source="Insulin" target="Diabetes Type 2">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin is a standard and necessary treatment for Diabetes Type 2 and not a consequence of failure to manage the condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a necessary and natural part of managing Diabetes Type 2, not a consequence of failure in self-care.&lt;SEP&gt;People with diabetes type 2 may require insulin if oral medications are insufficient to control high blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;People with diabetes type 2 may require insulin if oral medications are insufficient to control high blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;In diabetes type 2, insulin is produced but does not function properly, leading to resistance and declining production.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease management,disease progression,glycemic control,insulin resistance,medical necessity,treatment,treatment indication,treatment option</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
