<edge source="Continuous Glucose Monitoring" target="Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Continuous glucose monitoring significantly impacts glycemic outcomes in adults with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM is particularly important for individuals with type 1 diabetes due to their high need for precise glucose monitoring and insulin regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring is used to manage and monitor glucose levels in individuals with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring is used in the intensive treatment of type 1 diabetes to provide real-time glucose data and improve outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time continuous glucose monitoring is superior to flash monitoring for glucose control in patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring is used to manage type 1 diabetes and has been shown to reduce hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring is used in patients with type 1 diabetes to reduce glucose variability through informed insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes management,disease management,glucose control,glycemic outcomes,hypoglycemia reduction,monitoring,real-time monitoring,target population,therapeutic benefit,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4e05859597c5f1693c2f9fe1ef0a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0a49a3e1aba9780862b94a266490691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce5b147555a2c6ba2644e98fb3d31f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c7e3d6615d1076ae20653358419ff4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643709</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Continuous Glucose Monitoring" target="Time In Range">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Time in range is a key clinical target derived from continuous glucose monitoring data.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range (TIR) is a key metric derived from continuous glucose monitoring to assess glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring is used to obtain Time In Range values for patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical target,data source,glucose monitoring,glucose tracking,metric derivation,monitoring method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5647e96fec802433abcc8922a33d23b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f7252ca9147660b04b7329edbe843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eccbaa35bd49db810bbf9c4a8d650469</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689345</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
