  <data key="d12">1776644107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Glicosímetro">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The sensor can replace the frequent use of a glucometer in many cases.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative monitoring,reduced usage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642919</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sensor" target="Você">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">If you have type 1 diabetes, frequent hypoglycemia, or use insulin multiple times daily, using a sensor may be beneficial.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes management,glucose monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642922</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Interstitial Fluid" target="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The glucose sensor measures glucose concentration in the interstitial fluid, which correlates with blood glucose levels but exhibits a time lag.</data>
  <data key="d9">measurement medium,physiological basis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642919</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glucose Reader" target="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The glucose sensor sends glucose readings to the glucose reader, which displays current values, trends, and alerts.</data>
  <data key="d9">data transmission,device integration</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642920</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Smartphone" target="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The glucose sensor transmits data wirelessly to a smartphone, enabling real-time monitoring and alerts through a dedicated app.</data>
  <data key="d9">data transmission,mobile integration</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642921</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Intramuscular injection of long-acting insulin can lead to rapid absorption and increase the risk of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637744</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Removable-Needle Syringe">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using long needles from removable-needle syringes may inject insulin into muscle, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,injection risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Syringe With Removable Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using syringes with removable needles can increase the risk of hypoglycemia due to intramuscular insulin delivery from long needles.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,injection error</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638341</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Irregular insulin absorption due to lipo-hypertrophy can lead to episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood sugar fluctuation,complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638358</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Low blood glucose levels indicate hypoglycemia, detectable through regular testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia occurs when blood glucose falls below 70 mg/dL, and is particularly dangerous if the individual does not recognize symptoms or has a history of severe episodes.</data>
  <data key="d9">abnormal condition,low glucose risk,low levels,symptom awareness</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638367</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Continuous Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pregnant women using continuous glucose monitoring experience fewer episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">monitoring benefit,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638374</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A history of severe hypoglycemia or impaired awareness may lead to adjustments in insulin dosing to prioritize safety over strict glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk factor,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638458</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using a subcutaneous fold prevents insulin from being injected into muscle, thereby avoiding hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">correct technique,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638699</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Leg">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin injection in the leg prior to physical activity may cause hypoglycemia due to accelerated absorption.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,site selection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c897fc79a7dde2715e95be7ca23f57f5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638702</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Patient">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The patient developed hypoglycemia as a result of incorrect insulin administration or timing.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,clinical outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639136</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Safe Insulin Practices">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adhering to safe insulin practices reduces the likelihood of hypoglycemia caused by preparation or administration errors.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical safety,risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639154</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Injection Site">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injecting insulin in active body parts, such as the leg before walking, increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ca576cb8eccfdd91ed235c273f829e81</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte insulinas.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639964</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lipodistrofia Generalizada">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypoglycemia can occur before hyperglycemia in generalized lipodystrophy, with serum glucose often below 80 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose dysregulation,metabolic anomaly</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b4cd4168b98a4b43209b773ecb18d316</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640970</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Medtronic 640G">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Medtronic 640G includes a hypoglycemia minimizer that reduces the risk of low blood glucose by adjusting insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk reduction,safety feature</data>
