<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="SICI">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin pump is a core component of the SICI system, responsible for continuous insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d9">device integration,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641869</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Pump Failure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pump failure is a known risk of insulin pumps, affecting about 25% of devices annually and potentially leading to severe metabolic consequences.</data>
  <data key="d9">device reliability,malfunction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641870</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Hydrostatic Effects">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hydrostatic effects influence insulin delivery accuracy based on the vertical position of the insulin pump relative to the infusion site.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery accuracy,fluid dynamics</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641871</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Atmospheric Pressure Reduction">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reduced atmospheric pressure during air travel can cause bubble formation in the insulin pump, disrupting delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">bubble formation,environmental effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641872</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Insulin Glulisine">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin glulisine has a higher tendency to form fibrils in insulin pumps, increasing the risk of occlusion compared to other rapid-acting analogs.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery risk,pharmaceutical compatibility</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641873</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion System">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin pump is the device used to deliver continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">device implementation,therapy delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641875</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Bolus Estendido">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin pump allows programming of bolus estendido to match prolonged food intake.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosing flexibility,programmable delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641876</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin pumps use ultra-rapid-acting insulin analogs, which provide more predictable absorption compared to traditional insulins like NPH and glargine.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug-device compatibility,pharmacokinetics</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641878</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Subcutaneous Tissue">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin pumps deliver insulin into the subcutaneous tissue, where absorption is more consistent due to fixed infusion sites and reduced site rotation variability.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption site,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641879</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Bolus Bifásico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin pump enables the use of bolus bifásico to better manage glucose from mixed meals.</data>
  <data key="d9">biphasic dosing,programmable delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641883</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Automated Insulin Delivery System">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Automated insulin delivery systems are often built upon insulin pump technology to provide advanced glucose-responsive insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated insulin delivery systems incorporate insulin pumps with sensor-augmented features to adjust insulin delivery automatically.</data>
  <data key="d9">device integration,glucose monitoring,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94e98f4cb6f97fceae5e6d8c30c871b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643724</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Pump" target="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin pumps are used to perform continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion, a standard method in diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion is delivered via an insulin pump for precise and adjustable insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are the devices used to deliver insulin via continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery method,device use,medical procedure,technical implementation,treatment method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49920639f738eae3de220d132cbc081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
