<edge source="Children" target="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 4 mm needle is the safest option for children, minimizing intramuscular injection risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4 mm needle is recommended for children aged 6 years and younger to prevent intramuscular injection and ensure safe insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">device suitability,injection safety,pediatric recommendation,safe injection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639102</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="5 mm Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using a 5 mm needle in children under 6 doubles the risk of intramuscular injection without a skin fold.</data>
  <data key="d9">increased risk,intramuscular injection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637712</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Children" target="6 mm Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using a 6 mm needle in children under 6 triples the risk of intramuscular injection when no skin fold is used.</data>
  <data key="d9">high risk,intramuscular injection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fee4c8681a7629eb6ff0eb2470a98e3</data>
