  <data key="d12">1776688858</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tecido Subcutâneo" target="Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin must be delivered into the subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper absorption and effective glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug absorption,injection site</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-780053d90e5c36ef6ea68e1a598cc53b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638170</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tecido Subcutâneo" target="Cânula">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A cânula é inserida no tecido subcutâneo para permitir a infusão contínua de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d9">aplicação,infusão</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8792cad0fa7c0226f159b670b4e743a1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639184</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lanceta" target="Glicosímetro">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The lanceta is used to obtain a blood sample that is then applied to the glicosímetro for glucose measurement.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood collection,testing procedure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644663</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Intensive Education">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Structured and continuous education led to greater reductions in HbA1c levels among type 2 diabetes patients compared to the control group.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637745</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Pregnancy">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pregnancy can alter HbA1c levels, making it less reliable for glucose monitoring during gestation.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c should be below 6.5% before pregnancy and during the first trimester, and below 6% in later trimesters.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy affects HbA1c accuracy due to changes in blood volume and red cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic target,inaccurate results,monitoring,physiological change,test inaccuracy,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644647</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is a key indicator used in diabetes treatment to evaluate long-term blood sugar control and guide therapeutic decisions.</data>
  <data key="d9">long-term monitoring,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638396</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Complications">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher HbA1c levels are associated with increased risks of diabetes complications such as eye, kidney, nerve, and cardiovascular diseases.</data>
  <data key="d9">health impact,risk correlation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638397</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Anemia">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Anemia can interfere with HbA1c testing, potentially leading to inaccurate readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Anemia can cause falsely low or high HbA1c readings, leading to incorrect assessment of glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d9">inaccurate results,medical interference,test inaccuracy,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644646</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Kidney Disease">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Kidney disease may affect the accuracy of HbA1c results due to changes in red blood cell turnover.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney disease can distort HbA1c results due to altered red blood cell metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d9">inaccurate results,medical interference,test inaccuracy,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644646</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Genetic Blood Disorders">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genetic variations in hemoglobin can lead to misleading HbA1c results.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic blood disorders can lead to erroneous HbA1c values due to abnormal hemoglobin.</data>
  <data key="d9">hemoglobin variant,inaccurate results,test inaccuracy,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644648</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Hybrid Closed-Loop System">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The use of hybrid closed-loop systems leads to improved HbA1c levels, indicating better long-term glycemic control in patients with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641827</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Insulin Pump Therapy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels are used to evaluate the effectiveness of insulin pump therapy in improving long-term glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Improved HbA1c levels are reported as an outcome of insulin pump therapy compared to other insulin delivery methods.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,outcome measure,treatment monitoring,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdbe9f47931df265e815faee2c67f81b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643816</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CSII has been associated with a 1.2% reduction in HbA1c compared to MDI in some studies.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic impact</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-45bbbee62d25d825935842af1930bb44</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641850</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion System">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The use of continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion system leads to improved glycemic control and reduced HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,therapy outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641876</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Insulina Lispro">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In a study comparing insulin lispro to regular human insulin in children, insulin lispro reduced the risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia without compromising HbA1c levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The use of insulina lispro did not compromise HbA1c levels while reducing nocturnal hypoglycemia in children.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic control,outcome measure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6a45688326f1b9dbe3fc7ae4ba51043a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b0164438dcfad197945cf23b924fe86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642344</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is used to assess the effectiveness of insulin therapies in maintaining long-term glycemic control in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,efficacy measure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-157fbe972c55a9a0df76dbef85b43e63</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642364</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reductions in HbA1c levels are a key outcome measure in evaluating the effectiveness of self-monitoring interventions in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic indicator,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-755e9677a7018e4cc382b7d903590786</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643722</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Mellitus Pré-Gestacional">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For women with pre-gestational diabetes, HbA1c levels below 6.5% before conception are recommended to reduce fetal anomaly risks.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,pregnancy planning</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644096</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Mellitus Gestacional">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During pregnancy, HbA1c levels below 6% in the second and third trimesters are associated with reduced risk of large-for-gestational-age infants.</data>
  <data key="d9">pregnancy monitoring,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-820baa925065d77af22437295373f686</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644097</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="TIR">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For every 10% change in TIR, HbA1c changes by 0.8%, indicating a strong correlation between these two metrics.</data>
  <data key="d9">correlation,glucose control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a08dc7008091e5ab01812c301e0aab1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644105</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels are analytically related to plasma glucose levels, as demonstrated in studies from the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker correlation,glycemic monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-aebc875b323050c4274610952a881b57</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644228</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lowering HbA1c is a primary objective in diabetes treatment to improve long-term outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is used as a diagnostic marker for diabetes based on average blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes management,diagnosis,glycemic control,treatment goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689057</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c does not capture rapid glucose spikes, limiting its ability to show hyperglycemic events.</data>
  <data key="d9">detection gap,limitation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644645</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is used as a predictor of future risk of diabetes in various studies.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-05070e0755e36e3375d401400cf75fce</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647718</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Diagnosis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels in early pregnancy are used to detect diabetes and identify women at risk for adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,screening tool</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647733</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Carpenter-Coustan Screening">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is used as an adjunct to Carpenter-Coustan screening for early detection of gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">adjunct testing,diagnostic enhancement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647735</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Elevated HbA1c levels in early pregnancy are associated with an increased risk of adverse pregnancy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical correlation,risk indicator</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647735</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Care">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Diabetes Care published a 2014 study showing that an early pregnancy HbA1c ≥5.9% is optimal for detecting diabetes and predicting adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d9">academic publication,clinical guideline</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4fab467dd1cac7fbb17a945a0aa8240f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647737</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Grupo De Pacientes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Different patient groups have tailored HbA1c targets based on age, health status, and hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical guidelines,treatment personalization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648249</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Mulheres Grávidas Com Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mulheres com diabetes antes da gravidez devem ter HbA1c menor que 6,5% antes da gestação e metas ainda mais rigorosas durante.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,pregnancy goal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648261</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c ≥6.5% is used as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes mellitus, proposed by the International Expert Committee.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus can be diagnosed using HbA1c levels of ≥6.5%.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is used as a primary test for detecting diabetes mellitus during screening.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c (≥6.5%) is used as a diagnostic criterion for Diabetes Mellitus, reflecting chronic hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is used as a diagnostic criterion for identifying Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,diagnostic criterion,diagnostic method,glycated hemoglobin,glycemic control marker,screening,testing,threshold value</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689054</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="International Expert Committee">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The International Expert Committee recommended HbA1c ≥6.5% as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes mellitus in 2009.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic standard,guideline recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689055</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Metanálise">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A meta-analysis of 17 studies showed HbA1c ≥6.5% has 50% sensitivity and 97.3% specificity for diagnosing diabetes using TTGO-2h as reference.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,sensitivity and specificity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689055</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diferenças Étnicas">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ethnic differences affect HbA1c measurements, with individuals of African descent potentially having higher HbA1c levels leading to false-positive diabetes diagnoses.</data>
  <data key="d9">false-positive diagnosis,measurement bias</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8fd2d58abc8f20df1ff7ae241f4cfee7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689056</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diagnostic Criteria For Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels are part of the standardized diagnostic criteria for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical guidelines,standardization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689057</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Kumar Pr">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Kumar PR and colleagues assessed the utility of HbA1c in diagnosing type 2 diabetes in a community-based study.</data>
  <data key="d9">community study,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689061</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Bennett Cm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bennett CM and colleagues conducted a systematic review on HbA1c as a screening tool for type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">research,systematic review</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689063</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Do Vale Moreira Nc">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Do Vale Moreira NC and colleagues studied glycated hemoglobin for diabetes diagnosis in a semi-urban Brazilian population.</data>
  <data key="d9">population study,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689066</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Cavagnolli G">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cavagnolli G and colleagues studied HbA1c measurement for the diagnosis of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cavagnolli G conducted research on the use of HbA1c for diagnosing diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,measurement analysis,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a796990fe8edf70e4463124a0233c32c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689067</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Rastreamento De Dm2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is recommended as one of the initial tests for type 2 diabetes screening, depending on local availability.</data>
  <data key="d9">initial testing,screening method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689071</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c is used in the detection of diabetes mellitus, though it has limited sensitivity compared to TTGO-based methods.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c is used as a diagnostic criterion for type 2 diabetes mellitus, reflecting average blood glucose levels over 2–3 months.&lt;SEP&gt;HbA1c levels, especially from 5.5% onward, are associated with significantly increased risk of developing DM2.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,diagnosis,diagnostic criterion,risk prediction,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689103</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="GJ">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c and GJ are complementary diagnostic tools with strong correlation, though they reflect different aspects of glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d9">complementary measures,correlation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689104</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Hemoglobinopathies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemoglobinopathies can cause inaccuracies in HbA1c measurements due to structural hemoglobin variants.</data>
  <data key="d9">inaccuracy,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689104</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Pregnancy And Puerperium">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pregnancy and puerperium can affect red blood cell turnover and lead to unreliable HbA1c results.</data>
  <data key="d9">physiological variation,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689105</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Chronic Kidney Failure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Chronic kidney failure affects erythrocyte lifespan and can distort HbA1c values, reducing test reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">altered metabolism,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689106</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Recombinant Erythropoietin Use">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Recombinant erythropoietin use alters red blood cell production, impacting HbA1c measurement accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d9">erythrocyte modulation,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Antiretroviral Drug Use">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Antiretroviral drugs may interfere with HbA1c levels, leading to potential misdiagnosis of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic impact,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Blood Transfusions">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood transfusions change hemoglobin composition and can invalidate HbA1c test results.</data>
  <data key="d9">hemoglobin alteration,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689108</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Tabela 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tabela 2 includes HbA1c as part of the recommended protocol for initial diabetes screening in settings with full technical and financial feasibility.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reference,screening protocol</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689108</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Quadro 3">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Quadro 3 outlines clinical situations such as hemoglobinopathies and chronic kidney failure that interfere with the accuracy of HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical interference,test limitation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689109</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Risco Cardiovascular">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels indicative of prediabetes are associated with increased cardiovascular risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">cardiovascular risk,prediabetes marker</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689133</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Pré-Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pré-Diabetes is associated with HbA1c levels between 5.7% and 6.4%.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic range,prediabetic state</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689195</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Variabilidade Intraindividual">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c shows lower intraindividual variability (3.6%) compared to other glycemic tests, making it more reliable.</data>
  <data key="d9">reproducibility,test reliability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689196</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Estudo ARIC">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Estudo ARIC followed participants for 14 years and found a strong correlation between baseline HbA1c levels and subsequent development of DM2.</data>
  <data key="d9">longitudinal study,risk correlation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689199</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes recommends HbA1c as a primary test for type 2 diabetes screening when available.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical guideline,screening recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ff472f3e453a6a19ce0b0606ae3427a7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689207</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels are correlated with average blood Glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,correlation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689212</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Ziemer D C">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ziemer D C studied glucose-independent racial differences in HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">racial differences,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689214</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Selvin E">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Selvin E studied short-term variability in HbA1c and its implications for diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d9">research,variability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689217</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Weykamp C">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Weykamp C published a review on the analytical and clinical aspects of HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d9">analytical aspects,review</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689218</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Gonzalez A">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Gonzalez A studied the impact of mismatches between HbA1c and glucose values on diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic classification,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689219</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabet Med">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Diabet Med published studies on HbA1c as a test for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic testing,research publication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689220</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Ann Intern Med">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ann Intern Med published studies on HbA1c and other glycemia measures for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemia,research publication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689221</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Ann Lab Med">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ann Lab Med published a review on the laboratory and clinical aspects of HbA1c testing.</data>
  <data key="d9">laboratory analysis,research publication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2bc23291d65efde6aaf97a925c92e183</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689221</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Pre-Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels are used to identify individuals with pre-diabetes and assess their proximity to diabetes diagnostic thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,risk stratification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689236</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Metas no Tratamento do Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HbA1c levels between 7.0% and 7.5% are recommended for elderly patients with preserved cognitive and functional status.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment target</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689382</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="NHANES III">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">NHANES III data showed that HbA1c levels above 8.0% are associated with increased all-cause mortality in elderly diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">epidemiological data,mortality correlation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689383</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Cohorte Retrospectiva do Reino Unido">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The UK cohort study linked HbA1c levels above 8.0% to higher mortality risk in patients aged 70 or older with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">long-term outcome,mortality risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689385</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="R3">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">R3 recommends HbA1c targets between 7.0% and 7.5% for elderly diabetic patients with preserved cognitive and functional status.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,treatment target</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689386</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="R4">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">R4 recommends considering an HbA1c target below 8.0% for elderly diabetic patients with functional or cognitive impairments to prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">hypoglycemia prevention,treatment target</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689390</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Diabetes Control and Complications Trial">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The DCCT showed that maintaining HbA1c below 7% significantly reduces microvascular complications in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689390</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The UKPDS found that reducing HbA1c below 7% is clearly associated with a lower risk of microvascular complications in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical benefit,glycemic target</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689391</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ADVANCE trial showed that intensive glucose control achieved a mean HbA1c of 6.5% compared to 7.3% in conventional care.</data>
  <data key="d9">intensive control,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689392</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Brazilian Diabetes Society">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Brazilian Diabetes Society recommends an HbA1c target of less than 7.0% for all diabetes patients to prevent long-term macrovascular complications.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical guideline,treatment recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689392</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Complicações Microvasculares">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A meta de HbA1c &lt; 7,0% é recomendada para prevenir complicações microvasculares em pessoas com diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">controle glicêmico,prevenção</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689404</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Complicações Macrovasculares">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A meta de HbA1c &lt; 7,0% também é recomendada para reduzir o risco de complicações macrovasculares em longo prazo.</data>
  <data key="d9">prevenção,risco cardiovascular</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-60b2f272c0228f3954c05180dd35ce90</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689405</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Estudo ADVANCE">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ADVANCE trial achieved a final HbA1c of 6.5% in the intensive group versus 7.3% in the conventional group but found no significant cardiovascular benefit.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic target</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Estudo ACCORD">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ACCORD study achieved a lower HbA1c (6.4% vs. 7.5%) but observed a 22% increase in all-cause mortality with intensive control.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic target,mortality risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Estudo VADT">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The VADT trial compared intensive (6.9%) and conventional (8.4%) HbA1c targets in type 2 diabetes without significant reduction in cardiovascular events.</data>
  <data key="d9">cardiovascular outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d39cd334b01ad820816bf3cb108c0e27</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689409</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Glicemia Média Estimada">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">There is a direct correspondence between HbA1c percentages and estimated average blood glucose levels, as shown in clinical data.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical correlation,glucose monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689414</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Time In Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher Time in Range percentages correlate with lower HbA1c levels; a TIR of 70% corresponds to an HbA1c of approximately 6.7%.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,inverse relationship</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689415</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c" target="Glicemia Capilar">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Studies show a strong correlation between capillary blood glucose readings and HbA1c levels in patients with type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical correlation,glucose measurement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689416</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GMI" target="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GMI is calculated using data collected from continuous glucose sensors, providing a real-time alternative to HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d9">calculation basis,data source</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644644</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GMI" target="Blood Sugar Control">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GMI helps patients and doctors better understand blood sugar control by estimating average glucose levels more accurately than HbA1c in certain cases.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose monitoring,treatment assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644644</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Flash Glucose Sensor" target="Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Flash glucose sensors allow people with diabetes to monitor glucose trends by scanning a sensor, supporting treatment decisions.</data>
  <data key="d9">data access,glucose tracking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638398</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Non-Invasive Glucose Monitor" target="Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Non-invasive glucose monitors are being developed to improve patient comfort by eliminating the need for finger pricks.</data>
  <data key="d9">emerging technology,patient comfort</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638399</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Wearable Glucose Sensor" target="Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Wearable glucose sensors like watch-based or contact lens devices represent innovative tools for continuous glucose monitoring in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">continuous tracking,innovation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638400</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tattoo-Like Glucose Sensor" target="Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tattoo-like glucose sensors are experimental devices that measure glucose through the skin, offering a novel approach to monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d9">experimental monitoring,skin-based sensing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638400</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Treatment" target="GLP-1 Agonist">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GLP-1 agonists are used in diabetes treatment as part of injectable subcutaneous therapies.</data>
  <data key="d9">injectable medication,pharmacological therapy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639126</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Treatment" target="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin injection procedure is a core component of diabetes treatment for patients requiring exogenous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease management,therapeutic intervention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639126</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Treatment" target="Patient Education">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Effective patient and clinician education is essential for successful outcomes in diabetes treatment involving insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical training,treatment success</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641889</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Diabetes Treatment" target="NovoNordisk">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">NovoNordisk contributes to diabetes treatment through the development and release of advanced insulin products like Fiasp.</data>
  <data key="d9">pharmaceutical innovation,therapeutic options</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7be6907597f74116387925485497fbd0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641896</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Capillary Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Walker R">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Walker R studied the role of capillary blood glucose monitoring in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes management,research focus</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bed2aa7fa8ee59d19d7f3898042c3742</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647306</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enzyme" target="Test Strip">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The test strip contains an enzyme that reacts with blood glucose to produce an electrical signal.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical reaction,detection mechanism</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638364</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enzyme" target="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The enzyme on the test strip reacts specifically with blood glucose to initiate the measurement process.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical interaction,glucose detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638365</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enzyme" target="Glucose Test Strip">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The enzyme on the glucose test strip reacts with blood sugar to produce an electrical signal used by the glucometer.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical reaction,signal generation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638398</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="70% Alcohol" target="Skin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">70% alcohol is applied to the skin before insulin injection and must be allowed to dry completely.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,skin preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin" target="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Healthcare professionals examine the skin during visits and teach patients how to properly rotate injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical assessment,patient education</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638358</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The skin should be visually inspected and palpated to detect signs of lipo-hypertrophy before insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">palpation,physical examination</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638363</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The subcutaneous fold is created by gently pinching the skin to lift the fatty layer and ensure proper insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">physical manipulation,technique application</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Skin" target="Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The needle is used to deliver insulin into the skin at the correct angle and must remain in place briefly after injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection tool,penetration</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638409</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Insulin Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Proper site rotation is a key strategy to prevent both lipoatrophy and lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">management,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637698</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Reuse of Syringes and Needles">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reusing syringes and needles increases the risk of lipodystrophy, making it an unsafe practice.</data>
  <data key="d9">health risk,safety concern</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637778</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Lipo-Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipo-hypertrophy is the most common type of lipodystrophy, characterized by hard lumps under the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipo-hypertrophy is a subtype of lipodystrophy, representing one of the two main forms of the condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,medical condition,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640284</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Lipoatrophy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipoatrophy is a rare form of lipodystrophy involving fat loss and skin depressions at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a subtype of lipodystrophy, representing the less common form involving fat loss.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,medical condition,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640284</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Abdomen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Avoiding repeated insulin injections in the same abdominal site helps prevent lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639178</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="CIDEC Gene">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A homozygous mutation in the CIDEC gene has been reported in a case of autosomal recessive lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">autosomal recessive inheritance,genetic cause</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c4fc351ae9ead9b05dca3f5378145b9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640990</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Generalized lipodystrophy is a specific form of lipodystrophy characterized by near-total absence of body fat.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease classification,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641001</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Insulin Resistance">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin resistance is a core metabolic feature of lipodystrophy, driving multiple complications.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic consequence,pathophysiology</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641002</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Hypertriglyceridemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypertriglyceridemia is a common and severe complication in lipodystrophy, potentially leading to acute pancreatitis.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease manifestation,metabolic complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641004</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Diabetes develops in about two-thirds of lipodystrophy patients, typically during puberty, due to worsening insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease progression,metabolic outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641009</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Hepatic Steatosis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hepatic steatosis is a common finding in lipodystrophy, detectable via ultrasound even in children.</data>
  <data key="d9">liver disease,organ involvement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641010</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Low Leptin Levels">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Low serum leptin levels are a hallmark of lipodystrophy and contribute to metabolic dysregulation.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic marker,hormonal deficiency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641011</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Childhood">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Symptoms of lipodystrophy worsen in childhood when transitioning from breastfeeding to regular diet.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease onset,progression</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641012</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Breastfeeding">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Breastfeeding may mitigate early disease severity due to the presence of leptin in maternal milk.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease modulation,early nutrition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641014</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Saturated Fat Restriction">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Saturated fat restriction is essential in managing hypertriglyceridemia in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">dietary management,treatment strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641015</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Metformin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Metformin is used early in lipodystrophy to address severe insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d9">insulin sensitization,pharmacological treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641017</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Thiazolidinediones">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Thiazolidinediones are not recommended in generalized lipodystrophy as they may worsen steatosis and hypertriglyceridemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,contraindicated treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641018</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Sulfonylureas">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sulfonylureas can be used in early diabetes stages in lipodystrophy patients with residual beta-cell function.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,pharmacological treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641019</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="DPP-4 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">DPP-4 inhibitors may be used in lipodystrophy despite lack of specific studies, aiding in glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,potential treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641020</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="SGLT2 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SGLT2 inhibitors are not well-studied in lipodystrophy but may help improve glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,potential treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641021</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="GLP-1 Analogues">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GLP-1 analogues may help control hyperphagia in lipodystrophy due to leptin deficiency, though not yet studied.</data>
  <data key="d9">appetite regulation,potential treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641022</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="DXA Scan">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">DXA scan is used to confirm low body fat percentage, typically below 7%, in generalized lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">body composition,diagnostic method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641024</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Abdominal Ultrasound">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Abdominal ultrasound detects hepatic steatosis and hepatosplenomegaly in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic method,liver assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641024</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Low Body Fat Percentage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients with generalized lipodystrophy have extremely low body fat, averaging around 5%.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,physical characteristic</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641025</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Normal or High Bone Density">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">DXA scans in lipodystrophy patients often show normal or increased bone density.</data>
  <data key="d9">bone health,diagnostic finding</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641026</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Serum Insulin Levels">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Serum insulin levels are markedly elevated in lipodystrophy, even during fasting.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical marker,metabolic state</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641030</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Serum Leptin Levels">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Low serum leptin levels help confirm the diagnosis of lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic marker,hormonal deficiency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641033</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Triglyceride Levels">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Triglyceride levels are often very high in lipodystrophy, though usually below 1,000 mg/dL, with higher levels in American cohorts.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical marker,disease severity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641034</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="HDL Cholesterol">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HDL cholesterol is inversely related to triglycerides and typically below 30 mg/dL in lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical marker,lipid profile</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641035</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Liver Enzymes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Liver enzymes such as TGP and GGT are elevated due to steatosis, but normalize in advanced disease, indicating worsening prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical marker,liver function</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641036</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Platelet Count">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Platelet count decreases in advanced stages of lipodystrophy, signaling progression to cirrhosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease progression,hematological marker</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641036</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Serum Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Serum glucose is normal to low early in lipodystrophy (&lt; 80 mg/dL) before progressing to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">biochemical marker,glycemic state</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8659fdffea91cf2a67039d59ea61cc65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641038</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Insulin Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients with lipodystrophy often require insulin therapy early in the disease course due to severe insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic management,treatment necessity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641042</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Metreleptin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Metreleptin is a disease-modifying therapy for generalized lipodystrophy, improving metabolic outcomes and reducing insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease-modifying treatment,metabolic improvement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffdf22a7b29fa94a79e1a638321da9e0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641042</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="CIDEC">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Homozygous mutation in CIDEC causes a rare autosomal recessive form of lipodystrophy with multilocular lipid droplets in adipose tissue.</data>
  <data key="d9">autosomal recessive inheritance,gene mutation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641051</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV-associated lipodystrophy is the most prevalent form of lipodystrophy today, affecting up to 50% of HIV-positive individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV-associated lipodystrophy is an acquired form of lipodystrophy linked to treatment with protease inhibitors and reverse transcriptase inhibitors.</data>
  <data key="d9">acquired form,antiretroviral therapy,disease prevalence</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647144</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Catheter Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rotating catheter sites is a recommended method to reduce the risk of lipodystrophy in patients using insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical practice,complication prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641825</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Rapid-Acting Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipodystrophy is a rare complication that may occur at infusion sites using rapid-acting insulin analogs.</data>
  <data key="d9">rare side effect,treatment complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-182332eb7daaa8deed5e90a79db308e8</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641830</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipodystrophy at infusion sites causes unpredictable insulin absorption, contributing to poor glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption variability,treatment complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641871</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Infusion Site">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipodystrophy, including lipoatrophy and lipohypertrophy, develops at the infusion site due to repeated insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">site complication,tissue change</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641872</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Radermecker Rp">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Radermecker RP studied lipodystrophy reactions to insulin and the effects of continuous insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,treatment side effects</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641928</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Piérard Ge">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Piérard GE co-authored a study on lipodystrophy reactions to insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,treatment side effects</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Scheen Aj">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Scheen AJ co-authored a study on lipodystrophy reactions to insulin and the effects of new insulin analogs.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,treatment side effects</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-93bddc99b2e70c378921ff59ddb3b954</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Diabetes mellitus can be associated with lipodystrophy syndromes, which are rare disorders involving loss of adipose tissue.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease association,rare syndromes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647140</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Congenital Generalized Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Congenital generalized lipodystrophy is a subtype of lipodystrophy caused by mutations in genes such as AGPAT2 and BSCL2.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic disorder,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647142</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Partial Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Partial lipodystrophy is a form of lipodystrophy characterized by fat loss in limbs and fat accumulation in central areas, caused by mutations in LMNA and PPARG genes.</data>
  <data key="d9">fat distribution disorder,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647143</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Metreleptina">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Metreleptina (recombinant leptin) is indicated for selected cases of generalized and partial lipodystrophy with low leptin levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">therapy indication,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647146</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Skinfold Thickness Measurement">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Skinfold thickness measurement is used to identify lipodystrophy by detecting abnormally low subcutaneous fat levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Skinfold thickness measurement is used to assess fat loss in lipodystrophy, with values below 10 mm in men and 22 mm in women suggesting the condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical assessment,diagnostic method,fat loss assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647147</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="DEXA">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">DEXA scanning is used to evaluate partial lipodystrophy, particularly in patients with diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d9">body composition analysis,diagnostic imaging</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647148</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Trunk Fat Percentage To Lower Limb Fat Percentage Ratio">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A ratio of trunk to lower limb fat percentage ≥ 1.5 is a key indicator of partial lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical indicator,diagnostic threshold</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647149</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Brazilian Diabetes Society">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Brazilian Diabetes Society recommends considering genetic testing for lipodystrophy in patients with diabetes and generalized or partial loss of body fat, especially in familial forms.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic suspicion,genetic testing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c51943f25319629d0e145186a85c3b59</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647190</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipoatrophy" target="Insulin Application">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin should not be injected into areas with lipoatrophy until tissue recovery occurs.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection safety,site selection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-035472811a4a16d98e62eba23a86dceb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637725</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipoatrophy" target="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Failure to rotate injection sites during insulin administration can lead to lipoatrophy, which impairs insulin absorption and causes hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,injection site rotation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-51960dcc8f6bd8e9d62d3512fa1e35af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638709</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipoatrophy" target="Infusion Sets">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infusion set use is associated with lipoatrophy, though less frequently than lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">side effect,skin complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643833</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Insulin Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Proper rotation of insulin injection sites reduces the risk of lipohypertrophy, with only 5% of correct rotators affected compared to 98% of those who do not rotate or do so incorrectly.</data>
  <data key="d9">prevention,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637698</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Unexplained Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients with lipohypertrophy experience unexplained hypoglycemia at a rate of 39.1%, compared to 5.9% in those without the condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical consequence,metabolic instability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637700</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Blood Glucose Variability">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">49.1% of patients with lipohypertrophy exhibit blood glucose variability, compared to 6.5% in those without.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical consequence,metabolic instability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637702</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Daily Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients with lipohypertrophy require higher daily insulin doses (56 UI/day vs. 41 UI/day), increasing treatment costs.</data>
  <data key="d9">cost implication,treatment intensity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637707</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Multicenter Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A multicenter study in Spain found that 64% of diabetic patients had lipodystrophy, with 98% of those with lipohypertrophy failing to rotate injection sites properly.</data>
  <data key="d9">prevalence,research finding</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7a2bb9a343108d712fe87613f1b48d18</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637709</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Moscow Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipohypertrophy incidence decreased in patient groups that received structured injection training.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication reduction,injection practice</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7740b86f0b3f110bb2c3f3d05e4da41</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637746</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Healthcare professionals must examine injection sites regularly and educate patients, families, and caregivers about the risks of lipohypertrophy and the importance of site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d9">education,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639101</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipohypertrophy at injection sites causes inconsistent insulin absorption and contributes to poor glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">irregular absorption,tissue change</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639115</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipohypertrophy" target="Infusion Sets">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Repeated use of infusion sets can lead to lipohypertrophy at pump sites.</data>
  <data key="d9">side effect,skin complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643832</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Injection Site Rotation" target="Lipohipertrofia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Proper rotation of insulin injection sites helps prevent lipohipertrofia caused by repeated injections in the same location.</data>
