</edge>
<edge source="Type 1 Diabetes" target="Insulin Pump Therapy">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin pump therapy is indicated for type 1 diabetes patients with poor glycemic control, frequent hypoglycemia, or specific needs like pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pump therapy is recommended for individuals with type 1 diabetes who are on multiple daily injections and not using automated systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pump therapy is used in individuals with type 1 diabetes and has been shown to improve glycemic control and reduce hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pump therapy is used in the management of type 1 diabetes, often in conjunction with continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pump therapy is used as a treatment method for managing type 1 diabetes in children and adults.</data>
  <data key="d9">advanced treatment,clinical benefit,clinical guideline,delivery method,disease management,glycemic control,treatment indication,treatment method,treatment option</data>
