<edge source="NPH Insulin" target="Regular Insulin">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">NPH insulin was mixed with regular insulin and injected subcutaneously in diabetic patients as part of a combined insulin therapy regimen.&lt;SEP&gt;When using both types, Regular insulin is drawn before NPH after air injection to prevent contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;When mixing NPH and regular insulin, regular insulin must be aspirated first to prevent contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;When mixing NPH and Regular insulin, Regular insulin must be aspirated first to prevent contamination and ensure accurate dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;When mixing insulins, regular insulin must be drawn into the syringe before NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration sequence,combination therapy,insulin combination,insulin mixture,insulin regimen,sequential mixing</data>
