<edge source="Regular Insulin" target="Insulin NPH">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin NPH was mixed with regular insulin and administered to diabetic patients to evaluate pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;When combining insulin types, regular insulin must be aspirated before insulin NPH to prevent contamination and ensure correct dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH and Regular Insulin are combined in the same syringe during preparation, requiring specific handling order.</data>
