<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Children Under 6 Years">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Children under 6 years should always use the subcutaneous fold technique during insulin injection to prevent intramuscular delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The subcutaneous fold technique is recommended for children under 6 years during insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">age-specific care,patient safety,recommended use</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638409</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Adolescents And Adults With Low Body Fat">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adolescents and adults with low body fat are advised to use the subcutaneous fold to ensure accurate insulin placement.&lt;SEP&gt;The subcutaneous fold technique is advised for adolescents and adults with low body fat to avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">body composition,injection safety,patient safety,recommended use</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638410</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Insulin Application Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Creating a subcutaneous skin fold ensures the insulin is injected into the correct tissue layer.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery,injection technique</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e68da6d45eb01c249e854b711007d805</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638210</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Muscle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The subcutaneous fold helps prevent insulin from being injected into the muscle, which could cause pain and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">error prevention,injection safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Adults With High Body Fat">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adults with high body fat may not need the subcutaneous fold technique, especially when using short needles.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical guidance,conditional use</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638416</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Fold" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Creating a subcutaneous fold during injection helps prevent intramuscular delivery by isolating the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk prevention,technique</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8b2243846b349d5b78af57a8e77b6ff5</data>
