<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin is injected into the subcutaneous tissue, where it is gradually absorbed into the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug delivery,injection site</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-180dc3d244f7d832cf505b09cfc34746</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639125</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The insulin injection technique requires the needle to remain in the subcutaneous tissue for at least 10 seconds to prevent backflow.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection site,needle retention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-78692c868b2064d1fbeaf7aec1c44948</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subcutaneous Tissue" target="Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The length of the needle must be appropriate for the thickness of the patient's subcutaneous tissue to ensure proper insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d9">anatomical interaction,injection depth</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5bbc7b2df438b8290a4da57f63f1ff5d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639188</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using shorter needles (4–6 mm) reduces the risk of intramuscular injection, especially in adults and children with lower BMI.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection safety,risk prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637742</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Body Mass Index">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Body Mass Index influences the risk of intramuscular injection, with individuals having lower BMI being more susceptible when using longer needles (≥8 mm).</data>
  <data key="d9">injection safety,personalized care</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637745</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Insulin Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needle length influences the correct insulin injection technique, with shorter needles (4–5 mm) allowing 90° injection without skin fold in most patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">device selection,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637747</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Tabela 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tabela 1 specifies the recommended needle lengths for different patient groups and injection conditions.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage safety,guideline reference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ee3024e95a663f89ec3c7a35028cc636</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637748</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="People With Motor Limitations">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">People with motor limitations may require longer needles or assistance for easier insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">accessibility,usability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638329</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Syringe With Fixed Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needle length is a feature of syringes with fixed needles, with 6 mm being the best option for patient use.</data>
  <data key="d9">device feature,optimal choice</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639642</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Glycemic Variation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Changes in insulin injection sites may cause glycemic variation, requiring intensified blood glucose monitoring and possible medical prescription review.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical response,monitoring need</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5ea5432a4b376d5a48f31d6694c76d8e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776637743</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Fasting Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fasting blood glucose is measured as part of routine blood glucose monitoring to assess diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical metric,diabetes tracking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638361</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Postprandial Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Postprandial blood glucose is monitored to evaluate how meals affect blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical metric,diabetes tracking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638362</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Diabetes Technology">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring using meters or CGM is a core component of diabetes technology used to track glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose monitoring is a foundational diabetes technology for measuring blood sugar levels using meters and strips.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose measurement,glucose tracking,technology category</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-54930ff88c0a13a8693f1c1b3407ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643766</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Glycemic Targets">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring is used to assess whether glycemic targets are being met throughout the day.</data>
  <data key="d9">data collection,goal tracking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-768c26e20aaed169fbf07de7ca22c08d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641899</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="People With Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">People with diabetes use blood glucose monitoring to manage their condition effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;People with diabetes use blood glucose monitoring to evaluate their response to therapy and ensure safe glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes management,disease management,self-care,self-monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643706</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="A1C">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Increased frequency of blood glucose monitoring is associated with lower A1C levels in people with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring helps reduce A1C levels when integrated into structured diabetes therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical correlation,glycemic control,health outcome,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643706</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Intensive Insulin Therapies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Individuals on intensive insulin therapies are advised to perform frequent blood glucose monitoring to prevent hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">safety monitoring,treatment requirement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643707</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Basal Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">There is insufficient evidence on the optimal frequency of blood glucose monitoring for people using basal insulin without intensive therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical uncertainty,treatment monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643708</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Lancing Devices">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lancing devices are used to obtain blood samples for monitoring, and less painful designs can improve user experience.</data>
  <data key="d9">sample collection,user comfort</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643709</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Integrated Health Platforms">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Some blood glucose meters can connect to integrated health platforms for comprehensive data use.</data>
  <data key="d9">data integration,digital health</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643709</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Real-Time Advice">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Certain meters provide real-time advice during glucose monitoring to assist users in making immediate health decisions.</data>
  <data key="d9">decision support,user guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643710</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Pharmacologic Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring data is used to adjust pharmacologic therapy for better diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d9">therapy optimization,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7c03aef84b96134fc1f0a2a4d8466e0d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643712</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Glycemic Management">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring is an integral part of intensive glycemic management shown to reduce diabetes complications.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication prevention,treatment guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643716</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Medical Nutrition Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Results from blood glucose monitoring can guide medical nutrition therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">dietary guidance,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643717</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Prandial Insulin Doses">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring results are used to adjust prandial insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d9">dose adjustment,therapy guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e8bc02d862fc2c83e40dafc871482c2c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643719</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Hypoglycemia Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring is required for accurate diagnosis and treatment of hypoglycemia in hospitalized patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">approved use,clinical decision-making</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c13cc105f4fbcaf9606f9a0faa1e2d31</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643753</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Adjunctive CGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adjunctive CGM systems require users to perform blood glucose monitoring for insulin dosing and hypoglycemia treatment.</data>
  <data key="d9">device limitation,treatment requirement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643760</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Nonadjunctive CGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Nonadjunctive CGM systems do not require blood glucose monitoring for treatment decisions in most clinical situations.</data>
  <data key="d9">device capability,reduced dependency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-418c63d7f8a7a0408d9107e40d9251db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643761</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="U.S. Food and Drug Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration approves blood glucose meters for accuracy and safety.</data>
  <data key="d9">device approval,regulatory oversight</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643767</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Health Care Professionals">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Health care professionals must understand differences in blood glucose meter accuracy and recommend FDA-approved devices.</data>
  <data key="d9">accuracy awareness,clinical guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-90452c5625b363eb503added0caf901d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring is used in people with type 2 diabetes to assess treatment effectiveness and guide self-management.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease management,self-monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643807</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose Monitoring" target="Diabetes Monitoring">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring using finger-prick tests improved the accuracy of glucose tracking in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose measurement,technological advancement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644658</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intramuscular Injection" target="Individuals">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">All individuals face a high risk when intramuscular insulin injection is administered, emphasizing the need for proper technique.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639173</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
