  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Impaired Fasting Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Impaired fasting glucose is a known risk factor for the development of type 2 diabetes, though less predictive than one-hour postload hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease progression,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2977bb9a41689e74de2c536343624744</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689081</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Metabolic Dysfunction-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">MASLD is closely linked to type 2 diabetes, with management considerations overlapping between the two conditions.</data>
  <data key="d9">comorbidity,disease association</data>
