<edge source="Tabela 1" target="Fatores que Podem Interferir no Resultado da Glicemia Capilar">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A Tabela 1 classifica e descreve fatores que podem interferir no resultado da glicemia capilar, incluindo causas de imprecisão técnica e humana.&lt;SEP&gt;A Tabela 1 classifica e descreve fatores que podem interferir no resultado da glicemia capilar, incluindo causas de imprecisão técnica e humana.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,reference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4d2f09f4f3ead9f5bcbe0e4c9697887b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776688869</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tabela 1" target="Metas no Tratamento do Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tabela 1 presents individualized glycemic targets based on patient health status as part of the treatment goals for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">evidence presentation,individualization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8434e93fae47721617db0727fcd99b1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689385</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="iCGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The use of iCGM resulted in a reduction of A1C compared to BGM in adults with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643774</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="isCGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Most observational and retrospective studies show improvement in A1C levels in individuals with type 1 diabetes using isCGM.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic outcome,observational evidence</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fdddb31a1876a8809b8555564982acd4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643777</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Insulin Pump Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Studies show that insulin pump therapy modestly lowers A1C levels compared to multiple daily injections.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b36191c270d1cc8ff8c1fc610d7a533b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643782</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Structured BGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Structured BGM leads to greater A1C reduction when used to adjust medications in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical improvement,treatment adjustment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f12d6a3cebf5c39bed5629c359502cae</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643800</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Insulin Pumps">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Randomized controlled trials show a modest improvement in A1C levels with insulin pump therapy compared to MDI.</data>
  <data key="d9">effectiveness,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f357ebc59eb6ed3dd2035a13da0df52f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643831</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="rtCGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Use of rtCGM during pregnancy in type 1 diabetes is associated with reduced A1C levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,diabetes management</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643835</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Fasting Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Both A1C and fasting glucose are low-cost tests used to assess glucose metabolism in early pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative testing,early detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647474</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Anemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Anemia can cause falsely elevated A1C values due to reduced red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d9">elevated values,test inaccuracy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647474</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Hemoglobinopathies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemoglobinopathies can lead to inaccurately low A1C readings due to increased red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d9">reduced values,test inaccuracy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647475</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Prediabetes">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C levels between 5.7% and 6.4% are used to define and screen for prediabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A1C is used as a diagnostic method for identifying prediabetes, with values of 5.7% or higher indicating increased risk.&lt;SEP&gt;An A1C level between 5.7% and 6.4% is used to define prediabetes and indicates increased risk for developing diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,diagnostic criteria,diagnostic method,risk assessment,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc7d59e52d23bbcf0d499f8423581f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647493</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Recommendation 2.10">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Recommendation 2.10 includes A1C as an appropriate test for screening prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic method,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e3bdf442194477639404123cea5d5974</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647496</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Cystic Fibrosis–Related Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C is not recommended as a screening test for cystic fibrosis–related diabetes despite proposed threshold values.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic limitation,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647510</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Recommendation 2.17">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Recommendation 2.17 explicitly states that A1C is not recommended for screening cystic fibrosis–related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic guideline,exclusion</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c53f409a49620f4d40ad687bd0c0df19</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647520</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Diagnostic Tests For Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C is used as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes when measured using NGSP-certified methods standardized to the DCCT assay.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,standardized testing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647610</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Diabetes Control And Complications Trial">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C testing methods must be standardized to the DCCT assay to ensure accuracy and reliability in diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">assay reference,test standardization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647611</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="National Glycohemoglobin Standardization Program">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The NGSP certifies A1C testing methods to ensure they are standardized and reliable for clinical use.</data>
  <data key="d9">laboratory certification,quality control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-85b36fc8288de16b0682d3530712dcb4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647612</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="PTDM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C levels are used with fasting glucose to identify high-risk individuals for PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk identification,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647680</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Diabetes Diagnosis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C is used as a primary diagnostic criterion for diabetes when levels are at or above 6.5%.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,glycemic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647738</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="African American">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">African American individuals may have higher A1C levels for a given mean glucose, suggesting potential differences in glycemic burden.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic marker variation,population difference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647739</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Afro-Caribbean People">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Afro-Caribbean people may have lower A1C levels than predicted by glucose levels, indicating population-specific variations.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic marker variation,population difference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647740</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Taiwanese Population">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the Taiwanese population, age and sex are associated with increased A1C levels, particularly in men.</data>
  <data key="d9">age and sex association,population variation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647740</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Sickle Cell Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sickle cell disease increases red blood cell turnover, making A1C less reliable for assessing glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reliability,red blood cell turnover</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647741</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Pregnancy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During the second and third trimesters of pregnancy, A1C is less reliable due to changes in red blood cell lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reliability,physiological change</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647742</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase Deficiency">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">This deficiency causes increased red blood cell destruction, reducing the accuracy of A1C as a glycemic marker.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reliability,hemolysis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647742</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Hemodialysis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemodialysis affects red blood cell survival, leading to unreliable A1C readings.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reliability,treatment effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647743</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Blood Transfusion">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Recent blood transfusion alters red blood cell age distribution, invalidating A1C as a reliable test.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood composition,diagnostic interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647744</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Erythropoietin Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Erythropoietin therapy increases young red blood cells, which can lower A1C independently of glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic interference,red blood cell production</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647744</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Postpartum State">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the postpartum period, A1C is less reliable than plasma glucose for assessing glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reliability,physiological state</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647745</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="HIV">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV treated with certain antiretrovirals is associated with altered A1C reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,medication effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647747</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Protease inhibitors used in HIV treatment may interfere with A1C measurement accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,pharmacological interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647749</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">NRTIs used in HIV treatment may affect the relationship between A1C and actual glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,pharmacological interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647749</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Iron-Deficient Anemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Iron-deficient anemia can cause falsely elevated A1C levels, reducing its reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic interference,hematological condition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-20b3e88dda40e2d303af38aea0d19b86</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647750</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="GLT">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C testing at 24–28 weeks of gestation is less effective than the 50-g GLT for screening GDM.</data>
  <data key="d9">screening effectiveness,test comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d936160aac8a6b8ba40b196280422fe5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647776</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher A1C levels are strongly associated with an increased risk of progressing to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease progression,prediction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647783</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Diabetes Prevention Program">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">An A1C of 5.7% or higher is associated with a diabetes risk similar to that of high-risk participants in the Diabetes Prevention Program.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical evidence,risk comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647784</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C" target="Cardiovascular Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Baseline A1C is a predictor of cardiovascular events, independent of fasting glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">comorbidity,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1a862c4dc9595df3958bd7626f7145d3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647784</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
