  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Safe Disposal" target="Disease Transmission">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Safe disposal of used sharps minimizes the risk of disease transmission such as hepatitis.</data>
  <data key="d9">health risk reduction,infection control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641145</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Diabetes Type 2">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Studies show that 28% to 64% of people with diabetes type 2 may develop lipo-hypertrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Studies show that people with diabetes type 2 can also develop lipo-hypertrophy, though it is less prevalent than in type 1.</data>
  <data key="d9">association,medical condition,prevalence</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640296</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Same Injection Site">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using the same injection site repeatedly contributes to the development of lipo-hypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,medical complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638352</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Irregular Insulin Absorption">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipo-hypertrophy causes irregular insulin absorption, leading to unpredictable blood sugar levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">physiological effect,treatment impact</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638357</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Improper insulin delivery in lipo-hypertrophy areas can result in hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood sugar fluctuation,complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638359</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Insulin Injection Site">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin should not be applied in lipo-hypertrophy-affected areas to ensure proper absorption and allow tissue recovery.</data>
  <data key="d9">site avoidance,tissue health</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638361</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="New Needle Use">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using a new needle for each injection reduces the risk of tissue damage and lipo-hypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection control,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638361</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Insulin Application Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Regular rotation of injection sites is a key method to prevent the development of lipo-hypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">prevention,tissue preservation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638362</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipo-Hypertrophy" target="Skin Palpation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Skin palpation is a key method for detecting lipo-hypertrophy, especially when visual signs are not apparent.</data>
  <data key="d9">detection method,diagnostic practice</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640297</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
