  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Ideal Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Maintaining blood glucose within the ideal range is a key goal in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d9">health monitoring,target level</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638368</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose readings are used to determine whether insulin dosage needs to be adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage control,treatment decision</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638368</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Capillary Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Capillary blood glucose provides instant readings of current blood sugar levels, enabling timely interventions for hypo- or hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary blood glucose provides instant readings of current blood sugar levels for timely clinical or self-management decisions.</data>
  <data key="d9">immediate feedback,real-time measurement,real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648247</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Time in Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Time in Range measures how often blood glucose stays between 70 and 180 mg/dL, aiming for at least 70% of the time to ensure stable control.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose stability,target range</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638457</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Severely Compromised Elderly">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For severely compromised elderly patients, the focus shifts from numerical targets to preventing symptoms of extreme blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;For severely compromised elderly patients, the focus shifts from numerical targets to preventing symptoms of hypo- or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">palliative approach,symptom avoidance,symptom prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648249</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blood Glucose" target="Time In Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Time In Range measures how often blood glucose stays within the target range of 70–180 mg/dL, promoting stable glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">continuous monitoring,glucose stability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648247</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Pen Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needle retention on the insulin pen led to insulin loss and unexplained hyperglycemia in the child.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse outcome,technical error</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639171</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Unplanned Disconnection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Unplanned disconnection of the insulin pump can lead to hyperglycemia and potentially diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic risk,treatment interruption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641872</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Planned Disconnection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During planned disconnection, glucose levels increase by 1 mg/dL per minute if the disconnection lasts longer than 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose rise,intentional interruption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641873</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Professional CGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Professional CGM helps evaluate periods of hyperglycemia to inform treatment adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic use,pattern detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643838</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Retinopathy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Prolonged high blood sugar increases the risk of developing retinopathy in people with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication risk,disease progression</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776644649</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Kidney Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sustained high blood sugar levels contribute to kidney damage and the development of kidney disease.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication risk,organ damage</data>
