<edge source="Insulin Dose" target="Carbohydrate Intake">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The amount of insulin needed is influenced by carbohydrate intake, requiring dose adjustments based on meals.</data>
  <data key="d9">dose calculation,nutritional influence</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642062</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Dose" target="Illness or Infection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During illness or infection, the body may require higher insulin doses temporarily due to increased metabolic stress.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic stress,temporary increase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642065</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="U100 Syringe" target="Syringe With Fixed Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringes with fixed needles are preferred because they reduce dead space, allow accurate dosing, and can be used to mix different types of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">device safety,precision</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638307</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="U100 Syringe" target="Syringe With Removable Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringes with removable needles are not recommended for insulin due to risks of dosing errors, dead space, long needles, and inability to mix insulins safely.</data>
  <data key="d9">device risk,improper use</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638339</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="U100 Syringe" target="Dose Accuracy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using the correct syringe calibrated for the insulin concentration, such as U100 syringes for U100 insulin, ensures accurate dosing and prevents medication errors.</data>
  <data key="d9">calibration,measurement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638340</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Fixed Needle" target="Safe Insulin Practices">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using a syringe with a fixed, short needle is a recommended practice to prevent insulin waste and dosing inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d9">proper equipment,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9c96e22adae6d8c02ec9ce8430d0cf64</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639153</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Fixed Needle" target="Syringe With Removable Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringe with fixed needle is compared to syringe with removable needle in terms of safety and precision in insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,medical device types</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639636</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Fixed Needle" target="Dose Measurement">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringe with fixed needle allows precise dose measurement, especially for small and odd doses, reducing risk of errors.</data>
  <data key="d9">accuracy,error prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639636</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Removable Needle" target="13 mm Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 13 mm needle associated with removable-needle syringes increases the risk of intramuscular injection, which can lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection risk,needle length</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638340</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Removable Needle" target="Dead Space">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringes with removable needles have dead space that traps insulin, leading to wasted medication and inaccurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosing error,medication waste</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638340</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Syringe With Removable Needle" target="Dose Measurement">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Syringe with removable needle, being graduated, carries a higher risk of errors in dose measurement.</data>
  <data key="d9">error potential,measurement risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c66bff09b476d15a54c71ff3efac594d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639637</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="8 mm Needle" target="Adults">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">An 8 mm needle is considered appropriate for adults due to the variable thickness of subcutaneous tissue across injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d9">appropriate use,tissue variation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-eb4a4dec39574c303988e93b87c351d4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639104</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Rotation Of Injection Sites" target="Quadrants">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Quadrants are used to organize the rotation of injection sites in a structured and repeatable manner.</data>
  <data key="d9">organization,systematic approach</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638409</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="4 Mm Needle" target="Thin Individuals">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Thin individuals should use 4 mm needles with subcutaneous prega to prevent intramuscular insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">body composition,injection safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638326</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Arms" target="Recommended Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Arms are one of the recommended sites for insulin injection due to ease of access and distance from joints and bones.</data>
  <data key="d9">accessibility,injection location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639174</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Buttocks" target="Insulin Absorption Rate">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The buttocks have the slowest insulin absorption rate among common injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The buttocks exhibit the slowest insulin absorption rate among recommended injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption speed,injection site,prolonged action,slowest absorption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dde6c55191737188788dc809811837cc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639114</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Buttocks" target="Recommended Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Buttocks, specifically the upper outer lateral quadrant, are a recommended site for insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">accessibility,injection location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639175</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thighs" target="Recommended Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Thighs are a recommended site for insulin injection, located on the anterior and outer lateral upper part.</data>
  <data key="d9">accessibility,injection location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-48b0f8a5b356409be05a1e866ce0ed8d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776639176</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Pregnancy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Gestational diabetes occurs during pregnancy and requires careful glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d9">maternal condition,metabolic disorder</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638374</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Fasting Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fasting blood glucose should be measured four times daily in gestational diabetes with a target below 95 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">monitoring,target level</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638386</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Postprandial Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Postprandial glucose should be measured 1 hour after meals with a target below 140 mg/dL or 2 hours after meals below 120 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">monitoring,target level</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638387</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Insulin and How to Use It Safely">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The course Insulin and How to Use It Safely includes information on insulin use for people with gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease management,treatment education</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0dd0ac30945c224efc81753de13bdebf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642531</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Insulin Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin treatment may be included in the management of gestational diabetes when other methods are inadequate.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose management,pregnancy-related care</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0522904b9c236fceb86e75d6da872d4b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642535</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Long-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Women with gestational diabetes may also use long-acting insulin for extended glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d9">insulin regimen,treatment requirement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642561</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Insulin Regimen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Women with gestational diabetes follow insulin regimens typically involving rapid-acting insulin before meals and sometimes long-acting insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">medical management,treatment plan</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642565</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Diabetes Classification Guideline">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The guideline recognizes Gestational Diabetes as a distinct category occurring during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,pregnancy-related condition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f5847db7a558804738e20dca9fd8d746</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776646998</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="ADA Risk Test">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The original algorithm for the ADA risk test was validated without including gestational diabetes as a factor.</data>
  <data key="d9">exclusion,model limitation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a51a13b6846af5dd45aca8b13432e7fc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647537</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="International Association Of Diabetes And Pregnancy Study Groups">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The International Association of Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups established standardized criteria for diagnosing gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criteria,standardization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647702</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="National Diabetes Data Group Criteria">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The National Diabetes Data Group criteria serve as an alternative method for diagnosing gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical application,diagnostic method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647703</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Mo X">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mo X conducted a systematic review on the economic evaluations of gestational diabetes mellitus screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">economic evaluation,screening analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647704</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Saccone G">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Saccone G performed a meta-analysis of randomized trials comparing one-step and two-step approaches for screening gestational diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d9">meta-analysis,screening method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647705</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Ethridge Jk Jr">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ethridge Jk Jr studied the perinatal outcomes associated with the diagnosis of gestational diabetes using IADPSG criteria.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,perinatal outcomes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647706</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Carpenter-Coustan Criteria">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Carpenter-Coustan criteria are used as a clinical method for diagnosing gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical application,diagnostic method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647706</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Mayo K">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mayo K evaluated the impact of adopting IADPSG criteria on the screening and diagnosis of gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,guideline impact,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-69bf97ae94c34166c23acdc1a684b6bb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647707</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gestational Diabetes" target="Diabetes Risk Test">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A diagnosis of gestational diabetes is a factor considered in the Diabetes Risk Test for women.</data>
  <data key="d9">medical history,risk factor inclusion</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2a874190e40ad535ac9b317a469571d7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
