</edge>
<edge source="Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin" target="Bolus Insulin">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ultra-rapid-acting insulin serves as bolus insulin with faster onset, ideal for immediate blood sugar control around meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-rapid-acting insulin is used as bolus insulin due to its quick onset, ideal for managing glucose from food.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-Rapid-Acting Insulin is used in Bolus Insulin regimens for quicker correction of postprandial glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-rapid-acting insulin is used as bolus insulin due to its quick onset, ideal for managing glucose from food.</data>
  <data key="d9">fast action,fast-acting coverage,functional role,immediate action,insulin therapy,mealtime dosing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0d8750807baddcd948055c83422234</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642058</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Long-Acting Insulin" target="Basal Insulin">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Long-acting insulin functions as basal insulin, providing a steady level of insulin throughout the day and night.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin serves as basal insulin, providing a steady level of insulin throughout the day and night.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin serves as basal insulin, providing a steady level of insulin throughout the day and night.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-acting insulin is used as basal insulin to provide a steady level of insulin throughout the day with minimal peak.</data>
  <data key="d9">background control,background insulin,duration of action,functional role,sustained effect,sustained release</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776642556</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ultra-Long-Acting Insulin" target="Basal Insulin">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ultra-long-acting insulin acts as basal insulin with a duration of up to 42 hours, offering prolonged glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-long-acting insulin is used as basal insulin due to its prolonged effect of up to 42 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-long-acting insulin is used as basal insulin due to its prolonged effect of up to 42 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra-long-acting insulin serves as basal insulin with effects lasting beyond 24 hours, supporting long-term glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d9">background control,background insulin,duration of action,extended duration,functional role</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2841f77ed9254c0e5372f3c45f6d3da2</data>
