  <data key="d9">developmental factor,dose sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638345</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Age" target="Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Age influences diabetes classification, with autoimmune forms more common under 50 and monogenic forms suspected before age 25.</data>
  <data key="d9">age of onset,diagnostic criterion</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e575f95ec5a02f7900989e00da53749f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647184</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Age" target="Screening For Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Age is a major risk factor, and diabetes screening should begin by age 35 for all individuals.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk factor,testing recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8317327cb2c248762b2dc3852c662000</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647600</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Age" target="A1C Test">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A1C was initially validated in adults, but current guidance allows its use in children and adolescents for diabetes testing.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic consideration,population applicability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
