<edge source="Diabetes Mellitus" target="Glicemia De Jejum">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Glicemia de jejum is used to assess diabetes control, with normal levels between 70 and 100 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus can be diagnosed using fasting blood glucose levels, with a threshold of ≥126 mg/dl.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting blood glucose (≥126 mg/dL) is one of the primary diagnostic criteria for Diabetes Mellitus as defined in the guideline.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood glucose measurement,diagnostic criterion,diagnostic method,laboratory test,monitoring</data>
