<edge source="Diabetes Mellitus" target="Random C-Peptide">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Random C-peptide measurement helps differentiate between types of Diabetes Mellitus, particularly type 1 and type 2 or monogenic forms.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Random C-peptide levels help distinguish between type 1B, type 2, and monogenic diabetes after five years of disease duration.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,classification tool,differential diagnosis</data>
