  <data key="d12">1776643777</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="TIR">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM provides data used to calculate TIR, a key metric for assessing glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d9">data metric,glycemic monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643835</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="BGM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM is compared with BGM in RCTs, showing improved A1C outcomes in users of CGM.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes monitoring,technology comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643839</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="Contact Dermatitis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Contact dermatitis, both irritant and allergic types, has been reported with the use of CGM devices that attach to the skin.</data>
  <data key="d9">side effect,skin reaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1f5c2bbe2ca0e80b85850ca2f9a5c84</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776643840</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="Time In Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM is used to measure Time in Range, providing data on the percentage of time blood glucose levels remain between 70 and 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical metric,glucose monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689452</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="Hipoglicemia Nível 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM devices are used to detect and quantify time spent in hypoglicemia nível 1 (glucose &lt; 70 mg/dL).</data>
  <data key="d9">hypoglycemia detection,real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689455</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGM" target="Hipoglicemia Nível 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM devices are used to monitor and report time spent in hipoglicemia nível 2 (glucose &lt; 54 mg/dL).</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical safety,severe hypoglycemia monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0778abb680b777bec45d5985b757c743</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689458</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Capillary Blood Glucose" target="Time In Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Capillary blood glucose measurements contribute to understanding glucose patterns, though Time In Range requires continuous monitoring for full assessment.</data>
  <data key="d9">data source,monitoring method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776648245</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Capillary Blood Glucose" target="Hba1c">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ADAG Study established a correlation between capillary blood glucose levels and HbA1c, guiding target ranges for fasting and postprandial glucose.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical correlation,target setting</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689407</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Capillary Blood Glucose" target="Adag Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ADAG Study provided evidence for recommended capillary blood glucose targets to achieve desired average glucose and HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">evidence base,glucose targets</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02fb9dc2bae2939b212aa5df09194ee4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Time in Range" target="Adults with Type 1 or Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adults with diabetes are advised to spend more than 70% of their time in the glucose target range of 70–180 mg/dL to reduce complications.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose monitoring,treatment goals</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638457</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Time in Range" target="Target Blood Glucose Range">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Time in Range is calculated based on the percentage of time blood glucose remains within the target range of 70 to 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose monitoring,measurement framework</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1776638459</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Time in Range" target="Hybrid Closed-Loop System">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hybrid closed-loop systems improve time in range, increasing the percentage of time patients maintain glucose levels between 70 and 180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,performance metric</data>
