  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV Infection" target="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV infection contributes to HIV-associated lipodystrophy through direct infection of adipocytes and macrophages, altering adipocyte phenotype and promoting inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease association,viral contribution</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640787</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV Infection" target="Antiretroviral Therapy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV infection is treated with antiretroviral therapy, which may contribute to metabolic complications including insulin resistance and diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk factor,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b0f94f216119cfdc3c74eab51c88a823</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689138</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV Infection" target="Screening For Diabetes Mellitus Type 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Individuals with HIV infection should undergo diabetes screening due to increased risk from the disease or its treatment.</data>
  <data key="d9">comorbidity,screening indication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689238</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV Infection" target="Antiretroviral Agents">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Antiretroviral agents are used to treat HIV infection and may contribute to metabolic side effects including diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">pharmacological intervention,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689238</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="First-Generation Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">First-generation protease inhibitors such as nelfinavir and indinavir are associated with the development of HIV-associated lipodystrophy by impairing adipocyte differentiation and inducing insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug toxicity,metabolic side effects</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640788</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Second-Generation Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Some second-generation protease inhibitors like ritonavir and lopinavir contribute to HIV-associated lipodystrophy through oxidative stress, while others like atazanavir and amprenavir do not have deleterious effects when used alone.</data>
  <data key="d9">differential toxicity,drug effects</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640789</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">First-generation nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors like stavudine and zidovudine are linked to subcutaneous lipoatrophy in HIV-associated lipodystrophy due to mitochondrial dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d9">drug association,mitochondrial toxicity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640789</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Tenofovir">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tenofovir, a second-generation nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is not associated with the development of lipodystrophy and lacks the toxic effects seen with earlier drugs.</data>
  <data key="d9">metabolic neutrality,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640790</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Adipose Tissue">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adipose tissue is directly affected in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, exhibiting inflammation, altered adipokine secretion, and adipocyte apoptosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">pathological changes,tissue involvement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640792</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Leptin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Serum leptin levels are normal or elevated in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, reflecting disrupted adipose tissue function.</data>
  <data key="d9">hormonal regulation,metabolic marker</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640792</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Adiponectin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adiponectin levels are reduced in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, contributing to insulin resistance and systemic inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d9">hormonal dysregulation,metabolic dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Oxidative stress is a key mechanism in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, induced by both antiretroviral drugs and HIV infection, leading to adipocyte dysfunction and premature aging.</data>
  <data key="d9">cellular damage,pathogenic mechanism</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640795</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Visceral Fat Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Visceral fat hypertrophy is a feature of HIV-associated lipodystrophy, induced by protease inhibitors, increasing abdominal girth and metabolic complications.</data>
  <data key="d9">body composition change,metabolic risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640796</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Lipid Metabolism Disorders">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lipid metabolism disorders in HIV-associated lipodystrophy include increased hepatic VLDL production due to protease inhibitor use, contributing to hypertriglyceridemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">hepatic effect,metabolic disturbance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640798</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Carbohydrate Metabolism Disorders">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Carbohydrate metabolism disorders in HIV-associated lipodystrophy result from insulin resistance caused by antiretroviral drugs and chronic inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose regulation,metabolic disruption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640799</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Antiretroviral Therapy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Antiretroviral therapy, especially with older drugs, contributes to HIV-associated lipodystrophy; switching to safer regimens reduces inflammation but does not reverse fat loss.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV-associated lipodystrophy is linked to antiretroviral therapy, prompting consideration of switching to less metabolically toxic drugs.</data>
  <data key="d9">causal association,drug toxicity,long-term impact,treatment side effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640800</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Tesamorelin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tesamorelin is indicated for reducing visceral fat in HIV-associated lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">fat reduction,treatment indication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d0e841f6957bc713f769fbd0c5b5ee33</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640890</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="HIV">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV infection is directly linked to HIV-associated lipodystrophy, a condition often triggered by antiretroviral therapy used to treat the virus.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease association,treatment side effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d73e3363161503fcfc16ffb54b8e5388</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641057</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Protease inhibitors such as ritonavir and lopinavir are associated with the development of HIV-related lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,drug association</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647144</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HIV-Associated Lipodystrophy" target="Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reverse transcriptase inhibitors like lamivudina, zidovudina, and estavudina are linked to acquired lipodystrophy in HIV patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,drug association</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647145</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Adipose Tissue" target="Macrophages">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Macrophages infiltrate adipose tissue in HIV infection, shifting from an anti-inflammatory M2 phenotype to a pro-inflammatory M1 phenotype, exacerbating tissue inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d9">immune infiltration,phenotypic shift</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640792</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Adipose Tissue" target="Pro-Inflammatory Cytokines">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pro-inflammatory cytokines are secreted by infected macrophages and stressed adipocytes in adipose tissue, promoting local and systemic inflammation in HIV-associated lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d9">inflammatory signaling,tissue damage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Adipose Tissue" target="Adipokines">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adipokines are signaling molecules produced by adipose tissue that are dysregulated in HIV-associated lipodystrophy, contributing to metabolic and inflammatory disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d9">hormonal signaling,metabolic regulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ritonavir" target="Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ritonavir is a protease inhibitor associated with lipodystrophy in HIV patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,drug classification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02efb2a3687e39bf186d9b0146d95077</data>
