  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Macrophages" target="M1 Phenotype">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Upon HIV infection, macrophages in adipose tissue shift to the M1 phenotype, characterized by secretion of pro-inflammatory cytokines.</data>
  <data key="d9">immune activation,inflammatory response</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776640793</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Macrophages" target="M2 Phenotype">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The M2 phenotype represents the normal anti-inflammatory state of macrophages in adipose tissue, which is disrupted by HIV infection.</data>
  <data key="d9">anti-inflammatory state,immune regulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e6c6decf87d73d5f87597055ec503ae1</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
