  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HIV infection may disrupt the correlation between A1C and actual glucose levels, affecting test reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;The A1C test may underestimate glycemia in people with HIV and is not recommended for diagnosis in this population.&lt;SEP&gt;The A1C test may underestimate glycemia in people with HIV and is not recommended for diagnosis in this group.</data>
