  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Infusion Set" target="Infusion Occlusion">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infusion occlusion occurs when the infusion set becomes blocked, often due to prolonged use or insulin fibril formation.</data>
  <data key="d9">blockage,mechanical failure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641871</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Infusion Set" target="Infusion Site">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The infusion set connects to the infusion site, where complications like irritation, infection, or lipodystrophy may develop.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication risk,delivery interface</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-679c193ea4fd33e94141ac2c9fef69c9</data>
