  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Bolus" target="Bolus">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bolus is the general concept referring to insulin bolus, a dose given to manage mealtime or corrective glucose needs.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage method,insulin delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641873</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Bolus" target="Bolus Padrão">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bolus Padrão is a type of insulin bolus delivered immediately at mealtime, requiring food consumption shortly after.</data>
  <data key="d9">mealtime dosing,standard delivery</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641874</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Bolus" target="Bolus Estendido">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bolus Estendido is a form of insulin bolus delivered gradually over hours, useful for prolonged eating events.</data>
  <data key="d9">extended delivery,prolonged absorption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641875</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulin Bolus" target="Bolus Bifásico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bolus Bifásico combines immediate and extended insulin delivery to manage glucose from complex meals.</data>
  <data key="d9">biphasic delivery,mixed meal management</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b266ecc39f9ba0b5277aacb36089b4db</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776641876</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pump Failure" target="Do-It-Yourself Closed-Loop Systems">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Users of DIY closed-loop systems should have a backup plan in case of pump failure.</data>
