  <data key="d12">1776647680</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Renal Transplant Recipients" target="Sitagliptin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sitagliptin has been studied for short-term efficacy and safety in stable renal transplant recipients with new-onset diabetes after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical trial,treatment efficacy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647687</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Post-Transplantation Diabetes Mellitus" target="Hyperglycemia Management">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hyperglycemia management is a key component in treating patients with post-transplantation diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical management,treatment strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647681</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glycaemic Control" target="Allograft Rejection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Early peri-operative glycaemic control may reduce the risk of allograft rejection in diabetic transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical outcome,risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647682</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Differential Diagnosis Of DM1 And DM2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Monogenic Diabetes can mimic both type 1 and type 2 diabetes, requiring specific testing for accurate classification.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic diagnosis,misclassification risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fff9929a18d525e3805a8ed08356d41b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647116</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="MODY Probability Calculator">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The MODY probability calculator is used to determine the likelihood of monogenic diabetes in young-onset patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical tool,diagnostic method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647195</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Biomarker-Based Screening Pathway">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A biomarker-based screening pathway helps diagnose monogenic diabetes in young patients through targeted testing.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic aid,precision medicine</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647196</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Classification of Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Monogenic diabetes is a distinct category in diabetes classification, caused by single-gene mutations.</data>
  <data key="d9">diabetes subtype,genetic cause</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-1fb7f10473b84f2de23852febe7ef317</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647228</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Random C-Peptide">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">C-peptide levels above 0.6 ng/ml may indicate monogenic diabetes rather than type 1 diabetes.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic differentiation,secretory capacity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-45f87c8aceb9340a61d8283da6282edc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647235</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="SEARCH For Diabetes In Youth Study Group">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The SEARCH for Diabetes in Youth Study Group conducted research on the prevalence and diagnosis of monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,research study</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647538</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Islet Cell Autoantibodies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Positivity for islet cell autoantibodies in monogenic diabetes is associated with later onset and higher HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical marker,disease association</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647538</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="HbA1c Level">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher HbA1c levels are observed in patients with monogenic diabetes who are positive for islet cell autoantibodies.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical indicator,disease severity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647539</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Neonatal Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Neonatal diabetes is a subtype of monogenic diabetes that occurs in infants under 6 months of age.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647544</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY) is a subtype of monogenic diabetes characterized by early-onset hyperglycemia and autosomal dominant inheritance.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647545</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Table 2.6">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Table 2.6 provides a summary of the most common genetic causes of monogenic diabetes, including clinical features and inheritance patterns.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,reference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647548</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders is a reference that contains a comprehensive list of genetic causes of monogenic diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic Diagnosis of Endocrine Disorders provides a comprehensive list of causes of monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">comprehensive list,reference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647549</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Genomic Testing">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genomic testing enables accurate diagnosis of monogenic diabetes, improving clinical management.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic method,precision medicine</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647684</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="HNF1A-MODY">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HNF1A-MODY is a genetically defined subtype of monogenic diabetes with specific clinical features.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,genetic subtype</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647687</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="UNITED Team">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The UNITED Team conducted systematic screening using biomarkers and genetic testing to identify monogenic diabetes in the U.K. pediatric population.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic testing,population screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647688</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="KCNJ11">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mutations in the KCNJ11 gene are associated with monogenic diabetes, particularly permanent or transient neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">gene-disease association,neonatal diabetes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647804</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="ABCC8">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">ABCC8 gene mutations cause monogenic diabetes that can be transient or permanent and are often responsive to sulfonylureas.</data>
  <data key="d9">gene-disease association,sulfonylurea response</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647805</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="INS">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">INS gene mutations are linked to monogenic diabetes diagnosed within the first 6 months of life.</data>
  <data key="d9">early onset,gene-disease association</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647806</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="PLAGL1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">PLAGL1, located on 6q24, is associated with transient neonatal diabetes due to epigenetic or genetic alterations.</data>
  <data key="d9">gene-disease association,transient diabetes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647806</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="GATA6">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GATA6 mutations cause monogenic diabetes with pancreatic and cardiac malformations.</data>
  <data key="d9">gene-disease association,organ malformation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647807</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Genetic Testing">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genetic testing is used to confirm a diagnosis of monogenic diabetes and identify specific genetic subtypes.</data>
  <data key="d9">confirmation,diagnostic method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647808</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Cardiovascular Risk">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Individuals with HNF1A- and HNF4A-MODY have a cardiovascular risk profile similar to type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,long-term outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647809</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Autoantibodies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The presence of autoantibodies typically suggests type 1 diabetes and may preclude monogenic diabetes, though rare exceptions exist.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic exclusion,differential diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647810</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Urinary C-Peptide/Creatinine Ratio">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Urinary C-peptide/creatinine ratio is used as part of a biomarker screening pathway to determine eligibility for genetic testing in suspected monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker screening,patient selection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647811</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="6q24">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 6q24 chromosomal region is associated with transient neonatal diabetes, often due to epigenetic or genetic alterations such as paternal duplication or maternal methylation defects.</data>
  <data key="d9">chromosomal locus,transient diabetes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647811</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="IUGR">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR) is a common clinical feature observed in various forms of monogenic diabetes, including neonatal diabetes and MODY subtypes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical feature,prenatal indicator</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647812</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Monogenic Diabetes" target="Macroglossia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Macroglossia is a clinical manifestation associated with transient neonatal diabetes, particularly in cases linked to 6q24 abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical manifestation,transient diabetes</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-311745e1d3e05390ed93d1e683c07243</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647813</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GCK-MODY" target="Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GCK-MODY is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the GCK gene, leading to stable fasting hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,genetic cause</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647546</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GCK-MODY" target="US National Monogenic Diabetes Registry">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The US National Monogenic Diabetes Registry includes patients with GCK-MODY and has documented previously unpublished genetic variants.</data>
  <data key="d9">data collection,variant reporting</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647684</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HNF1A-MODY" target="Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HNF1A-MODY is a form of MODY caused by mutations in the HNF1A gene, associated with progressive insulin deficiency and sulfonylurea sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,genetic cause</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647547</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="Hattersley AT">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hattersley AT is a key researcher in neonatal diabetes, including genetic testing and treatment strategies.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic testing,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ad3acc8463b5ff47461b1c16ae2559cb</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647231</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="Genetic Testing">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genetic testing is recommended for all individuals diagnosed with diabetes in the first six months of life to confirm neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Advances in genetic testing have improved the diagnosis and treatment of neonatal diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,recommendation,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f780163f31c33c2bd7449fb5a87b42ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647539</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="KCNJ11">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mutations in the KCNJ11 gene are a cause of neonatal diabetes and are often responsive to sulfonylurea treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutations in KCNJ11 are a common cause of permanent neonatal diabetes and may allow treatment with sulfonylureas instead of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic cause,treatment implication,treatment response</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647546</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="INS">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mutations in the INS gene cause permanent neonatal diabetes and are associated with intrauterine growth restriction.&lt;SEP&gt;INS gene mutations are the second most common cause of permanent neonatal diabetes and are typically inherited in an autosomal dominant manner.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic cause,inheritance pattern</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647546</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="ABCC8">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Mutations in the ABCC8 gene can lead to permanent or transient neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;ABCC8 mutations cause permanent neonatal diabetes and may be responsive to sulfonylurea therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic cause,treatment implication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647547</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="6q24">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Abnormalities in the 6q24 chromosomal region, particularly paternal duplications, are linked to transient or permanent neonatal diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The 6q24 chromosomal region is implicated in about half of transient neonatal diabetes cases and may be treatable with non-insulin medications.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic cause,recurrence,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2773e1fe0d693b781b10643e037fc085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647548</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Neonatal Diabetes" target="EIF2B1">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A de novo mutation in EIF2B1 is associated with neonatal diabetes and hepatic dysfunction, resembling Wolcott-Rallison syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;De novo mutations in the EIF2B1 gene have been identified as a cause of neonatal or early-onset diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">comorbidity,de novo mutation,genetic cause</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-50c85dba4b510b2463c6766fd8a2dbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0c65f0481b400f36e5caa3f51fabe</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647680</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
