  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Classification and Diagnosis of Diabetes" target="Diabetes Care Journal">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Diabetes Care Journal published content on the classification and diagnosis of diabetes in its Volume 46, Supplement 1.</data>
  <data key="d9">publication,topic coverage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-dd2e74b5f8450784b7c60acd6751ae14</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647720</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="75-G OGTT" target="International Association of the Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The IADPSG established the diagnostic thresholds for the 75-g OGTT based on data from the HAPO study.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criteria,standardization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647481</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="75-G OGTT" target="One-Step Strategy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The one-step strategy uses the 75-g OGTT as the sole diagnostic test for GDM without prior screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic method,single test</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647486</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="O'Sullivan and Mahan Criteria" target="Two-Step Approach">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The O'Sullivan and Mahan criteria are the original standards that informed the development of the two-step approach for GDM diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic evolution,historical foundation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647479</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="50-G Screen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The two-step approach begins with a 50-g screen to identify individuals who will undergo further testing with a 100-g OGTT.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic pathway,initial screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647487</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="100-G OGTT">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 100-g OGTT is used as the second step in the two-step approach to confirm a diagnosis of GDM after a positive 50-g screen.</data>
  <data key="d9">confirmatory testing,diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7f182d57176633ee05e1a23031d6ad2a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647488</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="Carpenter-Coustan">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Carpenter-Coustan thresholds are used in the two-step approach and represent lower diagnostic values for the 3-hour OGTT.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic thresholds,lower criteria</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647727</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="National Diabetes Data Group">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The National Diabetes Data Group established higher diagnostic thresholds used in the two-step approach for GDM.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic thresholds,higher criteria</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647728</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="Neonatal Macrosomia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Treatment of maternal hyperglycemia identified by the two-step approach reduces the rate of neonatal macrosomia.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk reduction,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647728</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="NIH Panel">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The NIH panel supported the two-step approach due to concerns about overdiagnosis and medicalization of pregnancy with the one-step method.</data>
  <data key="d9">decision-making,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
