</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="Shoulder Dystocia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Treatment based on the two-step approach reduces the incidence of shoulder dystocia during childbirth.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk reduction,treatment outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647731</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="Small-For-Gestational-Age Births">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Treatment of maternal hyperglycemia via the two-step approach does not increase the risk of small-for-gestational-age births.</data>
  <data key="d9">no adverse effect,treatment safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647731</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="GLT">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 50-g GLT is used in the two-step approach and does not require fasting, making it easier for patients to complete.</data>
  <data key="d9">no fasting required,screening method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
