  <data key="d12">1776647732</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Two-Step Approach" target="One-Step Strategy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Data comparing population-wide outcomes between the one-step and two-step approaches have been inconsistent to date.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparative outcomes,inconsistent data</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647733</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="One-Step Strategy" target="NIH Panel">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The NIH panel did not endorse the one-step strategy due to lack of clinical trial data demonstrating its benefits.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical evidence,decision-making</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647726</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="One-Step Strategy" target="Cost-Effectiveness">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A systematic review found the one-step strategy to be more likely cost-effective than the two-step method despite identifying more GDM cases.</data>
  <data key="d9">economic evaluation,screening efficiency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7869f89a9c58ace31efe679a36aab7cf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647728</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hemoglobinopathies" target="A1C Test">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hemoglobin variants can interfere with A1C assays, necessitating the use of non-interfered methods for accurate diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobinopathies such as sickle cell disease can interfere with A1C assay accuracy, requiring alternative diagnostic methods.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,diagnostic limitation,test interference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-5b5fc9e82121669cb9d4aff08c8c9019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
