  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="Hemoglobin Glycation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The A1C test measures hemoglobin glycation, which reflects average blood glucose levels over time.</data>
  <data key="d9">biological basis,measurement principle</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647767</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="Genetic Background">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Genetic variants such as HbS and G6PD G202A can alter A1C levels independent of glucose, affecting test reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic influence,test reliability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647769</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="Sickle Cell Trait">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Individuals with sickle cell trait may have unreliable A1C results and should use an A1C assay that is not affected by hemoglobin variants.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic interference,test adjustment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647770</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="HbS">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Heterozygous carriers of HbS may have A1C levels approximately 0.3% lower than non-carriers for the same glycemic level.</data>
  <data key="d9">genetic variant,measurement bias</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647771</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase G202A">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Homozygous carriers of G6PD G202A variant show reduced A1C levels by about 0.7–0.8%, independent of glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">A1C reduction,genetic variant</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776647772</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="A1C Test" target="Tanzania">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In Tanzania, high prevalence of hemoglobinopathies and HIV may reduce A1C reliability for diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">geographic limitation,public health challenge</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-146b6bf0e9a99df13de25f5e1318178a</data>
