<edge source="Botnia Study" target="TTGO-1h">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the Botnia Study, TTGO-1h demonstrated superior sensitivity and specificity in predicting DM2 compared to GJ and TTGO-2h.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical evidence,diagnostic comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The oral glucose tolerance test (TTGO) is used to diagnose diabetes mellitus, particularly in high-risk individuals where other tests may not detect the condition.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic method,glucose tolerance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689105</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO" target="Pre-Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO results are used to diagnose pre-diabetes and evaluate how close an individual is to meeting diabetes criteria.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,risk stratification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689238</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO-1h is more accurate than other markers in predicting progression to type 2 diabetes, as shown in multiple studies.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is recommended for detecting undiagnosed type 2 diabetes or predicting future risk in individuals with prediabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">early detection,prediction,risk assessment,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689105</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Israel GOH Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Israel GOH Study reported a 4.35-fold increased risk of developing DM2 for individuals with TTGO-1h ≥ 155 mg/dl.</data>
  <data key="d9">long-term follow-up,risk ratio</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="RISC Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The RISC Study showed that elevated TTGO-1h values are associated with higher insulin resistance and progression to glucose intolerance.</data>
  <data key="d9">insulin resistance,metabolic dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689129</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="GJ">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO-1h has higher sensitivity than GJ in detecting individuals at risk for DM2, as demonstrated in the San Antonio Heart Study.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,diagnostic accuracy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="TTGO-2h">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A blood glucose level of 209 mg/dl at TTGO-1h is considered equivalent to 200 mg/dl at TTGO-2h for diagnosing diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h outperforms TTGO-2h in sensitivity and positive predictive value for predicting DM2.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,diagnostic equivalence,diagnostic performance,glucose tolerance testing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-2h" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO-2h is used to confirm diabetes diagnosis and has been shown to identify cases missed by fasting glucose or HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis confirmation,sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GJ" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GJ is used as a primary screening tool for diabetes, but has lower sensitivity compared to TTGO-1h.&lt;SEP&gt;GJ, or fasting plasma glucose, is a primary diagnostic measure for identifying type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood glucose level,diagnosis,diagnostic criterion,screening</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689104</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GJ" target="Simultaneous Measurement">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">GJ and HbA1c can be measured simultaneously from a single fasting blood sample, improving screening efficiency for type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">screening efficiency,single sample</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689105</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GJ" target="Tabela 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Tabela 2 specifies the use of GJ measurement in fasting blood samples for initial diabetes screening, especially in settings with partial technical and financial resources.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic reference,screening protocol</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GJ" target="Risco Cardiovascular">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fasting plasma glucose (GJ) levels in the prediabetes range are linked to higher cardiovascular risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">cardiovascular risk,prediabetes marker</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689133</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="GJ" target="Pre-Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fasting plasma glucose (GJ) values help define pre-diabetes and determine progression risk toward diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,risk stratification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689237</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Simultaneous Measurement">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Simultaneous measurement of GJ and HbA1c enhances the accuracy of initial type 2 diabetes screening in settings with full technical and financial feasibility.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic accuracy,early detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8c3c6ce19ad6bc3cc3df22e5e10b0702</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689107</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Low Birth Weight">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Low birth weight increases the risk of insulin resistance and DM2 later in life by sevenfold.</data>
  <data key="d9">developmental risk,long-term effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689119</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Prevalence Of DM2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The prevalence of DM2 increased by 30.5% from 2001 to 2009 and was 3.3% in Brazilian adolescents according to the ERICA study.</data>
  <data key="d9">disease trend,epidemiology</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689122</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="TODAY Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The TODAY study characterized DM2 in youth, showing high rates in females, obesity, and early beta-cell deterioration.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,disease characterization</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fd83fee2b80ad551bb282975932751ce</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689125</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Glicose No TTGO-1h">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Elevated glucose levels at one hour during the oral glucose tolerance test (≥155 mg/dl) are associated with an increased risk of developing Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,risk prediction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689128</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="GHO">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The GHO study contributed data on the predictive value of one-hour glucose levels for Type 2 Diabetes incidence.</data>
  <data key="d9">epidemiological evidence,prospective research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689130</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Botnia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Botnia study demonstrated a direct association between one-hour glucose levels and the development of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">epidemiological evidence,prospective research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689161</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Fiorentino E Cols">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fiorentino and colleagues found that individuals with glucose ≥155 mg/dl at one hour had a 4.02 times higher risk of developing Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical research,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689162</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Rastreamento Para Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Screening for Type 2 Diabetes is recommended for individuals aged 35 or older or those with overweight and additional risk factors to enable early diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">early detection,screening strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689162</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="VIGITEL 2023">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">VIGITEL 2023 data show increasing prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes with age, supporting age-based screening recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d9">epidemiological data,national surveillance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689163</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DM2" target="Glicemia de Jejum">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fasting glucose levels, such as 101 mg/dL, are used to identify individuals at higher risk of developing DM2.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic criterion,risk stratification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689197</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="FINDRISC" target="Rastreamento De Dm2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">High or very high FINDRISC scores are used to identify individuals who should undergo screening for type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk stratification,screening indication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ea289ce35cdd947df9d56e9e4b5c8566</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689067</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="FINDRISC" target="Diabetes Mellitus Screening">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">FINDRISC is used to categorize individuals into risk levels to guide recommendations for additional diabetes testing.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk stratification,screening recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb6ee71a842cf35dd741ee96a80c624b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689127</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="FINDRISC" target="Rastreamento Para Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">FINDRISC is used to identify individuals with high or very high risk for Type 2 Diabetes who should undergo screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk assessment tool,screening criterion</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4e72b56afa6bad1b13c937a3ff9bd13d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689163</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="FINDRISC" target="Pessoas com Baixo Risco de DM">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">FINDRISC is used to classify individuals as having low to moderate risk for DM2 based on risk factor scoring.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2b3097da75459ebf108182050a889e65</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689198</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="FINDRISC" target="Screening For Diabetes Mellitus Type 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">High or very high FINDRISC scores indicate elevated diabetes risk and justify annual screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">risk assessment,screening indication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2d8f51fe0c33fe28ed188c855a82a3af</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689237</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia De 2 Horas No TTGO" target="Pré-Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pré-Diabetes is indicated by 2-hour post-glucose blood glucose levels between 140–199 mg/dl.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic range,impaired glucose tolerance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689194</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia De 2 Horas No TTGO" target="Variabilidade Intraindividual">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Two-hour glucose levels show higher intraindividual variability (16.7%), reducing diagnostic reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">high variability,measurement inconsistency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689195</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia De 2 Horas No TTGO" target="Prevalência De DM Não Diagnosticado">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Undiagnosed Diabetes Mellitus prevalence was 9% with one abnormal two-hour test, dropping to 6.7% with confirmation, a 26% reduction.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic confirmation,prevalence estimation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0842e3c99a8c4dc96abdcb05ee7fe0f3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
