</edge>
<edge source="Intensive Treatment" target="Conventional Treatment">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In multiple studies, intensive treatment was compared to conventional treatment to assess differences in glycemic control and complication rates.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical trial design,treatment comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2ad6cd6b0bad77397aa6685ccb2cfaef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689390</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="HbA1c %" target="UKPDS">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The UKPDS showed that HbA1c below 7% reduces microvascular complications in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical evidence,microvascular risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689395</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glicemia De Jejum E Pré Prandial" target="TIR 70-180 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TIR 70-180 mg/dL is a comprehensive metric that includes time spent in target during fasting, pre-meal, and other periods.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,monitoring metric</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689393</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="T Hipog &lt;70 Mg/Dl" target="T Hipog &lt;54 Mg/Dl">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">T Hipog &lt;70 mg/dL and T Hipog &lt;54 mg/dL represent different thresholds for hypoglycemia, with the latter indicating severe episodes.</data>
  <data key="d9">hypoglycemia severity,risk monitoring</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689393</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Valores Normais De Glicemia De Jejum" target="Adultos Não Gestantes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal fasting glucose range of 70-99 mg/dL applies specifically to non-pregnant adults.</data>
  <data key="d9">normal physiology,reference range</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0a582234d1973113fc899208b5457f47</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1776689395</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Valores Normais De HbA1c" target="Adultos Não Gestantes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The normal HbA1c level of less than 5.7% is defined for non-pregnant adults without diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">glycemic control,reference range</data>
